E["item:ancient-statuette"] = {t="item",n="Ancient Statuette",z="ashenvale",s="Along Ashenvale's northwestern shore, Talen seeks the Ancient Statuette he recovered from Zoram's sunken ruins. The night elf effigy came from a city lost beneath the waves.",h="Along Ashenvale's northwestern shore, Talen seeks the Ancient Statuette he recovered from Zoram's sunken...",sec={{t="A Relic in the Shallows",b="The sunken ruins of Zoram lie off northwestern Ashenvale. The pre-Sundering night elven city was lost beneath the waves ten thousand years ago. Recently, the explorer Talen surveyed the ruins from a small craft, searching for historical relics. Naga attacked and drove him ashore. In his flight, he left most of his belongings behind, including the ancient statuette he had dredged up. It lies on the tideline sand near his scuttled skiff.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of Zoram",b="Talen calls the statuette his most prized possession and the reason he braved the monster-infested coast. He believes the effigy can help decipher Zoram's architecture, history, and arcane secrets, all hidden beneath the surf of Zoram Strand.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Ancient Statuette?",a="The Ancient Statuette came from the sunken ruins of Zoram, an ancient night elven city off Ashenvale's northwestern coast.",al={"what is statuette","ancient statuette lore","what is this item"},it="identity"},{q="Who is looking for the statuette?",a="The night elf explorer Talen seeks the statuette. Naga attacked while he surveyed the submerged ruins by boat, and he dropped the relic on the beach as he fled.",al={"who wants statuette","talen statuette","who lost the statuette"}},{q="Why is the statuette important?",a="Talen believes the statuette can help uncover Zoram's history and the secrets hidden in its ruins beneath the waves.",al={"why does talen want it","statuette purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are naga prowling around where it was found?",a="Naga have infested the coastal waters and ruins of Zoram Strand. They attack surface dwellers who venture near the sunken remains of their submerged territory.",al={"why naga on beach","zoram strand naga"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see the statuette as a fragment of Kaldorei civilization from before the Great Sundering, preserved under the sea for millennia.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help Talen document and reclaim night elven heritage from the naga encroaching along Ashenvale's coast."},kw={"ancient statuette","ashenvale","naga","ruins of zoram","statuette","talen","zoram","zoram strand"},rel={"quest:1007","npc:talen","subzone:zoram-strand","zone:ashenvale","topic:naga","quest:1009","quest:1008"},src={"Ancient Statuette","The Ancient Statuette"}}
E["item:bathran-s-hair"] = {t="item",n="Bathran's Hair",z="ashenvale",s="Among the ruins of Bathran's Haunt in northwestern Ashenvale, Bathran's Hair remains a rare herb. Night elf healers value its power against afflictions of the flesh and spirit.",h="Among the ruins of Bathran's Haunt in northwestern Ashenvale, Bathran's Hair remains a rare herb.",sec={{t="A Remedy for the Spirit",b="Bathran's Hair grows among the ancient ruins north of Maestra's Post, where night elf healers have long valued it. Common herbs soothe wounds of the body, but Bathran's Hair is said to restore the spirit as well. When a young night elf in Astranaar falls gravely ill, herbalist Orendil Broadleaf seeks the rare plant to prepare a remedy.",sp=0},{t="Gathering Amid the Ruins",b="Bathran's Hair is harder to find among the ruins. It lies in discarded plant bundles and beneath leaf piles scattered across Bathran's Haunt, near the border of Darkshore. Forsaken have also been seen among the ruins, news that troubles Orendil Broadleaf.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Bathran's Hair used for?",a="Night elf healers use Bathran's Hair against grave afflictions beyond ordinary sickness. Orendil Broadleaf combines it into a curative draft for a dying child whose spirit is wasting away.",al={"what does bathrans hair do","bathrans hair purpose","bathran hair use"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Bathran's Hair grow?",a="Bathran's Hair grows within Bathran's Haunt, an ancient ruined settlement in northern Ashenvale, east of the main road leading north into Darkshore.",al={"where to find bathrans hair","bathran hair location","where is bathrans hair"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken interested in Bathran's Haunt?",a="Orendil Broadleaf learns that Forsaken are at Bathran's Haunt and finds their presence troubling, but what they want there is not explained. Elsewhere in Ashenvale, night elves report Forsaken at ruins and barrows, and fear they mean to spread disease across the forest.",al={"why are undead at bathrans haunt","forsaken in bathrans haunt","undead bathran"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Orendil Broadleaf?",a="Orendil Broadleaf is an herbalist at Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale. He studies local plants and prepares medicines for travelers and wounded defenders of the forest.",al={"orendil broadleaf","who wants bathran hair"},it="people"},{q="What is Bathran's Hair?",a="Bathran's Hair is a rare, delicate herb found growing amid the ancient ruins of Bathran's Haunt in northern Ashenvale. Renowned among night elf herbalists, the plant possesses potent restorative qualities capable of mending ailments of the spirit as well as bodily afflictions.",al={"what is bathrans hair","bathran hair plant","bathran's hair plant"},it="identity",add="b940f392"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Trained herbalists can find Bathran's Hair more readily, sensing hidden plant bundles among the debris with a practiced eye for wild flora.",["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, Forsaken among the ruins where healing plants like Bathran's Hair grow trouble the preservation of their ancient homeland."},kw={"ashenvale","bathran's hair","bathran's haunt","bathrans hair","maestra's post","orendil broadleaf","plant bundle"},rel={"quest:1010","subzone:bathran-s-haunt","npc:orendil-broadleaf","quest:1020","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:ashenvale","topic:forsaken"},src={"Bathran's Hair","Bathran's Hair (Classic)"}}
E["item:bottle-of-disease"] = {t="item",n="Bottle of Disease",z="ashenvale",s="Forsaken alchemists brew disease near the Dor'Danil Barrow Den in Ashenvale. The bottles hold virulent concoctions found at their encampment.",h="Forsaken alchemists brew disease near the Dor'Danil Barrow Den in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Blight in the Sacred Woods",b="Near the Dor'Danil Barrow Den, Forsaken alchemists brew contagions in an outpost beyond the Warsong Outriders' front lines. The bottles give night elves at Forest Song evidence of an offensive aimed at sickening the woodland soil and wildlife instead of meeting their sentinels in open combat.",sp=0},{t="Kayneth Stillwind's Investigation",b="Kayneth Stillwind, a night elf sentry at Forest Song, seeks proof of Forsaken ambitions. He wants a Bottle of Disease so he can study its contents. The night elves fear the mixtures could corrupt sacred barrows and break the minds and bodies of the forest's defenders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Bottle of Disease?",a="Forsaken apothecaries brew synthetic poisons and magical contagions in the bottle. The Royal Apothecary Society conducts broader experiments with virulent blights.",al={"what is in the bottle","bottle of disease contents","forsaken potion"},it="item"},{q="Where are these bottles found?",a="The bottles are in an isolated Forsaken encampment south of Forest Song, near the entrance to Dor'Danil Barrow Den in eastern Ashenvale.",al={"where to find bottle of disease","bottle of disease location","forsaken camp ashenvale"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Bottle of Disease?",a="Kayneth Stillwind, a night elf protector at Forest Song, wants you to retrieve a bottle so he can test its contents and learn the Horde's intentions.",al={"who takes bottle of disease","turn in bottle of disease","kayneth stillwind quest"},it="target"},{q="Why are the Forsaken brewing diseases in Ashenvale?",a="The night elves suspect the Forsaken mean to infect the sacred forest and desecrate nearby barrow dens, poisoning the ecosystem and weakening night elven resistance from within.",al={"why forsaken in ashenvale","undead goal in ashenvale","forsaken barrow dens"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Bottle of Disease?",a="It is a sealed vial containing virulent toxins and blights concocted by the Forsaken. Agents of the Undercity brew these vile concoctions in secret camps across Ashenvale, bottling them for transport and deliberate spreading across the ancient elven woodlands.",al={"what is bottle of disease","bottle of disease lore","bottle of disease info"},it="identity",add="4091970d"},{q="Where does the Bottle of Disease come from, and who made it?",a="The bottle is brewed by Forsaken apothecaries stationed at a secluded camp south of Forest Song, near the Dor'Danil Barrow Den. Lurking near sacred night elven barrows, these undead alchemists actively harvest and distill dangerous poisons and blights on Kalimdor soil.",al={"who made bottle of disease","bottle of disease origin","where did bottle of disease come from"},it="origin",add="62494cf6"},{q="Why does Kayneth Stillwind want the Bottle of Disease?",a="Kayneth Stillwind at Forest Song needs an intact sample to analyze what the Forsaken are plotting. By testing the concoction's alchemical properties, the night elves hope to confirm whether the undead aim to blight Ashenvale itself and prepare an effective countermeasure.",al={"why want bottle of disease","why get bottle of disease","why does kayneth want disease bottle"},it="why_wanted",add="9d281de4"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know that undead contagion on Ashenvale's soil is an unforgivable affront, especially near Dor'Danil Barrow Den.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know blighted mixtures and artificial plagues oppose natural balance. You must act swiftly to preserve the woodland."},kw={"ashenvale","blight","bottle of disease","dor'danil barrow den","forest song","forsaken","forsaken diseases","kayneth stillwind"},rel={"quest:1011","quest:1012","subzone:forest-song","subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den","zone:ashenvale","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:druid"},src={"Bottle of Disease","Forsaken Diseases"}}
E["item:branch-of-cenarius"] = {t="item",n="Branch of Cenarius",z="ashenvale",s="In eastern Ashenvale, Geltharis holds the Branch of Cenarius, sacred to the dryads. Anilia died defending the relic, and her dying wish was to see it recovered.",h="In eastern Ashenvale, Geltharis holds the Branch of Cenarius, sacred to the dryads.",sec={{t="A Sacred Bough Fallen to Shadow",b="The Branch of Cenarius is sacred to the dryads who follow the Forest Lord. Anilia and her sister Illiyana treasured it until corrupt satyrs ambushed them. Their leader, Geltharis, seized the branch and mortally wounded Anilia near the tainted ruins of eastern Ashenvale. As she lay dying, Anilia pointed north toward the arch where Geltharis lurks. She pleaded for a champion to take back the bough and return it to the dryads at Forest Song.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Branch of Cenarius?",a="The Branch of Cenarius is a sacred relic treasured by Ashenvale’s dryads. It bears the Forest Lord’s name and blessing, and represents their bond with the ancient forest.",al={"branch of cenarius lore","what is this branch","dryad branch"},it="identity"},{q="Who stole the Branch of Cenarius?",a="Geltharis stole the Branch of Cenarius after leading an ambush on the dryads near eastern Ashenvale. He mortally wounded Anilia and fled north beyond a stone arch with the branch.",al={"who took the branch","who stole it","who drops branch of cenarius"},it="threat"},{q="Who does the branch belong to?",a="The branch belongs to the dryads of Forest Song. Anilia died defending it, and her sister Illiyana receives the relic in keeping with Anilia’s dying wish.",al={"who gets the branch","who wants the branch","who do i give it to"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="Where is the branch recovered?",a="Geltharis carries the branch just north of the ruins in eastern Ashenvale where Anilia falls, near the border with Azshara.",al={"branch location","where is geltharis","where to find branch"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Branch of Cenarius so important to retrieve?",a="The dryads of Ashenvale consider the branch an invaluable sacred relic tied to their father, Cenarius. When the dryad Anilia was mortally wounded by corrupted satyrs near Xavian, her dying wish was to ensure the stolen bough was wrested back from Geltharis and safely returned into dryad hands at Forest Song.",al={"why retrieve branch of cenarius","why dryads want branch","branch of cenarius purpose"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",add="4e4ec82f"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share a duty to reclaim the Branch of Cenarius from the satyr who defiled it.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf of Ashenvale, you have a sacred duty to aid the dryads and recover their ancestral treasures."},kw={"anilia","ashenvale","branch of cenarius","dryad","forest song","geltharis","illiyana","satyr"},rel={"quest:1031","quest:1021","npc:illiyana","subzone:forest-song","zone:ashenvale","topic:cenarius","topic:satyr"},src={"Branch of Cenarius","The Branch of Cenarius (Classic)"}}
E["item:dal-bloodclaw-s-skull"] = {t="item",n="Dal Bloodclaw's Skull",z="ashenvale",s="In northern Ashenvale, Dal Bloodclaw's Skull marks the end of a threat to Astranaar. Raene Wolfrunner receives it as proof that an attack on the night elf settlement has been averted.",h="In northern Ashenvale, Dal Bloodclaw's Skull marks the end of a threat to Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Chieftain's Downfall",b="The Thistlefur furbolgs north of Astranaar have grown in number and aggression. Like much of Ashenvale's ancient forest, they have been corrupted. Raene Wolfrunner, a night elf sentinel, fears they will soon march on Astranaar. She orders their ranks culled and their leader, Dal Bloodclaw, slain. His skull gives grim proof that the tribe's leadership has been shattered, buying Astranaar's defenders precious time.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Dal Bloodclaw?",a="Dal Bloodclaw led the Thistlefur furbolgs at Thistlefur Hold, just north of Astranaar. The hostile tribe grew rapidly under his leadership and threatened the nearby night elf outpost.",al={"dal bloodclaw","who is bloodclaw","thistlefur chief"},it="target"},{q="Why does Raene Wolfrunner want the skull?",a="Raene Wolfrunner wants proof that the Thistlefur chieftain is dead. The night elves hope the surviving furbolgs will fall into disarray and lose any organized plans to attack Astranaar.",al={"why skull","raene wolfrunner skull","proof of death"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the Thistlefur furbolgs so hostile?",a="Like many furbolg tribes in Ashenvale, the Thistlefurs have succumbed to corruption spreading through the forest. They have become violent and territorial, threatening those who once lived beside them.",al={"why furbolgs aggressive","furbolg corruption","thistlefur mad"},it="threat"},{q="What is Dal Bloodclaw's Skull?",a="It is the severed skull of Dal Bloodclaw, chieftain of the corrupted Thistlefur furbolgs residing in Thistlefur Hold north of Astranaar. It serves as gruesome physical proof of his demise.",al={"what is dal bloodclaws skull","dal skull","what is this skull"},it="identity",add="b1ad26a7"},{q="Where does Dal Bloodclaw's Skull come from?",a="The skull is taken directly from the remains of Dal Bloodclaw himself within Thistlefur Hold, deep in northern Ashenvale, after he is slain to break the leadership of his growing tribe.",al={"where does dal bloodclaws skull come from","who made dal bloodclaws skull","dal bloodclaw skull origin"},it="origin",add="fa2f0114"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may see the sorrow in defeating fallen furbolg leaders. Corruption has twisted ancient allies, and they now threaten settlements such as Astranaar.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure Astranaar's northern flank. The settlement is the Alliance's main sanctuary in central Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","dal bloodclaw","furbolg","raene wolfrunner","skull","thistlefur"},rel={"quest:1054","npc:raene-wolfrunner","subzone:thistlefur-hold","subzone:astranaar","topic:furbolg","zone:ashenvale","zone:darnassus","topic:elune"},src={"Dal Bloodclaw's Skull","Culling the Threat"}}
E["item:divined-scroll"] = {t="item",n="Divined Scroll",z="ashenvale",s="At Silverwind Refuge, the Divined Scroll can expose the mage behind Ashenvale's troubled waters. Night elves use magic from intact water elemental bracers to reveal the summoner's identity.",h="At Silverwind Refuge, the Divined Scroll can expose the mage behind Ashenvale's troubled waters.",sec={{t="Tracing the Summoner",b="Mystral Lake's tainted waters trouble the Sentinels guarding Ashenvale. Sentinel Velene Starstrike gives travelers an uncharged divining scroll to trace whoever manipulates the water elementals infesting the lake. Gather intact bracers from slain elementals and use them as an arcane reagent; their latent bindings pass into the parchment. The Divined Scroll then reveals the magical signature of the rogue wizard behind the infestation.",sp=0},{t="The Mage Exposed",b="The Divined Scroll's script points Sentinel Velene to a mortal culprit: a reckless mage deliberately corrupting the woodland pools. With this revelation, the Sentinels can plan retribution and send scouts to hunt the summoner responsible for despoiling their sacred wilderness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Divined Scroll used for?",a="The Divined Scroll reveals the spellcaster summoning and binding hostile water elementals in Ashenvale's lakes, so Sentinel Velene Starstrike can target the culprit.",al={"what does divined scroll do","divined scroll purpose","why make divined scroll"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How is the Divined Scroll created?",a="Cast Sentinel Velene Starstrike's blank Divining Scroll upon five Intact Elemental Bracers gathered from defeated water elementals around Mystral Lake.",al={"how to make divined scroll","crafting divined scroll","how do i get divined scroll"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why are the elemental bracers needed to divine the scroll?",a="The bracers bind the elementals to the mortal plane. Their residual enchantments give the scroll the magical signature it needs to identify the wizard who conjured them.",al={"why intact bracers","purpose of elemental bracers"}},{q="Who do I bring the Divined Scroll to?",a="Bring the finished Divined Scroll to Sentinel Velene Starstrike at Silverwind Refuge, along the road in southern Ashenvale.",al={"where do i turn in divined scroll","who wants divined scroll"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Divined Scroll?",a="The Divined Scroll is the result of using a divining scroll alongside intact bracers harvested from water elementals fouling Ashenvale's waters. Infused with arcane traces lingering on those bindings, the scroll reveals mystical information regarding the specific conjurer responsible for summoning and corrupting the elementals.",al={"what is divined scroll","divined scroll purpose","what does the divined scroll do"},it="identity",add="155064fc",nx={6}},{q="Where does the Divined Scroll come from, and who made it?",a="You create the Divined Scroll yourself by channeling Sentinel Velene Starstrike's divining scroll upon several intact elemental bracers. The bracers serve as an arcane reagent, allowing the scroll's divination magic to focus and record the magical signatures of the elementals' creator.",al={"who made divined scroll","divined scroll origin","how was divined scroll created"},it="origin",add="ebb5ddd6"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can see the principle at work: elemental bindings carry the arcane signature of the wizard who forged them.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you know divination tools help the Sentinels find mortal polluters whose arcane meddling threatens Ashenvale's sacred waters."},kw={"ashenvale","divined scroll","divining scroll","elemental bracers","mystral lake","silverwind refuge","velene starstrike"},rel={"item:divining-scroll","quest:1016","quest:1017","npc:sentinel-velene-starstrike","subzone:silverwind-refuge","zone:ashenvale","topic:mage"},src={"Divined Scroll","Elemental Bracers (quest)"}}
E["item:divining-scroll"] = {t="item",n="Divining Scroll",z="ashenvale",s="At Silverwind Refuge, Sentinel Velene Starstrike gives investigators the Divining Scroll to trace the corrupted elementals to their creator.",h="At Silverwind Refuge, Sentinel Velene Starstrike gives investigators the Divining Scroll to trace the...",sec={{t="Tracing Unnatural Elementals",b="Corrupt water elementals rise from Ashenvale’s pools, and the Sentinels know the disturbance is unnatural. Sentinel Velene Starstrike obtains a scroll to find who is responsible. With intact elemental bracers as a focus, its magic draws out the summoner’s signature. The blank parchment becomes a Divined Scroll and names the guilty party.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Divining Scroll used for?",a="The Divining Scroll identifies who created the corrupt water elementals in Ashenvale. Intact elemental bracers focus its magic, which reads the caster’s aura and records their identity.",al={"what does the scroll do","divining scroll purpose","why use divining scroll"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Divining Scroll?",a="Sentinel Velene Starstrike gives the scroll to Alliance investigators at Silverwind Refuge in southern Ashenvale as she investigates the tainted waters.",al={"who gives divining scroll","where to get scroll","velene starstrike scroll"},it="origin"},{q="Why are intact elemental bracers needed?",a="Most bracers shatter beyond recognition in combat. A few remain intact, holding enough of their summoner’s binding magic to focus the divination spell.",al={"why bracers","intact elemental bracers","reagent for scroll"}},{q="What happens after the scroll is used?",a="Used in the presence of five intact bracers, the scroll is consumed and becomes a Divined Scroll. It reveals that a rogue mage is deliberately summoning corrupt elementals into the forest’s lakes.",al={"divined scroll","after using scroll","what does it turn into"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Divining Scroll?",a="The Divining Scroll is an enchanted parchment used to uncover magical origins. When focused using intact elemental bracers as a reagent, its magic can trace the binding signatures on the water elementals troubling Ashenvale and identify the rogue spellcaster who summoned them into the forest's pristine waters.",al={"what is divining scroll","divining scroll lore","divining scroll item"},it="identity",add="51ca655d"},{q="Why is the Divining Scroll wanted?",a="Sentinel Velene Starstrike needs the scroll to discover who is filling Ashenvale's lakes and pools with corrupt water elementals. Without the scroll's divining magic, the night elves cannot pinpoint the mage responsible or stop the ongoing defilement of their sacred wilderness.",al={"why do you need divining scroll","why is the scroll needed","purpose of divining scroll"},it="why_wanted",add="af5653e2"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The scroll uses divination to track arcane resonance. It reveals that a fellow practitioner is abusing elemental summoning within sacred kaldorei groves.",["race:NightElf"]="For the Sentinels who protect Ashenvale, the scroll can expose outsiders who defile the forest’s pristine waters with unnatural corruption."},kw={"ashenvale","divined scroll","divining scroll","elemental bracers","silverwind refuge","velene starstrike","water elementals"},rel={"quest:1016","item:divined-scroll","npc:sentinel-velene-starstrike","subzone:silverwind-refuge","quest:1017","zone:ashenvale","topic:mage"},src={"Divining Scroll","Elemental Bracers (quest)"}}
E["item:elune-s-tear"] = {t="item",n="Elune's Tear",z="ashenvale",s="On Ashenvale's central island, Elune's Tear offers night elf healers a sacred means to cleanse corruption and sickness.",h="On Ashenvale's central island, Elune's Tear offers night elf healers a sacred means to cleanse corruption and...",sec={{t="A Sacred Cleansing Stone",b="Elune's Tear rests on a small islet in Iris Lake, east of Astranaar. Night elves believe the stone carries the Moon Goddess's purity. Corruption has turned the lake green, and twisted bog beasts roam its shores. Local herbalists and healers, including Orendil Broadleaf, seek the stone as an emergency remedy when ordinary woodland poultices cannot wash away deep corruption.",sp=0},{t="A Desperate Remedy",b="Relara Whitemoon, a young night elf in Astranaar, falls ill with a mysterious wasting sickness. Her father, Pelturas, exhausts ordinary medicines. At apothecary Orendil's counsel, Pelturas seeks Elune's Tear to brew into a restorative stew. The stone gives immediate hope against the strange malady, but Ashenvale's stubborn corruption often calls for greater rites of cleansing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Elune's Tear?",a="Elune's Tear is a rare magical mineral on an island in Iris Lake, Ashenvale. Night elves regard it as sacred to Elune and use it to cleanse unnatural corruption and deadly sickness.",al={"elunes tear","what is this stone","what does elunes tear do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Elune's Tear be found?",a="Elune's Tear lies on the island in the middle of Iris Lake, east of Astranaar in central Ashenvale. Follow the stream path north from the main road to reach it.",al={"where is elunes tear","iris lake stone location","find elunes tear"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Pelturas Whitemoon need the tear?",a="Pelturas seeks Elune's Tear to help his ailing daughter, Relara. When ordinary herbal cures fail against her strange sickness, apothecary Orendil advises him to use the stone's restorative power.",al={"why pelturas want it","relara cure","who needs elunes tear"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What guards the stone at Iris Lake?",a="Twisted bog beasts roam the shores of Iris Lake, whose waters have turned green under Ashenvale's spreading corruption.",al={"iris lake enemies","what protects elunes tear"},it="danger",gp=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know relics bearing Elune's name as sacred gifts. The stone's use to save an innocent child reflects the kaldorei bond with the Moon Mother's healing grace.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you recognize the stone's power to purge shadow and rot. Its healing reflects the restorative miracles attributed to the Priesthood of Elune."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","cure","elune's tear","iris lake","orendil","pelturas","relara"},rel={"quest:1033","subzone:iris-lake","subzone:astranaar","quest:1020","quest:1010","topic:elune","zone:ashenvale","quest:1034"},src={"Elune's Tear","Elune's Tear (Classic)"}}
E["item:fallen-moonstone"] = {t="item",n="Fallen Moonstone",z="ashenvale",s="At Fallen Sky Lake in Ashenvale, night elves gather luminous, magically charged Fallen Moonstones from its tranquil waters. Sacred lunar energy gives the stones restorative power that can renew vitality and cure severe frailty.",h="At Fallen Sky Lake in Ashenvale, night elves gather luminous, magically charged Fallen Moonstones from its...",sec={{t="Gifts of the Night Sky",b="Southeast of Astranaar, Fallen Sky Lake once yielded many stones along its shores and shallows. Night elves prized their restorative magic and lunar blessing when ordinary remedies failed. Gathering them grew dangerous after corrupt Shadethicket bog beasts overran the lake. Their leader, a Shadethicket Oracle, hoarded every stone it found on a small island at the lake’s center, cutting the local Kaldorei off from a vital source of healing.",sp=0},{t="A Father's Salvation",b="In Astranaar, young Relara Whitemoon fell gravely ill. Ordinary treatments broke her fever, but left her faded and near death, with only a few breaths remaining. Her father, Pelturas Whitemoon, knew only a moonstone’s concentrated restorative power could renew her depleted vitality. A stone recovered from the Shadethicket Oracle’s hoard gave the child the strength she needed to live.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Fallen Moonstone?",a="A Fallen Moonstone is a luminous, magically charged stone from Fallen Sky Lake in Ashenvale. Sacred lunar energy gives it restorative power, which night elves use to replenish strength in the severely weakened.",al={"what is fallen moonstone","fallen moonstone lore","moonstone ashenvale"},it="identity"},{q="Where are Fallen Moonstones found?",a="Fallen Moonstones come from Fallen Sky Lake, southeast of Astranaar in Ashenvale. Once scattered across the lake bed, they were gathered and hoarded on a central island by the hostile Shadethicket bog beasts.",al={"where to find fallen moonstone","fallen moonstone location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who possesses the moonstones at Fallen Sky Lake?",a="The Shadethicket Oracle hoarded the Fallen Moonstones on an island in the center of Fallen Sky Lake. The Oracle leads the corrupted bog beasts there.",al={"who has the fallen moonstone","shadethicket oracle moonstone"},it="residents"},{q="Why does Pelturas Whitemoon need a Fallen Moonstone?",a="Pelturas Whitemoon needs a Fallen Moonstone to save his young daughter, Relara. Though she survived a debilitating fever, she remained critically frail, and he knew a moonstone’s magic could restore her vigor.",al={"pelturas whitemoon daughter","why need moonstone","relara cure"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, relics linked to Elune’s radiance are sacred instruments of preservation. They offer divine healing when mortal medicine fails.",["class:Priest"]="Devotees of the Sisterhood of Elune see the lunar glow of these stones as a sign of healing grace."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","fallen moonstone","fallen sky lake","moonstone","pelturas whitemoon","relara","shadethicket oracle"},rel={"quest:1035","npc:pelturas-whitemoon","subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","topic:elune","quest:1034","quest:1033","quest:1020"},src={"Fallen Moonstone","Fallen Sky Lake (quest)"}}
E["item:glowing-gem"] = {t="item",n="Glowing Gem",z="ashenvale",s="At Lake Falathim, the Glowing Gem lies among the murlocs after Teronis fell seeking it. The stone holds magic needed to restore Dartol's rod.",h="At Lake Falathim, the Glowing Gem lies among the murlocs after Teronis fell seeking it.",sec={{t="A Lost Relic of Dartol",b="Murlocs near Lake Falathim hold the Glowing Gem, a stone with latent magic. Teronis, a young night elf from Astranaar, went after it to find a way to push back the corruption spreading through Ashenvale's forests. Teronis died at the lake, but the stone remained intact among the scavengers along the shore.",sp=0},{t="Restoring the Rod",b="After the Glowing Gem and Teronis's journal are recovered, Sentinel leader Raene Wolfrunner sends the bearer northeast to Shael'dryn, a dryad keeping watch at a nearby moonwell. Shael'dryn knows how to bind the gem to the other missing pieces of Dartol's rod, carrying Teronis's work forward.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Glowing Gem come from?",a="Murlocs carry the Glowing Gem along the shores and shallow waters around the shrine at Lake Falathim in western Ashenvale, where Teronis fell.",al={"glowing gem location","who drops glowing gem","where to get glowing gem"},it="origin"},{q="Why was Teronis looking for this gem?",a="Teronis sought a way to cleanse the growing foulness in Ashenvale. His research named the Glowing Gem as a key part needed to rebuild a magical rod devised by Dartol.",al={"teronis quest","why teronis wanted gem","purpose of gem"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who should I take the Glowing Gem to?",a="Show the Glowing Gem and Teronis's journal to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar, then take the stone northeast to Shael'dryn, the dryad at the moonwell east of Iris Lake.",al={"who needs glowing gem","turn in glowing gem","what to do with gem"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the rod of Dartol?",a="Dartol's rod is a magical instrument he created. Its pieces were scattered across the forest, and the Glowing Gem is needed to rebuild it.",al={"dartol rod","what did dartol make","dartols rod"}},{q="What is the Glowing Gem?",a="The Glowing Gem is an enchanted stone needed to recreate the rod Dartol made. Teronis sought it during his research into Ashenvale's corruption, and Raene Wolfrunner directs the search for the rod's remaining pieces.",al={"what is glowing gem","tell me about glowing gem","glowing gem lore"},it="identity",add="464fc9d6"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, recovering the gem and carrying out Teronis's mission honors the fallen scout and helps the Sentinels protect Ashenvale from spreading corruption.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Teronis's research into the spreading corruption and the relic he hoped to restore concern you."},kw={"astranaar","cleansing rod","dartol","glowing gem","iris lake","murloc","raene wolfrunner","shael'dryn","teronis"},rel={"npc:teronis-corpse","item:teronis-journal","npc:raene-wolfrunner","npc:shael-dryn","subzone:iris-lake","subzone:astranaar","topic:murloc","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale"},src={"Glowing Gem","Raene's Cleansing (2)","Raene's Cleansing (3)"}}
E["item:handful-of-stardust"] = {t="item",n="Handful of Stardust",z="ashenvale",s="In the Ruins of Stardust, a pale frost gathers on the bushes south of Astranaar. Night elven healers use the powder to cool intense fevers.",h="In the Ruins of Stardust, a pale frost gathers on the bushes south of Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Cooling Herbal Remedy",b="Stardust clings to shrubs in the Ruins of Stardust, south of Astranaar. The fine powder shines like frost. Lingering elemental spirits haunt the ruins, yet plants thrive among the broken stones and take in a rare glow. Night elven healers make the residue into poultices for dangerous, persistent fevers. They turn to it when ordinary salves and moonwell waters bring no full relief.",sp=0},{t="A Father's Hope",b="Pelturas Whitemoon, a worried father in Astranaar, followed herbalist Orendil Broadleaf's advice and sought the powder. His young daughter, Relara, suffered from a stubborn magical ailment and nightmares. A blessing from a stone touched by Elune first calmed her mind, but her intense fever remained. Pelturas sought stardust to make a cooling paste and save her life.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Handful of Stardust found?",a="You can gather stardust from the shining bushes in the Ruins of Stardust, south of Astranaar in central Ashenvale.",al={"stardust location","where to find stardust","stardust covered bushes"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is this stardust used for?",a="Pelturas Whitemoon uses the powder in a soothing poultice for the unrelenting fever afflicting his daughter, Relara.",al={"use of stardust","pelturas cure","stardust purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What dangers surround the stardust bushes?",a="Hostile water elementals lurk near the shoreline and among the fallen pillars in the Ruins of Stardust, where the bushes grow.",al={"ruins of stardust enemies","ruins of stardust mobs"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Is stardust related to the goddess Elune?",a="Night elves revere celestial powers, and the ruins bear a starry name, but herbalists recommend stardust for its frosted, cooling nature as a physical medicine.",al={"is stardust magic","elune connection stardust"}},{q="What is a Handful of Stardust?",a="A Handful of Stardust is a shimmering, frosted powder collected from the glistening foliage within Ashenvale's ancient Ruins of Stardust. This rare botanical residue possesses soothing, magical cooling properties, making it invaluable for preparing potent herbal poultices to treat stubborn, life-threatening fevers.",al={"what is handful of stardust","what is stardust","stardust item lore"},it="identity",add="8cce1335"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="You gather stardust by hand from shining bushes. It reflects the night elves' use of rare local plants in restorative medicine.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf defending Ashenvale, you can see the bond between local remedies and your people's ancient ruins and herbal traditions."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","orendil","pelturas","poultice","relara","ruins of stardust","stardust"},rel={"quest:1034","subzone:ruins-of-stardust","subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","quest:1033","quest:1020","quest:1035","quest:1010"},src={"Handful of Stardust","The Ruins of Stardust (quest)"}}
E["item:iron-pommel"] = {t="item",n="Iron Pommel",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, the Iron Pommel is the last missing piece of Dartol's Rod. The long-dead wizard Dartol made the rod, and the night elves of Astranaar seek it to slow the furbolg attacks on their people. Druids at Dor'Danil Barrow Den kept the pommel safe until their sanctuary was overrun and they were slaughtered.",h="In Ashenvale, the Iron Pommel is the last missing piece of Dartol's Rod.",sec={{t="A Slain Circle's Burden",b="Dartol's Rod was split apart and scattered across Ashenvale to guard its mystic power. Night elf druids near the road south toward the Barrens took charge of the Iron Pommel. Their circle was massacred at Dor'Danil Barrow Den, and their shelter fell silent in ruins. The pommel vanished amid the destruction, swallowed by the bubbling oozes now moving through the defiled glade.",sp=0},{t="Recovered from the Mire",b="The pommel lies in the tainted hollow south of Splintertree Post, inside a sturdy chest. Those who search through the corrupt slimes find the chest intact within an ooze's acidic mass. The Iron Pommel is the final piece needed to rebuild Dartol's Rod.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Iron Pommel used for?",a="The Iron Pommel is the final piece needed to reassemble Dartol's Rod. Bring it to Shael'dryn at the moonwell, and she can mend the ancient artifact to help slow the furbolg attacks on the night elves of Ashenvale.",al={"iron pommel purpose","why do i need iron pommel","what does iron pommel do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who originally had the pommel?",a="Night elf druids near the road toward the Barrens had charge of the pommel. The circle was slaughtered before the rod could be reunited, and their haven lies in ruins.",al={"who guarded the pommel","who had iron pommel","dor'danil druids"},it="origin"},{q="Where is the pommel found?",a="The pommel is locked inside a chest carried within one of the corrupted slimes in the tainted hollow east of the main road. The hollow lies south of Splintertree Post and north of the Barrens border.",al={"iron pommel location","where is iron pommel","where do i get iron pommel"},gp=true},{q="Who do I bring the pommel to?",a="Bring the pommel to Shael'dryn, a dryad tending the moonwell east of Iris Lake. She knows the ritual needed to reconstruct Dartol's Rod.",al={"turn in iron pommel","where to take iron pommel","who wants the pommel"},gp=true},{q="What is the Iron Pommel?",a="The Iron Pommel is the final missing component required to reconstruct Dartol's Rod, a rod created by the long-dead wizard Dartol. Before their tragic fall, the druids residing at the Dor'Danil Barrow Den were entrusted with safeguarding this weighty metal piece. Lost amid the corruption and violence that swept through their sanctuary, the pommel eventually ended up locked away inside an old chest in the wild, awaiting someone capable of recovering it.",al={"what is iron pommel","iron pommel lore","what is the pommel for dartol's rod"},it="identity",add="9716c2ef"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can remember the fallen druids of Dor'Danil, whose sacred charge ended in slaughter at the forest's edge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, retrieving the pommel brings Dartol's Rod closer to completion, a vital aid in defending Ashenvale against creeping corruption."},kw={"ashenvale","dartol's rod","dor'danil","iron pommel","oso's chest","raene's cleansing","shael'dryn"},rel={"quest:991","npc:shael-dryn","zone:ashenvale","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},src={"Iron Pommel","Raene's Cleansing (5)"}}
E["item:iron-shaft"] = {t="item",n="Iron Shaft",z="ashenvale",s="Near Felwood, the Iron Shaft waits in a locked chest. It is one piece of Dartol's Rod, sought by Teronis to slow the furbolg assaults on Ashenvale.",h="Near Felwood, the Iron Shaft waits in a locked chest.",sec={{t="A Piece of Dartol's Rod",b="Dartol made the rod, then its pieces were scattered across Ashenvale. One was placed in the care of the druids of Dor'Danil. The Iron Shaft is the rod's sturdy metal core, kept in a locked chest in a glade near Ashenvale's northern border, close to Felwood.",sp=0},{t="The Forest's Blight",b="The key to the Iron Shaft's chest lies with treants that once tended these woods. Demonic corruption from Felwood has driven the Crazed and Withered Ancients mad. Shael'dryn, a dryad, asks travelers to recover the shaft so Dartol's Rod can be reforged and Teronis's work completed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Iron Shaft used for?",a="The Iron Shaft is one piece of the broken Dartol's Rod. Shael'dryn seeks the pieces so the rod can be reassembled and Teronis's effort to slow the furbolg assaults on Ashenvale can be completed.",al={"iron shaft purpose","what is this shaft","why do i need iron shaft"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where is the Iron Shaft found?",a="The Iron Shaft lies in a locked chest in a glade west of the road toward Felwood, in northern Ashenvale.",al={"iron shaft location","find iron shaft","where is the chest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you open the chest containing the shaft?",a="A Wooden Key opens the chest. The corrupted Crazed and Withered Ancients carry it as they wander the woods northeast of Raynewood Retreat.",al={"how to open chest","chest key","iron shaft key"},gp=true},{q="Who is looking for the Iron Shaft?",a="Shael'dryn, a dryad at a moonwell in central Ashenvale, directs travelers to gather Dartol's Rod's pieces to help cleanse the forest.",al={"who wants iron shaft","iron shaft quest giver"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is the Iron Shaft?",a="The Iron Shaft is a key segment of Dartol's Rod, a relic created by Dartol. The rod's pieces were scattered across Ashenvale, and this one ended up locked away inside a hidden chest near the borders of Felwood, its key carried by the corrupted treants nearby.",al={"what is iron shaft","iron shaft item","dartol rod iron shaft"},it="identity",add="ad78a81b"},{q="Where does the Iron Shaft come from, and who made it?",a="It was forged as part of a magical rod created by Dartol. The rod's pieces were later scattered, and this particular shaft was secured in a worn chest hidden in a glade near Felwood, guarded indirectly by the corrupted treants that hold its key.",al={"who made the iron shaft","origin iron shaft","dartol iron shaft"},it="origin",add="45340e91"},{q="Why is the Iron Shaft wanted?",a="Raene Wolfrunner and Shael'dryn seek to reassemble Dartol's Rod, which Teronis believed could slow the furbolg attacks on the night elves of Ashenvale. Rebuilding the relic requires gathering its missing components, and this sturdy iron shaft forms the central handle and core necessary to hold the rod's magical gem and pommel together.",al={"why do they want the iron shaft","why collect iron shaft","iron shaft quest motive"},it="why_wanted",add="3705c59d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, recovering the Iron Shaft means putting down forest treants you hold dear, corrupted by the demonic blight seeping from Felwood.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, reassembling Dartol's Rod calls on your duty to tend the land and use forgotten tools to heal it."},kw={"ashenvale","crazed ancient","dartol's rod","felwood","iron shaft","raene's cleansing","shael'dryn","withered ancient","wooden key"},rel={"quest:991","item:wooden-key","npc:shael-dryn","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","subzone:raynewood-retreat","zone:ashenvale","zone:felwood"},src={"Iron Shaft","Raene's Cleansing (4)"}}
E["item:laughing-sister-s-hair"] = {t="item",n="Laughing Sister's Hair",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, laughing sisters' hair draws weavers seeking its natural magic. Kil'hala at the Crossroads uses the gathered locks to make enchanted robes.",h="In Ashenvale, laughing sisters' hair draws weavers seeking its natural magic.",sec={{t="A Rare Weaving Component",b="Near Raynewood Retreat in Ashenvale, laughing sisters are dryads whose hair holds natural magic. Dryads protect the woods and are linked to Cenarius and the night elves. Horde craftsmen prize their hair as a potent crafting material. Kil'hala, a troll tailor at the Crossroads, spins the locks into enchanted robes for Deino's promising pupils of the arcane.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Laughing Sister's Hair come from?",a="The hair comes from laughing sisters, dryads that wander the enchanted groves near Raynewood Retreat in central Ashenvale.",al={"where to get laughing sisters hair","laughing sister hair location","dryad hair source"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Kil'hala looking for dryad hair?",a="Kil'hala, a tailor at the Crossroads in the Barrens, uses the magical strands to weave enchanted cloth robes for Deino's promising pupils.",al={"why kilhala wants hair","use for laughing sister hair","troll tailor dryad hair"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Will the laughing sisters give up their hair willingly?",a="No. Laughing sisters guard nature and protect Ashenvale. As Kil'hala notes, dryads would never willingly surrender their hair to agents of the Horde.",al={"can you ask dryads for hair","do dryads donate hair"}},{q="What is Laughing Sister's Hair?",a="Laughing Sister's Hair consists of shorn locks gathered from laughing sisters, the woodland dryads dwelling near Raynewood Retreat in Ashenvale. Imbued with the natural grace and magic of Cenarius's daughters, these strands are prized by skilled clothiers as rare weaving material for potent spellcasting garments.",al={"what is laughing sisters hair","laughing sister hair info","dryad hair material"},it="identity",add="3a458879"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="For a tailor, dryad locks offer an exotic thread for binding nature magic into cloth.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you must enter night elf territory in Ashenvale and slay woodland spirits to take their locks, harvesting local magic by force."},kw={"ashenvale","cloth","crossroads","deino","dryad","hair","kil'hala","laughing sister","raynewood retreat"},rel={"quest:1945","npc:kil-hala","npc:deino","subzone:raynewood-retreat","zone:ashenvale","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","topic:horde"},src={"Laughing Sister's Hair","Laughing Sisters"}}
E["item:logging-rope"] = {t="item",n="Logging Rope",z="ashenvale",s="At the Warsong Lumber Camp, Logging Rope keeps the mills and machinery supplied. Furbolg tribes have stolen shipments across Ashenvale, leaving the Warsong to recover the line they need.",h="At the Warsong Lumber Camp, Logging Rope keeps the mills and machinery supplied.",sec={{t="Stolen Lines",b="Logging Rope shipments meant for the Warsong Lumber Camp have been stolen. The Foulweald and Thistlefur furbolgs intercepted the line before it reached the loggers. The tribes keep the ropes in their encampments across northern and central Ashenvale. Corruption has driven the furbolgs mad, and they fiercely defend their ancestral woods.",sp=0},{t="Supplying the War Effort",b="Locke Okarr at Splintertree Post seeks to recover the stolen supplies before work at the Warsong Lumber Camp stops. The heavy rope lets the Horde secure timber, bind logs, and rig saw machinery. Furbolg resistance continues across the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Logging Rope used for?",a="The Warsong Lumber Camp uses Logging Rope to secure harvested timber, haul logs, and rig heavy machinery in Ashenvale.",al={"logging rope use","why warsong needs rope","warsong logging rope"},it="purpose"},{q="Who stole the logging rope?",a="The Foulweald and Thistlefur furbolgs stole the logging rope and keep it in their village dens and encampments across Ashenvale.",al={"who took the rope","rope thief","which furbolgs have rope"},it="threat"},{q="Who wants this rope back?",a="Locke Okarr at Splintertree Post wants the rope returned with the other stolen supplies so work at the Warsong Lumber Camp can continue.",al={"who needs logging rope","logging rope quest giver"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do the furbolgs steal logging supplies?",a="The furbolgs steal logging supplies to disrupt the Horde's lumber mills and resist its logging in their ancestral woods.",al={"furbolg motive","why furbolgs attack shipments"},it="motive"},{q="What is Logging Rope?",a="Logging Rope is heavy-duty cordage vital to the Warsong clan's extensive timber operations across Ashenvale. Used for securing, hauling, and binding massive felled trees, it is an indispensable staple of the lumber camp's daily harvest.",al={"what is logging rope","logging rope info","warsong logging rope"},it="identity",add="26f07746"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Recovering Logging Rope helps keep the Warsong clan supplied with timber despite the furbolg ambushes.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you depend on Ashenvale lumber for settlement in Kalimdor. Stolen logging supplies threaten that work."},kw={"ashenvale","foulweald","locke okarr","logging rope","splintertree post","thistlefur","warsong lumber camp","warsong supplies"},rel={"quest:6571","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","topic:furbolg","item:warsong-oil","item:warsong-axe-shipment","quest:6581","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Logging Rope","Warsong Supplies (quest)"}}
E["item:orendil-s-cure"] = {t="item",n="Orendil's Cure",z="ashenvale",s="In northern Ashenvale, Orendil Broadleaf brews a draught for a child in Astranaar. He uses rare Bathran's Hair to treat Relara Whitemoon's mysterious, deathly sickness.",h="In northern Ashenvale, Orendil Broadleaf brews a draught for a child in Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Father's Hope",b="Relara Whitemoon, still young, fell deathly ill in Astranaar, and ordinary remedies failed. Her father, Pelturas Whitemoon, sought help from Orendil Broadleaf, a hermit and master of natural medicine who lives in northern Ashenvale. Orendil used bundles of rare Bathran's Hair gathered from the haunted ruins of Bathran's Haunt to brew a draught for Relara. When the vial arrives, it gives Pelturas hope. Yet the cure only slows the disease, so he must seek the further remedies Orendil suggested.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Orendil's Cure used for?",a="Orendil's Cure is meant to soothe and treat Relara Whitemoon, a young night elf child in Astranaar. Her sudden, severe illness has left her stricken.",al={"orendil cure purpose","what does the cure do","who is the cure for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who crafted the cure?",a="Orendil Broadleaf prepared the cure. He is a reclusive night elf herbalist in Ashenvale's northern woods, renowned for his mastery of forest plants and remedies.",al={"who made orendils cure","creator of orendils cure"},it="origin"},{q="What ingredients were used to make it?",a="The cure uses Bathran's Hair, a delicate, uncommon plant gathered among the ruins of Bathran's Haunt in northern Ashenvale.",al={"cure ingredients","what is in orendil's cure"},it="item"},{q="Does this potion completely heal the child?",a="No. Pelturas learns that Orendil's Cure only slows the disease afflicting his daughter, so he seeks the stronger remedy Orendil suggested: Elune's Tear.",al={"did it cure relara","is relara healed"},sp=1},{q="What is Orendil's Cure?",a="Orendil's Cure is a medicinal concoction brewed by the herbalist Orendil Broadleaf in northern Ashenvale. Designed as a specialized treatment for a sudden, severe ailment, it represents an urgent effort to save the life of a young night elf child suffering from a mysterious affliction.",al={"orendils cure lore","what is orendil cure","orendils remedy"},it="identity",add="8e86537e"},{q="Why is Orendil's Cure needed?",a="In Astranaar, Pelturas Whitemoon's young daughter, Relara, lies deathly ill. Desperate for a remedy when standard treatments proved ineffective, her father sought the expertise of Orendil Broadleaf. The herbalist prepared this specific mixture in hopes of stabilizing the child before the illness claims her life.",al={"why need orendils cure","who needs orendils cure","why deliver orendils cure"},it="why_wanted",add="6add91d1"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Ashenvale's native plants hold great medicinal power. Bathran's Hair is one such herb, growing only in select, shadowed corners of the forest.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves in Astranaar, saving Relara is an urgent matter for the community. Hermits like Orendil bring woodland knowledge, while faith in Elune brings divine aid."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","bathran's hair","orendil broadleaf","orendil's cure","pelturas whitemoon","relara"},rel={"quest:1020","quest:1010","npc:pelturas-whitemoon","subzone:astranaar","quest:1033","quest:1034","zone:ashenvale","topic:elune"},src={"Orendil's Cure","Orendil's Cure (Classic)"}}
E["item:pridewing-venom-sac"] = {t="item",n="Pridewing Venom Sac",z="ashenvale",s="Around Mirkfallon Lake, Pridewing Venom Sacs are sought by the night elves of Astranaar. Reports suggest Horde agents harvest the poison for covert attacks, and the Sentinels mean to deny them that supply.",h="Around Mirkfallon Lake, Pridewing Venom Sacs are sought by the night elves of Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Threat in the Crags",b="Pridewings hunt from the crags south of Ashenvale, especially around Mirkfallon Lake. These airborne predators are native to the Stonetalon Mountains, and their venom can be gathered from the glands in their bodies. Reports from Theramore suggest Horde assassins are taking that poison to coat blades for covert attacks on night elf settlements. In Astranaar, Sentinels send scouts to hunt the wyverns and collect their venom glands before Horde agents can claim them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures yield a Pridewing Venom Sac?",a="Young pridewings, skyhunters, patriarchs, and consorts around Mirkfallon Lake yield the venom sacs.",al={"where to get pridewing venom sac","who drops pridewing venom sac","pridewing venom sources"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Astranaar want Pridewing Venom Sacs?",a="Shindrell Swiftfire received reports that Horde agents use pridewing poison on weapons for silent attacks against the Alliance. Confiscating or destroying the glands can prevent those strikes.",al={"why collect venom sacs","shindrell swiftfire venom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who accepts these venom sacs in Ashenvale?",a="Shindrell Swiftfire collects the venom sacs in Astranaar, the night elf town in Ashenvale, to protect her people from covert attacks.",al={"who takes pridewing venom","pridewing quest turn in"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Are the pridewings naturally allied with the Horde?",a="No. The pridewings around Mirkfallon Lake are wild beasts, not willing allies of the Horde. Orc agents exploit their venom for warfare.",al={"are pridewings horde","do pridewings work for orcs"},it="ties"},{q="What is a Pridewing Venom Sac?",a="A Pridewing Venom Sac is an organ harvested from the pridewing wyverns nesting in the Stonetalon Mountains. It contains the potent natural toxins these winged predators produce to subdue their prey. In the fragile standoff between the night elves and the Horde, such venom has become a prized weapon for covert attacks, prompting the defenders of Astranaar to take notice.",al={"what is pridewing venom sac","pridewing venom sac item","what are pridewing venom sacs"},it="identity",add="e2bba8d5"},{q="Where does a Pridewing Venom Sac come from?",a="These sacs are harvested directly from the bodies of pridewings—fierce, wild wyverns that roost near Mirkfallon Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains. Because they are natural bodily organs produced by the beasts themselves rather than manufactured goods, obtaining them requires hunting the wyverns through the crags and securing the venom before Horde agents can harvest it.",al={"pridewing venom sac source","where do pridewing venom sacs come from","who drops pridewing venom sac"},it="origin",add="816b56c2"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Denying Horde agents pridewing venom helps protect frontier patrols from unseen assassins along the contested borders of Stonetalon and Ashenvale.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may regret that innocent wild beasts must be hunted, but protecting elven lives from poisoned blades comes first."},kw={"astranaar","mirkfallon lake","pridewing","shindrell swiftfire","stonetalon","venom sac","wyvern"},rel={"quest:1134","npc:shindrell-swiftfire","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","subzone:astranaar","zone:stonetalon","zone:ashenvale","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Pridewing Venom Sac","Pridewings of Stonetalon"}}
E["item:ran-bloodtooth-s-skull"] = {t="item",n="Ran Bloodtooth's Skull",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Ran Bloodtooth's Skull bears proof that a corrupted furbolg chieftain has fallen. The night elves of Astranaar receive it as a sign that a fierce threat to their woodland realm has ended.",h="In Ashenvale, Ran Bloodtooth's Skull bears proof that a corrupted furbolg chieftain has fallen.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Ashenvale's Defense",b="The furbolgs of Ashenvale have fallen into murderous madness under demonic taint and wilderness corruption. Ran Bloodtooth led one of the fiercest tribes. His skull gives the night elf Sentinels proof that he has fallen and his hold over the local furbolgs is broken, bringing some respite to Astranaar.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Fallen",b="Sentinel Raene Wolfrunner receives Ran Bloodtooth's Skull in Astranaar, where it marks the end of an investigation begun by the fallen scout Teronis. Dartol's Rod, rebuilt after Teronis set out to find it, is displayed beside the skull. Together they honor those who fought to preserve the sacred forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Ran Bloodtooth?",a="Ran Bloodtooth led a corrupted furbolg tribe in Ashenvale, and the night elf Sentinels counted him among the fiercest threats in the region.",al={"who is ran bloodtooth","ran bloodtooth lore","who was bloodtooth"}},{q="Why do the Sentinels want his skull?",a="Raene Wolfrunner receives the skull in Astranaar as proof that Ran Bloodtooth has fallen. It is placed beside Dartol's Rod to remember those lost defending Ashenvale.",al={"why do i need the skull","raene wolfrunner skull","what is the skull for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was Teronis?",a="Teronis was Raene Wolfrunner's longtime friend and an ally of the Sentinels in Ashenvale. He sought a gem for a rod made by the dead wizard Dartol, hoping it would slow the furbolg attacks, but murlocs slew him at Lake Falathim. Raene Wolfrunner and visiting adventurers took up his task.",al={"teronis lore","who is teronis","teronis astranaar"}},{q="What is Ran Bloodtooth's Skull?",a="This is the severed skull of Ran Bloodtooth, one of the fiercest and most dangerous corrupted furbolg threats prowling Ashenvale. Taken as proof of his defeat, it marks an end to the terror he brought against the Sentinels and the forest.",al={"ran bloodtooth skull","what is ran skull","ran bloodtooth head"},it="identity",add="4d0a3ce4"},{q="Where did Ran Bloodtooth's Skull come from?",a="The skull is claimed directly from Ran Bloodtooth after slaying him in Ashenvale. It is not an artifact forged or crafted by mortal hands, but rather the grim trophy harvested from the chieftain himself.",al={"where did ran skull come from","who made ran bloodtooth skull","ran bloodtooth skull source"},it="origin",add="f5c7858d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the skull marks a somber victory and honors Teronis's unfinished task. It also recalls how deeply demonic corruption has ravaged their former furbolg allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="Delivering the grim trophy shows the mettle of Alliance champions defending Ashenvale's fragile borders beside the Sentinels."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","bloodtooth skull","bloodtooth","furbolg","raene wolfrunner","raene's cleansing","ran bloodtooth"},rel={"npc:raene-wolfrunner","quest:991","zone:ashenvale","subzone:astranaar","topic:furbolg","topic:sentinels","topic:alliance"},src={"Ran Bloodtooth's Skull","Raene's Cleansing (11)"}}
E["item:ring-of-zoram"] = {t="item",n="Ring of Zoram",z="ashenvale",s="At Zoram, the ring of the city's rulers has surfaced again after millennia beneath the sea. The naga now hold it, and Talen seeks the key to an ancient statuette.",h="At Zoram, the ring of the city's rulers has surfaced again after millennia beneath the sea.",sec={{t="Ring of the Sunken City",b="Before the Well of Eternity collapsed, Zoram stood on Kalimdor's western coast as a jewel of the night elven empire. Its rulers wore the Ring of Zoram, whose inner band bears a strange code in the night elven language. The Great Sundering shattered the continent ten thousand years ago, and the ring sank with the city beneath the tides. It lies beneath the waters of what is now the Zoram Strand.",sp=0},{t="Reclamation by the Naga",b="For millennia, silt and ruins hid the ring. Then naga began scouring Ashenvale's coast, and Ruuzel, a naga leader who dwells on an islet off the northern strand, uncovered it among the sunken debris. The night elf scholar Talen seeks the ring for more than its age. It is the only key that can unlock relics salvaged from the depths, including ancient statuettes sealed on the sea floor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Ring of Zoram used for?",a="Before the Sundering drowned Zoram, its rulers wore the ring, and it served as the key to an ancient lock. Talen now seeks it to open a locked statuette recovered from the submerged ruins.",al={"ring of zoram purpose","what does the ring do","ring of zoram lore"},it="power"},{q="Who possesses the Ring of Zoram?",a="Naga invading the Zoram Strand dredged the ring from the ruins. Their leader Ruuzel holds it on an island off the northern coast, though the prominent naga Lady Vespia has also been known to carry it.",al={"who has the ring","ring of zoram drop","where to get ring of zoram"},it="target"},{q="Why does Talen want the ring?",a="Talen wants to uncover the secrets of an ancient statuette recovered from the Zoram Strand. Without the Ring of Zoram as its key, the statuette's mechanism cannot be opened.",al={"why talen wants ring","talen ring quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where did the city of Zoram go?",a="Before the Great Sundering, Zoram was a night elven city on Kalimdor's western edge. When the Well of Eternity imploded ten thousand years ago, the city was destroyed and drowned beneath the waves, leaving only the Zoram Strand.",al={"what happened to zoram","city of zoram lore"},it="place"},{q="What is the Ring of Zoram?",a="The Ring of Zoram is an ancient relic once worn by the rulers of the sunken city of Zoram, before the waves of the Great Sundering drowned it. A strange code is written inside the band in the language of the night elves, and the ring is the key to the ancient lock of a statuette recovered from the ruins.",al={"what is ring of zoram","ring of zoram lore","ring of zoram item"},it="identity",add="7e40c0d5"},{q="Where does the Ring of Zoram come from, and who made it?",a="The ring originates from the pre-Sundering night elven city of Zoram, along the coast of ancient Kalimdor. It belonged to the city's rulers before cataclysmic tidal waves drowned Zoram ten thousand years ago, leaving the relic lost to the sea until the naga recently dredged it up from the ruins.",al={"ring of zoram origin","who made the ring of zoram","where did ring of zoram come from"},it="origin",add="770adfa7"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ring is a tangible piece of pre-Sundering heritage, from before arcane hubris and drowning seas tore apart the Kaldorei empire.",["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering the ring from the naga helps the night elf scholar Talen reclaim Kaldorei history along Ashenvale's contested borders."},kw={"ancient statuette","ashenvale","lady vespia","ring of zoram","ruuzel","talen","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:talen","quest:1009","item:ancient-statuette","subzone:zoram-strand","zone:ashenvale","topic:naga","quest:1007","quest:1008"},src={"Ring of Zoram","Ruuzel (Classic)"}}
E["item:sarilus-foulborne-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Sarilus Foulborne's Head",z="ashenvale",s="Across the border from the Barrens, Sarilus Foulborne's Head reaches Ashenvale as proof of the sorcerer's death. The undead mage defiled Ashenvale's waters, and the Sentinels demanded his head.",h="Across the border from the Barrens, Sarilus Foulborne's Head reaches Ashenvale as proof of the sorcerer's...",sec={{t="A Defiler Silenced",b="Sarilus Foulborne was a Forsaken spellcaster atop Dreadmist Peak in the northern Barrens. He drew the night elves' anger by corrupting and binding swarms of water elementals. From Silverwind Refuge, Sentinel Velene Starstrike recognized his work and sent champions across the frontier into Horde territory to end his experiments. Starstrike would accept only his severed head as proof that the mocking mage was dead, and that the troubled waters of Ashenvale might know some peace.",sp=1,bt={"q1016.2"}}},faq={{q="Who was Sarilus Foulborne?",a="Sarilus Foulborne was an undead mage who established himself atop Dreadmist Peak in the northern Barrens. He angered the night elves by twisting and summoning vast numbers of water elementals, so Sentinel Velene Starstrike ordered his death.",al={"who is sarilus","sarilus foulborne lore","who is foulborne"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"q1016.2"}},{q="Why does Sentinel Velene Starstrike want his head?",a="Velene Starstrike wanted certainty that the arrogant sorcerer was dead. Sarilus mocked her while defiling the region's water spirits, and his severed head was the only proof she would accept that the threat had ended.",al={"why take his head","velene starstrike head","proof of death"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Sarilus Foulborne located?",a="Sarilus Foulborne lairs atop Dreadmist Peak in the northern Barrens, just south of the Ashenvale border.",al={"where to find foulborne","sarilus location","dreadmist peak mage"},sp=1,it="place",gp=true,bt={"q1016.2"}},{q="Why was Foulborne defiling water elementals?",a="Sarilus Foulborne used arcane summonings to bend numerous water elementals to his will and corrupt them. His reckless manipulation disrupted the natural balance of waters flowing near Ashenvale, drawing swift retaliation from the Sentinels.",al={"why corrupt elementals","water elemental corruption","foulborne motives"},it="motive"},{q="Where did Sarilus Foulborne's Head come from?",a="This severed head is taken directly from Sarilus Foulborne, a Forsaken mage who established himself atop Dreadmist Peak in the northern Barrens. Operating near the borders of Ashenvale, Foulborne spent his days defiling water elementals and antagonizing the night elves until Sentinel Velene Starstrike sent an adventurer into enemy territory to put an end to his mockery.",al={"origin of sarilus head","sarilus head origin","where did foulborne head come from"},it="origin",add="a996e76e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Taking Foulborne's head answers the Sentinels' vengeance against an arcane defiler who desecrated the spirits of the land.",["faction:Alliance"]="This strike requires infiltrating deep into hostile Horde lands in the Barrens to eliminate a dangerous rogue caster."},kw={"barrens","dreadmist peak","head","mage summoner","sarilus foulborne","silverwind refuge","velene starstrike","water elementals"},rel={"quest:1017","npc:sentinel-velene-starstrike","subzone:dreadmist-peak","subzone:silverwind-refuge","quest:1016","zone:barrens","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels"},src={"Sarilus Foulborne's Head","Mage Summoner"}}
E["item:satyr-horns"] = {t="item",n="Satyr Horns",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Satyr Horns draw dryads seeking vengeance and traders bound for Ratchet. The horns come from satyrs whose corruption has taken root in the ancient forest.",h="In Ashenvale, Satyr Horns draw dryads seeking vengeance and traders bound for Ratchet.",sec={{t="Trophies of Vengeance and Commerce",b="Ashenvale’s satyrs bear horns that mark their demonic corruption. At the Shrine of Aessina, the dryad Illiyana gathers them in grief and vengeance for her lost sister Anilia. Pixel, a traveling goblin resting at Splintertree Post, seeks them for trade. Demand for satyr horns has risen in Ratchet, where hunters can sell these remnants of slain demons.",sp=0},{t="Culling the Corrupted Enclaves",b="Satyr Horns must be cut from the beasts themselves; ordinary suppliers do not sell them. Satyrs hold strongholds across Ashenvale, including the corrupted groves of Xavian, the hollows of Satyrnaar, and the ruins of Night Run. Clearing these enclaves drives back the lingering demonic taint and supplies grieving guardians and eager merchants with proof of the cull.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Illiyana want Satyr Horns?",a="Illiyana seeks Satyr Horns to avenge her sister Anilia, whom the satyrs of Ashenvale murdered. The horns show that the satyrs’ numbers are falling and bring peace to Anilia’s spirit.",al={"illiyana horns","anilia satyrs","forest song quest"},it="motive"},{q="Why is Pixel collecting Satyr Horns?",a="Pixel, an enterprising traveler staying at Splintertree Post, collects Satyr Horns for the journey to Ratchet. She has learned that they fetch a high price in the goblin port and hires hunters to face the danger before she departs.",al={"pixel splintertree","why does pixel want horns","ratchet satyr horns"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the best places to find satyrs with these horns?",a="Satyrs dwell in several corrupted areas of Ashenvale. Many are found in Xavian and Satyrnaar in the northeast, and in Night Run in the east-central forest.",al={"satyr locations ashenvale","where are satyrs","satyr camps"},gp=true},{q="What are satyrs, and why do they have horns?",a="Satyrs are ancient night elves transformed into demonic, beastly beings through pacts made during the War of the Ancients. Their hooves, tails, and horns mark the demonic corruption granted by the Burning Legion.",al={"what is a satyr","why do satyrs have horns"},it="origin"},{q="What are Satyr Horns?",a="Satyr Horns are the curved, fiendish horns severed from the heads of slain satyrs lurking in Ashenvale. As demonic corruptions of ancient night elves, satyrs bear these menacing growths as marks of their cursed affliction. In the hands of adventurers, they serve primarily as grim proof of a satyr's demise or as prized, exotic oddities traded across Kalimdor.",al={"what are satyr horns","satyr horns item","satyr horn identity"},it="identity",add="2131c67f"},{q="Why does anyone want Satyr Horns?",a="Different factions seek satyr horns for very different reasons. For the dryad Illiyana at Forest Song, they serve as undeniable trophies of retribution against the corrupt demons who murdered her sister Anilia. Meanwhile, opportunistic merchants such as Pixel collect them to sell in the bustling port of Ratchet, where demand thrives for exotic alchemical reagents, curiosities, and beast parts.",al={"who wants satyr horns","why collect satyr horns","why are satyr horns wanted"},it="why_wanted",add="8a39621c"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, taking satyr horns is a bitter duty. It cleanses their ancestral forest of cousins who traded their heritage for demonic service.",["faction:Horde"]="From Splintertree Post, Horde warriors clear satyrs threatening their timber operations and sell the horns to goblin buyers bound for Ratchet."},kw={"anilia","forest song","illiyana","night run","pixel","satyr horns","satyrnaar","splintertree post","xavian"},rel={"topic:satyr","zone:ashenvale","quest:1032","quest:6441","npc:illiyana","npc:pixel","subzone:forest-song","subzone:splintertree-post"},src={"Satyr Horns","Satyr Slaying! (Classic)","Satyr Horns (quest)"}}
E["item:shindrell-s-note"] = {t="item",n="Shindrell's Note",z="ashenvale",s="In Astranaar, Shindrell Swiftfire writes a missive about corruption near the town and along Ashenvale's coast. She sends the intelligence report east through the forest to Kayneth Stillwind.",h="In Astranaar, Shindrell Swiftfire writes a missive about corruption near the town and along Ashenvale's coast.",sec={{t="A Missive Across the Woods",b="Sentinels and druids coordinate to watch Ashenvale's borders as unrest spreads through the forest. In Astranaar, Sentinel Shindrell Swiftfire writes of troubling disturbances along the western coast and among the central canopies. She addresses her report to Kayneth Stillwind, a druid at the shrine of Forest Song in the Nightsong Woods to the east. Couriers carry Shindrell's firsthand observations to aid Kayneth's investigation of corruption creeping through the sacred groves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Shindrell's Note?",a="Sentinel Shindrell Swiftfire's field report describes disturbances and suspected corruption near Astranaar and along the Ashenvale coastline.",al={"what is this note","shindrell note","what does the note say"},it="identity"},{q="Who is meant to receive the note?",a="The note is addressed to Kayneth Stillwind, a night elf druid at Forest Song in the Nightsong Woods in eastern Ashenvale.",al={"who do I give this to","where does it go","who is the note for"},it="target"},{q="Why was the note written?",a="Kayneth Stillwind requested reports of unusual occurrences in the western forests because he feared corruption was taking root there. Shindrell gathered her sightings to help him judge the threat.",al={"why write the note","what corruption is shindrell talking about","purpose of report"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does Shindrell Swiftfire reside?",a="Shindrell Swiftfire is a night elf sentinel stationed at Astranaar, a settlement in central Ashenvale.",al={"where is shindrell","shindrell swiftfire location","who sent this"}},{q="Where does Shindrell's Note come from, and who made it?",a="The note was penned by Sentinel Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar. Written as a formal field report, it details the troubling events she observed along the Ashenvale coast and throughout the surrounding woodlands.",al={"who wrote shindrell's note","who made shindrells note","origin of shindrells note"},it="origin",add="ed6c40b2"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The missive shows Sentinels defending Ashenvale's settlements working with Cenarion druids who study the forest's sickness.",["class:Druid"]="Shindrell's observations help Kayneth Stillwind and his fellow druids uncover the roots of the unnatural blight troubling Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","forest song","kayneth stillwind","nightsong woods","shindrell swiftfire","shindrell's note"},rel={"quest:4581","zone:ashenvale","subzone:astranaar","subzone:forest-song","subzone:nightsong-woods","topic:druid","quest:456"},src={"Shindrell's Note","Kayneth Stillwind (quest)"}}
E["item:teronis-journal"] = {t="item",n="Teronis' Journal",z="ashenvale",s="Teronis' Journal follows a scout's search through Ashenvale for a gem tied to a rod he hoped could slow furbolg attacks.",h="Teronis' Journal follows a scout's search through Ashenvale for a gem tied to a rod he hoped could slow...",sec={{t="A Scout's Final Record",b="Teronis, a longtime friend of Raene Wolfrunner, aided the Sentinels and searched Ashenvale for a gem. He believed it belonged to a rod that could slow the furbolg attacks on his people. Near the shore, aggressive creatures brought his journey to an end. The journal was recovered from his personal effects in remarkably good condition. Its findings about a radiant gem that once formed part of the rod give Astranaar's defenders a trail to follow in his unfinished search.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who did this journal belong to?",a="Teronis, a night elf and longtime friend of Raene Wolfrunner, owned the journal. He searched Ashenvale for a gem tied to a rod he believed could slow furbolg attacks, but died in the wilds before returning with his findings.",al={"who wrote the journal","who is teronis","teronis lore"},it="origin"},{q="Where is the journal found?",a="The journal is found among Teronis' belongings after his slain body is discovered in the wilds of Ashenvale, near the shore where local murlocs live.",al={"where to find journal","teronis journal location","how to get journal"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of bringing the journal to Astranaar?",a="Returning the journal to Raene Wolfrunner tells Astranaar of Teronis' death and gives the Sentinels his notes to continue his search for the rod he hoped could slow the furbolg attacks.",al={"why bring journal to raene","who do i give the journal to","journal turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What item was Teronis looking for according to his mission?",a="Teronis sought a glowing gem, one piece of a rod made by the dead wizard Dartol. His investigation suggested nearby murlocs may have scavenged the artifact.",al={"what was teronis hunting","what gem was he after","teronis gem"},it="motive"},{q="What is Teronis' Journal?",a="Teronis' Journal is a personal notebook kept by the night elf scout Teronis. Found among his belongings beside his body in Ashenvale, it details his mission and initial scouting efforts regarding a strange gem he was dispatched to find before he met his untimely demise.",al={"what is teronis journal","teronis journal item","about teronis journal"},it="identity",add="5fb93f8f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, Teronis' journal recalls the danger faced by scouts protecting Ashenvale's ancient woodlands from encroaching corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="Taking Teronis' field notes back to Astranaar helps the garrison coordinate relief and recover their fallen scout's remains."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","glowing gem","raene wolfrunner","raene's cleansing","sentinels","teronis","teronis' journal"},rel={"npc:teronis-corpse","npc:raene-wolfrunner","quest:991","item:glowing-gem","subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels","topic:murloc"},src={"Teronis' Journal","Raene's Cleansing (2)"}}
E["item:troll-charm"] = {t="item",n="Troll Charm",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Troll Charms have been taken from fallen Darkspear travelers. The Thistlefur furbolgs seized the sacred amulets after ambushing the party on its way to Zoram'gar Outpost.",h="In Ashenvale, Troll Charms have been taken from fallen Darkspear travelers.",sec={{t="Sacred Trinkets of the Darkspear",b="Darkspear trolls carry spiritual charms as marks of dignity. Scout Mitsuwa says a troll without one is as diminished as an orc without battle scars. A party of Darkspear kin traveled through Ashenvale's canopy toward Zoram'gar Outpost when corrupted Thistlefur furbolgs ambushed and slaughtered them. Their spirits were commended to the afterlife, while the furbolgs took the charms as trophies and stashed them in chests deep within Thistlefur Hold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Troll Charms used for?",a="Darkspear trolls carry Troll Charms as sacred spiritual wards and marks of personal dignity.",al={"purpose of troll charm","troll charm lore","why do trolls carry charms"},it="purpose"},{q="Where are these charms found?",a="The charms are locked in chests within Thistlefur Hold, a cavern system behind Thistlefur Village in northern Ashenvale.",al={"where are troll charms","how to find troll charm","troll chest location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the furbolgs have these charms?",a="Thistlefur furbolgs ambushed and killed Darkspear travelers bound for Zoram'gar Outpost, then ransacked their belongings and kept the charms.",al={"why furbolgs have them","who stole the charms"},it="history"},{q="Who wants the charms back?",a="Mitsuwa, a Darkspear troll stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand, seeks the charms to restore honor to his slain kin.",al={"who takes the charms","mitsuwa quest"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Troll Charm?",a="A Troll Charm is a sacred tribal talisman carried by Darkspear trolls. These charms carry profound personal and spiritual significance among trollkind, regarded as essential tokens of identity and standing—so much so that a troll without their charm is considered by their peers to be akin to an orc without battle scars.",al={"what is troll charm","troll charm item","sacred troll charm"},it="identity",add="5fe70fe7"},{q="Where do Troll Charms come from, and who made them?",a="These charms were crafted and borne by Darkspear trolls journeying through Ashenvale toward Zoram'gar Outpost. Tragically, the travelers were ambushed and killed along the road by hostile Thistlefur furbolgs, who looted the sacred objects and locked them away inside chests deep within Thistlefur Hold.",al={"origin of troll charms","who made troll charms","where do troll charms come from"},it="origin",add="6d34290e"},{q="Why does Mitsuwa want the Troll Charms returned?",a="Mitsuwa at Zoram'gar Outpost mourns the fallen travelers but accepts that they will reunite in the afterlife. However, allowing crude and hostile furbolgs to keep such sacred relics is seen as an intolerable insult to troll heritage. Recovering them restores honor to the memories of the slain.",al={"why get troll charms","why does mitsuwa want charms","why are troll charms wanted"},it="why_wanted",add="77137dd7"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, leaving sacred charms with savage furbolgs is an intolerable insult to your fallen kin.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, recovering the stolen charms weakens the aggressive Thistlefur tribe and avenges Horde travelers slain on Ashenvale's treacherous paths."},kw={"ashenvale","darkspear","mitsuwa","thistlefur hold","thistlefur village","troll charm","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:mitsuwa","quest:6462","subzone:thistlefur-hold","subzone:thistlefur-village","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","topic:furbolg","topic:troll","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Troll Charm","Troll Charm (quest)"}}
E["item:warsong-axe-shipment"] = {t="item",n="Warsong Axe Shipment",z="ashenvale",s="At Booty Bay, the Warsong Axe Shipment waits for its voyage to Ashenvale. The newly forged axes are bound for the Warsong Outriders and the work at their lumber camp.",h="At Booty Bay, the Warsong Axe Shipment waits for its voyage to Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Long Voyage Across the Seas",b="Axes for the Warsong Lumber Camp wait in Booty Bay. The camp’s woodcutters need a steady supply of durable tools, and not every tool can be forged on the front lines. Orders cross the Great Sea to this neutral goblin port, where the crate is stored near Wharfmaster Lozgil. The sharpened axes are meant for Splintertree Post, where they can be sent onward to the camp. Keeping distant frontier camps supplied takes a long journey across the sea.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Warsong Axe Shipment located?",a="The crate sits on the docks of Booty Bay, at the southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"axe shipment location","where is axe shipment","booty bay axe crate"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is a shipment for Ashenvale all the way down in Booty Bay?",a="The Blackwater Raiders and the Steamwheedle Cartel carry merchant cargo across the Great Sea. Booty Bay connects distant lands, so the Horde’s tools pass through its port.",al={"why booty bay","why is it in stranglethorn","warsong axes in booty bay"},it="why_here"},{q="Who needs these axes?",a="Locke Okarr, an outrider at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale, needs the axes to replenish the Warsong Lumber Camp’s dwindling stocks.",al={"who needs the axes","who is the shipment for","locke okarr axes"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who oversees the delivery in Booty Bay?",a="Wharfmaster Lozgil oversees maritime cargo at Booty Bay, where the shipment waits for transport to Kalimdor.",al={"who has the shipment","wharfmaster lozgil","booty bay wharfmaster"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Warsong Axe Shipment?",a="It is a crated delivery of heavy logging axes bound for the Warsong Clan's timber operations in Ashenvale. Orcish loggers constantly wear through their tools harvesting the ancient forests of Kalimdor, making regular shipments of freshly forged lumber blades vital for keeping their lumber mills and cutting crews fully supplied.",al={"what is warsong axe shipment","warsong axe shipment identity","crate of axes ashenvale"},it="identity",add="445f7bbf"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, this crate helps keep the Warsong Lumber Camp supplied and productive under constant pressure from hostile forces in Ashenvale.",["race:Orc"]="For the Warsong clan, sharp axes mean more timber for the growing foundations of Orgrimmar and Durotar."},kw={"ashenvale","axes","booty bay","locke okarr","splintertree post","warsong axe shipment","warsong supplies","wharfmaster lozgil"},rel={"quest:6571","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","zone:ashenvale","zone:stranglethorn","item:logging-rope","item:warsong-oil"},src={"Warsong Axe Shipment","Warsong Supplies (quest)"}}
E["item:warsong-oil"] = {t="item",n="Warsong Oil",z="ashenvale",s="At the Warsong Lumber Camp, Warsong Oil keeps the logging machinery running. A satyr ambush has carried a shipment into corrupted forest enclaves.",h="At the Warsong Lumber Camp, Warsong Oil keeps the logging machinery running.",sec={{t="Stolen Machinery Fuel",b="Warsong Oil keeps the Warsong Clan's logging machinery running in Ashenvale. Goblin-engineered shredders and massive sawmills need a steady supply of the lubricant. Without it, timber cutting could halt, slowing the lumber needed to build Orgrimmar and fortify Horde settlements across Durotar and the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Rituals of the Satyr",b="Satyrs ambushed a shipment of Warsong Oil before it could reach Splintertree Post and the logging camps. They carried the containers into corrupted enclaves, including Night Run, Satyrnaar, and Xavian, where they use the flammable lubricant in their rituals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Warsong Oil used for?",a="Warsong Oil keeps the Warsong Lumber Camp's heavy shredders, saws, and timber-cutting machinery running.",al={"purpose of warsong oil","why need oil","what is it for"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do the satyrs have the oil?",a="Satyrs ambushed a supply convoy bound for Splintertree Post on the roads of Ashenvale. They took the oil for their rituals in ruined settlements.",al={"who stole the oil","why do satyrs have it","where did the oil go"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Warsong Oil be found?",a="Satyr-controlled sites in Ashenvale hold containers of Warsong Oil, especially Night Run, Satyrnaar, and Xavian.",al={"warsong oil location","where to find warsong oil","oil locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who needs the oil recovered?",a="Locke Okarr at Splintertree Post needs Warsong Oil, saw blades, rope, and axes to resupply the struggling Warsong lumber operation.",al={"who wants the oil","warsong oil quest giver"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Warsong Oil?",a="Warsong Oil is a crucial industrial lubricant and fuel provisioned for the Horde's logging machinery in Ashenvale. Used to keep heavy machinery and saw blades running smoothly at the Warsong lumber camp, it is an indispensable resource in maintaining the clan's timber operations against harsh wilderness wear.",al={"warsong oil what is it","what is the oil","warsong oil info"},it="identity",add="7f00f21d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Ashenvale timber supports its footholds in Durotar and the Barrens. When demon-worshiping satyrs take the machinery oil, construction in those young settlements suffers.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers know goblin-designed shredder joints and buzzsaws need steady lubrication. Without it, they burn out within hours of timber logging."},kw={"ashenvale","locke okarr","night run","satyrnaar","splintertree post","warsong oil","warsong supplies","xavian"},rel={"quest:6571","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","subzone:satyrnaar","subzone:night-run","subzone:xavian","item:logging-rope","item:warsong-axe-shipment"},src={"Warsong Oil","Warsong Supplies (quest)"}}
E["item:warsong-saw-blades"] = {t="item",n="Warsong Saw Blades",z="ashenvale",s="Warsong Saw Blades keep the Horde's lumber machinery cutting in Ashenvale. The Warsong Clan relies on goblin-made machines for its logging, and these blades supply its clear-cutting work.",h="Warsong Saw Blades keep the Horde's lumber machinery cutting in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Industrial Forestry",b="In Ashenvale, the Warsong Clan's logging depends on heavy machinery supplied and maintained by goblin engineers. Axes alone cannot meet the Horde's demand for Kalimdor lumber, so steam engines and circular saws cut through raw timber. Ashenvale's ancient hardwood quickly dulls and breaks ordinary blades. Replacement saw blades must keep arriving for the mills at the Warsong Lumber Camp to keep running.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Shipment",b="Getting mechanical parts through disputed territory brings constant trouble. Hostile furbolgs and satyrs often intercept other logging supplies, while goblin contacts such as Pixel at Splintertree Post handle the saw blade shipments. Lumber master Locke Okarr gathers the blades with rope, oil, and axes to keep the camp operating despite sabotage from Ashenvale's defenders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Warsong Saw Blades used for?",a="The blades replace parts in the circular saws and heavy lumber machinery at the Warsong Lumber Camp in southeastern Ashenvale.",al={"purpose of saw blades","saw blades use","what are they for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides these saw blades to the Horde?",a="Goblin merchants and logisticians handle the blades. Pixel, a goblin at Splintertree Post, oversees their arrival for the Warsong outriders.",al={"who made saw blades","where do blades come from","saw blade supplier"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Horde need so many saw blades?",a="Ashenvale's dense, ancient trees quickly wear down cutting edges. The Horde needs great quantities of timber to build settlements across the arid plains of Durotar and the Barrens, and constant logging wears out machinery faster than local smiths can reforge it.",al={"why so many blades","warsong logging demand","why need saws"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is collecting the logging supplies?",a="Locke Okarr, an orc who oversees supply runs from Splintertree Post, organizes the collection of saw blades, oil, ropes, and axes for delivery to the lumber camp.",al={"who wants the saw blades","who takes saw blades","locke okarr quest"},it="people"},{q="What are the Warsong Saw Blades?",a="These heavy-duty metal blades are essential mechanical components built for the industrial lumber machinery of the Warsong Outriders. The orcs rely heavily on mechanized logging to harvest the ancient, dense timber of Ashenvale, but the thick trees wear down cutting teeth quickly. Without a steady supply of sharp, durable saw blades, the Warsong lumber operations grind to a halt.",al={"what are warsong saw blades","warsong saw blades item","what are the saw blades"},it="identity",add="12f75673"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's expansion into central Kalimdor depends on Ashenvale timber, so keeping Warsong milling equipment in repair is a strategic priority.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see each crate of goblin-forged saw blades as another assault on Ashenvale's ancient canopy and its sacred woodland spirits."},kw={"ashenvale logging","locke okarr","pixel","splintertree post","warsong lumber camp","warsong saw blades"},rel={"quest:6571","quest:6581","npc:pixel","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","item:logging-rope","item:warsong-axe-shipment","item:warsong-oil"},src={"Warsong Saw Blades","Warsong Supplies (quest)"}}
E["item:wooden-key"] = {t="item",n="Wooden Key",z="ashenvale",s="In northern Ashenvale, the Wooden Key rests in the hands of maddened ancients near Felwood’s border. It opens a concealed chest with a remnant of Dartol's Rod.",h="In northern Ashenvale, the Wooden Key rests in the hands of maddened ancients near Felwood’s border.",sec={{t="A Key in Mad Hands",b="Crazed and Withered Ancients carry the Wooden Key along the shaded trails north of Raynewood Retreat. Shael'dryn once knew the local treants, but now says corruption has twisted their nature. One carries the key to a chest holding a piece of Dartol's Rod.",sp=0},{t="Unlocking the Rod",b="Shael'dryn sends adventurers to retrieve the key and open a hidden, worn chest in a small glade west of the Felwood road. The Iron Shaft lies inside, one of the components needed to rebuild Dartol's Rod and fight the corruption poisoning the sacred forests.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does the Wooden Key unlock?",a="The Wooden Key opens a worn chest in a small glade west of the main road heading north into Felwood. Inside lies the Iron Shaft, a piece needed to rebuild Dartol's Rod.",al={"what does wooden key open","wooden key chest","where to use wooden key"},it="purpose"},{q="Who carries the Wooden Key?",a="Crazed Ancients and Withered Ancients carry the key through the woods north of Raynewood Retreat, near the Felwood border.",al={"who drops wooden key","where to find wooden key","wooden key drop"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why do the ancients have this key?",a="Shael'dryn says one of the corrupted treants near Felwood carries the key. She does not explain how it came into the treant's possession.",al={"why do treants have the key","ancient key lore"},it="motive"},{q="Who sends you to retrieve the Wooden Key?",a="Shael'dryn, a dryad tending the Moonwell of Purity in Ashenvale, directs adventurers to recover the key as part of the effort to rebuild Dartol's Rod.",al={"wooden key questgiver","who wants the wooden key"},it="why_me",gp=true},{q="What is the Wooden Key?",a="The Wooden Key is a simple carved key carried by the corrupted treants wandering northern Ashenvale near Felwood. It was designed to lock away a hidden chest containing a relic of the late night elf Dartol.",al={"wooden key info","what is wooden key","about wooden key"},it="identity",add="ebbbe3a2"},{q="Why does Shael'dryn want the Wooden Key?",a="Shael'dryn requires the key so you can unlock the worn chest hidden in a glade near the Felwood border. Inside lies an iron shaft, a crucial fragment needed to reassemble Dartol's Rod and cleanse the land.",al={"why need wooden key","why retrieve wooden key","why is wooden key wanted"},it="why_wanted",add="a6fc69e1"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For any child of the stars, seeing Kalimdor's beloved ancients driven mad and clutching lost relics along the Felwood road is sorrowful.",["class:Druid"]="The twisted ancients holding this key reflect how far the demonic blight has reached into the Cenarion groves between Ashenvale and Felwood."},kw={"ashenvale","crazed ancient","dartol's rod","felwood","iron shaft","shael'dryn","withered ancient","wooden key"},rel={"npc:shael-dryn","item:iron-shaft","quest:991","zone:ashenvale","zone:felwood","subzone:raynewood-retreat","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale"},src={"Wooden Key","Raene's Cleansing (4)"}}
E["item:xavian-water-sample"] = {t="item",n="Xavian Water Sample",z="ashenvale",s="At Xavian, ancient waters hold arcane power sought by Horde mages in Orgrimmar. They seek it to unravel the latent magic preserved in Ashenvale's oldest sacred sites.",h="At Xavian, ancient waters hold arcane power sought by Horde mages in Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Waters of the Ancient City",b="Xavian was a fabled ancient elven city, and its old knowledge remains known among the learned. Even in ruin, its waters are said to hold great magical power. Deino, an arcane instructor in Orgrimmar, sends rising mages deep into Ashenvale to draw fresh water from the pool beneath Xavian's tallest waterfall. They must cross dangerous ground, for corrupt satyrs now guard the ruins fiercely and oppose spellcasters who meddle there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the water sample collected?",a="Fill Deino's Flask at the pool beneath the tallest waterfall in Xavian's ruins. The site lies in northeastern Ashenvale, north past the lakes beyond Splintertree Post and Satyrnaar.",al={"where do I get xavian water","xavian waterfall location","how to get xavian water sample"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Deino want this water?",a="Deino, an arcane instructor in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, wants the water for her studies of potent and unusual magic. She teaches young Horde practitioners and seeks the ancient magical essence held in Xavian's undisturbed waters.",al={"who wants xavian water","why collect water from xavian","deino purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What threats guard the waters of Xavian?",a="Satyrs inhabit the ancient elven ruins and fiercely defend their ground from curious mages. Aggressive beasts, including river crocolisks, also live in the surrounding waterways.",al={"what enemies are at xavian","who lives in xavian","xavian dangers"},it="danger"},{q="What happens once the sample is returned to Orgrimmar?",a="When the sample returns to Orgrimmar, Deino begins studying its arcane properties at once. She uses the gathered magic to advance her research and help train and instruct Horde mages.",al={"turning in xavian water","what is the water used for"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Xavian Water Sample?",a="It is a flask filled with water gathered directly from the base of the highest waterfall in the ruined city of Xavian. The waters of this ancient night elven settlement are said to possess vast magical powers, drawing the intense curiosity of Horde scholars.",al={"what is xavian water sample","xavian water sample","flask of xavian water"},it="identity",add="ff7d6737"},{q="Where does the Xavian Water Sample come from, and who made it?",a="The water is drawn from the natural cascade at the heart of Xavian, an ancient elven city nestled deep in eastern Ashenvale. No mortal artisan created it; rather, the pristine waters flow through ruins steeped in ancient night elven magic and the lingering corruption of the satyrs who now claim the grounds.",al={"where does xavian water come from","who made xavian water sample","source of xavian water"},it="origin",add="27a4db96"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Horde mage, retrieving the sample tests your skill with natural arcane power and your ability to cross hostile, demon-tainted ground.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see how gathering Xavian's ancient arcane resources aids Orgrimmar's scholars as the Horde strengthens its presence around Splintertree Post in Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","deino","orgrimmar","satyr","splintertree","water sample","xavian"},rel={"quest:1944","npc:deino","subzone:xavian","zone:ashenvale","zone:orgrimmar","topic:satyr","subzone:splintertree-post","topic:mage"},src={"Xavian Water Sample","Waters of Xavian"}}
E["npc:delgren-the-purifier"] = {t="npc",n="Delgren the Purifier",z="ashenvale",s="At Maestra's Post, Delgren the Purifier aids the night elves against demonic and shadow magic on Ashenvale's northern edge. He works with Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand to guard the frontier.",h="At Maestra's Post, Delgren the Purifier aids the night elves against demonic and shadow magic on Ashenvale's...",sec={{t="A Crusader on the Kaldorei Frontier",b="Delgren the Purifier keeps watch over travelers heading south from Auberdine. Human paladins are rare in Kalimdor's ancient forests, but he came west with a band of holy warriors from the Argent Dawn. They set out to help the Alliance's new night elf allies face demons and undead remnants left by the Third War. Delgren is stationed near the border of Darkshore and Ashenvale, where that danger reaches the road.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Dark Strand",b="Delgren and Balthule Shadowstrike confront the Cult of the Dark Strand around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. The cult's dark rituals threaten the frontier. Delgren sends adventurers into its territory to strike down cultists, shatter their summoning focuses, and hunt warlocks who traffic with demonic shadow.",sp=1},{t="An Unorthodox Mind",b="Delgren's devotion to the Holy Light has not kept him from studying Kalimdor's tangled politics. He learned Orcish, to the annoyance and disdain of his conservative superiors. The language gives him a way to understand the enemies and neighbors who share this untamed continent, beyond the teachings of his order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren is a human paladin at Maestra's Post, along the road in northern Ashenvale. He serves with the Argent Dawn and aids the night elves against demonic corruption, cultists, and shadows left by the Legion's invasion.",al={"who is delgren","delgren lore","who is the paladin at maestras post"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Delgren?",a="Delgren stands at Maestra's Post, a small night elven outpost in northwestern Ashenvale, just south of the trail leading into Darkshore.",al={"where is delgren","delgren location","delgren coordinates"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is a human paladin all the way out in Ashenvale?",a="Delgren traveled west with a company of Argent Dawn paladins to aid the Alliance's night elven allies. They work to purge demons, undead remnants, and dark cults threatening northern Kalimdor.",al={"why is delgren in ashenvale","why are there humans in ashenvale","delgren mission"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Delgren's connection to the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="Delgren and his companions watch the corrupt activity around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. He sends adventurers to investigate the ruin, hunt the Cult of the Dark Strand, and break its dark summoning practices.",al={"delgren althalaxx","tower of althalaxx quests","cult of the dark strand"},it="purpose"},{q="Why did Delgren learn Orcish?",a="Delgren learned Orcish to better understand Kalimdor and its inhabitants. His superiors in the order disapproved.",al={"delgren speaks orcish","does delgren speak orcish","delgren orc language"},it="motive"},{q="Who does Delgren work with at Maestra's Post?",a="Delgren works alongside Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand at Maestra's Post. Together, they watch for border threats, handle logistics, and fight shadow cultists along the Ashenvale frontier.",al={"delgren companions","who is at maestras post"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Delgren the Purifier on?",a="Delgren is a human paladin aligned with the Argent Dawn and loyal to the Alliance. He and his fellow paladins traveled across the sea specifically to aid their night elf allies in purifying Kalimdor of lingering evils.",al={"delgren faction","delgren alliance or horde","who does delgren serve"},it="side",add="616c1190"},{q="What does Delgren the Purifier want?",a="Delgren seeks to cleanse the ancient lands of Ashenvale and Darkshore of demonic taint and undead corruption. His primary focus is dismantling the Cult of the Dark Strand and ending their dark rituals around the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"delgren goal","what is delgren doing","delgren mission"},it="wants",add="30d7c847"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, Delgren shows how the Holy Light reaches Kalimdor. His crusade against demons and dark magic carries far beyond the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers heading south from Darkshore, Delgren and his companions offer a military foothold along the dangerous Ashenvale road.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may distrust foreign creeds, but Delgren's company fights the demonic cults troubling ancient ruins."},kw={"althalaxx","argent dawn","ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","cult of the dark strand","delgren","delgren the purifier","feero ironhand","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","npc:feero-ironhand","quest:965","topic:argent-dawn","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore"},src={"Delgren the Purifier"}}
E["npc:feero-ironhand"] = {t="npc",n="Feero Ironhand",z="ashenvale",s="At Maestra's Post, Feero Ironhand guards the road between Darkshore and Ashenvale. He works with Delgren the Purifier against the Cult of the Dark Strand.",h="At Maestra's Post, Feero Ironhand guards the road between Darkshore and Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Bulwark at Maestra's Post",b="Maestra's Post watches the road south from Darkshore into Ashenvale. Feero Ironhand serves at the outpost, keeping communication and trade with Auberdine moving while watching the surrounding woods. He and Delgren the Purifier oppose the Cult of the Dark Strand. Cultists and forest predators threaten the path between Darnassus's supply lines and Ashenvale's front lines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Feero Ironhand?",a="Feero Ironhand is an Alliance human paladin at Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale. He helps travelers on the road between Darkshore and Ashenvale and coordinates logistics with Auberdine.",al={"feero ironhand","who is feero","feero npc"},it="identity"},{q="What is Feero's purpose at Maestra's Post?",a="Feero helps defend Maestra's Post against local threats. He supports Delgren the Purifier against the Cult of the Dark Strand and helps keep courier and supply routes into Darkshore open.",al={"why is feero here","feero role","maestras post human"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Cult of the Dark Strand?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand operates in northern Ashenvale, practicing dark magic and foul rituals. Alliance forces at Maestra's Post work to disrupt and dismantle its operations.",al={"dark strand cult","cult of dark strand","dark strand"}},{q="Does Feero have connections to the Argent Dawn?",a="No connection to the Argent Dawn is recorded for Feero. He is a paladin who works closely with Delgren the Purifier, a fellow human paladin fighting dark forces in the forest.",al={"feero argent dawn","is feero argent dawn"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Feero Ironhand on?",a="Feero Ironhand stands firmly with the Alliance. Stationed at Maestra's Post, a crucial night elf outpost along the western border of Ashenvale, he aids travelers and local forces against the threats looming over the ancient forest.",al={"feero ironhand faction","is feero alliance","feero ironhand side"},it="side",add="996da789"},{q="What does Feero Ironhand want?",a="Feero aims to support the defenders of Maestra's Post and thwart the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand. Working alongside Delgren the Purifier, he seeks to purge their corrupting presence from northern Kalimdor and maintain supply lines between Ashenvale and Darkshore.",al={"feero ironhand goal","what does feero want","feero motive"},it="wants",add="bf9a9ed2"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers heading south from Darkshore, Feero offers a foothold in Ashenvale's dangerous, contested wilderness.",["race:Human"]="As a human, seeing Feero stand guard in Ashenvale's ancient elven woods is a welcome sign of the Alliance working across its peoples."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","cult of the dark strand","delgren the purifier","feero ironhand","maestra's post"},rel={"subzone:maestra-s-post","npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:auberdine","zone:ashenvale","quest:976","zone:darnassus"},src={"Feero Ironhand"}}
E["npc:gurda-ragescar"] = {t="npc",n="Gurda Ragescar",z="ashenvale",s="Gurda Ragescar fell at a Horde camp southwest of Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. She and Feran Strongwind died defending it against dangers in the shadowed forest.",h="Gurda Ragescar fell at a Horde camp southwest of Splintertree Post in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Slain Outpost",b="Gurda Ragescar and her guards fell at a small Horde camp southwest of Splintertree Post. The outpost stood beneath Ashenvale's dense canopy, deep in territory contested by night elven defenders and wild beasts. Gurda and Feran Strongwind were killed when the camp was overrun. Only remnants of their last stand remain for passing allies to find.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Scouts",b="Travelers near the trail may find the scene of Gurda's defeat. The camp's possessions and unfinished work point to Horde efforts across the woods, including missing documents and orders disrupted by the ambush.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gurda Ragescar?",a="Gurda Ragescar was an orc scout at a small Horde camp southwest of Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. She died with her companions when the outpost was overrun.",al={"who is gurda","gurda ragescar lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Gurda Ragescar be found?",a="Her body lies at an overrun camp southwest of Splintertree Post, off the road through central Ashenvale.",al={"gurda location","where is gurda ragescar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was killed alongside her?",a="Feran Strongwind and their guards died beside her when their small camp was attacked.",al={"who died with gurda","feran strongwind"},it="ties"},{q="What quest involves Gurda Ragescar?",a="Gurda is tied to The Lost Pages, which involves recovering scattered documents in the Ashenvale wilderness.",al={"gurda quests","the lost pages"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Which faction does Gurda Ragescar belong to?",a="Gurda Ragescar was loyal to the Horde. Stationed out of a small outpost just southwest of Splintertree Post, she and her fellows represented the Horde's fortified presence deep within Ashenvale's disputed borders.",al={"gurda ragescar faction","is gurda horde or alliance","who does gurda fight for"},it="side",add="28561f13"},{q="Why was Gurda Ragescar stationed southwest of Splintertree Post?",a="Gurda Ragescar maintained a forward Horde camp southwest of Splintertree Post alongside Feran Strongwind and a contingent of guards. Located along the contentious woodland trails, her post served to support Horde operations and recover lost assets across the hostile forests of Ashenvale.",al={"why is gurda ragescar here","gurda camp purpose","why was gurda in ashenvale"},it="why_here",add="e9ae8f07"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Gurda's fallen camp marks the cost of securing a foothold in Ashenvale's forests."},kw={"ashenvale","feran strongwind","gurda","orc","ragescar","splintertree","the lost pages"},rel={"subzone:splintertree-post","quest:6504","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Gurda Ragescar"}}
E["npc:illiyana"] = {t="npc",n="Illiyana",z="ashenvale",s="Near the Shrine of Aessina, Illiyana keeps watch over the woods of southwestern Ashenvale. The ancient dryad protects the woodland from corruption and calls on Alliance champions to drive back the satyrs.",h="Near the Shrine of Aessina, Illiyana keeps watch over the woods of southwestern Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Daughter of the Forest",b="Illiyana patrols the woods of southwestern Ashenvale as one of Cenarius's daughters. Dryads live in peace, yet fiercely defend wild lands. As corruption spreads through the woodland, Illiyana guards sacred relics and groves, keeping watch over nature's primal sanctity.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of the Satyr",b="Satyrs remain a threat to the glades and Illiyana's dryad sisters. These twisted, demonic creatures seek to corrupt the woods. Illiyana calls on travelers to slay them and recover lost relics, including the Branch of Cenarius, so the woodland stays free of demonic taint.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Illiyana?",a="Illiyana is a dryad who patrols southwestern Ashenvale near the Shrine of Aessina. A daughter of Cenarius, she watches over the wildlands and protects her sisters from demonic forces.",al={"who is this dryad","illiyana ashenvale","what is illiyana"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Illiyana keep walking while I talk to her?",a="Illiyana keeps to an active patrol route through the woodland. She continues pacing the grove while speaking with travelers.",al={"illiyana moving","why does she walk away","illiyana quest walking"},gp=true},{q="What tasks does Illiyana offer?",a="Illiyana calls on travelers to hunt the satyrs menacing the region and recover sacred relics such as the Branch of Cenarius to protect her fellow dryads.",al={"illiyana quests","forest song quests"},gp=true},{q="Where is Illiyana located?",a="Illiyana patrols near the Shrine of Aessina in southwestern Ashenvale, watching the paths and nearby groves.",al={"illiyana location","where to find illiyana","forest song dryad location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the dryads in danger from satyrs?",a="Satyrs are ancient night elves warped by demonic corruption. They delight in defiling nature and subjugating Cenarius's children, making dryads targets of their malice.",al={"why do satyrs hate dryads","dryads and satyr lore"},it="threat"},{q="Does Illiyana help the Horde?",a="No. Illiyana is allied with the Night Elves and the Alliance. Horde members who enter her glade will find her and her allies hostile.",al={"is illiyana hostile to horde","can horde talk to illiyana"},it="side"},{q="What does Illiyana want?",a="Illiyana is dedicated to protecting Ashenvale and her fellow dryads from the corrupting influence of the satyrs. She seeks brave champions of the Alliance to hunt down the wicked satyrs lurking nearby, defend the sacred groves, and help recover the Branch of Cenarius to cleanse the woodland.",al={"illiyana goal","what does illiyana want","illiyana purpose"},it="wants",add="f493742a"},{q="Why is Illiyana at the Shrine of Aessina?",a="Illiyana watches over the Shrine of Aessina in southwestern Ashenvale, a sanctuary dear to the woodland spirits and the daughters of Cenarius. From this holy ground, she monitors the encroaching corruption of the satyrs and coordinates defense efforts with night elf and Alliance allies.",al={"why is illiyana here","illiyana shrine of aessina","why is illiyana in ashenvale"},it="why_here",add="925d87c3"},{q="Who is Illiyana tied to?",a="As a dryad, Illiyana is one of the daughters of the demigod Cenarius, sharing a deep spiritual and familial kinship with her dryad sisters, such as Shael'dryn, and the keepers of the grove. She also shares strong bonds with the night elves who revere Aessina and Cenarius.",al={"illiyana ties","illiyana cenarius","who is illiyana related to"},it="ties",add="abbc4abe"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, dryads like Illiyana are sacred kin of Cenarius and protectors of the wild. Their call to arms against demonic satyrs is answered without hesitation.",["class:Druid"]="Druids honor dryads as embodiments of the wild. Helping Illiyana preserve the sanctified glades serves the Cenarion duty to heal the land.",["faction:Alliance"]="Illiyana is a woodland ally in southwestern Ashenvale. She offers shelter and guidance to Alliance forces protecting the wilderness from encroaching evils."},kw={"ashenvale","branch of cenarius","cenarius","dryad","illiyana","satyr","shrine of aessina"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","topic:satyr","topic:cenarius","quest:1031","quest:1032","quest:1021","npc:shael-dryn"},src={"Illiyana"}}
E["npc:illiyana-moonblaze"] = {t="npc",n="Illiyana Moonblaze",z="ashenvale",s="At Silverwing Grove, Illiyana Moonblaze supplies the Alliance champions fighting the Warsong Outriders. She works alongside the Silverwing Sentinels in Ashenvale.",h="At Silverwing Grove, Illiyana Moonblaze supplies the Alliance champions fighting the Warsong Outriders.",sec={{t="Silverwing Supply Officer",b="Illiyana Moonblaze keeps supplies for the Silverwing Sentinels at Silverwing Grove. Her post is near the path into Warsong Gulch, where she outfits defenders holding Ashenvale's southern woods against the Warsong clan.",sp=0},{t="Supplies for the Front Lines",b="Illiyana equips Alliance volunteers preparing to fight the Warsong clan in Warsong Gulch. As champions earn favor with the Silverwing Sentinels, she provides custom rations, specialized draughts, and fine weapons for woodland skirmishes. She also repairs weapons and armor for weary fighters returning from the front, keeping the Sentinels supplied for war.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Illiyana Moonblaze?",a="Illiyana Moonblaze is at Silverwing Grove in southeastern Ashenvale, near the staging grounds and portal leading into Warsong Gulch.",al={"illiyana moonblaze location","where is illiyana","silverwing quartermaster location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Illiyana Moonblaze a member of the Sentinels?",a="Illiyana Moonblaze works alongside the Silverwing Sentinels as their supply officer, outfitting Alliance champions who fight beside them.",al={"is illiyana a sentinel","illiyana rank","illiyana faction"},it="identity"},{q="What does Illiyana offer to Alliance champions?",a="Illiyana Moonblaze offers care packages, battlefield weapons, armor, rings, tabards, and consumables to champions who gain favor with the Silverwing Sentinels.",al={"what does illiyana sell","warsong gulch rewards ashenvale","illiyana vendor"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does she provide equipment repairs?",a="Yes. Illiyana Moonblaze repairs weapons and armor for Alliance defenders resting at the grove, as well as supplying specialized military gear.",al={"can illiyana repair","silverwing repair vendor","repair in silverwing grove"},gp=true},{q="What care packages does she hand out?",a="Illiyana Moonblaze gives Alliance fighters Sentinel Basic, Standard, and Advanced Care Packages through her supply work, providing frontline defenders with essential battlefield provisions.",al={"sentinel care package","illiyana quests","warsong gulch packages"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Illiyana Moonblaze?",a="Illiyana Moonblaze is a night elf supply officer stationed at Silverwing Grove in Ashenvale. Operating alongside the Silverwing Sentinels as their supplier, she outfits and provisions the Alliance champions who fight in Warsong Gulch.",al={"who is illiyana","illiyana moonblaze lore","who is illiyana moonblaze"},it="identity",add="4fdd1f70"},{q="Whose side is Illiyana Moonblaze on?",a="Illiyana is firmly aligned with the Alliance and the Silverwing Sentinels. She dedicates herself to supplying the defenders of Ashenvale against the Horde incursions in Warsong Gulch.",al={"illiyana moonblaze faction","is illiyana alliance","what faction is illiyana"},it="side",add="ebeca23e"},{q="Why is Illiyana Moonblaze in Ashenvale?",a="Illiyana is stationed at Silverwing Grove to support the ongoing war against the Warsong Outriders. She serves as the main supplier for the Silverwing Sentinels, outfitting and provisioning Alliance champions who take up the fight for Warsong Gulch.",al={"why is illiyana moonblaze here","illiyana moonblaze silverwing grove","why is illiyana in ashenvale"},it="why_here",add="4e149737"},{q="What does Illiyana Moonblaze want?",a="Illiyana seeks to bolster the Silverwing Sentinels against the Horde. She wants dedicated Alliance fighters to push the Warsong clan out of Ashenvale's ancient woods, and she rewards those who prove their valor in Warsong Gulch with specialized armaments, rations, and gear from her stores.",al={"what does illiyana want","illiyana moonblaze goals","illiyana purpose"},it="wants",add="e94ef362"},{q="Who is Illiyana Moonblaze tied to?",a="Illiyana works closely with the Silverwing Sentinels defending Ashenvale, outfitting the champions who fight for them in Warsong Gulch from her post at Silverwing Grove.",al={"illiyana moonblaze ties","who is illiyana connected to","illiyana silverwing sentinels"},it="ties",add="0bec8647"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance fighter marching south toward the contested border of Warsong Gulch, you can look to Illiyana Moonblaze for weapons, armor, and rations.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Illiyana Moonblaze keeping the Silverwing Sentinels supplied as the kaldorei rally to safeguard Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","care package","illiyana moonblaze","sentinel","silverwing grove","warsong gulch"},rel={"subzone:silverwing-grove","subzone:silverwing-outpost","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels","topic:night-elf"},src={"Illiyana Moonblaze"}}
E["npc:karang-amakkar"] = {t="npc",n="Karang Amakkar",z="ashenvale",s="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Karang Amakkar watches Ashenvale's rocky coast and the threats closing in around the Horde.",h="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Karang Amakkar watches Ashenvale's rocky coast and the threats closing in around the...",sec={{t="On the Coast of Ashenvale",b="At Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand, Karang Amakkar guards one of the Horde's most exposed borders. The camp faces pressure from the sea, the night elves, and wild beasts inland. Karang watches the hostile peoples along the road east, guarding Horde couriers and scouts from ambush by tribes defending their territory.",sp=0},{t="Dealing with the Furbolgs",b="Karang Amakkar gives much of his attention to the furbolgs of the ancient woods, especially the Foulweald tribe. Corruption and primal hostility drive these bear-folk into frenzies. Karang sends capable warriors to bring down their leader and clear their dens before the tribes can gather for an organized assault on Zoram'gar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Karang Amakkar?",a="Karang Amakkar is an orc scout at Zoram'gar Outpost on Ashenvale's coast. He serves the Horde by watching regional threats, especially hostile furbolg clans.",al={"karang","who is karang","karang amakkar lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Karang Amakkar?",a="Karang Amakkar is at Zoram'gar Outpost on Ashenvale's northwestern shore, along the Zoram Strand.",al={"karang location","where is karang amakkar","karang amakkar spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Karang Amakkar offer?",a="Karang sends Horde adventurers against nearby furbolg tribes and directs a strike against the king of the Foulweald.",al={"karang quests","karang tasks","what does karang want"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is Karang worried about the furbolgs?",a="Ashenvale's furbolgs have grown savage and corrupt. They attack travelers and threaten to cut Zoram'gar Outpost off from the Horde's other strongholds in the region.",al={"why kill furbolgs","furbolg threat ashenvale","foulweald threat"},it="threat"},{q="Is Karang Amakkar related to Initiate Amakkar?",a="Karang Amakkar and Initiate Amakkar share a clan name or family surname, but their exact family relationship is unconfirmed.",al={"amakkar family","initiate amakkar relative","karang family"},it="ties"},{q="Does Karang fight the night elves directly?",a="Karang Amakkar's duties at Zoram'gar focus on defending the territory and confronting wild threats such as the Foulweald furbolgs. Other Horde commanders handle direct military action against the night elves.",al={"karang vs night elves","karang alliance"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Karang Amakkar on?",a="Karang Amakkar is loyal to the Horde, serving its interests directly within the dense forests of Ashenvale. Operating alongside fellow orcs out of Zoram'gar Outpost along the coast, his efforts are focused on protecting Horde outposts and subduing regional threats like hostile furbolgs.",al={"karang amakkar faction","is karang horde","karang allegiance"},it="side",add="b0298d21"},{q="What does Karang Amakkar want?",a="Karang wants to quell the dangerous native tribes of Ashenvale that threaten the Horde's foothold. He actively seeks capable adventurers to strike down aggressive furbolg populations, specifically the Foulweald tribe and its king, before they can overrun nearby encampments.",al={"karang amakkar goal","what does karang want","karang motive"},it="wants",add="481f1d87"},{q="Why is Karang Amakkar here in Ashenvale?",a="Karang is stationed in Ashenvale to support the Horde's expansion and defense in an intensely hostile territory. Situated at Zoram'gar Outpost, he monitors the wilderness and directs warriors to neutralize hostile beast tribes that menace the Horde's presence along the Zoram Strand.",al={"why is karang here","karang amakkar purpose ashenvale","why is karang in zoramgar"},it="why_here",add="7b1509e6"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Karang Amakkar aids Horde travelers in western Ashenvale, sending them against hostile creatures around Zoram'gar Outpost.",["race:Orc"]="Far from Durotar, Karang Amakkar holds a remote outpost, showing the grit of orc sentries who guard dangerous borders."},kw={"ashenvale","foulweald","furbolg","karang amakkar","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","zone:ashenvale","quest:6621"},src={"Karang Amakkar"}}
E["npc:kil-hala"] = {t="npc",n="Kil'hala",z="ashenvale",s="At the Crossroads in the Barrens, Kil'hala teaches Horde tailors to work cloth. He also weaves nether-lace robes for young Horde mages who bring him locks of hair from Ashenvale's laughing sisters.",h="At the Crossroads in the Barrens, Kil'hala teaches Horde tailors to work cloth.",sec={{t="Tailor of the Barrens",b="Kil'hala trains tailors at the Crossroads, where Horde recruits and travelers can learn his craft. He teaches work with common spun bolts and garments suited to life on the dry plains. At Deino's request, he also makes nether-lace robes for young mages who bring him hair from the laughing sisters, the dryads of Ashenvale's forests.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kil'hala?",a="Kil'hala is a Darkspear troll who trains tailors at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He teaches Horde tradesfolk the basics of weaving cloth and making garments.",al={"kilhala identity","who is kilhala","crossroads tailor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Kil'hala?",a="Find Kil'hala at the Crossroads, the central Horde settlement in the Barrens. He is alongside the other Horde trade trainers.",al={"kilhala location","where is kilhala","kilhala spot"},gp=true},{q="What tasks does Kil'hala give to tailors?",a="Kil'hala does not send tailors out himself. Young Horde mages sent by Deino bring him locks of hair from the Laughing Sisters, dryads near Ashenvale's Raynewood Retreat, and he weaves the hair into a nether-lace garment for them.",al={"kilhala quests","laughing sisters quest","nether lace garment"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Kil'hala on?",a="Kil'hala is loyal to the Horde and his Darkspear troll kin. Situated at the heart of the Crossroads, he serves as a tailoring instructor to help equip travelers, warriors, and aspiring crafters making their way across Kalimdor.",al={"kil'hala horde or alliance","kil'hala faction","who does kil'hala serve"},it="side",add="5b372e18"},{q="What does Kil'hala want?",a="Kil'hala seeks to share his expertise in weaving and cloth working with fellow Horde members. He trains aspiring tailors and, as a favor to the mage Deino, weaves fine nether-lace robes for young mages who bring him the hair of the Laughing Sisters.",al={"kil'hala goal","kil'hala purpose","what does kil'hala need"},it="wants",add="d6c7e4b6"},{q="Why is Kil'hala here?",a="Kil'hala makes his home at the Crossroads, a vital hub connecting Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern wilds. Being stationed here allows him to offer his needlecraft and guidance to the steady stream of Horde adventurers traversing the Barrens.",al={"why is kil'hala at crossroads","why is kil'hala in barrens","kil'hala location reason"},it="why_here",add="218c0279"}},ang={["profession:Tailoring"]="As a Horde tailor, you can learn the craft from Kil'hala at the Crossroads. He also offers a way to weave exotic magical robes.",["faction:Horde"]="At the Crossroads, Kil'hala teaches textile crafts and provides goods for Horde warbands and travelers making a foothold in the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","kil'hala","kilhala","laughing sisters","nether-lace","tailoring","trainer"},rel={"subzone:crossroads","quest:1945","quest:1946","zone:ashenvale","topic:troll"},src={"Kil'hala"}}
E["npc:krolg"] = {t="npc",n="Krolg",z="ashenvale",s="South of Mystral Lake, Krolg lives uncorrupted in an isolated hut in Ashenvale. Cast out from the Foulweald tribe, he kept his sanity when his kin fell to demonic madness. He speaks only with those who appear to be furbolgs.",h="South of Mystral Lake, Krolg lives uncorrupted in an isolated hut in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Mind Unbroken",b="South of Mystral Lake, Krolg remains lucid and untouched by madness. Most Foulweald furbolgs in Ashenvale have succumbed to the demonic taint left by the Burning Legion. In his secluded shelter, Krolg keeps a cautious vigil over the forest. He witnessed his brethren descend into senseless violence, and now speaks only with beings who appear to be kin.",sp=0},{t="Dartol's Legacy",b="Dartol's Rod of Transformation lets Alliance travelers take the shape of furbolgs. Seeing what seems to be a friendly kindred spirit, Krolg shares ways to cleanse the land. He sends heroes against Ran Bloodtooth and his guards, whose corruption and hatred threaten the forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why won't Krolg talk to me?",a="Krolg distrusts outsiders and fears the violent chaos consuming the forest. He ignores you unless Dartol's Rod of Transformation has made you appear to be a furbolg during Raene's Cleansing.",al={"krolg wont speak","cant talk to krolg","why is krolg silent"},gp=true},{q="Where can Krolg be found?",a="Krolg lives in Krolg's Hut, just south of Mystral Lake in south-central Ashenvale.",al={"krolg location","where is krolg","krolg hut"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tribe does Krolg belong to?",a="Krolg was once part of the Foulweald tribe. His kin fell to corruption and demonic frenzy, but he kept his sanity and was cast out.",al={"krolg tribe","is krolg foulweald"},it="origin"},{q="Is Krolg hostile to players?",a="Krolg attacks outsiders who approach without appearing to be furbolgs. Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation before approaching him.",al={"does krolg attack","is krolg an enemy"},it="hostile",gp=true},{q="Why does Krolg want Ran Bloodtooth dead?",a="Krolg sees Ran Bloodtooth as power-hungry and strengthened by corruption. Though he blames the night elves for his kin's suffering, he will not let Ran threaten their children or the forest's other creatures.",al={"krolg ran bloodtooth","why kill ran bloodtooth"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Who was Dartol, whose rod lets adventurers speak with Krolg?",a="Dartol was an evil wizard who created the enchanted Rod of Transformation before his death. During Raene's Cleansing, adventurers recover its lost pieces and have it remade so they can approach Krolg in furbolg form.",al={"who is dartol","dartols rod backstory"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Krolg?",a="Krolg is an uncorrupted furbolg living in self-imposed exile south of Mystral Lake in Ashenvale. Formerly a member of the Foulweald tribe, he managed to resist the dark corruption that overtook his brethren. Now isolated in his humble hut, he preserves his wits and wisdom while mourning what his people have become, willing to assist outsiders who approach him disguised in furbolg form.",al={"who is krolg","krolg identity","who is the furbolg at krolgs hut"},it="identity",add="4c25d8d9"},{q="Whose side is Krolg on?",a="Krolg is not pledged to the Alliance or the Horde; he stands alone as one of the few sane, uncorrupted furbolgs left in the region. However, he will only treat with Alliance adventurers who approach him disguised as a fellow furbolg using Dartol's Rod, offering them guidance and ritual knowledge in their struggle against the corrupted Foulweald.",al={"is krolg alliance or horde","krolg faction","whose side is krolg on"},it="side",add="19bbdb38"},{q="What does Krolg want?",a="Krolg seeks an end to the madness destroying his former kin. He asks transformed adventurers to slay Ran Bloodtooth and his guards because their corruption threatens the night elves and the forest's other creatures.",al={"what does krolg want","krolg motives","krolg goal"},it="wants",add="39fdb4f1"},{q="Why is Krolg here?",a="Krolg was cast out of his tribe and settled south of Mystral Lake, one of the few furbolgs untouched by the corruption that warped the Foulweald. Living in isolation keeps him safe from his maddened former brothers while he keeps a watchful eye on their territory.",al={"why is krolg here","why did krolg leave the foulweald","why does krolg live near mystral lake"},it="why_here",add="640007b0"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Astranaar, Krolg recalls their ancient furbolg allies, before demonic corruption shattered the tribes.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid seeking to restore balance to Ashenvale, you can turn to Krolg, a lucid voice amid wildlife tainted by corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance scout aiding Raene Wolfrunner, you rely on Krolg to dismantle the leadership of the hostile Foulweald furbolgs."},kw={"ashenvale furbolg","chief murgut","dartol's rod","foulweald","krolg","krolg's hut","mystral lake","raene's cleansing"},rel={"quest:991","quest:6621","npc:raene-wolfrunner","subzone:mystral-lake","zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","topic:alliance"},src={"Krolg"}}
E["npc:kuray-bin"] = {t="npc",n="Kuray'bin",z="ashenvale",s="Kuray'bin watches the forest trails outside Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. The Darkspear scout guards the Horde encampment from night elf scouts.",h="Kuray'bin watches the forest trails outside Splintertree Post in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Forest Edge",b="Outside Splintertree Post, Kuray'bin watches the forest for Alliance scouts. Silverwing Sentinels patrol the canopy and send swift outrunners across the border. Their task is to gather intelligence on Horde lumber operations and defenses. Kuray'bin sends Horde fighters to hunt the outrunners before they can report to Silverwing Outpost, since scouts left unchecked can become an ambushing force.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kuray'bin?",a="Kuray'bin is a Darkspear troll watchman outside Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. He sends Horde fighters to hunt night elf scouts in the surrounding woods.",al={"kuraybin","who is kuraybin","splintertree troll scout"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Kuray'bin?",a="Kuray'bin stands just outside Splintertree Post's stockade gates, watching the road approaches in central-eastern Ashenvale.",al={"kuraybin location","where is kuraybin"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Kuray'bin want the Silverwing Outrunners dead?",a="Silverwing Outrunners are Silverwing Sentinels scouting close to Splintertree Post. Kuray'bin wants them stopped before they can gather intelligence on Horde positions or coordinate surprise attacks.",al={"why kill outrunners","ashenvale outrunners quest lore"},it="wants"},{q="Does Kuray'bin offer any other tasks?",a="No. Kuray'bin's duty at the outpost perimeter is to oversee the effort against the night elf outrunners.",al={"kuraybin quests","kuray bin task"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Kuray'bin on?",a="Kuray'bin serves the Horde. Stationed just outside Splintertree Post, he works to secure the settlement against Alliance incursions and keeps watch over the contested borders of Ashenvale.",al={"kuraybin faction","who does kuraybin serve","is kuraybin horde"},it="side",add="65134a3b"},{q="Why is Kuray'bin stationed here in Ashenvale?",a="Kuray'bin stands watch at an outpost just outside Splintertree Post to monitor hostile movements. With night elf scouts encroaching deeply into Horde territory, his duty is to detect threats before they strike the settlement.",al={"why is kuraybin here","kuraybin purpose ashenvale","why is kuraybin at splintertree post"},it="why_here",add="bfddbb0e"},{q="Who is Kuray'bin tied to?",a="Kuray'bin is tied directly to the Horde garrison at Splintertree Post. As a jungle troll sentry, he works in coordination with the orcs and fellow defenders holding this tenuous Ashenvale foothold against the night elves.",al={"kuraybin ties","kuraybin allies","who does kuraybin work with"},it="ties",add="189aca6f"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see why Kuray'bin keeps watch: night elf guerrillas could surround and overrun Splintertree Post.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you share the jungle tracking instincts Kuray'bin uses to spot night elf scouts among the trees."},kw={"ashenvale outrunners","darkspear","kuray'bin","kuraybin","silverwing sentinels","splintertree post"},rel={"subzone:splintertree-post","quest:6503","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels","topic:horde","topic:troll","topic:alliance"},src={"Kuray'bin"}}
E["npc:marukai"] = {t="npc",n="Marukai",z="ashenvale",s="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Marukai holds a remote Horde beachhead against the Wrathtail naga. The Darkspear jungle troll coordinates efforts to drive the naga back along Ashenvale's foggy northwest coast.",h="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Marukai holds a remote Horde beachhead against the Wrathtail naga.",sec={{t="Holding the Strand",b="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Marukai works to keep the encampment from being overwhelmed. The outpost sits on the northern edge of the Zoram Strand, surrounded by ancient ruins, hostile night elf territory, and the restless sea. Wrathtail naga emerge in force from the waters and ancient elven ruins to claim the shoreline. Marukai directs Horde champions to push them back into the tide and collect their heads, keeping the outpost a viable coastal stronghold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marukai?",a="Marukai is a jungle troll defending Zoram'gar Outpost, the Horde's isolated coastal encampment on Ashenvale's northwestern shore.",al={"marukai lore","who is marukai","marukai npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Marukai fighting the naga?",a="Wrathtail naga have infested the nearby Zoram Strand and surrounding ruins. To secure the outpost's borders and ensure Horde survival on the coast, Marukai hires adventurers to hunt them directly and thin their numbers.",al={"why kill naga","marukai naga quest","zoram strand naga"},it="wants"},{q="Where is Marukai located?",a="Marukai stands with her kin at Zoram'gar Outpost, at the mouth of the Zoram Strand in northwestern Ashenvale, just south of the submerged ruins of Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"where is marukai","marukai location","find marukai"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Marukai on?",a="Marukai is loyal to the Horde. Operating out of Zoram'gar Outpost along the coast of Ashenvale, she stands guard over Horde interests and relies on Horde travelers to defend the settlement against local dangers.",al={"marukai faction","is marukai horde","who does marukai serve"},it="side",add="53dc13db"},{q="Why is Marukai here at Zoram'gar Outpost?",a="Marukai is stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost to defend the Horde's foothold on the Zoram Strand. With the aggressive Wrathtail naga returning to the beaches and threatening the camp's borders, she coordinates efforts to secure the perimeter and keep the outpost safe.",al={"why is marukai in ashenvale","marukai purpose","what brings marukai here"},it="why_here",add="1bf5ddde"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="In night elf territory, Marukai anchors one of the Horde's most precarious coastal camps. She relies on allied champions to keep the local naga from overrunning their position.",["race:Troll"]="Far from the warm echoes of Sen'jin Village, Marukai shows the Darkspear tribe's resilience as they carve out fortified footholds for the Horde across Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","darkspear","jungle troll","marukai","naga","wrathtail","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","subzone:zoram-strand","quest:6442","npc:mitsuwa","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde","topic:troll"},src={"Marukai"}}
E["npc:mastok-wrilehiss"] = {t="npc",n="Mastok Wrilehiss",z="ashenvale",s="At Splintertree Post in eastern Ashenvale, Mastok Wrilehiss helps hold the Horde’s ground. He directs scouts and warriors to watch nearby borders and confront corrupting elemental forces amid the night elves’ hostility.",h="At Splintertree Post in eastern Ashenvale, Mastok Wrilehiss helps hold the Horde’s ground.",sec={{t="A Bulwark in the Ancient Woods",b="Deep beneath Ashenvale’s canopy, Splintertree Post is surrounded by hostile night elf territory. Mastok Wrilehiss helps defend the outpost and watches its supply routes and the forest around it. The Sentinels see the settlement as an intrusion that despoils their lands, and they strike quickly at any sign of weakness.",sp=0},{t="Coordinating the Front",b="From within the stockade, Mastok gives passing adventurers duties tied to the Horde’s defense. He watches the borders toward the Stonetalon Mountains and sends scouts to speak with shamans such as Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring at Zoram'gar Strand. His work also follows the strange corruption afflicting local elementals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mastok Wrilehiss?",a="Mastok Wrilehiss is an orc officer at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. He helps defend the outpost against night elf attacks and investigates threats in the region.",al={"who is mastok","mastok wrilehiss role","who is this orc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Mastok Wrilehiss be found?",a="You can find Mastok Wrilehiss inside Splintertree Post, a fortified Horde outpost in east-central Ashenvale along the main forest road.",al={"mastok location","where is mastok wrilehiss","mastok map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Mastok assign to adventurers?",a="Mastok assigns Horde adventurers to investigate corrupted elementals, secure routes toward Stonetalon, and carry messages to Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring.",al={"mastok quests","quests from mastok"},it="wants"},{q="Why is Splintertree Post under constant pressure?",a="Splintertree Post is a Horde logging hub and stronghold in Ashenvale. The night elves regard the orcs’ presence and timber harvesting as a desecration of sacred lands, and skirmishes continue.",al={"why are night elves attacking splintertree","splintertree post conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Mastok send travelers to Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Mastok sends travelers to Je'neu Sancrea because the Earthen Ring shamans study and heal Ashenvale’s elemental instability. Their knowledge can help address tainted water elementals and strange disturbances.",al={"why contact earthen ring","mastok and jeneu"},it="motive"},{q="Is Mastok Wrilehiss hostile to Alliance players?",a="Yes. Mastok serves the Horde and defends Splintertree Post. He attacks Alliance members who approach the encampment.",al={"can alliance talk to mastok","is mastok killable"},it="side"},{q="Why is Mastok Wrilehiss in Ashenvale?",a="Mastok Wrilehiss is stationed at Splintertree Post to help secure the Horde's foothold in the contested forests of Ashenvale. As an experienced defender among the Warsong forces, he oversees local defense efforts, tracks disturbances affecting the surrounding wilds, and enlists capable travelers to deal with corrupting elemental threats and neighboring night elf hostilities.",al={"why is mastok here","mastok wrilehiss splintertree post","why is mastok at splintertree"},it="why_here",add="414a3ea9"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion, you can look to Mastok for duties that help hold the Horde’s frontier in Ashenvale.",["faction:Alliance"]="Mastok represents the orc military presence in Ashenvale and defends Splintertree Post against night elf Sentinels.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may be directed by Mastok to seek the Earthen Ring’s guidance at Zoram'gar Strand about corrupted elementals."},kw={"ashenvale","earthen ring","mastok","orc","splintertree","stonetalon","wrilehiss"},rel={"subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","quest:824","quest:1918","quest:25","topic:alliance"},src={"Mastok Wrilehiss"}}
E["npc:mitsuwa"] = {t="npc",n="Mitsuwa",z="ashenvale",s="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Mitsuwa mourns the trolls slain on their journey through Ashenvale. He calls on Horde champions to recover their stolen charms.",h="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Mitsuwa mourns the trolls slain on their journey through Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Avenging the Fallen Kin",b="Mitsuwa serves the Horde at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand, alongside Marukai. Thistlefur furbolgs of northern Ashenvale ambushed and slaughtered a group of traveling trolls bound for the outpost. Mitsuwa sees their deaths as a grievous offense. He sends warriors to the Thistlefur dens to reclaim the stolen troll charms and honor the spirits of his kin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mitsuwa?",a="Mitsuwa is a Darkspear jungle troll at Zoram'gar Outpost in northwestern Ashenvale. He watches over the post alongside Marukai and directs the response to nearby threats.",al={"mitsuwa","who is mitsuwa","mitsuwa lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the trolls traveling to Zoram'gar?",a="Thistlefur furbolgs ambushed and slaughtered a group of trolls traveling across Ashenvale to Zoram'gar Outpost. The furbolgs stripped the fallen of their possessions.",al={"dead trolls ashenvale","thistlefur attack trolls"}},{q="Why are the troll charms so important to Mitsuwa?",a="The charms hold spiritual and cultural meaning for the Darkspear. Leaving these sacred relics with the Thistlefur furbolgs dishonors the spirits of the slain.",al={"why troll charms","troll charm quest reason"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the charms located?",a="The Thistlefur furbolgs carried the charms to their village and den in northern Ashenvale, east of the Zoram Strand.",al={"where are troll charms","thistlefur village location"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Mitsuwa on?",a="Mitsuwa is loyal to the Horde and resides among his kin at Zoram'gar Outpost along the coast of Ashenvale. He works closely with fellow Horde travelers and looks to Horde adventurers to avenge fallen comrades.",al={"mitsuwa faction","is mitsuwa horde","who does mitsuwa serve"},it="side",add="24ae2c07"},{q="What does Mitsuwa want?",a="Mitsuwa seeks justice for a group of fellow trolls slaughtered on their way to Zoram'gar Outpost. The aggressive Thistlefur furbolgs ambushed the travelers and stole their sacred troll charms, and Mitsuwa wants those stolen heirlooms reclaimed from the beasts.",al={"mitsuwa goal","what does mitsuwa need","mitsuwa quest"},it="wants",add="ec72a5f0"},{q="Why is Mitsuwa here at Zoram'gar Outpost?",a="Mitsuwa is stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost, a remote Horde encampment on the western shore of Ashenvale. From here, he monitors the surrounding wilds and looks after travelers braving the treacherous roads through furbolg and night elf territory.",al={"why is mitsuwa in zoramgar","mitsuwa purpose ashenvale","why is mitsuwa here"},it="why_here",add="b936450a"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear adventurers, Mitsuwa's call is personal. Recovering ancestral charms from the furbolgs honors their murdered kin and brings peace to their spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="Zoram'gar Outpost is an isolated, besieged garrison. Helping Mitsuwa strengthens the Horde's precarious position against wild beasts and Alliance scouts in western Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","darkspear","furbolg","marukai","mitsuwa","thistlefur","troll","troll charm","zoram'gar"},rel={"quest:6462","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","npc:marukai","topic:furbolg","topic:troll","topic:horde","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Mitsuwa"}}
E["npc:orendil-broadleaf"] = {t="npc",n="Orendil Broadleaf",z="ashenvale",s="At Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale, night elf Orendil Broadleaf tends to the sick. His knowledge of forest plants helps him make remedies for young lives in the troubled woodlands.",h="At Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale, night elf Orendil Broadleaf tends to the sick.",sec={{t="Healer of the Forest Border",b="At Maestra's Post on Ashenvale's western border, Orendil Broadleaf cares for the sick. The skilled healer knows the local herbs and how to use them in restorative remedies. He depends on travelers passing through to gather rare plants and other natural ingredients. Tension and conflict press closer to the forest, but Orendil remains focused on protecting his kin and easing their ailments.",sp=0},{t="A Race Against Sickness",b="Orendil Broadleaf plays a central part in the effort to cure Relara Whitemoon, an afflicted child in Astranaar. He studies Ashenvale's plants, including Bathran's hair, and devises potent elixirs to hold back the deadly sickness. Relara's illness remains a danger, and Orendil's remedies are meant to keep it at bay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Orendil Broadleaf?",a="Orendil Broadleaf is a night elf herbalist and healer at Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale. He is known for his skill with herbs and healing.",al={"orendil broadleaf","who is orendil","orendil ashenvale"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Orendil Broadleaf be found?",a="Orendil Broadleaf can be found at Maestra's Post, a night elf outpost along the main path in western Ashenvale, near the border with Darkshore.",al={"orendil broadleaf location","find orendil","where is orendil"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Orendil trying to cure?",a="Orendil formulates a curative draught to save Relara Whitemoon, an ailing night elf child in Astranaar. He uses rare herbs gathered from Ashenvale's wild reaches.",al={"orendil cure","who is orendil curing","relara whitemoon cure"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Orendil Broadleaf on?",a="Orendil Broadleaf stands firmly with the Alliance and the night elves of Darnassus. Stationed at Maestra's Post, he works alongside the Sentinels to defend Ashenvale against Horde aggression and tends to the injuries and ailments of his kin.",al={"orendil broadleaf faction","is orendil broadleaf alliance","orendil broadleaf allegiance"},it="side",add="c4fe2e8b"},{q="What does Orendil Broadleaf want?",a="Orendil Broadleaf seeks to heal the sick and wounded while safeguarding the forest. His foremost concern is concocting a vital cure for Relara Whitemoon, an ailing night elf child in Astranaar, and he relies on outside travelers to gather the rare herbs needed to save her.",al={"what does orendil want","orendil broadleaf goals","orendil broadleaf motive"},it="wants",add="5dbbc739"},{q="Why is Orendil Broadleaf here?",a="Orendil remains at Maestra's Post as a dedicated herbalist and healer on Ashenvale's western border. There he tends to the ailments of his kin and relies on passing travelers to gather the rare herbs his remedies require.",al={"why is orendil broadleaf at maestras post","why is orendil in ashenvale","what is orendil broadleaf doing here"},it="why_here",add="9af45c4c"},{q="Who is Orendil Broadleaf tied to?",a="Orendil Broadleaf works alongside the Sentinels defending Maestra's Post and coordinates closely with Pelturas Whitemoon in Astranaar to safeguard Pelturas's young daughter, Relara.",al={"orendil broadleaf connections","who does orendil broadleaf work with","orendil apprentices"},it="ties",add="7beb4a99"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Orendil shows how regional plants can save lives, relying on rare botanicals such as Bathran's hair to brew potent antidotes in the field.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf defending Ashenvale, you can look to Orendil for remedies that may save even a deathly ill child."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","bathran's hair","maestra's post","orendil broadleaf","orendil's cure","relara whitemoon"},rel={"subzone:maestra-s-post","quest:1020","quest:1010","subzone:astranaar","npc:raene-wolfrunner","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels","topic:night-elf"},src={"Orendil Broadleaf"}}
E["npc:pelturas-whitemoon"] = {t="npc",n="Pelturas Whitemoon",z="ashenvale",s="In Astranaar, Pelturas Whitemoon fights to save his gravely ill daughter, Relara. He turns to the local herbalist Orendil Broadleaf and Alliance travelers for help, seeking sacred remedies in Ashenvale.",h="In Astranaar, Pelturas Whitemoon fights to save his gravely ill daughter, Relara.",sec={{t="A Father's Plight in Astranaar",b="Pelturas Whitemoon lives in Astranaar with his young daughter, Relara. They often gather moonstones together at Fallen Sky Lake. When Relara falls critically ill with a mysterious affliction, Pelturas turns from their quiet days to the urgent work of saving her. Though Astranaar faces dangers on many fronts, his daughter is all that matters to him.",sp=0},{t="Ancient Cures and Corrupted Groves",b="Ordinary herbs fail to ease Relara’s illness, so Pelturas seeks help from Orendil Broadleaf. Her care calls for rare, sacred reagents tied to the land and the Moon Goddess. An Elune's Tear and shimmering, powdered stardust from ancient Kaldorei ruins are needed to cool Relara’s burning fever. Each remedy barely keeps death at bay, as corruption in Ashenvale’s soil and waters reaches its people.",sp=1},{t="Fallen Sky Lake",b="Pelturas seeks a moonstone from the Shadethicket Oracle at Fallen Sky Lake to restore Relara’s strength. The lake was once a peaceful place where father and daughter gathered stones together, but corrupted bog beasts have made it perilous. Pelturas crushes the recovered moonstone into a restorative tea, and Relara’s lingering weakness finally lifts. She is well again.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Pelturas Whitemoon?",a="Pelturas Whitemoon lives in Astranaar, in central Ashenvale. He seeks help from passing Alliance travelers to gather sacred ingredients for his seriously ill daughter, Relara.",al={"pelturas","who is pelturas whitemoon","pelturas astranaar"},it="identity"},{q="What is wrong with his daughter, Relara?",a="Relara suffers from a sudden, virulent disease that brings severe fever and deep weakness. The unnatural sickness appears tied to corruption spreading through Ashenvale’s wilds, resists ordinary medicine, and calls for sacred remedies.",al={"relara illness","why is relara sick","relara disease"},it="threat"},{q="Who helps Pelturas treat the sickness?",a="Pelturas seeks counsel from Orendil Broadleaf, a local night elf herbalist. Orendil prescribes traditional Kaldorei remedies, including cleansing stones and herbal poultices.",al={"pelturas herbalist","who helps relara","orendil broadleaf pelturas"},it="allies"},{q="What reagents are needed to cure Relara?",a="Relara needs an herbal draught from Orendil, a cleansing Elune's Tear, and shimmering, powdered stardust from ancient ruins to break her burning fever. A moonstone from Fallen Sky Lake, brewed into tea, restores her strength.",al={"cure reagents pelturas","relara cure ingredients","what cures relara"},it="item"},{q="Why is Fallen Sky Lake significant to Pelturas?",a="Pelturas and Relara used to gather moonstones together at Fallen Sky Lake. Hostile Shadethicket bog beasts now threaten the lake, so Pelturas asks travelers to retrieve the moonstone needed for Relara’s recovery.",al={"fallen sky lake pelturas","moonstone fallen sky lake"},it="place"},{q="Is Pelturas a member of the Cenarion Circle or the Sentinels?",a="No. Pelturas is a civilian resident of Astranaar, one of the Kaldorei families living amid Ashenvale’s dangers.",al={"is pelturas a sentinel","pelturas faction role"}},{q="Whose side is Pelturas Whitemoon on?",a="Pelturas is loyal to the night elves of Darnassus and stands firmly with the Alliance. Living in Astranaar, he relies on the protection of his fellow kaldorei and welcomes any Alliance traveler willing to lend a hand to his family in their hour of need.",al={"pelturas whitemoon faction","is pelturas alliance","pelturas allegiance"},it="side",add="6580d64d"},{q="What does Pelturas Whitemoon want?",a="Above all else, Pelturas wants to save his beloved daughter Relara from the mysterious illness gripping her. He is desperate to gather potent restorative reagents—from sacred tears to ancient stardust—in hopes of concocting a remedy that will finally break her fever and restore her vitality.",al={"what does pelturas want","pelturas whitemoon goal","what is pelturas trying to do"},it="wants",add="806ac345"},{q="Why is Pelturas Whitemoon in Astranaar?",a="Pelturas makes his home in Astranaar, the heart of night elf settlement in Ashenvale. While he once roamed the nearby woods and shores like Fallen Sky Lake with his daughter, he now remains confined to the safety of the town to tend to her deteriorating condition.",al={"why is pelturas in astranaar","why is pelturas here","where does pelturas live"},it="why_here",add="8d08bbb7"},{q="Who is Pelturas Whitemoon tied to?",a="Pelturas's life revolves around his young daughter, Relara, whom he is fighting tirelessly to protect. In his efforts to heal her, he works closely with Orendil Broadleaf, a local night elf skilled in medicinal remedies who guides him toward potential cures.",al={"pelturas whitemoon family","who is pelturas related to","pelturas daughter"},it="ties",add="3f413488"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Pelturas’s struggle shows how corruption and regional conflict threaten everyday Kaldorei families and ancient glades.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Pelturas save Relara reflects the Alliance’s commitment to defending and aiding Kaldorei settlements in Kalimdor.",["class:Priest"]="Elune’s cleansing rites and sacred reagents reflect the healing power and reverence the Sisterhood of Elune brings to night elf culture.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Relara’s draughts, poultices, and botanical tinctures reflect the place of herbal lore in Kaldorei medicine."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","elune's tear","fallen sky lake","moonstone","orendil broadleaf","pelturas","relara","ruins of stardust","whitemoon"},rel={"subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","npc:orendil-broadleaf","quest:1020","quest:1033","quest:1034","quest:1035","topic:elune"},src={"Pelturas Whitemoon"}}
E["npc:pixel"] = {t="npc",n="Pixel",z="ashenvale",s="At Splintertree Post, Pixel carries Warsong goods through dangerous lands for a fee. She keeps the saw blades until she is paid, and looks for other cargo worth carrying.",h="At Splintertree Post, Pixel carries Warsong goods through dangerous lands for a fee.",sec={{t="Business in the Deep Woods",b="Pixel carries freight for the Warsong Clan from Splintertree Post, where the Horde holds a fortified post in Ashenvale. She takes goods through active war zones to support the clan’s logging work, but coin and contracts guide her choices. The saw blades stay with her until she receives payment. For this shipment, she wants a deadly blunderbuss to guard herself on the road. Pixel also pays travelers for satyr horns, which are in high demand in Ratchet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pixel?",a="Pixel is a goblin courier working from Splintertree Post in eastern Ashenvale. She carries cargo through dangerous lands and has a shipment of saw blades for the Warsong logging effort.",al={"who is this goblin","pixel lore","splintertree goblin"},it="identity"},{q="Why won't Pixel hand over the saw blades immediately?",a="Pixel holds on to the saw blades until she receives payment or trade goods to cover her fee. Even with the Horde’s urgent needs in Ashenvale, she sticks to her business terms.",al={"why does pixel want payment","warsong saw blades delivery","saw blades quest"},it="wants"},{q="Why does she want satyr horns?",a="Pixel wants satyr horns because they are in high demand in Ratchet, where she is headed next. She cannot take on the satyrs of Night Run, Satyrnaar and Xavian herself, so she pays travelers to gather horns for her to sell.",al={"why satyr horns","pixel satyrs","satyr quest splintertree"},it="motive"},{q="Is Pixel officially a member of the Horde?",a="Pixel works with the Horde at Splintertree Post through profitable contracts for the Warsong logging operations. Her chief loyalty is to trade, profit and fulfilling her delivery agreements.",al={"is pixel horde","pixel faction","is pixel neutral"},it="side"},{q="Why is Pixel in Ashenvale?",a="Pixel is an enterprising goblin courier who earns her living hauling freight across Kalimdor and beyond. She traveled into Ashenvale's contested forests to deliver a critical shipment of Warsong saw blades directly to the Horde outpost at Splintertree Post.",al={"why is pixel here","pixel splintertree post why","pixel ashenvale"},it="why_here",add="c8b7be1d"},{q="Who is Pixel working for?",a="Pixel operates independently as a freelance delivery specialist rather than swearing allegiance to any single faction. Her current business dealings tie her to the Warsong Outriders and the forces stationed at Splintertree Post, supplying the industrial machinery necessary for their lumber efforts in the forest.",al={"who is pixel tied to","pixel employer","pixel connections"},it="ties",add="37ebabcf"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion helping establish a foothold in Ashenvale, you can rely on Pixel to supply the industrial hardware the Warsong Clan needs to keep its logging machinery running."},kw={"ashenvale","courier","goblin","pixel","satyr horns","splintertree post","warsong saw blades"},rel={"subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","quest:6581","quest:6441","topic:goblin","topic:satyr"},src={"Pixel"}}
E["npc:raene-wolfrunner"] = {t="npc",n="Raene Wolfrunner",z="ashenvale",s="In Astranaar, Raene Wolfrunner directs the Sentinels’ defense of Ashenvale. Her wolf and saber cat companions stay close as she faces Horde forces and corrupted furbolg tribes.",h="In Astranaar, Raene Wolfrunner directs the Sentinels’ defense of Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Defender of Astranaar",b="Raene Wolfrunner keeps watch in Astranaar with Korra, her saber cat, and Dagri, her wolf. A Sentinel officer, she oversees patrols across Ashenvale and coordinates intelligence from beyond the forest. She sends scouts such as Kaela Shadowspear into neighboring regions, including the Stonetalon Mountains.",sp=0},{t="Stemming the Forest's Corruption",b="Raene also works to counter the corruption sickening Ashenvale’s native denizens. She directs campaigns against hostile furbolg tribes, including strikes on Foulweald camps that harass travelers and efforts to remove rising Thistlefur leaders. Her scouts watch for changes in furbolg behavior. Under Raene’s command, they protect local settlements and passing travelers from coordinated ambushes.",sp=0},{t="Dartol's Rod",b="Raene’s personal cause is Dartol’s Rod, an ancient relic tied to furbolg purification. Her longtime friend Teronis was slain while seeking its missing gemstone. Raene ordered his body recovered and pledged to complete his research. With the dryad Shael'dryn, she helps champions assemble the relic. It lets an adventurer take furbolg guise and speak with chieftain Krolg, then defeat the tainted leader Ran Bloodtooth and purge the regional threat.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Raene Wolfrunner be found?",a="Raene Wolfrunner is in Astranaar, Ashenvale’s central night elf town. She stands outdoors with her two animal companions.",al={"raene wolfrunner location","where is raene","raene astranaar spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are the animals standing next to Raene?",a="Raene’s companions are Korra, a saber cat, and Dagri, a wolf. Both stay beside her in Astranaar.",al={"raene wolfrunner pets","raene wolf and cat","raene companions"}},{q="What is Raene's role within the Sentinels?",a="Raene is a ranking Sentinel officer in central Ashenvale. She issues orders to scouts, manages outposts, and coordinates operations against local threats.",al={"raene rank","is raene an officer","raene sentinel role"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Raene's friend Teronis?",a="Teronis was seeking a gemstone needed for Dartol’s Rod when he was slain in the field. Raene arranged to recover his remains and complete his mission.",al={"who is teronis","raene friend teronis","teronis death"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="Why is Raene focusing so heavily on the furbolgs?",a="Corrupted furbolg tribes such as the Foulweald and Thistlefur have grown more aggressive. They ambush travelers on forest roads and threaten Astranaar’s stability.",al={"raene furbolg quest","why fight thistlefur","foulweald ashenvale problem"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the purpose of Dartol's Rod in her questline?",a="Dartol’s Rod lets an adventurer take furbolg form and speak with Krolg. This opens the way to confront the corrupt chieftain Ran Bloodtooth.",al={"dartols rod purpose","what does dartols rod do","raenes cleansing rod"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Whose side is Raene Wolfrunner on?",a="Raene is a steadfast defender of the night elves and the Alliance. As an officer among the Sentinels, she coordinates patrols and defenses out of Astranaar, dedicated wholly to protecting her people and driving encroaching dangers from the ancient woods.",al={"raene wolfrunner faction","is raene alliance","who does raene fight for"},it="side",add="0f58d83b"},{q="What does Raene Wolfrunner want?",a="Raene wants to cleanse Ashenvale of corruption and secure Astranaar against surrounding threats. She is determined to finish the work of her fallen comrade Teronis, purge hostile furbolg tribes like the Foulweald and Thistlefur, and preserve the sanctity of the wilderness from defilement.",al={"raene wolfrunner goal","what is raene trying to do","raene wolfrunner purpose"},it="wants",add="c8e1b22c"},{q="Why is Raene Wolfrunner here in Ashenvale?",a="Raene is stationed at Astranaar, where she hopes to ease the corruption that has taken hold of the ancient forest. Deeply attuned to Ashenvale's welfare, she commands Sentinel scouts, repels corrupted furbolg attacks, and oversees regional efforts against rising threats in the wilderness.",al={"why is raene in astranaar","why did raene come to ashenvale","raene wolfrunner background"},it="why_here",add="eb1515b1"},{q="Who is Raene Wolfrunner tied to?",a="Raene commands local Sentinels and scouts, including Kaela Shadowspear and Selarin. She held a deep bond with the late Teronis and maintains friendly respect with the dryad Shael'dryn.",al={"raene wolfrunner allies","raene friends","who knows raene"},it="ties",add="86b9293d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers from Darkshore, Raene coordinates Ashenvale’s military and ecological defense.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Raene’s dedication to Elune and Kalimdor’s wilderness in her defense of Ashenvale’s woodland sanctuaries.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you may recognize Raene’s mastery of the wilderness and bond with beasts. She commands a wolf and a saber cat."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","dagri","dartol","korra","raene","sentinels","teronis","thistlefur","wolfrunner"},rel={"subzone:astranaar","quest:991","zone:ashenvale","npc:shael-dryn","npc:krolg","npc:kaela-shadowspear","quest:1025","quest:1054"},src={"Raene Wolfrunner"}}
E["npc:ruul-snowhoof"] = {t="npc",n="Ruul Snowhoof",z="ashenvale",s="Deep in northern Ashenvale, Ruul Snowhoof waits for rescue. The tauren druid is trapped in bear form inside a crude cage at Thistlefur Hold, relying on Horde adventurers to free him and guide him to safety.",h="Deep in northern Ashenvale, Ruul Snowhoof waits for rescue.",sec={{t="A Bear in a Cage",b="Ruul Snowhoof entered northern Ashenvale and fell into the hands of the corrupt Thistlefur furbolgs. He took the shape of a bear, and his captors mistook him for a wild beast. They locked him in a wooden cage deep within Thistlefur Hold instead of killing him. Now weakened and unable to safely leave his form or fight his way out alone, Ruul waits for Horde allies to open the cage, drive off his captors, and clear a path through the den. He hopes to return to his sister, Yama Snowhoof, at Splintertree Post.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Ruul Snowhoof a bear in a cage?",a="Ruul Snowhoof took Bear Form when the Thistlefur furbolgs confronted him. They mistook the tauren druid for a wild beast and locked him in a cage deep inside their hold.",al={"why is ruul a bear","ruul snowhoof bear form","why is he caged"},it="why_here"},{q="Why don't the furbolgs just kill Ruul?",a="The Thistlefur furbolgs keep Ruul captive in bear form and let him slowly starve in his cage. The reason they chose this over killing him is not known.",al={"why starving ruul","what do furbolgs want with ruul"}},{q="Where does Ruul go after escaping Thistlefur Hold?",a="After Ruul escapes Thistlefur Hold, he asks his rescuers to tell his sister, Yama Snowhoof, that he survived. She is at Splintertree Post.",al={"where does ruul go","ruul snowhoof destination"},it="next_step"},{q="Can Alliance players interact with Ruul Snowhoof?",a="No. Ruul Snowhoof is loyal to the Horde and offers help escaping only to Horde adventurers who find his cage.",al={"is ruul horde only","alliance ruul snowhoof"},gp=true},{q="Who is Ruul Snowhoof?",a="Ruul Snowhoof is a tauren druid trapped deep within Thistlefur Hold in Ashenvale. Captured by the hostile Thistlefur furbolgs while shifted into Bear Form, he has survived by concealing his true nature from his captors, who mistake him for an ordinary beast. Despite his grim predicament, he remains steadfast, relying on his training and inner strength until friendly travelers can break him out of his confinement.",al={"who is ruul","ruul snowhoof lore","who is the bear in thistlefur hold"},it="identity",add="6802c209"},{q="Whose side is Ruul Snowhoof on?",a="Ruul is loyal to the Horde, sharing the deep cultural and druidic ties of the tauren people. When trapped inside Thistlefur Hold, he places his trust entirely in Horde champions to open his cage and escort him past the furbolg patrols to freedom. Alliance adventurers will find he pays them no heed and offers them no audience.",al={"is ruul horde or alliance","ruul faction","ruul snowhoof allegiance"},it="side",add="f3e5b1ed"},{q="What does Ruul Snowhoof want?",a="Ruul wants nothing more than to escape his cage and survive the furbolgs' slow starvation. Once sprung from his prison, his immediate goal is to safely fight his way out of the den and return word of his survival to his kin, directing those who aid him to bring the good news to his family nearby.",al={"what does ruul want","ruul snowhoof goal","why help ruul"},it="wants",add="503a6073"},{q="Who is Ruul Snowhoof tied to?",a="Ruul is the brother of Yama Snowhoof, who is currently stationed at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. Upon reaching safety outside Thistlefur Hold, his foremost concern is relieving her dread by sending his rescuers to inform her that he has escaped their captors alive.",al={"ruul snowhoof family","ruul sister","who is ruul related to"},it="ties",add="ebe6887d"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, finding Ruul caged in bear form shows the taint spreading through Ashenvale's wildlife and furbolg tribes.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, rescuing Ruul Snowhoof brings a member of the Snowhoof family back alive to his sister Yama at Splintertree Post."},kw={"bear form","freedom to ruul","ruul snowhoof","splintertree post","thistlefur furbolgs","thistlefur hold","yama snowhoof"},rel={"quest:6482","subzone:thistlefur-hold","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","topic:druid","topic:furbolg","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Ruul Snowhoof"}}
E["npc:senani-thunderheart"] = {t="npc",n="Senani Thunderheart",z="ashenvale",s="At Splintertree Post in Ashenvale, Senani Thunderheart puts hunters to the test. She serves the Horde by sending travelers after the forest’s fiercest predators, a trial of skill that also thins the beasts near Horde territory.",h="At Splintertree Post in Ashenvale, Senani Thunderheart puts hunters to the test.",sec={{t="The Master of the Hunt",b="At Splintertree Post, Senani Thunderheart carries on the tauren hunting traditions in Ashenvale. Far from Mulgore’s open plains, she sends Horde hunters against the forest’s great beasts to test their tracking and fighting skill. For Senani, the hunt is an honorable challenge and a way to survive in a wild, contested land.",sp=0},{t="The Beasts of Ashenvale",b="Senani directs hunters toward three feared predators: the bear Ursangous, the cat Shadumbra, and the hippogryph Sharptalon. Their tokens are a paw, a head, and a claw. Claiming them marks a hunter’s passage and shows respect for the land and mastery of its fiercest beasts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Senani Thunderheart?",a="Senani Thunderheart is a tauren huntress at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. She serves the Horde by sending hunters after the forest’s most dangerous wildlife.",al={"who is senani","senani thunderheart lore","silverwind refuge questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Senani Thunderheart?",a="You can find Senani at Splintertree Post, the Horde outpost in Ashenvale directly north of the Barrens.",al={"senani location","where is senani","where is silverwind refuge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Ashenvale Hunt?",a="The Ashenvale Hunt is a series of challenges Senani gives hunters. They track and slay three famed predators: Ursangous the bear, Shadumbra the nightsaber, and Sharptalon the hippogryph.",al={"the ashenvale hunt","what does senani want","hunting quests ashenvale"},it="purpose"},{q="Which trophies does Senani require for the hunt?",a="Senani asks hunters to bring back Ursangous’s Paw, Shadumbra’s Head, and Sharptalon’s Claw as proof that they bested all three beasts.",al={"hunt trophies","ashenvale hunt items","what does senani need"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Does Senani have any connection to the furbolgs in the area?",a="Senani’s hunts do not concern the furbolgs. Her charge is the Ashenvale Hunt, while the Foulweald and other furbolg tribes are among the forest’s dangers.",al={"foulweald quest","king of the foulweald","senani furbolg"},it="conflict"},{q="Is Senani affiliated with the Cenarion Circle?",a="No. Senani serves the Horde and the tauren tribes, and meets the woods as a traditional hunter rather than as a druidic guardian of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"is senani a druid","senani cenarion circle"},it="side"},{q="Why is Senani Thunderheart here at Splintertree Post?",a="Senani Thunderheart makes her camp at Splintertree Post to oversee the great hunts across Ashenvale. As a tauren hunter, she tests the prowess of Horde champions against the ancient and elusive beasts roaming the deep forest, such as Ursangous, Shadumbra, and Sharptalon.",al={"why is senani thunderheart in ashenvale","senani thunderheart silverwind refuge purpose","why is senani here"},it="why_here",add="cd4c9488"},{q="What does Senani Thunderheart want from you?",a="Senani challenges hunters of the Horde to prove their tracking and combat mastery in the ancient woods. She asks you to track down and slay Ashenvale's most cunning predators, Ursangous, Shadumbra, and Sharptalon, and to bring back their prized trophies.",al={"what does senani want","senani thunderheart quests","what does senani ask for"},it="wants",add="13e7db62"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren traveler, meeting Senani recalls the Earth Mother’s trials and the ancient balance between hunter and quarry, far from Mulgore.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you face Senani’s test of tracking against Ashenvale’s elusive beasts: Ursangous, Shadumbra, and Sharptalon.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you’ll find Splintertree Post is your foothold in Ashenvale, where Senani helps scouts prove their worth and secure the wilderness."},kw={"ashenvale","ashenvale hunt","mystral lake","senani","shadumbra","sharptalon","thunderheart","ursangous"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","quest:235","quest:247","quest:23","quest:24","quest:2","quest:6621"},src={"Senani Thunderheart"}}
E["npc:sentinel-farsong"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Farsong",z="ashenvale",s="At Silverwing Grove, Sentinel Farsong helps defend Ashenvale’s southern border. She rallies champions against the Warsong Outriders in Warsong Gulch.",h="At Silverwing Grove, Sentinel Farsong helps defend Ashenvale’s southern border.",sec={{t="Guardian of Silverwing Grove",b="Sentinel Farsong keeps watch at Silverwing Grove as the Warsong clan cuts lumber and advances into night elf lands. She calls Alliance champions to strike at Warsong Outriders and sends field reports to Silverwing command. Her work helps check the Horde’s expansion and protect the woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Farsong?",a="Sentinel Farsong is a night elf sentinel with the Silverwing Sentinels in Ashenvale. She is stationed at Silverwing Grove near the entrance to Warsong Gulch, where she recruits Alliance adventurers and gathers battle intelligence.",al={"farsong","sentinel farsong lore","who is farsong"},it="identity"},{q="Where can she be found?",a="Sentinel Farsong can be found at Silverwing Grove in southeastern Ashenvale, where the Alliance stages its efforts in Warsong Gulch.",al={"sentinel farsong location","where is farsong","farsong ashenvale map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is she fighting the Warsong Outriders?",a="The Warsong Outriders are harvesting timber and defiling Ashenvale’s sacred forests. Sentinel Farsong helps defend the woods and recover territory claimed by the Horde.",al={"why fight warsong outriders","farsong motivation","ashenvale conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Farsong on?",a="Sentinel Farsong serves the Darnassus Sentinels and the Silverwing Sentinels, fighting on behalf of the Alliance. Stationed at the Silverwing Grove in Ashenvale, she stands steadfast against the Horde's incursions, rallying night elves and their allies to preserve their ancestral woodlands.",al={"farsong faction","who does farsong serve","sentinel farsong alliance"},it="side",add="e9cb1820"},{q="What does Sentinel Farsong want?",a="Sentinel Farsong seeks the complete removal of the Warsong Outriders and Horde invaders from Ashenvale. She organizes military reports from the front lines, gathers resources, and calls upon Alliance champions to vanquish the invading forces threatening the sacred forest.",al={"what does farsong need","farsong goal","sentinel farsong quests"},it="wants",add="a1fa54ea"},{q="Why is Sentinel Farsong here?",a="Sentinel Farsong is stationed at Silverwing Grove to oversee operations along the northern borders of Warsong Gulch. Ashenvale remains under constant siege by the Horde, and she acts as a pivotal liaison coordinating troops and reconnaissance against the encroaching lumber operations.",al={"why is farsong in ashenvale","farsong silverwing grove","why is sentinel farsong here"},it="why_here",add="ffcf1925"},{q="Who is Sentinel Farsong tied to?",a="Sentinel Farsong is bound to the Silverwing Sentinels and the broader night elf military under Darnassus. She operates alongside the Alliance defenders stationed in Silverwing Grove, maintaining direct communication with commanders orchestrating the defense against the Warsong Clan.",al={"farsong allies","sentinel farsong connections","who does farsong report to"},it="ties",add="31bb4497"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Sentinel Farsong directs Alliance volunteers in the fight against the Warsong Clan in Ashenvale.",["race:NightElf"]="As a protector of Elune’s sacred woods, Sentinel Farsong reflects the kaldorei’s resolve to drive out those who defile the ancient groves."},kw={"ashenvale","sentinel farsong","silverwing grove","silverwing sentinels","warsong gulch","warsong outriders"},rel={"subzone:silverwing-grove","npc:warsong-outrider","zone:ashenvale","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Sentinel Farsong"}}
E["npc:sentinel-onaeya"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Onaeya",z="ashenvale",s="At Maestra's Post, Sentinel Onaeya guards the northern edge of Ashenvale. The night elf guardian rallies Alliance adventurers to protect the forest and aid fellow sentinels.",h="At Maestra's Post, Sentinel Onaeya guards the northern edge of Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Guard on the Frontier",b="Maestra's Post is a wayside outpost on the road from Darkshore into Ashenvale. Sentinel Onaeya guards the lodge outside the settlement and coordinates its defense. Hostile wildlife, corrupting forces, and border tensions threaten night elf settlements in the region.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Post",b="Sentinel Onaeya hears that Sentinel Aynasha was attacked by furbolgs while carrying an important message through Darkshore. Onaeya rewards those who protect the poisoned sentinel until her antidote takes effect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Onaeya?",a="Sentinel Onaeya is a night elf guardian at Maestra's Post in northwestern Ashenvale. She directs travelers to help defend the outpost.",al={"onaeya","sentinel onaeya","who is onaeya"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Sentinel Onaeya located?",a="Sentinel Onaeya stands outside the main building at Maestra's Post, along the northern road in Ashenvale just below the border with Darkshore.",al={"onaeya location","where is sentinel onaeya","find onaeya"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What faction does Sentinel Onaeya belong to?",a="Sentinel Onaeya belongs to the Night Elf Sentinels and is loyal to the Alliance. Horde adventurers find her hostile on sight.",al={"onaeya faction","is onaeya alliance","onaeya friendly to horde"},it="side"},{q="How is Onaeya connected to Sentinel Aynasha?",a="Sentinel Aynasha sends adventurers to report to Onaeya at Maestra's Post after they protect her from attacking furbolgs. Onaeya rewards them and is glad Aynasha survived.",al={"onaeya aynasha","sentinel aynasha reward"}},{q="What kind of tasks does Sentinel Onaeya give?",a="Onaeya rewards adventurers who protect Sentinel Aynasha from furbolgs in Darkshore and bring word of her safety to Maestra's Post.",al={"onaeya quests","what quests does onaeya have"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Maestra's Post important to the Sentinels?",a="Maestra's Post is a checkpoint connecting Darkshore's supply routes to Ashenvale's heart. Holding it keeps hostile forces from cutting off night elf travelers moving south.",al={"why maestras post","maestras post importance"},it="place"},{q="Why is Sentinel Onaeya stationed at Maestra's Post?",a="Sentinel Onaeya stands watch just outside the main shelter of Maestra's Post in northwestern Ashenvale. As a night elf sentinel stationed along the frontier, she helps safeguard the outpost against surrounding threats and receives reports from travelers who help fellow sentinels such as Aynasha.",al={"why is onaeya here","sentinel onaeya location reason","why is onaeya at maestras post"},it="why_here",add="e1ad0868"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf traveling south from Darkshore, you find Onaeya on the front line defending Ashenvale woodland from outside threats.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can help Onaeya with defensive work as you leave the coastal wilds for Ashenvale's contested forests.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you face Onaeya, a sentinel guarding Maestra's Post and Ashenvale's northern approaches."},kw={"ashenvale","darkshore","maestra's post","night elf","onaeya","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","quest:5713"},src={"Sentinel Onaeya"}}
E["npc:sentinel-selarin"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Selarin",z="ashenvale",s="In Auberdine, Sentinel Selarin seeks help for Ashenvale's defenders. She carries Raene Wolfrunner's appeal to the coastal settlement as dangers threaten the forest.",h="In Auberdine, Sentinel Selarin seeks help for Ashenvale's defenders.",sec={{t="A Plea for Reinforcements",b="Sentinel Selarin carries Raene Wolfrunner's appeal from Ashenvale to Auberdine. With threats mounting across Ashenvale, the garrison is stretched thin. Selarin travels north along the forest road into Darkshore to find Terenthis and ask for help from the sentinels and scouts stationed on the coast.",sp=0},{t="Rallying the Wayfarers",b="Terenthis cannot answer Selarin's appeal in person, so she remains in Auberdine to enlist travelers passing through Darkshore. She sends capable adventurers south to Astranaar, where they can bring their blades and spells to Raene Wolfrunner's beleaguered forces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Selarin?",a="Sentinel Selarin is a night elf warrior of the Sentinels. She carries messages and seeks aid for Ashenvale's defenders in Auberdine, Darkshore.",al={"selarin lore","who is selarin","sentinel selarin"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Selarin come to Auberdine?",a="Raene Wolfrunner ordered Selarin to find Terenthis in Auberdine and seek reinforcements against the growing dangers in Ashenvale.",al={"why is selarin in darkshore","selarin mission","what is selarin doing"},it="why_here"},{q="Why didn't Terenthis go to Ashenvale with her?",a="Terenthis is occupied with local duties and cannot go to Ashenvale. Selarin recruits independent Alliance travelers to journey south in his place.",al={"why doesn't terenthis help","terenthis and selarin","terenthis busy"}},{q="Where does she send adventurers?",a="Selarin sends adventurers south across the border into Ashenvale, to report to Raene Wolfrunner at Astranaar.",al={"where does selarin send me","selarin quest destination","after selarin"},it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Selarin on?",a="Sentinel Selarin is a loyal soldier of the Night Elf Sentinels, serving the Alliance and answering directly to superiors within Ashenvale's defense forces, such as Raene Wolfrunner.",al={"selarin faction","is sentinel selarin alliance","who does selarin serve"},it="side",add="5ef6a9e4"},{q="What does Sentinel Selarin want?",a="Selarin seeks reinforcements for the escalating troubles across Ashenvale. She initially came to summon Terenthis, but recognizing his own crucial duties in Darkshore, she aims to rally capable adventurers to travel south and aid Raene Wolfrunner instead.",al={"selarin goal","what does selarin need","what is selarin trying to do"},it="wants",add="bee3573a"},{q="Who is Sentinel Selarin tied to?",a="Selarin serves under Raene Wolfrunner, who stationed in Ashenvale sent her on her mission. She is also closely acquainted with Terenthis in Auberdine, coordinating with him to secure aid and funnel promising recruits toward the front lines.",al={"who does selarin work for","selarin connections","selarin raene wolfrunner"},it="ties",add="8a8a2168"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you meet Selarin as she helps travelers journey south from Darkshore into Ashenvale's contested wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share the Sentinels' duty to guard the ancestral borders of the kaldorei."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","darkshore","raene wolfrunner","selarin","sentinel selarin","sentinels","terenthis"},rel={"npc:terenthis","npc:raene-wolfrunner","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","quest:990","topic:sentinels","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Selarin"}}
E["npc:sentinel-velene-starstrike"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Velene Starstrike",z="ashenvale",s="At Silverwind Refuge, Sentinel Velene Starstrike guards central Ashenvale. She protects the sanctuary and nearby waters from rogue elementals and foul sorcerers, keeping their magic from corrupting the ancient woodland.",h="At Silverwind Refuge, Sentinel Velene Starstrike guards central Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Guardian of Silverwind",b="At Mystral Lake, Sentinel Velene Starstrike keeps watch from Silverwind Refuge. Night elf sentinels across Ashenvale work to preserve the forest's balance and defend elven sanctuaries. Silverwind Refuge offers travelers a place to rest in the central woods, and Velene helps keep the area safe.",sp=0},{t="Disturbances at Mystral Lake",b="Peace around Silverwind Refuge can be easily disturbed. Velene watches Mystral Lake, where unruly elemental spirits and reckless mage summoners upset the wilderness. She directs champions against rogue water elementals and the careless spellcasters who disturb the spirits of the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Sentinel Velene Starstrike located?",a="Sentinel Velene Starstrike is stationed at Silverwind Refuge in central Ashenvale, near the southeastern shore of Mystral Lake.",al={"velene starstrike location","where is velene","silverwind refuge quest giver"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Sentinel Velene assign?",a="Velene sends adventurers to gather bracers from restless elementals and stop the rogue summoners stirring trouble in the waters around Mystral Lake.",al={"velene starstrike quests","what quests does velene give"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is the threat at Mystral Lake?",a="Aggressive water elementals trouble Mystral Lake, stirred up and exploited by mortal mage summoners who practice without regard for the forest's balance.",al={"mystral lake problem","why are elementals at mystral lake"},it="threat"},{q="Is Velene related to anyone else in Kalimdor?",a="Velene shares the Starstrike surname with Layo Starstrike, a night elf stationed far to the south in Silithus. They may belong to the same lineage or house.",al={"starstrike family","layo starstrike relative"},it="ties"},{q="What is Silverwind Refuge?",a="Silverwind Refuge is a night elf retreat on the shores of Mystral Lake in Ashenvale. It offers a haven and a tactical outpost for Sentinels and allied travelers crossing the forest's wild interior.",al={"what is silverwind refuge","silverwind refuge lore"}},{q="Why do the Sentinels care about elemental activity?",a="Night elves regard the wilderness as a sacred, living ecosystem. Violent or corrupted elementals disrupt wildlife and waterways, so the Sentinels intervene to restore balance.",al={"why do night elves fight elementals","sentinels and elementals"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Sentinel Velene Starstrike?",a="Sentinel Velene Starstrike is a night elf guardian of the Sentinels stationed at Silverwind Refuge in Ashenvale. Like her sisters-in-arms, she is dedicated to defending the sacred forests of Kalimdor from corruption and hostile intruders, watching vigilantly over nearby territories such as Mystral Lake.",al={"who is velene","velene starstrike lore","who is sentinel velene starstrike"},it="identity",add="8f53b9bb"},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Velene Starstrike on?",a="Sentinel Velene Starstrike is loyal to the Sentinels of the night elves and stands firmly with the Alliance. She offers aid, guidance, and missions to travelers serving the Alliance who wish to help safeguard Ashenvale.",al={"velene starstrike faction","sentinel velene alliance","velene starstrike allegiance"},it="side",add="2ad68975"},{q="Why is Sentinel Velene Starstrike here?",a="Velene is posted at Silverwind Refuge to monitor the wilderness and coordinate sentinel efforts in central Ashenvale. The area faces mounting dangers from aggressive wildlife, unruly elementals around Mystral Lake, and foreign incursions threatening the sanctity of the woodlands.",al={"why is velene at silverwind refuge","velene starstrike purpose","why is velene starstrike in ashenvale"},it="why_here",add="33a0de05"},{q="What does Sentinel Velene Starstrike want?",a="Velene seeks to restore harmony and security to the surrounding wilds. She recruits capable Alliance champions to investigate disturbing elemental unrest at Mystral Lake, counter magical threats, and push back any hostile forces encroaching on the refuge.",al={"what does velene want","velene starstrike goal","what is velene trying to do"},it="wants",add="9d94d468"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Velene's commitment to guarding Ashenvale from reckless magic and protecting the forest's balance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find safety at Silverwind Refuge along a dangerous road. Velene coordinates efforts to protect central Ashenvale.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may find Velene has little patience for reckless spellcasters whose conjurations stir local elementals and foul natural waters."},kw={"ashenvale","elemental bracers","mage summoner","mystral lake","sentinel","silverwind refuge","starstrike","velene"},rel={"subzone:silverwind-refuge","subzone:mystral-lake","zone:ashenvale","quest:1016","quest:1017","topic:night-elf","zone:silithus"},src={"Sentinel Velene Starstrike"}}
E["npc:shael-dryn"] = {t="npc",n="Shael'dryn",z="ashenvale",s="Beside the Moonwell of Purity, Shael'dryn watches corruption spread through Ashenvale. East of Iris Lake, she aids night elf scouts and Astranaar's sentinels with relics tainted by demonic and foul influences.",h="Beside the Moonwell of Purity, Shael'dryn watches corruption spread through Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Moonwell",b="Beside the Moonwell of Purity, Shael'dryn watches the forest's eastern approaches with the night elf sentinels. When corruption touches local wildlife or tainted relics threaten the land's harmony, she draws on her deep understanding of nature to guide adventurers in restoring spiritual balance.",sp=0},{t="Purification of the Woods",b="Shael'dryn works with Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar. When sentinels recover tainted artifacts, including corrupted glowing gems and lost pieces of Dartol's Rod, she knows the obscure rituals, moonwell waters, and natural tokens needed to purify them. The artifacts become potent cleansing tools for the Alliance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Shael'dryn?",a="Shael'dryn is a dryad beside the Moonwell of Purity in Ashenvale. She shares woodland lore and natural magic with Alliance adventurers, along with puns and jokes.",al={"who is she","shael dryn lore","shaeldryn identity"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Shael'dryn?",a="Shael'dryn waits beside the Moonwell of Purity, east of Iris Lake in Ashenvale.",al={"shaeldryn location","where is shael'dryn","raynewood dryad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Shael'dryn's connection to Raene Wolfrunner?",a="Raene Wolfrunner directs adventurers to Shael'dryn for her spiritual knowledge. She helps investigate and cleanse corrupted gems and relics recovered throughout the forest.",al={"raene and shaeldryn","raenes cleansing dryad","why send me to shaeldryn"},it="ties"},{q="What is unique about Shael'dryn's appearance?",a="Shael'dryn and her fellow dryad Illiyana share an uncommon coloration that sets them apart from most other dryads encountered across Kalimdor.",al={"dryad model","unique skin","shaeldryn color"},gp=true},{q="Is Shael'dryn friendly to the Horde?",a="No. Shael'dryn stands beside the Moonwell of Purity and is closely allied with the Astranaar Sentinels. She is hostile toward members of the Horde.",al={"can horde talk to shaeldryn","horde rep","is shaeldryn alliance only"},it="side"},{q="What does Shael'dryn want?",a="Shael'dryn is working to help protect and cleanse the surrounding woods of Ashenvale. She assists allies like Raene Wolfrunner by directing travelers to investigate threats, gather ancient forest relics, and restore balance to corrupted lands.",al={"shael'dryn goal","what is shael'dryn doing","shael dryn purpose"},it="wants",add="70f31310"},{q="Why is Shael'dryn at the Moonwell of Purity?",a="As a daughter of Cenarius, Shael'dryn keeps watch over eastern Ashenvale from the Moonwell of Purity east of Iris Lake. From this moonwell, she monitors the encroaching corruptions of the forest and aids the night elves defending their sacred groves.",al={"why is shael dryn here","why is shael'dryn in ashenvale","shael'dryn raynewood"},it="why_here",add="3c3b07cb"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei, you can welcome Shael'dryn as a sister of the forest. Her natural ties to Cenarius make her indispensable when cleansing tainted woodland relics.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can value Shael'dryn's natural connection to the spirits of Kalimdor and her insight into restoring flora and fauna warped by dark powers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to the Moonwell of Purity as a sanctuary in Ashenvale. Shael'dryn aids Alliance forces resisting corruption and hostile encroachment."},kw={"ashenvale","cenarius","cleansing","dryad","illiyana","raene","raynewood","shael'dryn","shaeldryn"},rel={"npc:illiyana","quest:991","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Shael'dryn"}}
E["npc:shindrell-swiftfire"] = {t="npc",n="Shindrell Swiftfire",z="ashenvale",s="Astranaar’s defense reaches beyond Ashenvale’s forest. Shindrell Swiftfire, a night elf sentinel and scout, watches from the town at the heart of night elf operations in Ashenvale. Alert to changing dangers along Kalimdor’s western reaches, she directs capable Alliance adventurers toward threats on the coast and nearby mountain passes, helping coordinate local defense against dangers from sea and wilds.",h="Astranaar’s defense reaches beyond Ashenvale’s forest.",sec={{t="A Watchful Eye in Astranaar",b="From Astranaar’s winding walkways, Shindrell Swiftfire watches the frontiers beyond Ashenvale. Sentinels face Horde logging incursions from the east and south, while Shindrell keeps watch beyond the woodland itself. Travelers arrive from Darkshore or set out toward Stonetalon’s jagged ridges, and she helps ensure Astranaar is not left undefended against danger from the flank.",sp=0},{t="The Menace on the Coast",b="On Ashenvale’s northwestern shore, the troubled Zoram Strand draws Shindrell’s attention. Hostile naga have emerged from the ocean depths, a grave mystery and a direct threat to Kaldorei settlements. Shindrell sends seasoned fighters to investigate the shoreline and coordinate with scouts near the coast, seeking to contain the serpentine invaders before they gain a lasting foothold on ancient night elf lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Shindrell Swiftfire?",a="Shindrell Swiftfire is stationed in Astranaar, the central night elf town in Ashenvale. Among its wooden walkways, she coordinates scouting and receives travelers.",al={"shindrell swiftfire location","where is shindrell","find shindrell swiftfire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Shindrell's role in Astranaar?",a="In Astranaar, Shindrell coordinates scouts and gives Alliance adventurers directions toward threats beyond the town. These include naga on the western coast and wild beasts in nearby mountain ranges.",al={"what does shindrell do","who is shindrell swiftfire","shindrell purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does she send scouts to the Zoram Strand?",a="Hostile naga have surged onto Ashenvale’s western shores, claiming ruins and threatening night elf borders. Shindrell sends adventurers to scout the beaches and help field sentinels curb the serpentine threat.",al={"why zoram strand","shindrell naga quest","the zoram strand mission"},it="motive"},{q="What connects Shindrell to Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Hidden sources in Theramore report that orc assassins gather venom from pridewings near Mirkfallon Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains for secret raids against the Alliance. Shindrell sends adventurers to collect the venom sacs and deny the Horde that poison.",al={"stonetalon quests","pridewings quest","why stonetalon"}},{q="Does Shindrell have ties to Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Shindrell has no direct ties to Blackfathom Deeps. She sends adventurers against the Wrathtail naga on the Zoram Strand, the northwestern coast where the Deeps lies, but sends no one into the Deeps itself.",al={"shindrell blackfathom","blackfathom deeps connection","shindrell bfd"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Kayneth Stillwind, and why does Shindrell mention him?",a="Kayneth Stillwind is a druid at the shrine of Forest Song in eastern Ashenvale. Fearing corruption is moving through the forest, he asked Shindrell for a report on the coast and Astranaar; she sends adventurers to carry it to him.",al={"who is kayneth","kayneth stillwind quest","kayneth connection"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Shindrell Swiftfire?",a="Shindrell Swiftfire is a night elf stationed in Astranaar, serving as a vigilant coordinator for the defense of Ashenvale. Operating at the heart of the settlement, she tracks rising threats across the forest borders and marshals Alliance adventurers to confront encroachments from hostile creatures, dark cults, and invading forces threatening night elf lands.",al={"who is shindrell","shindrell swiftfire lore","who is shindrell swiftfire"},it="identity",add="2412c5d9"},{q="Whose side is Shindrell Swiftfire on?",a="Shindrell stands firmly with the night elves of the Sentinels and the Alliance. Stationed within the sanctuary of Astranaar, her sole loyalty is to the defense of Kalimdor's sacred woods and the safety of her kin.",al={"shindrell faction","is shindrell alliance","what faction is shindrell swiftfire"},it="side",add="1fb1d96b"},{q="What does Shindrell Swiftfire want?",a="Shindrell seeks to secure Ashenvale and its surrounding territories from mounting perils. She sends travelers to drive the naga back from the Zoram Strand, deny the orcs the pridewing venom of the Stonetalon Mountains, and carry her reports to the druid Kayneth Stillwind at Forest Song.",al={"what does shindrell want","shindrell swiftfire goal","shindrell motivation"},it="wants",add="00b2b10b"},{q="Why is Shindrell Swiftfire here?",a="Astranaar is the primary hub of defense for the night elves in Ashenvale. Shindrell remains here to organize scouting efforts, gather reports from distant outposts, and recruit capable travelers passing along the central roadway to help protect the borders of the forest.",al={"why is shindrell in astranaar","why is shindrell swiftfire here","shindrell purpose in astranaar"},it="why_here",add="4632c876"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Shindrell as one of the vigilant Sentinels guarding Ashenvale’s fringes against ancient foes like the naga, while most of their forces face the Horde.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance arrival in Astranaar, you can look to Shindrell as an operational bridge guiding you deeper into central Kalimdor’s contentious and dangerous terrain.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you may recognize the value of tracking pridewings and assessing untamed coastlines, work suited to scouts and rangers who know how to survive in the wild."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","naga","pridewings","sentinel","shindrell","stonetalon","swiftfire","zoram strand"},rel={"subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","subzone:zoram-strand","quest:1008","quest:1134","quest:4581","topic:naga","topic:night-elf"},src={"Shindrell Swiftfire"}}
E["npc:talen"] = {t="npc",n="Talen",z="ashenvale",s="At his camp by the Zoram Strand, Talen searches for kaldorei relics along the coast. Nearby naga and Horde outposts make the work dangerous.",h="At his camp by the Zoram Strand, Talen searches for kaldorei relics along the coast.",sec={{t="Scholar on the Coast",b="At a camp beside the Zoram Strand, Talen studies the past instead of taking up arms. Naga and Horde outposts make the coast dangerous, but he keeps searching the ruins beneath the waves and sands for lost kaldorei relics. He depends on travelers to face the Wrathtail naga and recover artifacts, including pristine statuettes and the Ring of Zoram, held by their leader Ruuzel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Talen?",a="At his camp near the Zoram Strand, Talen studies ancient kaldorei relics buried along the shore. He is a night elf scholar and amateur archaeologist, not a sentinel or soldier.",al={"who is this night elf","talen ashenvale","talen zoram strand"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Talen camping near the Zoram Strand?",a="Talen camps near the Zoram Strand to investigate its sunken ruins and recover ancient kaldorei artifacts. Violent naga roam the beach, and the Horde outpost of Zoram'gar lies nearby, so he stays in a small camp away from the main shoreline.",al={"why is talen here","talen purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="What artifacts does Talen want?",a="Talen asks travelers to search the coast for ancient statuettes washed ashore and to hunt Ruuzel, a powerful naga on a nearby offshore isle. Ruuzel holds the Ring of Zoram, which unlocks the statuette.",al={"talen quests","what does talen need","ruuzel quest"},it="wants"},{q="Is Talen hostile to the Horde?",a="Talen is allied with the night elves, but he is a scholar. He does not attack Horde travelers unless they provoke or attack him first.",al={"does talen attack horde","horde friendly talen"},it="hostile"},{q="Whose side is Talen on?",a="Talen is aligned with the Alliance, as a night elf camped within Ashenvale. While he primarily focuses on scholarly archaeology rather than military campaigns, his loyalties lie with his kin and their allies. Horde travelers will find he defends himself if threatened, but his true concern remains the relics buried in the surrounding sands rather than open warfare.",al={"talen faction","is talen alliance","talen allegiance"},it="side",add="76deb443"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the Zoram Strand recalls the Sundering. Talen seeks to preserve and recover the heritage lost when ancient coastal estates sank into the Great Sea.",["faction:Alliance"]="Talen gives Alliance travelers a field contact in contested northern Ashenvale, near Maestra's Post."},kw={"ancient statuette","archaeologist","ashenvale","ruuzel","talen","zoram strand"},rel={"subzone:zoram-strand","quest:1007","quest:1009","zone:ashenvale","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","subzone:maestra-s-post","topic:night-elf"},src={"Talen"}}
E["npc:teronis-corpse"] = {t="npc",n="Teronis' Corpse",z="ashenvale",s="On an island in western Ashenvale, Teronis' Corpse lies in Lake Falathim. The night elf scout left Astranaar to find Dartol's Rod and help cleanse the forest.",h="On an island in western Ashenvale, Teronis' Corpse lies in Lake Falathim.",sec={{t="A Scout's Grim Fate",b="Teronis was sent from Astranaar to recover Dartol's Rod. Raene Wolfrunner gave the night elf scout this charge, seeking an ancient relic that could cleanse corrupted woodland magic. Teronis searched the waters of Lake Falathim, but hostile murlocs swarmed the island and killed him. His journal remains there, while the murlocs took the rod's radiant gemstone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Teronis?",a="Teronis was a night elf scout sent from Astranaar by Sentinel Raene Wolfrunner. He sought Dartol's Rod, an old artifact meant to cleanse demonic corruption in Ashenvale's soil and waters.",al={"who is teronis","teronis lore","identity of teronis"},it="identity"},{q="How did Teronis die?",a="Aggressive murlocs ambushed and killed Teronis as he tried to secure the rod's components in Lake Falathim.",al={"who killed teronis","teronis cause of death","how did he die"},it="history"},{q="Where is his lost gemstone?",a="Local murlocs around Lake Falathim scavenged the glowing gemstone that crowned Dartol's Rod after Teronis was killed.",al={"where is the gem","lost gem","teronis gem"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is recovering his mission so important to Astranaar?",a="Ashenvale's wildlife and woodland pools suffer from demonic and fel taint. The Sentinels hope Dartol's Rod can cleanse the land or hold back the spreading rot.",al={"why help raene","dartol rod purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side was Teronis on?",a="Teronis served the night elves of Ashenvale and the Alliance. Sent from Astranaar by Raene Wolfrunner, his loyalties were devoted to the defense and cleansing of his people's sacred woodland.",al={"teronis faction","teronis corpse side","is teronis alliance"},it="side",add="6a989bf2"},{q="What did Teronis want before his death?",a="Teronis sought the lost pieces of Dartol's Rod, specifically seeking out a gemstone hidden within Lake Falathim. He hoped its magic could aid his kin in purging the dark corruption spreading across Ashenvale.",al={"teronis mission","teronis goals","what was teronis doing"},it="wants",add="7cdf0db0"},{q="Why is Teronis' corpse located at Lake Falathim?",a="His search for Dartol's Rod brought him to the island in Lake Falathim, where he believed a vital gemstone rested. Surrounded by the hostile murlocs inhabiting the waters, he was overwhelmed and slain before he could return to Astranaar.",al={"why is teronis here","why is his body at the lake","teronis lake falathim"},it="why_here",add="7065b032"},{q="Who is Teronis tied to?",a="Teronis answered directly to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar. It was Raene who dispatched him to Lake Falathim to recover Dartol's Rod, and it is her lingering concern that directs travelers to find his remains.",al={"who sent teronis","teronis raene wolfrunner","who does teronis work for"},it="ties",add="2ab2ec0c"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Finding Teronis fallen in the wilds shows how dangerous Ashenvale has become, even for seasoned Sentinels and scouts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Honoring Astranaar's fallen scouts means carrying on their unfinished work to cleanse the land of corruption."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","dartol's rod","lake falathim","murloc","raene wolfrunner","teronis","teronis' corpse"},rel={"quest:991","subzone:lake-falathim","zone:ashenvale","topic:murloc","topic:night-elf"},src={"Teronis' Corpse"}}
E["npc:therylune"] = {t="npc",n="Therylune",z="ashenvale",s="At the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, Therylune waits for a chance to escape her captors. Twilight's Hammer cultists have trapped the dryad at the ancient site, and she needs a traveler's help to reach safety.",h="At the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, Therylune waits for a chance to escape her captors.",sec={{t="Captive of the Cult",b="Therylune is a dryad, a daughter of Cenarius who guards nature. She came from the tranquil woodlands of northern Kalimdor to the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore. Twilight's Hammer cultists have gathered at the ancient excavation and ambushed her. Surrounded by their swarms, she cannot fight her way free alone. She needs an escort through the cultists and out to safety.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Therylune?",a="Therylune is a dryad, one of the woodland daughters of the demigod Cenarius. Twilight's Hammer cultists have captured her at the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore.",al={"who is therylune","therylune lore","what is therylune"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Therylune trapped at the Master's Glaive?",a="Therylune was ambushed and pinned down by Twilight's Hammer cultists. They have established a dark camp around the giant petrified remains at the Master's Glaive.",al={"why is she captured","how did therylune get caught","masters glaive cultists"},it="why_here"},{q="Does Therylune have any family?",a="Yes. Therylune is the sister of Therysil, another dryad who dwells in the woodlands of northern Kalimdor.",al={"therylune sister","therysil therylune","therylune family"},it="ties"},{q="What happens once you help her escape?",a="Once you clear a path through the hostile cultists, Therylune flees the Master's Glaive and returns to the safety of the surrounding wilds.",al={"therylunes escape","quest 945","what does therylune do"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Therylune on?",a="Therylune is an ally to the night elves and the forces of nature. As a dryad and daughter of Cenarius, she stands firmly against dark forces like the Twilight's Hammer cultists who have captured her, gladly welcoming the aid of friendly travelers to win her freedom.",al={"therylune faction","is therylune alliance","therylune friendly"},it="side",add="f442f40d"},{q="What does Therylune want?",a="Therylune wants nothing more than to break free from the clutches of the Twilight's Hammer cultists holding her captive. She needs a capable protector to escort her safely away from the corrupted grounds of the Master's Glaive so she can rejoin her kin.",al={"what does therylune need","therylune goal"},it="wants",add="7872ea33"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share a kinship with Cenarius and his kin. You feel an urgent duty to rescue a dryad captured by malevolent cultists.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share ancient, sacred ties with the daughters of Cenarius. Therylune's captivity at Twilight's Hammer's hands is an affront to Kalimdor's balance."},kw={"cenarius","darkshore","dryad","escort","master's glaive","therylune","therysil","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:945","subzone:master-s-glaive","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer","npc:therysil","quest:944"},src={"Therylune"}}
E["npc:therysil"] = {t="npc",n="Therysil",z="ashenvale",s="At the Shrine of Aessina in central Ashenvale, Therysil waits for word of her sister. The dryad is devoted to protecting nature, but Therylune has been taken by the Twilight's Hammer cultists.",h="At the Shrine of Aessina in central Ashenvale, Therysil waits for word of her sister.",sec={{t="A Guardian's Vigil",b="Therysil keeps watch near the waters of the Shrine of Aessina in Ashenvale's ancient woods. As a dryad and daughter of Cenarius, she is bound to defend the wild and its spirits. Her thoughts now turn to Therylune, captured nearby by the deranged Twilight's Hammer cult. Therysil waits anxiously for a wandering ally who can help rescue her sister.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Therysil?",a="Therysil is a dryad who dwells at the Shrine of Aessina in Ashenvale. She is a daughter of Cenarius and Therylune's sister.",al={"who is therysil","therysil lore","dryad at aessina"},it="identity"},{q="What is Therysil's concern?",a="Therysil fears for her sister, Therylune, whom Twilight's Hammer cultists ambushed and captured at the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore. She waits at the shrine, hoping someone can guide Therylune safely home.",al={"what is therysil doing","why is therysil worried","therysil quest"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Therylune?",a="Therylune is Therysil's sister and a dryad of Ashenvale. The Twilight's Hammer captured her, and she needs an escort to escape and reunite with Therysil.",al={"therylune","therysil sister","who is therylune"},it="ties"},{q="Where can Therysil be found?",a="Find Therysil at the Shrine of Aessina, a sacred natural haven along the roadway in central Ashenvale.",al={"therysil location","where is therysil","shrine of aessina dryad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Therysil on?",a="Therysil is a daughter of Cenarius and dwells under the protection of the night elves and the wilderness spirits. Like most dryads, she stands with the natural order of Ashenvale and the Alliance, fiercely opposing dark intruders such as the Twilight's Hammer cultists who defile the ancient woods.",al={"therysil faction","is therysil alliance","who does therysil serve"},it="side",add="f765b898"},{q="Why is Therysil here at the Shrine of Aessina?",a="Therysil maintains a vigil at the Shrine of Aessina, an ancient sacred hollow dedicated to the forest spirit. Beyond tending to the shrine, she waits anxiously for word of her sister, Therylune, who wandered toward the Master's Glaive and fell into the hands of the sinister cultists lurking there.",al={"why is therysil here","why is therysil at shrine of aessina","therysil purpose here"},it="why_here",add="fc91e3f7"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a daughter of Cenarius, Therysil reflects the close bond between the Cenarion Circle and Ashenvale's natural spirits. Her plight is especially urgent for visiting druids.",["race:NightElf"]="Dryads have long stood with the kaldorei to safeguard Ashenvale's sacred groves, including the Shrine of Aessina."},kw={"ashenvale","cenarius","dryad","shrine of aessina","therylune","therysil","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:therylune","quest:945","subzone:shrine-of-aessina","zone:ashenvale","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Therysil"}}
E["npc:thyn-tel-bladeweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver",z="ashenvale",s="At Darnassus's Warrior's Terrace, Thyn'tel Bladeweaver searches for the vanished Priestess Velinde Starsong. She sends trusted Alliance adventurers after clues to Velinde's whereabouts and the mystery of the Scythe of Elune.",h="At Darnassus's Warrior's Terrace, Thyn'tel Bladeweaver searches for the vanished Priestess Velinde Starsong.",sec={{t="A Sentinel's Inquest",b="On the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus, Thyn'tel Bladeweaver keeps watch as a night elf sentinel. Priestess Velinde Starsong vanished without a word, and Thyn'tel refuses to let her trail go cold. Believing grave forces may be involved, she sends trusted adventurers to search Velinde's belongings and learn where her journey led.",sp=0},{t="Tracing Velinde's Steps",b="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver sends investigators to examine the effects Velinde left in Darnassus. Among the clues is a journal describing Velinde's communion with Elune and the terrifying worgen beasts summoned through the Scythe of Elune. The trail leads south through the port of Ratchet and into the Barrens, where travelers seek the place from which the desperate priestess sailed before vanishing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thyn'tel Bladeweaver?",a="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver is a night elf sentinel on the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus. She begins an inquiry into the disappearance of Priestess Velinde Starsong.",al={"thyntel bladeweaver","who is thyntel","thyn'tel info"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Thyn'tel Bladeweaver?",a="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver keeps watch on the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus, among the kaldorei warriors and sentinels.",al={"thyn'tel location","where is thyn'tel bladeweaver","thyntel map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Thyn'tel Bladeweaver offer?",a="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver guides an inquiry into Velinde Starsong's disappearance, beginning with Velinde's Effects and continuing through The Barrens Port to Answered Questions.",al={"thyntel quests","what quest does she give"},gp=true},{q="Why is she interested in Velinde Starsong?",a="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver seeks to learn what happened to Velinde Starsong, a priestess who served in Ashenvale before vanishing abruptly and leaving her work unfinished.",al={"why investigate velinde","what happened to velinde"},it="motive"},{q="Where does her quest chain lead?",a="The trail leads from Velinde's effects in Darnassus south to Ratchet in the Barrens, where investigators search for records of her voyage.",al={"velinde quest path","where does the quest go"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is Thyn'tel Bladeweaver an Alliance-only contact?",a="Yes. Thyn'tel Bladeweaver is stationed in Darnassus and offers her help to members of the Alliance.",al={"can horde talk to thyntel","is she alliance"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Thyn'tel Bladeweaver on?",a="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the broader Alliance. Stationed among her kin, she dedicates her service to the defense and security of Kalimdor's sentinel holdings, assisting those loyal to the Alliance who seek answers regarding lost comrades.",al={"thyntel bladeweaver faction","is thyntel alliance"},it="side",add="294bf631"},{q="What does Thyn'tel Bladeweaver want?",a="Thyn'tel seeks the truth behind the disappearance of the night elf sentinel Velinde Starsong. She charges dependable adventurers with uncovering Velinde's final steps, recovering her personal effects, and following the enigmatic trail left behind across the barrens and beyond.",al={"what does thyntel want","thyntel goal"},it="wants",add="187a5321"},{q="Why is Thyn'tel Bladeweaver here?",a="Thyn'tel remains stationed to coordinate inquiries and support the needs of night elf forces. From her vantage, she acts as a liaison for investigations that venture far outside elven boundaries, directing trusted scouts toward distant lands to resolve unresolved mysteries threatening her people.",al={"why is thyntel here","thyntel bladeweaver purpose"},it="why_here",add="7964d285"},{q="Who is Thyn'tel Bladeweaver tied to?",a="Thyn'tel is connected closely to the missing sentinel Velinde Starsong, whose disappearance she actively investigates. Her tasks link her directly to the fate of Velinde's expedition, sending messengers across Kalimdor to unravel what became of the sentinel and the powerful relics she carried.",al={"thyntel bladeweaver connections","thyntel velinde starsong"},it="ties",add="48b9097d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Thyn'tel's inquiry reaches into their own people, as a revered priestess has vanished amid forces beyond her control.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes who visit the Warrior's Terrace receive Thyn'tel's trust and travel into neutral and contested territory to seek the truth.",["class:Warrior"]="Alliance warriors passing through Darnassus find Thyn'tel among the trainers on the Warrior's Terrace, a familiar sentinel face."},kw={"bladeweaver","darnassus","scythe of elune","sentinel","starsong","thyn'tel","velinde","warrior's terrace"},rel={"quest:1037","quest:1038","quest:1039","quest:1044","subzone:warrior-s-terrace","zone:darnassus","zone:barrens","topic:night-elf"},src={"Thyn'tel Bladeweaver"}}
E["npc:warsong-outrider"] = {t="npc",n="Warsong Outrider",z="ashenvale",s="On the road east from Ashenvale, the Warsong Outrider watches the Horde's frontier. She scouts for the Warsong clan, watches travelers, and sends intelligence to its forward encampments. She keeps watch unless someone provokes her.",h="On the road east from Ashenvale, the Warsong Outrider watches the Horde's frontier.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Eastern Frontier",b="The Warsong Outrider watches the road between Ashenvale and Azshara's shattered ruins. Far from Splintertree Post and the lumber camps, she tracks troop movements along the route. Her bow and toxic stingers are ready, but she fires only at Alliance trespassers who attack her.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can the Warsong Outrider be found?",a="She watches the main road in eastern Ashenvale, which leads into Azshara.",al={"outrider location","where is warsong outrider","warsong outrider map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Will the Warsong Outrider attack Alliance players on sight?",a="No. She does not attack passing Alliance travelers unless they strike her first.",al={"is she aggressive","does warsong outrider attack alliance","warsong outrider aggro"},it="hostile",gp=true},{q="What is her role in the Warsong clan's operations?",a="She scouts the Ashenvale and Azshara border, watches for threats, and sends field reports through scouts to the Warsong clan's leaders.",al={"what does outrider do","warsong outrider purpose","why is she here"},it="purpose"},{q="Does defeating the Warsong Outrider yield any treasure?",a="No. Defeating her yields no loot or specialized equipment. It only clears the road or disrupts Horde reconnaissance.",al={"warsong outrider loot","does she drop loot","outrider drops"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is the Warsong Outrider?",a="She is an orc scout belonging to the Warsong clan, stationed on the far eastern frontier of Ashenvale. Armed with a ranged bow and lethal stings, outriders like her keep watchful eyes on the borders connecting the contested forests with the rocky lands beyond.",al={"who is warsong outrider","warsong outrider identity","what is the warsong outrider"},it="identity",add="472f02e2"},{q="Whose side is the Warsong Outrider on?",a="She is pledged directly to the Warsong clan and loyal to the Horde. While she bears Horde allegiance, she maintains a defensive vigil on the road rather than actively hunting down passing travelers unless provoked.",al={"warsong outrider faction","is warsong outrider horde","warsong outrider side"},it="side",add="adb29283"},{q="Why is the Warsong Outrider stationed here?",a="She watches over the vital thoroughfare connecting eastern Ashenvale to Azshara. Her post ensures that Horde messengers, lumber convoys, and travelers can report changes along the border, providing essential intelligence updates on regional movements.",al={"why is warsong outrider here","warsong outrider location purpose","why is she on the road"},it="why_here",add="0609b6c9"},{q="Who is the Warsong Outrider tied to?",a="She serves the Warsong clan, operating in coordination with their extensive logging and military campaign across Ashenvale. Her reports keep the clan's outposts informed of happenings along the outer edges of the territory.",al={"warsong outrider ties","who does warsong outrider work for","warsong outrider clan"},it="ties",add="38bf0594"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Outriders like her keep supply and scouting routes open between Ashenvale's contested logging operations and Azshara's wild coasts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though she serves the Horde, this scout holds her fire against Alliance travelers unless provoked, letting wary travelers pass unharmed."},kw={"ashenvale","azshara","horde scout","outrider update","warsong clan","warsong outrider"},rel={"quest:6546","zone:ashenvale","zone:azshara","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Warsong Outrider"}}
E["quest:1007"] = {t="quest",n="The Ancient Statuette",z="ashenvale",s="Near Zoram Strand, The Ancient Statuette lies lost after a naga attack. Talen, an elf camped on the northwestern coast of Ashenvale, needs you to recover the relic he dropped in the surf.",h="Near Zoram Strand, The Ancient Statuette lies lost after a naga attack.",sec={{t="Ambush on the Coast",b="Naga attacked Talen as he steered a small vessel through the shallows by Zoram's sunken ruins on Ashenvale's northwestern shore. He scrambled ashore with only bare provisions and made a hasty camp. In his desperate flight, he dropped the ancient statuette he had found among the ruins into the sands.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of Old Zoram",b="Talen braved the naga-infested Zoram Strand for the ancient statuette. Once you return it, he explains that the drowned city holds centuries of forgotten mysteries. He believes the delicate carving is a key to understanding what remains hidden beneath the tides.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Talen and why is he alone on the Strand?",a="Talen is an elf explorer camped along the southern edge of Zoram Strand. His curiosity about history brought him to explore Zoram's drowned ruins, but naga ambushed his vessel and cast him ashore.",al={"who is talen","talen lore","talen ashenvale"},it="identity"},{q="Where did Talen lose the statuette?",a="Talen lost the statuette near the shoreline north of his camp. It lies half-buried in the sand near an overturned boat and a fallen tree, along the surf where his vessel was attacked.",al={"where is ancient statuette","statuette location","find ancient statuette"},gp=true},{q="What is the ancient statuette?",a="The ancient statuette is a night elven relic recovered from Zoram's submerged ruins. Talen says it has historical and mystical significance and is a key to the drowned city's lingering secrets.",al={"what is the statuette","significance of statuette"},it="item"},{q="Why are there naga at the Zoram Strand?",a="Naga have claimed Zoram's drowned ruins as their territory. They patrol Ashenvale's western beaches against outsiders, around elven ruins that sank beneath the sea ten thousand years ago, before the Sundering.",al={"why naga here","zoram strand naga","naga in ashenvale"},it="hostile"},{q="What happens after returning the statuette?",a="Returning the statuette lets Talen decipher more of the region's mysteries. The naga threat remains, and you are directed toward their leader, Ruuzel.",al={"what next after statuette","quest follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is the statuette guarded?",a="The statuette lies by the water's edge in territory crawling with hostile naga warriors and shore-stalking beasts. Retrieving it is perilous for a lone wanderer.",al={"is statuette guarded","enemies near statuette"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Why does Talen want the Ancient Statuette retrieved?",a="The ancient statuette is Talen's prized possession and the entire reason he dared to venture into the perilous Zoram Strand. He believes the submerged ruins of ancient Zoram hold deep secrets, and that this relic may be the key to unlocking them. Having fled with his life after being ambushed by naga, he cannot bear to leave his life's pursuit behind in the sand.",al={"why does talen want the statuette","talen motive","why does talen need the statuette"},it="motive",add="16a428a2"},{q="Why can't Talen retrieve the statuette himself?",a="Talen barely survived his initial encounter on the water. When the naga swarmed from the depths and shredded his small vessel with their claws, he scrambled ashore carrying only meager supplies before fleeing in terror. Shaken, wounded, and lacking any martial backup on this remote coast, he is in no condition to face the lurking shoreline beasts and aggressive naga to retrieve what he dropped.",al={"why cant talen get it himself","why does talen need me","why talen needs help"},it="why_me",add="ceee75b8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you can see the ruins of Zoram as remnants of Kaldorei civilization from before the Great Sundering. Preserving artifacts like the statuette keeps ancestral memory alive.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler in Ashenvale, you face threats from Horde outposts in the east and hostile naga claiming the western coast."},kw={"ancient statuette","ashenvale","naga","ruins of zoram","ruuzel","talen","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:talen","quest:1009","subzone:zoram-strand","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale","quest:1008"},m={start="Talen",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1007,ri={"Ancient Statuette"}},src={"The Ancient Statuette"}}
E["quest:1008"] = {t="quest",n="The Zoram Strand",z="ashenvale",s="Naga now threaten Ashenvale from the Zoram Strand. Shindrell Swiftfire of Astranaar sends Alliance champions to scour the northwestern coast, where an ancient ruined city lies. Stopping the naga protects the forest from a haunting echo of the night elves’ distant past.",h="Naga now threaten Ashenvale from the Zoram Strand.",sec={{t="Shadows on the Shore",b="At Ashenvale’s northwestern edge, the Zoram Strand meets the Veiled Sea. Its shore lies northwest of Astranaar, where the forest canopy gives way to the coast. The beach was quiet for ages, its stones left from a civilization shattered ten millennia ago. Now Wrathtail naga have come out of the dark tides in force. They have made a hostile beachhead on the borders of night elven territory, and threaten to press inland.",sp=0},{t="The Drowned City of Zoram",b="The city of Zoram lies shattered beneath the surf, submerged during the Great Sundering. For ages, it remained abandoned and nearly forgotten by the kaldorei. The naga’s sudden arrival among its ruins stirs bitter memories among Astranaar’s defenders. Sentinels such as Shindrell Swiftfire know the invaders as twisted cousins, born of their own ancient catastrophe. They will not let the depths claim the shore again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Zoram Strand?",a="The Zoram Strand runs along Ashenvale’s rugged northwestern shore, facing the Veiled Sea. Ancient Zoram, a kaldorei city swallowed by the ocean during the Sundering ten thousand years ago, lies there.",al={"zoram strand","where is zoram strand","what is zoram"},it="place"},{q="Why are the naga attacking Ashenvale's coast?",a="The Sentinels in Astranaar do not know exactly why the naga are attacking Ashenvale’s coast. Their military camps and aggression threaten the forests, so the night elves strike before the naga can advance.",al={"why are naga here","naga motive zoram","why wrathtails"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Shindrell Swiftfire?",a="Shindrell Swiftfire is a night elf sentinel stationed in Astranaar. She watches for threats to Ashenvale and organizes strikes against hostile incursions, including the naga on the coast.",al={"shindrell","quest giver astranaar","swiftfire"},it="leader"},{q="What history do the night elves share with the naga?",a="The naga were once Highborne night elves who served Queen Azshara. When the Well of Eternity collapsed during the Sundering, they were dragged into the abyssal depths and transformed into serpentine creatures. Their kinship makes every encounter bitter for the modern kaldorei.",al={"naga elf connection","history with naga","shared history"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after clearing the Zoram Strand?",a="After the naga are thinned along the strand, Shindrell Swiftfire sends Alliance defenders to face other aerial threats along the border. She directs scouts south toward Stonetalon to deal with vicious pridewings.",al={"next quest","what after zoram strand","pridewings"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is the Horde also present at the Zoram Strand?",a="Yes. Alliance champions from Astranaar hunt the shoreline’s naga, while the Horde holds Zoram’gar Outpost, a fortified seaside outpost on the strand. The Horde contests the region and battles both the naga and the Alliance.",al={"horde zoram strand","zoram'gar","is the horde there"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Shindrell Swiftfire want the naga slain?",a="Shindrell views the naga gathering at the Zoram Strand as a direct threat to Ashenvale's northwestern borders. The ruins of the submerged city of Zoram hold painful memories of the Sundering, and whatever dark purpose brought the serpent-kin back to shore, the night elves refuse to let them secure a foothold on sacred land. Slaying them and claiming their heads is meant to break their advance and drive them back into the deep seas before their invasion spreads further inland.",al={"why kill naga zoram","shindrell swiftfire motive","why does shindrell want naga heads"},it="motive",add="a15c1f29"},{q="Who are you sent to hunt at the Zoram Strand?",a="You are dispatched to hunt the Wrathtail naga crawling out from the Veiled Sea onto the shores of the Zoram Strand. These serpent-folk have established a hostile encampment around the sunken elven ruins, threatening the wilderness of northern Ashenvale. Shindrell demands proof of their defeat in the form of severed heads, hoping to blunt their invasion force before the night elves' ancient enemies can push any closer to Astranaar.",al={"wrathtail naga","who do i kill zoram strand","zoram strand target"},it="target",add="99414e89"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, every naga slain on the strand recalls Azshara’s arrogance and the Sundering that broke the ancient world. Sentinels will not let these twisted kin regain ground in Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, securing Ashenvale’s western flank keeps Astranaar from being caught between coastal invaders and Horde lumber operations.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can use the wind-battered coast and broken ruins as vantage points to track amphibious raiders emerging from the breakers."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","naga","shindrell","strand","sundering","swiftfire","wrathtail","zoram"},rel={"subzone:zoram-strand","npc:shindrell-swiftfire","subzone:astranaar","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale","quest:1134"},m={start="Shindrell Swiftfire",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=1008},src={"The Zoram Strand (quest)"}}
E["quest:1009"] = {t="quest",n="Ruuzel",z="ashenvale",s="Talen needs the Ring of Zoram to open an ancient statuette found on the strand. The naga have taken the ring to their island sanctuary.",h="Talen needs the Ring of Zoram to open an ancient statuette found on the strand.",sec={{t="The Key of Zoram",b="Talen believes the Ring of Zoram can open the ancient statuette recovered from the coast. Before the Great Sundering broke Kalimdor and sank its coastal cities, powerful night elven nobles ruled Zoram. The ring belonged among their regalia. After the cataclysm, it vanished beneath the waves for millennia, keeping the secrets of sunken relics from curious eyes.",sp=0},{t="The Naga Incursion",b="Naga have recently come to the Zoram Strand and begun searching the ruins of their former homeland. Ruuzel, who leads the local brood, found the Ring of Zoram and took it to her sanctuary on an island to the north. Talen, a night elf, asks Alliance travelers to hunt Ruuzel and reclaim the heirloom so he can open the statuette recovered from the shallows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ruuzel?",a="Ruuzel leads the naga on the Zoram Strand in northwestern Ashenvale. Her lair lies on an island offshore to the north, where she guards treasures recovered from the sunken night elf civilization.",al={"ruuzel lore","who is the naga leader","ruuzel boss"},it="target"},{q="What is the Ring of Zoram?",a="The Ring of Zoram belonged to the ancient rulers of Zoram before the Sundering. Talen believes it can open the lock on an ancient statuette.",al={"ring of zoram lore","what does the ring do","zoram key"},it="item"},{q="Why does Talen need the ring?",a="Talen wants to uncover the secrets inside an ancient Kaldorei statuette recently recovered from the strand. He believes only the Ring of Zoram can turn its lock.",al={"why get ring of zoram","talen statuette lock"},it="motive"},{q="Where did the city of Zoram go?",a="The Great Sundering destroyed the ancient Kaldorei city of Zoram ten thousand years ago. Most of its grand stonework sank into the Veiled Sea, leaving scattered ruins along the coast.",al={"what happened to zoram","zoram ruins"},it="history"},{q="Where is Ruuzel located?",a="Ruuzel dwells on a large rocky island off the northern edge of the Zoram Strand, with her serpentine followers around her.",al={"where is ruuzel","ruuzel island location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after retrieving the ring?",a="After you return the ring, Talen can finish his investigation on the strand. He rewards your aid and remembers your service.",al={"what does talen do next","ruuzel follow up"},it="next_step"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, reclaiming the Ring of Zoram brings a piece of your ancestral heritage back from the naga desecrating your forebears' sunken ruins.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help Talen blunt the naga threat pushing ashore along northern Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","naga","ring of zoram","ruuzel","sundering","talen","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:talen","quest:1007","subzone:zoram-strand","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale","quest:1008"},m={start="Talen",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=1009,ri={"Ring of Zoram"}},src={"Ruuzel (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1010"] = {t="quest",n="Bathran's Hair",z="ashenvale",s="At Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale, Orendil Broadleaf seeks Bathran's Hair for a sick child in Astranaar. He believes the illness afflicts the child's spirit, and sends you north to the ancient ruins where the uncommon restorative herb was gathered in the past.",h="At Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale, Orendil Broadleaf seeks Bathran's Hair for a sick child in Astranaar.",sec={{t="An Ailment of the Spirit",b="Orendil Broadleaf, a night elf herbalist at Maestra's Post, faces a troubling illness. The post lies just south of the Darkshore border. A young child in Astranaar is grievously ill, and ordinary remedies have failed. Orendil believes the sickness afflicts the child's spirit as well as the flesh. He seeks Bathran's Hair, an uncommon restorative herb gathered in the ancient elven ruins to the north.",sp=0},{t="Trespassers in the Ruins",b="Bathran's Haunt lies along the eastern side of the road leading into Darkshore. Forsaken agents have infiltrated the ruined enclave, making the search for bundled herbs hazardous. When the plants return to Maestra's Post, Orendil brews a soothing draught. The undead operating openly in northern Ashenvale leave him deeply unsettled.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Bathran's Hair?",a="Bathran's Hair is an uncommon medicinal plant native to Bathran's Haunt in Ashenvale. Night elf herbalists value its restorative qualities, especially its power to soothe ailments of the spirit rather than ordinary physical wounds.",al={"bathrans hair plant","what is the hair","bathran herb"},it="item"},{q="Who is sick at Maestra's Post?",a="No one at Maestra's Post is sick. Relara Whitemoon, a young night elf child in Astranaar, is ill; she is the daughter of Pelturas Whitemoon. Her condition worsens by the hour, and ordinary remedies have failed because the sickness appears spiritual, prompting Orendil Broadleaf to seek ancient botanical aid.",al={"sick child maestra","who is orendil healing","who needs the cure"}},{q="Where is Bathran's Haunt located?",a="Bathran's Haunt lies in northwestern Ashenvale, north of Maestra's Post and just east of the main road leading toward the Darkshore border. Hostile Forsaken operatives have overrun the ruins.",al={"bathrans haunt location","where to find bathrans hair","where is bathran"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are there Forsaken at Bathran's Haunt?",a="No one knows what the Forsaken are after. Orendil learns of them only when the herbs return, and undead lurking so deep in night elf lands trouble him greatly.",al={"undead at bathran","why forsaken in ashenvale","forsaken bathrans haunt"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after collecting the plant?",a="After you bring him five bundles of Bathran's Hair, Orendil prepares a medicinal concoction and asks you to hurry it to the ailing child in Astranaar. This begins the follow-up called Orendil's Cure.",al={"next quest after bathrans hair","what does orendil do with the hair","orendils cure chain"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can herbalists find the plant bundles easier?",a="Yes. The bundles lie scattered on the ground and can be hard to spot with the naked eye. Adventurers trained in Herbalism can detect them with their herb tracking ability.",al={"herbalism bathrans hair","tracking bathrans hair","plant bundle herb track"},gp=true},{q="Why does Orendil Broadleaf want Bathran's Hair?",a="A child in Astranaar has fallen terribly ill, and Orendil Broadleaf fears the affliction touches more than just the body. Believing the child's spirit itself is under assault, he needs Bathran's Hair to brew a special concoction capable of mending ailments of the soul before the illness claims the young one's life.",al={"why does orendil need bathrans hair","orendil broadleaf motive","why help orendil"},it="motive",add="b8c70a70"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalism tracking can reveal the bundles scattered throughout Bathran's Haunt, making the search among the ruins far easier.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you face the Forsaken presence at Bathran's Haunt, a grave threat to northern Ashenvale's sanctified borders and its children.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure medicine for the child in Astranaar and support the frontline settlements holding western Ashenvale against hostile Horde and Forsaken expansion."},kw={"ashenvale","bathran's hair","bathran's haunt","darkshore","forsaken","maestra's post","orendil broadleaf","plant bundle"},rel={"npc:orendil-broadleaf","subzone:bathran-s-haunt","subzone:maestra-s-post","quest:1020","quest:1033","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Orendil Broadleaf",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1010,ri={"Bathran's Hair"}},src={"Bathran's Hair (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1011"] = {t="quest",n="Forsaken Diseases",z="ashenvale",s="In eastern Ashenvale, Kayneth Stillwind watches the Forsaken draw nearer. He fears they are brewing blights to ravage sacred elven lands, and sends Alliance champions toward a camp near Dor'Danil Barrow Den to seize a sample.",h="In eastern Ashenvale, Kayneth Stillwind watches the Forsaken draw nearer.",sec={{t="A Plague on the Forests",b="Ashenvale's night elves have long faced satyrs, raging elementals, and orcish logging crews. The Forsaken bring a darker threat. The undead arm of the Horde is taking root near ancient ruins and sacred barrow dens. Their presence brings war and the fear of alchemical plague spreading through Kaldorei groves.",sp=0},{t="Infiltration at Dor'Danil",b="South of Forest Song, near Dor'Danil Barrow Den, Forsaken apothecaries and scouts have fortified a camp. They bottle untested toxins among brewing caldrons and foul reagents. Kayneth Stillwind sends scouts inside to recover an intact Bottle of Disease, so its volatile contents can be studied before the Forsaken unleash it across the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kayneth Stillwind?",a="Kayneth Stillwind is a night elf keeping watch from the ruins of Forest Song in eastern Ashenvale. He tracks hostile movements across the region, especially the Forsaken and corrupting influences near the barrow dens.",al={"kayneth stillwind","who gives forsaken diseases","forest song questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Forsaken camp located?",a="The Forsaken camp lies south of Forest Song, near Dor'Danil Barrow Den. Their forces have gathered around brewing tables and tents to concoct biological mixtures.",al={"where is the camp","where are the diseased bottles","dor'danil camp location"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken in Ashenvale?",a="The Forsaken pursue alchemical and biological aims in Ashenvale. Near ancient Kaldorei barrows, they gather reagents and brew toxic compounds, leading the elves to fear they mean to infect the land.",al={"why forsaken in ashenvale","undead in ashenvale","forsaken motives"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after retrieving the bottle?",a="Kayneth Stillwind examines the captured bottle to identify its contents. His investigation leads to the plight of sleeping druids inside nearby Dor'Danil Barrow Den, and he turns to that danger next.",al={"what next","after forsaken diseases","quest follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Forest Song?",a="Forest Song is an ancient, nearly abandoned night elf ruin in far eastern Ashenvale, near the border of Azshara. Kayneth Stillwind lives there alone and directs the fight against the Forsaken in the region.",al={"forest song outpost","what is forest song"},it="place"},{q="What are the barrow dens in Ashenvale?",a="Barrow dens are sacred underground sanctuaries where night elf druids sleep in communion with the Emerald Dream. Dor'Danil Barrow Den is one such site, making the Forsaken camp nearby a grave concern for the Kaldorei.",al={"what is a barrow den","dor'danil purpose","barrow dens"},it="place"},{q="Why does Kayneth Stillwind want a bottle of disease?",a="Kayneth fears the Forsaken are plotting to corrupt Ashenvale by spreading their foul contagions across the sacred night elf lands. He needs physical proof of their experiments so he can test the concoction himself and confirm exactly what malicious plagues the undead are brewing near the barrow dens.",al={"why does kayneth want this done","kayneth stillwind motive","why get bottle of disease"},it="motive",add="78e58974"},{q="What is the Bottle of Disease for?",a="The bottle holds a virulent mixture of poisons and plagues crafted by Forsaken apothecaries in their makeshift camp near Dor'Danil Barrow Den. Kayneth Stillwind intends to analyze the sample to unmask the true goals and scope of the Forsaken's biological warfare in Ashenvale.",al={"what is bottle of disease","bottle of disease purpose","forsaken bottle of disease"},it="item",add="53e7622a"},{q="Who are you sent against in this mission?",a="You are dispatched against a secretive contingent of Forsaken undead entrenched south of Forest Song near Dor'Danil Barrow Den. They have crept into Ashenvale to concoct unnatural blights and experiment near ancient elven sacred sites, threatening both the forest and its guardians.",al={"who are we fighting","forsaken enemies in ashenvale","who is at the camp"},it="target",add="1459855f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the undead presence near a sacred barrow den is an intolerable desecration. Defending the sleeping druids and Ashenvale from vile toxins means protecting their survival and honor.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold the barrow dens sacred as places of communion with the Emerald Dream. Bottled blights near Dor'Danil strike at the heart of the Cenarion Circle's guardianship.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Horde's Forsaken allies bring chemical warfare to Ashenvale. The threat shows Alliance leaders that the conflict in the forest reaches beyond disputes over wood."},kw={"apothecary","ashenvale","bottle of disease","dor'danil barrow den","forest song","forsaken","forsaken diseases","kayneth stillwind","night elf"},rel={"quest:1012","quest:4581","subzone:forest-song","subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den","zone:ashenvale","topic:forsaken","topic:druid","topic:horde"},m={start="Kayneth Stillwind",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=1011,ri={"Bottle of Disease"}},src={"Forsaken Diseases"}}
E["quest:1012"] = {t="quest",n="Insane Druids",z="ashenvale",s="A massacre in Dor'Danil Barrow Den leaves its druids' spirits in torment. Kayneth Stillwind, a night elf sentinel in eastern Ashenvale, learns of the slaughter through a vision while battling Forsaken toxins.",h="A massacre in Dor'Danil Barrow Den leaves its druids' spirits in torment.",sec={{t="A Vision of Slaughter",b="Kayneth Stillwind sees a massacre in a waking vision. The night elf sentinel is battling the effects of Forsaken toxins found in eastern Ashenvale when he witnesses what happened beneath the mounds of Dor'Danil Barrow Den. Undead infiltrators poisoned the druids in their sleep and slaughtered them. Their souls were torn from their bodies by the venom, leaving them as wild, shrieking spirits.",sp=0},{t="Mercy for the Slain Leaders",b="Kayneth Stillwind asks you to quiet the suffering beneath Dor'Danil Barrow Den. The druids' phantoms have been driven mad by the way they died, and cannot find release in the underground chambers. Their circle's three leaders, Taneel Darkwood, Uthil Mooncall, and Mavoris Cloudsbreak, remain among the restless dead. Lay them to rest, and the den may begin to heal from its defilement.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who poisoned the druids in Dor'Danil Barrow Den?",a="Forsaken infiltrators poisoned and murdered the druids in Dor'Danil Barrow Den. Kayneth Stillwind saw the crime in a vision while suffering from Forsaken toxins gathered from undead agents in Ashenvale.",al={"who killed dor'danil druids","who murdered the druids","forsaken poison druids"},it="origin"},{q="Why did the druids become insane ghosts?",a="The druids became mad spirits after they were killed in their sleep. The Forsaken's alchemical poisons tore their souls from their bodies in an unnatural, agonizing way.",al={"why are the druids ghosts","why are druids mad","why insane druids"},it="history"},{q="Who are Taneel Darkwood, Uthil Mooncall, and Mavoris Cloudsbreak?",a="Taneel Darkwood, Uthil Mooncall, and Mavoris Cloudsbreak led the druidic circle in Dor'Danil Barrow Den. Their spirits anchor the den's madness, so they must be laid to rest for the others to find peace.",al={"druid leaders","taneel darkwood","uthil mooncall","mavoris cloudsbreak"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Dor'Danil Barrow Den located?",a="Dor'Danil Barrow Den lies underground in southeastern Ashenvale, just south of the ruins of Forest Song.",al={"dor'danil location","where is dor danil","barrow den ashenvale"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to put the druids to rest?",a="Kayneth Stillwind, a night elf at Forest Song in eastern Ashenvale, asks you to help after you assist him in researching Forsaken diseases.",al={"who gives insane druids","kayneth stillwind quest","where to start insane druids"},it="in_charge",gp=true},{q="Does slaying the leaders purge the den entirely?",a="Slaying the three leaders eases the spiritual anguish in the barrow den. Kayneth says this is one step toward helping the remaining maddened spirits find peace.",al={"is dor'danil saved","does the den get cleansed"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Kayneth Stillwind want the druid leaders destroyed?",a="While Kayneth struggled against the Forsaken's toxins, a vision revealed to him the horrific fate of his kin in the Dor'Danil Barrow Den. The murdered druids linger as tormented, maddened ghosts, and their ongoing anguish haunts his very dreams. Kayneth hopes that by destroying their former leaders, their spiritual torment will end and allow the remaining troubled spirits in the barrows to finally find peace.",al={"kayneth motive","why kill insane druids","why destroy druid spirits"},it="motive",add="7181097d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see the slaughter of sleeping druids in Dor'Danil Barrow Den as an outrage against nature and the Kaldorei. The Forsaken must answer for it.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can grant Taneel Darkwood, Uthil Mooncall, and Mavoris Cloudsbreak a solemn mercy. You free fellow practitioners of the Cenarion arts from alchemical madness.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the Forsaken's cruelty reach far beyond Lordaeron. Their plagues are carried into distant lands to kill innocents in their sleep."},kw={"ashenvale","dor'danil barrow den","forest song","forsaken","insane druids","kayneth stillwind","mavoris cloudsbreak","taneel darkwood","uthil mooncall"},rel={"quest:1011","quest:4581","subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den","subzone:forest-song","topic:druid","topic:forsaken","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Kayneth Stillwind",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=1012},src={"Insane Druids (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1016"] = {t="quest",n="Elemental Bracers",z="ashenvale",s="At Silverwind Refuge, the night elves face tainted waters and seek the hand behind them. Sentinel Velene Starstrike asks you to gather intact bracers from the hostile elementals, so a divining scroll can identify who summoned them.",h="At Silverwind Refuge, the night elves face tainted waters and seek the hand behind them.",sec={{t="Tainted Waters",b="Rogue water elementals now trouble Ashenvale’s sacred waters. Unlike the wild spirits that naturally inhabit the world, these creatures show signs of artificial conjuration. At Silverwind Refuge, the Sentinels see their sudden arrival as a sign that outside corruption is reaching deeper into the forest’s waterways.",sp=0},{t="Divining the Conjurer",b="Sentinel Velene Starstrike believes someone deliberately bound and unleashed the elementals. She gives you a magical divining scroll to help identify the culprit. The spell needs a reagent tied to the summoned beings: intact bracers taken from the spirits before they dissipate. The scroll reads the lingering arcane signature on those bindings, tracing it to whoever called the elementals into being.",sp=0},{t="A Wizard's Meddling",b="When the divining scroll is cast over the intact bracers, the arcane residue confirms Velene’s worst fears: a solitary mage is churning corrupt elementals into Ashenvale’s pools. The discovery outrages the night elf defenders. They now prepare swift retribution against the summoner threatening the woodlands’ sanctity.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are there water elementals in Ashenvale?",a="The hostile water elementals are not natural inhabitants living in balance with Ashenvale. An outside spellcaster summoned them, disturbing the sacred pools and provoking the night elves.",al={"why are elementals here","ashenvale water elementals","where did elementals come from"},it="target"},{q="Who gives the quest Elemental Bracers?",a="Sentinel Velene Starstrike offers the work. She is stationed at Silverwind Refuge, on the shores of Mystral Lake in Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","who starts elemental bracers","where to pick up elemental bracers"},gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of the Divining Scroll?",a="The Divining Scroll reads the magical signature left on the elementals. Cast over five intact bracers, it traces the arcane tether to the summoner who created them.",al={"what does the scroll do","divining scroll purpose","why use divining scroll"},gp=true},{q="Why do only intact bracers work for the ritual?",a="Only intact bracers retain enough stable arcane resonance for the scroll to analyze. Destroying an elemental often damages or shatters its magical bindings, leaving them unable to reveal the conjurer.",al={"why intact bracers","broken bracers","intact elemental bracers"}},{q="What happens after divining the scroll?",a="After you return the Divined Scroll to Sentinel Velene Starstrike, she identifies the rogue spellcaster responsible and sends you to hunt the summoner in the follow-up, Mage Summoner.",al={"elemental bracers follow up","what comes next","next quest after elemental bracers"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Sentinel Velene care so much about these elementals?",a="Night elves revere the natural purity of Ashenvale’s forests and waters. A mortal wizard deliberately polluting and destabilizing their lakes with corrupted elementals insults their guardianship.",al={"sentinel velene motivation","why night elves care about elementals"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Divined Scroll for?",a="The Divined Scroll holds the mystical trace gathered from the elementals' intact bracers. By performing the divination ritual, you imprint the magical signatures of the water elementals onto the parchment. Returning this completed scroll to Sentinel Velene Starstrike provides the Sentinels with the vital arcane clues required to pinpoint the exact rogue mage responsible for summoning the corrupt creatures into Ashenvale's pristine waters.",al={"divined scroll purpose","why divined scroll","what does divined scroll do"},it="item",add="b81920f2"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Ashenvale’s natural pools are sacred ground. Arcane summoners who introduce foreign corruption affront the Kaldorei.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can recognize how the bindings worn by conjured elementals carry their master’s arcane signature, tracing reckless conjuration to its origin.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you strengthen your standing in central Ashenvale’s contested heartlands by aiding the Silverwind Sentinels."},kw={"ashenvale","divined scroll","divining scroll","elemental bracers","mage summoner","mystral lake","sentinel velene starstrike","silverwind refuge"},rel={"npc:sentinel-velene-starstrike","quest:1017","subzone:silverwind-refuge","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Sentinel Velene Starstrike",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=1016,ri={"Divined Scroll"}},src={"Elemental Bracers (quest)"}}
E["quest:1017"] = {t="quest",n="Mage Summoner",z="ashenvale",s="Sentinel Velene Starstrike sends a strike south from Silverwind Refuge. After investigating corrupted water elementals near Mystral Lake, the Sentinels send adventurers across the border into the Barrens to kill the undead mage Sarilus Foulborne atop Dreadmist Peak.",h="Sentinel Velene Starstrike sends a strike south from Silverwind Refuge.",sec={{t="A Crossing of Borders",b="Night elves rarely send scouts south into the Barrens without grave cause. After investigating unnatural disturbances among the water elementals around Mystral Lake, Sentinel Velene Starstrike traces the meddling to Sarilus Foulborne, a Forsaken conjurer practicing his arts just across the border. For the Sentinels at Silverwind Refuge, an enemy sorcerer defiling nature so close to their home cannot be tolerated.",sp=0},{t="The Conjurer on the Peak",b="Sarilus Foulborne has made his lair high on Dreadmist Peak, a craggy mountain crawling with Burning Blade cultists. From there, he summons ranks of water elementals and bends them to his will, defying night elf authority from Horde lands. Reaching him means braving enemy territory and cutting through his summoned forces. The Sentinels demand his severed head as proof that their vengeance reaches beyond the forest line.",sp=0},{t="Blessing of Elune",b="Velene Starstrike receives Foulborne's severed head and gives his slayer the Light of Elune. This sacred draught of moonlight is a treasured ward among priestesses and Sentinels, granting complete protection when death is near. The gift recalls the night elves' divine favor as foul magic spreads through Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sarilus Foulborne?",a="Sarilus Foulborne is an undead mage who fled into the Barrens and made his home atop Dreadmist Peak. He uses arcane summoning to enslave water elementals, drawing the Sentinels' anger from nearby Ashenvale.",al={"sarilus foulborne","who is the mage summoner","foulborne lore"},it="target"},{q="Where is Dreadmist Peak located?",a="Dreadmist Peak is a craggy mountain in the northern Barrens, directly south of the Ashenvale border. Sarilus Foulborne waits at its highest point.",al={"where is dreadmist peak","dreadmist peak location","how to find dreadmist peak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Velene Starstrike want Sarilus dead?",a="Sarilus has been defiling and corrupting water elementals near the Ashenvale border. Velene finds his defiance intolerable and seeks to end his unnatural conjurations, proving enemies cannot mock the Sentinels from across the border.",al={"why kill sarilus","velene starstrike motive"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Light of Elune given as a reward?",a="The Light of Elune is a rare vial blessed with divine moonlight. Drink it in dire moments to become entirely immune to damage and spell effects for a brief time, escaping otherwise certain death.",al={"light of elune potion","light of elune lore"},it="power"},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Before this, adventurers gather intact bracers from the divining water elementals around Mystral Lake in Ashenvale. Velene uses them to identify who is manipulating the elementals.",al={"prerequisite for mage summoner","quest before mage summoner"},it="history",gp=true},{q="Why is entering the Barrens dangerous for Alliance players?",a="The Barrens belongs to the Horde and is home to tauren and orcs. Alliance soldiers and adventurers who enter risk interception by Horde patrols and rival champions.",al={"barrens dangerous","horde territory quest"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Sentinel Velene Starstrike want Sarilus Foulborne's head?",a="Sentinel Velene Starstrike demands Sarilus Foulborne's head as definitive proof of his demise. The Forsaken mage has brazenly defiled Ashenvale's water elementals and mocked the Sentinels from his perch across the border. Bringing his severed head back to Silverwind Refuge ensures beyond all doubt that his arrogance has ended and wipes his repugnant smile away forever.",al={"sarilus foulborne head","why bring sarilus head","sarilus head purpose"},it="item",add="b17c8b5b"},{q="Why does Sentinel Velene Starstrike send you instead of going herself?",a="Sarilus Foulborne has taken refuge atop Dreadmist Peak, deep within the Barrens. Because that arid land is firmly Horde territory, dispatching a formal military squad of Night Elf Sentinels would risk triggering an open border conflict with the watchful Horde garrisons. A capable adventurer moving alone can cross the border unnoticed, strike down the necromantic mage, and return before the enemy mounts a defense.",al={"why send me mage summoner","why doesnt velene kill sarilus","why sentinel velene need me"},it="why_me",add="bcfc7529"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Sarilus's arcane defilement of nature across the forest border insults the Kaldorei. His execution concerns both woodland balance and pride.",["faction:Alliance"]="Striking a Forsaken target deep in the Barrens makes a bold show of force against Horde encroachments along Ashenvale's southern frontier.",["class:Mage"]="Confronting Foulborne pits Alliance arcanists against an undead practitioner who twists elemental conjuration to reckless extremes.",["class:Priest"]="Receiving the Light of Elune from the Sentinels links your path to the Goddess's rare, miraculous grace against undead corruption."},kw={"ashenvale","dreadmist peak","light of elune","sarilus foulborne","silverwind refuge","the barrens","velene starstrike","water elementals"},rel={"npc:sentinel-velene-starstrike","quest:1016","subzone:silverwind-refuge","subzone:dreadmist-peak","topic:sentinels","topic:elune","zone:barrens","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Sentinel Velene Starstrike",["end"]="Sentinel Velene Starstrike",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=1017,ri={"Sarilus Foulborne's Head"}},src={"Mage Summoner"}}
E["quest:1020"] = {t="quest",n="Orendil's Cure",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Orendil's Cure is bound for a sick child in Astranaar. Orendil Broadleaf sends an Alliance traveler with a remedy made from rare flora.",h="In Ashenvale, Orendil's Cure is bound for a sick child in Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Father's Despair",b="In Astranaar, Pelturas Whitemoon watches his daughter Relara waste away from a severe, mysterious sickness. With local knowledge exhausted, he sought help from herbalists across Ashenvale before hope faded.",sp=0},{t="A Race Across the Woodlands",b="Orendil Broadleaf brews a draught to halt Relara's affliction from the necessary components, including Bathran's hair. He entrusts the cure to you and sends you south and east along the forest highway to Astranaar, where Relara awaits it.",sp=0},{t="A Fragile Respite",b="Orendil's draught brings Relara relief, but it cannot end the supernatural malady gnawing at her spirit. The remedy buys time for a search among ancient Kaldorei ruins for relics blessed by Elune, which may complete her salvation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is sick in Astranaar?",a="Relara Whitemoon, Pelturas Whitemoon's young daughter, is bedridden in Astranaar. Her condition is critical, and her father is desperate to find a remedy.",al={"who is ill","who needs the cure","sick child astranaar"},it="target"},{q="Who brewed Orendil's Cure?",a="Orendil Broadleaf, a night elf herbalist in northern Ashenvale, brewed the mixture after receiving plant matter gathered from Bathran's Haunt.",al={"who made the cure","orendil broadleaf","where did cure come from"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Pelturas Whitemoon located?",a="Pelturas Whitemoon lives in Astranaar, the Alliance town on the main road through central Ashenvale. He watches over his daughter's sickbed inside one of the woodland dwellings.",al={"pelturas location","where is pelturas","find pelturas astranaar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Orendil's Cure completely heal Relara?",a="No. The draught stabilizes Relara's immediate condition and gives her father renewed hope, but her sickness needs deeper spiritual help. Travelers search for Elune's Tear.",al={"is relara cured","does the cure work","cure result"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What ingredients were used to create this cure?",a="Bathran's hair was the primary ingredient, gathered from the cursed ground of Bathran's Haunt north of Maestra's Post.",al={"cure ingredients","what is cure made of","bathrans hair"},it="item"},{q="Why didn't Astranaar's local healers brew the cure themselves?",a="Relara's affliction resisted Astranaar's everyday remedies, so Pelturas sought Orendil Broadleaf's specialized botanical expertise. Orendil knows how to handle the potent flora of northern Ashenvale.",al={"why orendil","why astranaar healers failed","why broadleaf"}},{q="Why does Orendil Broadleaf want this done?",a="Orendil Broadleaf is a skilled herbalist who knows that time is running out for Pelturas Whitemoon's young child, Relara. Having successfully prepared a mixture from the rare plant Bathran's hair, Orendil wants the remedy delivered to Astranaar without delay to halt the child's deadly affliction and save her life.",al={"why does orendil send the cure","orendil broadleaf motive","why help relara"},it="motive",add="49e0bc34"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalism shows how botany meets battlefield medicine: harvested Ashenvale herbs such as Bathran's hair can hold a child's life in the balance.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you help protect Astranaar's young and strengthen your people's community in a contested forest.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you know herbs can ease Relara's body for a time, while her lingering malady calls for Elune's sacred intervention and lunar rites."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","bathran's hair","cure","orendil broadleaf","pelturas whitemoon","relara"},rel={"npc:pelturas-whitemoon","npc:orendil-broadleaf","quest:1010","quest:1033","subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","topic:elune","quest:1034"},m={start="Orendil Broadleaf",["end"]="Pelturas Whitemoon",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1020},src={"Orendil's Cure (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1021"] = {t="quest",n="Vile Satyr! Dryads in Danger!",z="ashenvale",s="Illiyana searches Ashenvale for her sisters, missing after setting out to recover a stolen relic. She asks travelers to find them in the corrupted ruins of Xavian.",h="Illiyana searches Ashenvale for her sisters, missing after setting out to recover a stolen relic.",sec={{t="A Desperate Sister",b="Dryad Illiyana waits in Ashenvale, overwhelmed with worry for her sisters. They left for the corrupted northern reaches of the forest to recover the Branch of Cenarius, a holy relic stolen by satyrs. They promised to return swiftly, but two days have passed without word. Now Illiyana asks passing Alliance travelers to track them down before it is too late.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Xavian",b="Xavian lies to the northeast, an ancient night elf temple complex long corrupted by the Burning Legion. Fel-tainted satyrs swarm its ruins, making them a perilous place to search. Deep inside, Anilia, leader of the dryad expedition, lies gravely wounded and near death after the demonic inhabitants attacked her.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Illiyana?",a="Illiyana is a dryad who lives in the forests of Ashenvale. Worried for her sisters, she sends travelers toward Xavian to search for their missing party.",al={"illiyana","who gives vile satyr dryads in danger","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Branch of Cenarius?",a="The Branch of Cenarius is a sacred relic precious to dryads and night elves. Satyrs in northern Ashenvale stole it, and Anilia and her sisters set out on a dangerous journey into Xavian to recover it.",al={"branch of cenarius","what relic were they looking for","dryad artifact"},it="item"},{q="What is Xavian?",a="Xavian is an ancient night elf temple in eastern Ashenvale. Demonic satyrs have overrun the ruins, where fel corruption threatens nature's protectors.",al={"xavian","ruins of xavian","where are the dryads"},it="place"},{q="Who is Anilia?",a="Anilia is the dryad who led the search party to reclaim the Branch of Cenarius from the satyrs. Illiyana asks travelers to find her in Xavian.",al={"anilia","missing dryad leader","where is anilia"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Why are the dryads in conflict with the satyr?",a="Dryads are daughters of the demigod Cenarius, devoted to preserving nature and the forest's balance. Satyrs are ancient night elves twisted by demonic fel magic, and they corrupt the wilderness and desecrate sacred groves.",al={"why do dryads hate satyrs","dryad satyr war","satyr corruption"},it="conflict"},{q="What quest follows this one?",a="Finding Anilia completes the search and leads into 'The Branch of Cenarius', where the effort to recover the stolen relic continues.",al={"next quest","dryads in danger chain","after vile satyr"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Illiyana need help finding her sisters?",a="Illiyana is terrified for her sisters. Anilia led a band of dryads northeast into the corrupted ruins of Xavian to recover a sacred relic, the Branch of Cenarius, from the satyrs. They promised to return quickly, but two days have passed without any word. Fearing they have been ambushed or overwhelmed by the foul creatures lurking in the ruins, Illiyana urgently needs someone capable of braving Xavian to track them down and see if any survive.",al={"why does illiyana send you","illiyana motive","why find anilia"},it="motive",add="a04fd548"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share a bond with the dryads, daughters of Cenarius. Their distress and the defilement of ancient elven temples in Xavian call on your honor and spiritual duty.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share a deep kinship with the children of Cenarius. You are sworn to cleanse the demonic corruption spreading from satyr strongholds like Xavian.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you strengthen the Alliance's bond with Ashenvale's mystical denizens when you help Illiyana amid growing regional threats."},kw={"anilia","ashenvale","branch of cenarius","cenarius","dryad","illiyana","satyr","xavian"},rel={"quest:1031","subzone:xavian","topic:satyr","topic:cenarius","npc:illiyana","zone:ashenvale","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Illiyana",["end"]="Anilia",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=1021},src={"Vile Satyr! Dryads in Danger! (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1022"] = {t="quest",n="The Howling Vale",z="ashenvale",s="At the Howling Vale, worgen have overrun a ruined shrine near Felwood. Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow seeks the cause of their arrival in Ashenvale.",h="At the Howling Vale, worgen have overrun a ruined shrine near Felwood.",sec={{t="A Chilling Presence",b="Worgen cries echo from a ruined shrine in northern Ashenvale. The shrine of Mel'Thandris lies beyond a cavern path near the Felwood border. Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow fears the worgen may bring another disaster to the woodland realm. Night elf sentinels are already spending great effort holding back demonic corruption from Felwood.",sp=0},{t="The Living Chronicle",b="Melyria sends seekers to the overrun shrine to consult the Tome of Mel'Thandris. Mel'Thandris blessed its leaves to capture significant events. Opened among the hostile worgen, the tome summons a spectral vision of Priestess Velinde Starsong. The vision reveals her fateful invocation of the mysterious Scythe of Elune.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Howling Vale located?",a="The Howling Vale lies in north-central Ashenvale, just southwest of the Felwood border. A cave passage leads into the vale and to the ruined shrine of Mel'Thandris.",al={"howling vale location","how to get to howling vale","where is the shrine of mel'thandris"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are the wolf-men in the vale?",a="The wolf-men are worgen, specifically members of the Terrowulf pack. These savage, unnatural beasts walk on two legs and suddenly appeared in Kalimdor, terrorizing ruins near the Felwood frontier.",al={"wolf men ashenvale","what are the monsters in howling vale","terrowulf worgen"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Tome of Mel'Thandris?",a="The Tome of Mel'Thandris is an enchanted relic in the shrine ruins. Mel'Thandris blessed its leaves to capture and project visions of pivotal events to those who study it.",al={"tome of melthandris","what does the tome do","mel'thandris book"},it="item"},{q="Who was Velinde Starsong?",a="Velinde Starsong was a night elf priestess involved in the struggle against demons near Felwood. The Tome of Mel'Thandris may reveal more of her story.",al={"velinde starsong","priestess velinde","who is the ghost in the tome"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow asks from the Shrine of Aessina in Ashenvale. She is troubled by demonic incursions from Felwood and the unexplained arrival of nearby worgen.",al={"who starts the howling vale","howling vale quest giver","melyria frostshadow"},it="in_charge",gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Melyria care about the shrine?",a="Sentinels in Ashenvale guard against corruption from Felwood. After wolf-men seized an ancient night elf holy site near the border, the Sentinels needed to learn whether demons were behind it or a new danger had emerged.",al={"why investigate howling vale","forest song sentinels"},it="motive"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, the desecration of Mel'Thandris's shrine strikes at your duty to protect Ashenvale. The visions of Priestess Velinde Starsong bring a sorrowful glimpse of that burden.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you join the search for the origin of the terrifying worgen stalking northern Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may find the search for Priestess Velinde Starsong a sobering tale of devotion to Elune."},kw={"ashenvale","felwood","howling vale","mel'thandris","melyria frostshadow","scythe of elune","terrowulf","tome of mel'thandris","velinde starsong","worgen"},rel={"subzone:howling-vale","quest:1037","topic:worgen","topic:elune","zone:ashenvale","zone:felwood"},m={start="Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1022},src={"The Howling Vale (quest)"}}
E["quest:1023"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="At Lake Falathim, Raene's Cleansing turns from a search for Teronis into a grim recovery. Raene Wolfrunner sent the night elf sentinel there, and now you must bring back his journal and a glowing gem held by the murlocs before reporting to her in Astranaar.",h="At Lake Falathim, Raene's Cleansing turns from a search for Teronis into a grim recovery.",sec={{t="A Fallen Scout",b="Raene Wolfrunner sent you to Lake Falathim to find Teronis, a night elf sentinel. You find him dead beside the water. His belongings include an intact journal, with an account of his assignment and what he found about Ashenvale's strange disturbances.",sp=0},{t="The Glowing Gem",b="Teronis tracked a rare, glowing stone to Lake Falathim, but the lake's aggressive murlocs now hold it. You need to recover the gem and Teronis' journal to continue the work he began.",sp=0},{t="Grief in Astranaar",b="Raene Wolfrunner grieves when you return to Astranaar with news of Teronis. She must arrange a patrol to recover her fallen comrade's body, even as corruption threatens the forest. Raene asks you to take up Teronis' work and rebuild the rod he hoped would slow the furbolg attacks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Teronis?",a="Teronis was a night elf scout Raene Wolfrunner sent from Astranaar to investigate Lake Falathim and secure a mystical gem. Hostile wildlife killed him before he could finish his duty.",al={"teronis","who is teronis","teronis lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Glowing Gem found?",a="Murlocs carry the Glowing Gem in and around Lake Falathim, in northwestern Ashenvale, near where Teronis' body was found.",al={"where is the glowing gem","glowing gem location","find glowing gem"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why is Raene Wolfrunner so focused on this task?",a="Teronis was Raene's longtime friend, and he believed the rod could slow the furbolg attacks on her people. With furbolgs still raiding Ashenvale, Raene gives his unfinished work urgent attention despite his death.",al={"why raene cleansing","raene wolfrunner motive"},it="motive"},{q="What happens to Teronis' body after this quest?",a="Raene Wolfrunner pledges to send a detachment of Sentinels from Astranaar to retrieve Teronis' remains for mourning and traditional night elf funeral rites.",al={"teronis corpse fate","what happens to teronis"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Teronis' Journal for?",a="Teronis' Journal records his investigation of Dartol, a human wizard who used druidic magic to try to befriend and control the furbolgs. It also holds his notes on recovering the pieces of Dartol's rod.",al={"teronis journal","what is the journal"},it="item"},{q="Does this quest chain continue after turning it in?",a="Yes. When you bring the gem and journal to Raene Wolfrunner, she asks you to continue Teronis' work and seek the remaining pieces of Dartol's rod.",al={"quest progression","next quest after teronis"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is finding Teronis' journal and the gem important?",a="Teronis perished before he could complete the vital task entrusted to him by Astranaar. By recovering his intact journal and securing the Glowing Gem from the nearby waters, you ensure his sacrifice was not in vain and allow Raene Wolfrunner to understand and carry forward his cleansing mission.",al={"why find teronis journal","why recover glowing gem","teronis quest motive"},it="motive",add="699dfe26"},{q="What is the Glowing Gem?",a="The Glowing Gem is an enchanted stone that Teronis tracked to Lake Falathim before meeting his end. Highly sought after by Raene Wolfrunner for her cleansing efforts, the radiant relic was scavenged by the lake's aggressive murlocs and must be wrested back to resume Teronis' sacred duty.",al={"what is the glowing gem","glowing gem lore","why glowing gem"},it="item",add="9d747809"},{q="Why are the murlocs at Lake Falathim holding the gem?",a="The vile fin murlocs that infest the shores and waters of Lake Falathim scavenge anything shimmering or powerful that washes into their territory. Following Teronis' demise on the lake's edge, these feral creatures swiftly snatched up the radiating stone, fiercely guarding it among their clutches.",al={"why do murlocs have gem","murlocs lake falathim","lake falathim murlocs"},it="target",add="a4b5e1af"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the death of a fellow Sentinel at Lake Falathim points to danger creeping toward Kalimdor's ancient sacred groves.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help Raene Wolfrunner and the Sentinels hold Ashenvale's northern approaches from Astranaar."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","glowing gem","lake falathim","murloc","raene's cleansing","sentinels","teronis"},rel={"quest:991","npc:raene-wolfrunner","npc:teronis-corpse","subzone:astranaar","topic:murloc","topic:sentinels","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Teronis' Corpse",["end"]="Raene Wolfrunner",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1023,ri={"Glowing Gem"}},src={"Raene's Cleansing (2)"}}
E["quest:1024"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="A Glowing Gem brings Raene's Cleansing to a turning point in Ashenvale. Raene Wolfrunner sends you east of Iris Lake to ask the dryad Shael'dryn how Dartol's ancient rod can be restored.",h="A Glowing Gem brings Raene's Cleansing to a turning point in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Clue in Teronis's Notes",b="Raene Wolfrunner studies the field notes left by the sentinel Teronis, who died while investigating Ashenvale's troubled furbolgs. His research points to an ancient rod crafted by a night elf named Dartol. Raene has recovered a Glowing Gem, but her skill as a huntress cannot unravel the arcane and natural mysteries surrounding the relic.",sp=0},{t="Seeking the Daughters of Cenarius",b="Raene sends you northeast toward Iris Lake to seek Shael'dryn, a dryad who dwells beside a moonwell. As one of the Daughters of Cenarius, Shael'dryn understands the forest and ancient relics. Bring her the Glowing Gem, and she may reveal what else is needed to restore Dartol's Rod.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Teronis?",a="Teronis was a night elf scout sent by Astranaar to investigate the corruption spreading through Ashenvale. He died on that mission, but his recovered journal offered a clue: restoring Dartol's Rod might help the land.",al={"teronis","teronis notes","who is teronis"},it="people"},{q="What is Dartol's Rod?",a="Dartol's Rod is an ancient magical artifact that Raene Wolfrunner hopes will aid her investigation of Ashenvale's furbolgs. The recovered Glowing Gem is one piece needed to restore it.",al={"dartols rod","what is the rod","rod of dartol"},it="item"},{q="Where can I find Shael'dryn?",a="Shael'dryn lives beside a secluded moonwell northeast of Astranaar, in the hills just east of Iris Lake. Follow the road east, then turn north before the dangerous lands near Raynewood Retreat.",al={"where is shael'dryn","shaeldryn location","find the dryad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Glowing Gem?",a="The Glowing Gem is one piece of Dartol's Rod, recovered from the ruins of Teronis's investigation. Shael'dryn needs it to discover the rod's other pieces.",al={"glowing gem","what is the gem for","teronis gem"},it="item"},{q="Why does Raene Wolfrunner send you to a dryad?",a="Raene Wolfrunner is a huntress and leader of Astranaar's sentinels, focused on defending the town. Dryads, the Daughters of Cenarius, understand ancient relics and the restoration of nature.",al={"why see a dryad","raene wolfrunner dryad","why shael'dryn"},it="motive"},{q="Why is the forest around Iris Lake in danger?",a="Corruption and unrest are spreading among Ashenvale's wildlife and furbolg tribes. Raene hopes restoring the rod will help her understand the furbolgs' plight.",al={"ashenvale corruption","why is ashenvale corrupted","iris lake danger"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Raene need you to take the gem to Shael'dryn?",a="As a Huntress and leader stationed at Astranaar, Raene Wolfrunner is tied to coordinating the defense of Ashenvale against rising demonic and territorial threats. She cannot abandon her post to delve into obscure magical research or journey out to distant moonwells. Since you recovered Teronis's journal and the gem from the murlocs, she trusts you to see the fallen scout's work through to the end.",al={"why send me to shael'dryn","why doesn't raene go","why me raene's cleansing"},it="why_me",add="3ee5b81a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Restoring the rod carries on Teronis's unfinished investigation into the troubles of Ashenvale's furbolgs.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, helping Shael'dryn serves your Cenarion duty to mend the broken bonds between nature and Kaldorei magic.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, helping secure ancient artifacts and strengthen Astranaar's northern perimeter supports the war effort against growing threats in the region."},kw={"ashenvale","dartol's rod","glowing gem","iris lake","moonwell","raene wolfrunner","raene's cleansing","shael'dryn","teronis"},rel={"npc:raene-wolfrunner","npc:shael-dryn","subzone:iris-lake","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","subzone:raynewood-retreat","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Raene Wolfrunner",["end"]="Shael'dryn",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1024},src={"Raene's Cleansing (3)"}}
E["quest:1025"] = {t="quest",n="An Aggressive Defense",z="ashenvale",s="Raene Wolfrunner sends Alliance defenders against the Foulweald furbolgs in Ashenvale. Corruption has made the tribe dangerous along the road east of Astranaar.",h="Raene Wolfrunner sends Alliance defenders against the Foulweald furbolgs in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Threat to the Highway",b="Furbolgs now attack travelers on the road east from Astranaar toward the Falfarren River. Sentinel Raene Wolfrunner sends capable defenders to strike the Foulweald camps just south of the highway. The attacks have made this vital road through Ashenvale dangerous for anyone who travels it.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter History",b="The Foulweald were once friends and allies of the night elves. For ages, the kaldorei and furbolgs shared a reverence for nature and the wild gods. The Burning Legion's invasion left a taint that shattered many furbolg minds. Peaceful neighbors became violent reavers, and innocent travelers now face their attacks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this task and where are they located?",a="Sentinel Raene Wolfrunner offers the defense from Astranaar, the principal night elf settlement in central Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","who gives an aggressive defense","raene wolfrunner location"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Ashenvale hostile?",a="The Foulweald fell to demonic taint left by the Burning Legion during the Third War. Their minds turned violent, driving them to attack travelers and former allies.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","foulweald hostile","furbolg corruption"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the Foulweald camps found?",a="The Foulweald camps lie south of the main road east from Astranaar, west of the Falfarren River.",al={"foulweald location","where to find foulweald","where are the furbolgs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Were the furbolgs always enemies of the night elves?",a="No. Furbolgs and night elves lived side by side in harmony for thousands of years. Demonic corruption in Ashenvale and Felwood drove tribes like the Foulweald to hostility.",al={"furbolg night elf lore","were furbolgs good","kaldorei and furbolgs"},it="history"},{q="Does this quest connect to other events in Astranaar?",a="Raene's strike is one part of Astranaar's defense. She also directs defenders to investigate corrupted moonwells and help cleanse the forest.",al={"quest prerequisites","raene cleansing connection"},it="ties"},{q="What specific furbolgs must be eliminated?",a="Raene calls for one Foulweald Den Watcher, two Ursas, ten Totemics, and twelve Warriors to be slain, breaking the tribe's command near the road.",al={"quest targets","who do i kill","foulweald targets"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Raene Wolfrunner want the Foulweald furbolgs culled?",a="Corrupted Foulweald furbolgs have set up camps south of the road leading east toward the Falfarren River. Driven mad and vicious by the forest's tainted state, they prey directly upon travelers and innocent wayfarers. Raene needs their aggressive numbers thinned to safeguard the road and ease the pressure on Astranaar's strained defenders.",al={"why kill foulweald","raene wolfrunner motive","why aggressive defense"},it="motive",add="bc4e30a1"},{q="Who are the Foulweald furbolgs you are sent to fight?",a="The Foulweald are a local tribe of furbolgs dwelling in Ashenvale whose minds have fallen to the dark, corrupting energies seeping through the woodland. Once reclusive neighbors to the night elves, their madness now manifests as bloodthirsty predation, prompting them to ambush travelers along the highway east of Astranaar.",al={"foulweald furbolgs who","what are the foulweald","who are the targets"},it="target",add="bea6b71d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you face the grim need to fight former forest kin whose minds corruption has taken.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance defender, you help keep the road from Astranaar to eastern outposts clear for supplies and travelers.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the Foulweald's madness as a warning of fel taint in Kalimdor's sacred wild places."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","falfarren","foulweald","furbolg","raene wolfrunner","sentinels"},rel={"npc:raene-wolfrunner","subzone:astranaar","topic:furbolg","topic:sentinels","zone:ashenvale","subzone:falfarren-river","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","quest:1066"},m={start="Raene Wolfrunner",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=1025},src={"An Aggressive Defense"}}
E["quest:1026"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Raene's Cleansing brings Dartol's Rod closer to being whole. Shael'dryn knows where its iron shaft lies, in a chest near the Felwood border. The search leads toward treants changed by corruption.",h="In Ashenvale, Raene's Cleansing brings Dartol's Rod closer to being whole.",sec={{t="A Fragment Near the Blight",b="Raene Wolfrunner sends you to Shael'dryn, a keeper who watches over a moonwell deep in Ashenvale. Shael'dryn knows where Dartol's Rod's iron shaft lies, but reaching it means facing the taint spreading through the northern woods. The shaft is locked in an old chest in a quiet glade near the Felwood border.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Guardians",b="A wooden key is needed to open the chest, and Crazed and Withered Ancients hold it. These treants wander the mountain road north toward Felwood, their natural harmony shattered by corruption spreading south from the demonic wastes. Once guardians of the wild, they are now tormented and hostile, and the key lies with them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shael'dryn?",a="Shael'dryn is a dryad at a secluded moonwell in Ashenvale, east of Astranaar and south of the Felwood road. She knows the forest's history and Dartol's ancient craft, and offers counsel to those trying to mend the rod.",al={"shaeldryn","who is the moonwell keeper","shael'dryn lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the treants corrupted?",a="Demonic taint from the Third War still spreads south from Felwood into Ashenvale. It warps the treants along the northern ridges, driving the ancient protectors mad and twisting their bond with the land.",al={"corrupted treants","why are treants crazy","crazed ancients lore"},it="threat"},{q="What is Dartol's Rod?",a="Dartol's Rod is an enchanted relic made by Dartol, a now-dead evil wizard. Once assembled and purified, it can disguise its bearer as a furbolg, a power Raene needs to investigate the local tribes.",al={"dartols rod","rod of transformation","what does the rod do"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="Where is the hidden chest located?",a="The worn chest holding the iron shaft rests in a small, quiet glade just west of the mountain road that climbs north from Ashenvale toward Felwood.",al={"worn chest location","where is the iron shaft","where is the chest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Shael'dryn mourn the treants?",a="Shael'dryn mourns the treants because they are timeless caretakers of the Kaldorei forests, revered as sacred spirits of nature. Their madness and corruption have no known cure, so putting them down brings sorrow, not malice.",al={"shaeldryn treants","why is shaeldryn sad"},it="motive"},{q="How does this task fit into the wider cleansing chain?",a="Raene's Cleansing gathers the physical pieces of Dartol's broken rod. Once the iron shaft and other pieces are gathered, the work turns to purifying the rod's lingering magic.",al={"raene's cleansing chain","raene questline"},it="history"},{q="What is the Iron Shaft?",a="The Iron Shaft is a key component of Dartol's Rod, an ancient relic whose magic lets its bearer take the guise of a furbolg. The rod's pieces were scattered, and this metallic segment was locked away inside a hidden chest near the border of Felwood.",al={"what is iron shaft","iron shaft dartol","iron shaft raenes cleansing"},it="item",add="348d2e5e"},{q="What is the Wooden Key for?",a="The Wooden Key opens the worn, hidden chest near the Felwood border containing a piece of Dartol's Rod. Long entrusted to the guardians of the glade, the key remains held by the ancient treants who have since fallen to madness and blight.",al={"what does wooden key do","wooden key purpose","why need wooden key"},it="item",add="410ea010"},{q="Why must you fight the treants for the key?",a="The withered and crazed ancients northeast near the Felwood border were once noble protectors of the forest, but demonic corruption seeping from the north has shattered their minds. Shael'dryn mourns their fall, yet because their nature is twisted beyond reason, the key they guard can only be recovered through force.",al={"why kill treants","crazed ancients why hostile","why attack withered ancients"},it="target",add="8a6f94e5"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Putting down the Crazed Ancients is agonizing. These living trees were beloved companions and forest wardens before the demonic blight poisoned their spirits.",["class:Druid"]="The ancients' madness, brought on by Felwood's encroaching taint, recalls the Emerald Dream's struggle to heal the wounded surface world.",["faction:Alliance"]="Rebuilding Dartol's relic is essential to securing northern Ashenvale's roads against rising hostilities from corrupted furbolgs and demonic forces."},kw={"ashenvale","crazed ancient","dartol's rod","felwood","iron shaft","moonwell","raene's cleansing","shael'dryn","withered ancient","wooden key"},rel={"npc:shael-dryn","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","subzone:raynewood-retreat","zone:felwood","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Shael'dryn",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1026,ri={"Iron Shaft","Wooden Key"}},src={"Raene's Cleansing (4)"}}
E["quest:1027"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Raene Wolfrunner and Shael'dryn seek Dartol's Rod's final piece. They hope the relic can help cleanse the forest and slow the furbolg attacks on its night elves.",h="In Ashenvale, Raene Wolfrunner and Shael'dryn seek Dartol's Rod's final piece.",sec={{t="The Ruins of Dor'Danil",b="The iron pommel of Dartol's Rod was entrusted to the night elf druids at Dor'Danil barrow den. Disaster struck the sanctuary, and its caretakers were slain. With their refuge overrun, the pommel's hiding place was lost. Scavengers and wandering oozes now consume what remains in the ruins east of the southern road.",sp=0},{t="Rebuilding Dartol's Legacy",b="Dartol was an evil wizard who has since died, but the rod he made holds transformative powers. Raene Wolfrunner and Shael'dryn seek to reassemble it, hoping it can help slow the furbolg attacks on Ashenvale's night elves. The iron pommel is the final piece Shael'dryn needs before she can try to mend the fractured rod at the moonwell.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the iron pommel?",a="The iron pommel is the final piece of Dartol's Rod. Without it, the relic cannot be reforged or channeled to cleanse Ashenvale.",al={"iron pommel","final rod piece","what is pommel"},it="item"},{q="What happened to the druids of Dor'Danil?",a="The druids at Dor'Danil barrow den were slain when their sanctuary fell. Their refuge now lies abandoned to lurking oozes and beasts, and Shael'dryn finds their fate painful to discuss.",al={"dordanil druids","who killed the druids","dor danil"},it="history"},{q="Where is Dor'Danil located?",a="Dor'Danil lies in southern Ashenvale, east of the main road toward the Barrens border and south of Splintertree Post.",al={"where is dordanil","dor danil location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Shael'dryn?",a="Shael'dryn is a dryad who tends a sacred moonwell in Ashenvale. She helps Raene Wolfrunner track down the scattered pieces of Dartol's Rod and guides their repair.",al={"shaeldryn","who is shaeldryn"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the pommel swallowed by oozes?",a="After the barrow den fell, gelatinous slimes infested the area and consumed discarded relics, chests, and corpses. The oozes engulfed the iron pommel along with the other debris.",al={"slime chest","pommel slime","why do slimes have it"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after finding the pommel?",a="When you return the pommel to Shael'dryn, she can begin repairing the rod. Once mended, it can help Raene Wolfrunner cleanse the forest.",al={"next step","what does shaeldryn do"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Shael'dryn want this done?",a="Shael'dryn is aiding Raene Wolfrunner's efforts to cleanse Ashenvale of corruption. Recovering the final piece of Dartol's Rod—the iron pommel—is crucial, as reuniting all components will allow Shael'dryn to reconstruct the ancient artifact so it can be restored to full power.",al={"why help shael'dryn","shaeldryn motive","why find the rod piece"},it="motive",add="414ae6aa"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the losses the Cenarion Circle and Kaldorei druids have suffered in Ashenvale when you visit Dor'Danil's desecrated grounds.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, recovering Dartol's heirloom honors Dor'Danil's fallen caretakers and the defense of ancient Kaldorei lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Ashenvale's defense against corruption matters to the Alliance's hold on northern Kalimdor, with Horde forces advancing from Splintertree."},kw={"ashenvale","dartol's rod","dor'danil","iron pommel","moonwell","raene's cleansing","shael'dryn"},rel={"npc:shael-dryn","zone:ashenvale","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},m={start="Shael'dryn",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1027,ri={"Iron Pommel"}},src={"Raene's Cleansing (5)"}}
E["quest:1028"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="At Shael'dryn's direction, Raene's Cleansing now leads you to a mountain shrine with the rebuilt Rod of Dartol. The basin there holds the magic needed to restore its enchantment.",h="At Shael'dryn's direction, Raene's Cleansing now leads you to a mountain shrine with the rebuilt Rod of...",sec={{t="A Path into the Heights",b="Shael'dryn sends you from her moonwell into Ashenvale's wild southeastern slopes. The ancient shrines of Ashenvale often stood high among mountain crags, far from roads and hidden beneath dense forest canopies. You must cross unmarked ground along the rock faces and climb winding trails known mostly to Sentinels and woodland hermits.",sp=0},{t="Restoring Dartol's Rod",b="A stone basin waits in a quiet forest alcove. Though dormant, the shrine holds protective magic placed there by night elves long ago. Rest the rebuilt Rod of Dartol in the basin, and the shrine's sleeping power awakens. Its magic flows into the rod, restoring its enchantment so it can cleanse the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the hidden shrine located?",a="The shrine lies in the mountains southeast of Shael'dryn's moonwell. Leave the main roads, skirt the rocky cliff faces, and look for a winding path up into the ridges.",al={"shrine location","where is the shrine","how to find shrine","hidden shrine path"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Dartol?",a="Dartol was an evil wizard who created the rod and is now dead. Raene hopes its magic will help investigate the furbolg attacks in Ashenvale.",al={"who is dartol","dartol lore","creator of the rod"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Dartol's Rod need to be placed in the shrine?",a="Shael'dryn could rebuild the broken rod, but its ancient enchantments had been drained. The hidden shrine holds untouched nature magic that can restore its power.",al={"why recharge rod","rod purpose","what does the shrine do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Shael'dryn?",a="Shael'dryn is a dryad who lives beside a quiet moonwell in eastern Ashenvale. She helps Raene Wolfrunner research relics and rites that could cleanse the tainted wilderness.",al={"shaeldryn","quest giver","priestess at moonwell"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after the rod is recharged?",a="After the shrine restores the rod's power, you can return it to Shael'dryn for use in Raene's investigation of Ashenvale's furbolgs.",al={"what next","after shrine","next step"},it="next_step"},{q="Is the shrine guarded?",a="The shrine is a peaceful sanctuary, but wild beasts and corrupt furbolg tribes prowl the surrounding mountains and forests, making the climb dangerous.",al={"are there mobs at shrine","shrine dangers"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Why does Shael'dryn want Dartol's Rod recharged?",a="Shael'dryn seeks to restore Dartol's Rod to fulfill the ongoing cleansing of Ashenvale. Reconstructing the broken pieces was only the first step; without bathing it in the ancient magic of the hidden mountain shrine, the rod remains an inert relic incapable of unlocking its dormant transformative power.",al={"why recharge dartol's rod","shael'dryn motive","why does shael'dryn want this done"},it="motive",add="c5f164a1"},{q="Why does Shael'dryn send you to the hidden shrine instead of going herself?",a="Shael'dryn remains bound to the moonwell at Iris Lake, attending to its sacred waters and aiding the defenders of Astranaar. Having already proven your mettle by recovering the shattered pieces of Dartol's Rod across Ashenvale, you are the one she trusts to brave the untamed mountain paths and locate the forgotten shrine.",al={"why doesn't shael'dryn go","why send me to shrine","why me shael'dryn"},it="why_me",add="da3545ca"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Ashenvale's hidden mountain shrines as quiet sanctuaries your ancestors made in the wilderness before the modern invasions.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can sense how the shrine's subtle resonance reflects the deep bond between ancient night elven craft and nature's wild energies.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help Raene Wolfrunner secure Astranaar and heal the corrupted lands of northern Kalimdor by restoring this relic."},kw={"ashenvale","basin","dartol's rod","hidden shrine","moonwell","raene's cleansing","reconstructed rod","shael'dryn"},rel={"npc:shael-dryn","zone:ashenvale","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale"},m={start="Shael'dryn",["end"]="Hidden Shrine",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1028},src={"Raene's Cleansing (6)"}}
E["quest:1029"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="At Iris Lake, Shael'dryn entrusts you with Dartol's Rod of Transformation, restored for Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar. You carry it back to report success and honor Teronis, the fallen scout.",h="At Iris Lake, Shael'dryn entrusts you with Dartol's Rod of Transformation, restored for Raene Wolfrunner in...",sec={{t="The Rod Restored",b="Dartol's Rod of Transformation has been reforged with components and ancient gem fragments gathered from corrupted reaches of Ashenvale. Near Iris Lake, the dryad Shael'dryn cleanses and renews its magic, then sends you across the forest roads to Astranaar. Raene Wolfrunner awaits the restored artifact.",sp=0},{t="Honoring Teronis",b="Teronis began the search for Dartol's rod, hoping it would slow the furbolg attacks on his people. A longtime friend of Raene, he died atop the island in Lake Falathim, cut down by murlocs who had taken the gem he sought. Bringing the restored rod to Raene marks a bittersweet victory, and gives purpose to the sacrifice Teronis never lived to see fulfilled.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Dartol's Rod of Transformation?",a="Dartol's Rod of Transformation is a magical rod created by Dartol, a deceased evil wizard. Restored, it can aid Raene's investigation of the furbolg attacks in Ashenvale.",al={"dartols rod","what does the rod do"},it="item"},{q="Who was Teronis?",a="Teronis was a young night elf sentinel Raene Wolfrunner tasked with finding components of ancient magic in Ashenvale. Murlocs took the gem he sought and killed him atop the island in Lake Falathim, leaving passing Alliance travelers to complete his mission.",al={"who is teronis","teronis death"},it="people"},{q="Who is Raene Wolfrunner?",a="Raene Wolfrunner is an experienced night elf sentinel commander in the heart of Astranaar. She oversees the defense of central Ashenvale against demonic taint, hostile satyrs, and corrupted local beasts.",al={"raene","raene wolfrunner"},it="leader"},{q="Who is Shael'dryn?",a="Shael'dryn is a dryad who lives near the moonwell east of Iris Lake. Her knowledge of the forest and its ancient relics lets her purify corrupted relics and restore ancient tools of power.",al={"shaeldryn","iris lake priestess"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You travel from the banks of Iris Lake in central Ashenvale west along the main trails to Astranaar, the zone's primary Alliance hub.",al={"quest location","where do i go"},it="place"},{q="What happens after presenting the rod to Raene?",a="Raene is relieved and proud that Teronis's final mission succeeded. Ashenvale's cleansing continues, and she seeks ways to use the rod's power against the woodland's persistent corruption.",al={"next quest","raenes cleansing continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Shael'dryn want you to bring the rod to Raene?",a="With Dartol's Rod of Transformation finally restored, Shael'dryn knows her part in its preparation is complete. Raene Wolfrunner oversees the Sentinels in Astranaar and originally tasked Teronis with investigating the foul corruption plaguing Ashenvale. Shael'dryn sends you back to Raene so the night elf leadership can put the finished relic to use and decide how best to continue Teronis's unfinished mission.",al={"why bring rod to raene","shael'dryn motive","why see raene wolfrunner"},it="motive",add="f5799a7d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, carrying Teronis's legacy brings closure to Astranaar and shows that fallen kin are remembered amid rising threats to Kalimdor's sacred groves.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, helping Raene Wolfrunner strengthens your standing among the reclusive Sentinels of Astranaar."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","dartol's rod","raene wolfrunner","raene's cleansing","shael'dryn","teronis"},rel={"npc:raene-wolfrunner","npc:shael-dryn","subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Shael'dryn",["end"]="Raene Wolfrunner",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1029},src={"Raene's Cleansing (8)"}}
E["quest:1030"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Raene Wolfrunner seeks a way to speak with an uncorrupted furbolg. Southeast of Mystral Lake, Krolg offers a rare glimpse of the surviving furbolgs’ resentment toward the night elves.",h="In Ashenvale, Raene Wolfrunner seeks a way to speak with an uncorrupted furbolg.",sec={{t="A Guise of Fur and Claw",b="Raene Wolfrunner believes the late night elf meant to use Dartol’s restored Rod of Transformation to approach the furbolgs in disguise. Ashenvale’s woods have grown perilous, and madness spreads through the tribes, leaving no path to direct diplomacy. The rod gives you the shape of a furbolg, so you can try to pass their territorial rage and find someone willing to speak.",sp=0},{t="The Exile's Bitterness",b="Southeast of Mystral Lake, Krolg lives apart from his kin, untouched by Fel Moss. Believing you are one of his own, he speaks freely of his exile and sorrow. He does not see the night elves as allies or protectors. Instead, he blames their pride and old failures for the demonic taint ravaging his people.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Dartol's Rod of Transformation do?",a="Dartol’s Rod of Transformation briefly changes its bearer into a furbolg. The disguise lets you approach uncorrupted furbolgs without provoking an immediate attack.",al={"what does the rod do","dartol rod transformation","furbolg disguise rod"},it="power"},{q="Who is Krolg?",a="Krolg is an uncorrupted furbolg living in exile southeast of Mystral Lake. He escaped the Fel Moss that infected his kin and lives alone across a torch-lined stream, mourning his lost tribe and resenting the night elves.",al={"who is krolg","uncorrupted furbolg mystral lake","furbolg southeast of mystral lake"},it="target"},{q="Why will Krolg attack if you don't use the rod?",a="Krolg fears and distrusts outsiders, especially night elves, whom he blames for his people’s downfall. Without the rod’s disguise, he sees you as an intruder and attacks to defend his camp.",al={"why does krolg attack","krolg aggressive","why use the rod on krolg"},it="hostile"},{q="Why does Krolg blame the night elves for the corruption?",a="Krolg blames night elven pride for the demonic corruption ravaging the forest. He sees the ancient Kaldorei’s arcane meddling as bringing ruin to Kalimdor and leaving its indigenous tribes to suffer.",al={"why does krolg hate night elves","furbolg blame night elves","krolg night elf hatred"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can Krolg be found?",a="Krolg lives southeast of Mystral Lake in Ashenvale. A winding dirt path marked by burning torches crosses a small stream and leads to his solitary camp.",al={"where is krolg","krolg location","find uncorrupted furbolg"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Fel Moss and how did it affect the furbolgs?",a="Fel Moss is a demonic growth spreading through Ashenvale, tainting the soil and plants. Its influence drove local furbolg tribes into violent madness and fractured their society.",al={"what is fel moss","fel moss furbolgs","why did furbolgs go mad"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Raene Wolfrunner want you to find an uncorrupted furbolg?",a="Raene hopes that the restored rod will let you approach an uncorrupted furbolg and learn more about his tribe's plight. She sends you toward the lands southeast of Mystral Lake to continue the investigation.",al={"why find uncorrupted furbolg","raene wolfrunner motive","why does raene need this"},it="motive",add="b9c958d0"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, Krolg’s words show that many of Ashenvale’s native inhabitants see the Kaldorei as reckless bringers of the land’s recurring ruin, not its guardians.",["class:Druid"]="For a druid, the furbolgs’ plight is a stark sorrow: once close allies of nature, they now suffer terrible madness from lingering demonic taint.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Astranaar’s survival depends on uncovering the dangers along the border roads. This secret meeting can help secure eastern Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","dartol's rod of transformation","fel moss","furbolg","krolg","mystral lake","raene wolfrunner","raene's cleansing"},rel={"npc:krolg","npc:raene-wolfrunner","topic:furbolg","subzone:mystral-lake","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Raene Wolfrunner",["end"]="Krolg",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1030},src={"Raene's Cleansing (9)"}}
E["quest:1031"] = {t="quest",n="The Branch of Cenarius",z="ashenvale",s="In eastern Ashenvale, Anilia's final plea sends you after the Branch of Cenarius. Geltharis has taken the sacred relic, and Illiyana waits for its return.",h="In eastern Ashenvale, Anilia's final plea sends you after the Branch of Cenarius.",sec={{t="A Dying Request",b="You find Anilia near death while searching eastern Ashenvale for missing dryads. The wounded daughter of Cenarius points north, toward the satyr ruins. With her last breaths, she names Geltharis as the one who took the Branch of Cenarius and begs you to recover it.",sp=0},{t="Corruption in the Ruins",b="Geltharis hides among the ancient elven ruins of Xavian. The satyrs are ancient servants of the Burning Legion, and they prize relics tied to Cenarius as trophies to defile and mock. Taking the branch from Geltharis can answer Anilia's plea and help defend Ashenvale's sacred plants from the corruption these servants spread.",sp=0},{t="Sorrow Among the Dryads",b="You return the branch to Illiyana, but Anilia is gone. The sacred relic is safe from demonic corruption, while the news of Anilia's death grieves her surviving kin. The dryads of Ashenvale must face war and the corruption closing in around them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Branch of Cenarius?",a="The Branch of Cenarius is a sacred nature relic linked to the forest lord Cenarius and cherished by his dryad daughters. Satyrs took it, and Anilia was mortally wounded while leading her sisters in the effort to recover it; with her last breath, she named Geltharis as the thief.",al={"branch of cenarius relic","what is the branch","cenarius branch"},it="item"},{q="Who killed Anilia?",a="Anilia was fatally wounded in the satyr-held ruins of Xavian while trying to recover the Branch of Cenarius. With her dying breath, she named Geltharis as the satyr who took it.",al={"anilia killer","who attacked anilia","who killed the dryad"}},{q="Where is Geltharis located?",a="Geltharis hides in the Xavian ruins, north of where Anilia lay dying.",al={"geltharis location","find geltharis","where to kill geltharis"},gp=true},{q="Where do I take the Branch of Cenarius once it is recovered?",a="Take the recovered branch to Illiyana at the Shrine of Aessina in Ashenvale.",al={"turn in branch of cenarius","illiyana location","who gets the branch"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do the satyrs want Cenarius's artifacts?",a="Satyrs are ancient night elves transformed by demonic pacts. They hate nature and Cenarius, and stealing or corrupting sacred relics serves their demonic masters and their spite against their former kin.",al={"satyr motives","why steal cenarius branch","why did geltharis take it"}},{q="Who was Anilia to Illiyana?",a="Anilia and Illiyana were close dryad companions, sisters in spirit who spent countless days running and playing freely in Ashenvale's wilds before corruption's dangers took Anilia's life.",al={"anilia and illiyana","are the dryads sisters"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Anilia want the Branch of Cenarius recovered?",a="With her dying breath, Anilia's sole desire is to ensure that the sacred relic of her father does not remain in the hands of the vile satyrs. She entrusted its recovery to you so that the Branch of Cenarius can be returned safely to her sister dryads rather than be defiled.",al={"anilia motive","why recover branch","anilia dying wish"},it="motive",add="4863107a"},{q="Who is Geltharis and why are you sent against him?",a="Geltharis is the satyr responsible for ambushing Anilia and stealing the Branch of Cenarius. He lurks among the ancient ruins to the north, having seized the sacred relic from the dying dryad.",al={"who is geltharis","why kill geltharis","geltharis lore"},it="target",add="9fd6df2e"},{q="Why does Anilia need you to retrieve the branch?",a="Anilia cannot retrieve the artifact herself because her wounds are fatal. As she draws you close to whisper her final words, she breathes her last breath, leaving you as the only one present to avenge her and fulfill her dying wish.",al={"why me branch of cenarius","why does anilia need help"},it="why_me",add="59d5db2f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Cenarius's daughters as beloved allies. Avenge Anilia and purge the satyrs defiling your ancestral forests.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold Cenarius's relics sacred because he taught the first mortal druids. Reclaiming his branch from a demon-tainted satyr is a spiritual imperative.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can aid Ashenvale's dryads as they push back demonic threats in the untamed east."},kw={"anilia","ashenvale dryads","branch of cenarius","geltharis","illiyana","night run","satyr"},rel={"quest:1021","npc:illiyana","topic:cenarius","topic:satyr","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Anilia",["end"]="Illiyana",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=1031,ri={"Branch of Cenarius"}},src={"The Branch of Cenarius (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1032"] = {t="quest",n="Satyr Slaying!",z="ashenvale",s="At the Shrine of Aessina, Illiyana asks Alliance champions to strike at the satyrs of Ashenvale. Grieving her sister Anilia, she seeks vengeance and asks you to bring back satyr horns as proof.",h="At the Shrine of Aessina, Illiyana asks Alliance champions to strike at the satyrs of Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Dryad's Grief",b="Anilia's death has left Illiyana in grief at the Shrine of Aessina. Dryads are forest spirits bonded to nature, often playful and serene, and elusive to mortals. Anilia's brutal slaying shattered that calm for her sister. Illiyana now turns to Alliance travelers to strike down the demonic beasts responsible.",sp=0},{t="The Corrupted Kin",b="Satyrs were once night elves, but demonic energy corrupted them during the War of the Ancients. They lurk in defiled groves across Ashenvale and prey on the woods' inhabitants as servants of the Burning Legion. Bringing Illiyana their horns gives proof of vengeance and strikes at the fel presence encroaching on eastern Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Illiyana?",a="Illiyana is a dryad who lives at the Shrine of Aessina in Ashenvale. Gentle by nature, she mourns her sister Anilia, who was slain by local satyrs.",al={"illiyana lore","who is the quest giver","forest song dryad"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Anilia?",a="Anilia was a dryad and Illiyana's beloved sister. They spent ages among Ashenvale's ancient canopies until satyrs ambushed and killed Anilia.",al={"anilia","illiyana sister","who died"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Illiyana ask for satyr horns?",a="Illiyana asks for satyr horns as proof that the creatures who killed Anilia have been slain. She hopes this will bring her sister's spirit peace.",al={"why satyr horns","satyr horn proof"},it="item"},{q="What are satyrs?",a="Satyrs are night elves corrupted and changed by the Burning Legion's demonic powers during the War of the Ancients. They dwell in corrupted enclaves, spreading taint and destroying forest spirits.",al={"satyr lore","what are the satyrs in ashenvale"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Forest Song?",a="Forest Song is an ancient, nearly abandoned night elf ruin in far eastern Ashenvale, near the border of Azshara. Illiyana waits at the Shrine of Aessina, not at Forest Song.",al={"forest song location","where is forest song"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is this connected to any other hunts?",a="Illiyana continues to accept satyr horns after Anilia is avenged. Ashenvale's defenders are still working to drive the satyrs from the forest.",al={"satyr horns quest","followup quest","repeatable satyr quest"}},{q="Why does Illiyana want the satyrs slain?",a="Illiyana is grieving the loss of her sister, Anilia, who was taken and killed by the vile satyrs lurking in Ashenvale. Crushed by the loss of her beloved childhood companion, she seeks solace in vengeance. Slaying the creatures responsible and seeing their severed horns offers her a grim sense of peace and honors her fallen sister's memory.",al={"why kill satyrs","illiyana motive","why does illiyana want revenge"},it="motive",add="f313c3da"},{q="Why are the satyrs in Ashenvale?",a="Satyrs are twisted night elves who succumbed to demonic corruption during the War of the Ancients, cursed into beast-like fiends serving the Burning Legion. Pockets of these immortal horrors linger in the dark, corrupted recesses of Ashenvale, such as Xavian and Night Run, constantly plotting to blight the sacred forests and butcher any kaldorei they catch unaware.",al={"why are satyrs here","satyrs in ashenvale","what are satyrs doing here"},it="target",add="45b4e644"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, avenging a fallen dryad and taking the horns of demonic satyrs strikes at the corruption in Cenarius's favored wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know satyrs as a shameful reminder of the Highborne's ancient fall into fel servitude. Helping Illiyana cleanses the land of this ancestral blight.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you help thin the satyr ranks and make Ashenvale's forest safer from the wild threats around you."},kw={"anilia","ashenvale","dryad","illiyana","satyr","satyr horns","satyr slaying"},rel={"npc:illiyana","topic:satyr","zone:ashenvale","quest:6441"},m={start="Illiyana",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=1032,ri={"Satyr Horns"}},src={"Satyr Slaying! (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1033"] = {t="quest",n="Elune's Tear",z="ashenvale",s="In Astranaar, Pelturas Whitemoon seeks a cure for his ailing daughter, Relara. The brew made from Bathran's hair slowed her sickness, but did not cleanse it. He asks you to bring Elune's Tear from Iris Lake, hoping its sacred power can drive the corruption from her.",h="In Astranaar, Pelturas Whitemoon seeks a cure for his ailing daughter, Relara.",sec={{t="A Father's Growing Panic",b="Pelturas Whitemoon's young daughter, Relara, lies gravely ill in Astranaar. He hoped a draught made from Bathran's hair would heal her, but though Orendil Broadleaf's brew slowed the sickness, it did not clear it from her body. Ordinary remedies have not been enough. Pelturas now turns to the old traditions of his people and seeks a cure touched by divine cleansing light.",sp=0},{t="The Stone of Iris Lake",b="Orendil Broadleaf named a stronger remedy in case the herbal brew failed: Elune's Tear, a sacred stone found on an island in Iris Lake, east of Astranaar. Night elves believe the stone bears the Moon Goddess's blessing and can purge corruption from the living. Troubled water elementals patrol the lake's shallows and banks, guarding its waters.",sp=0},{t="A Measure of Hope",b="When you bring the stone to Astranaar, Pelturas plans to steep it in a medicinal broth for Relara. He gives thanks, but the corruption still lingers, and her life remains in danger.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Elune's Tear?",a="Elune's Tear is a sacred stone found on the central isle of Iris Lake in Ashenvale. Night elven lore says it can cleanse severe poisons and lingering corruption.",al={"what is elunes tear","elune tear item","stone of iris lake"},it="item"},{q="Why did Orendil's previous cure fail?",a="Orendil Broadleaf's brew, made from Bathran's hair, slowed Relara's illness but could not overcome it. Pelturas turned to sacred remedies when herbs proved insufficient.",al={"why did orendil cure fail","did orendil cure work","relara still sick"},it="history"},{q="Where is Iris Lake located?",a="Iris Lake lies east of Astranaar in Ashenvale. Follow the main road east out of town, then take the dirt path north beside a stream that feeds the lake.",al={"where is iris lake","iris lake location","how to find iris lake"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What dangers lurk around Iris Lake?",a="Territorial water elementals inhabit Iris Lake and its central isle. Anyone approaching the isle to claim the Tear must pass these hostile nature spirits.",al={"iris lake enemies","what attacks at iris lake"},it="threat"},{q="How does Pelturas plan to use the stone?",a="Pelturas plans to steep Elune's Tear in a medicinal stew for his daughter Relara, hoping its cleansing power will drive out her affliction.",al={"how to use elunes tear","elunes tear stew"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Relara Whitemoon?",a="Relara Whitemoon is the young night elf daughter of Pelturas Whitemoon, and she lives in Astranaar. An unnatural corruption has left her gravely ill and threatens her life.",al={"who is relara","pelturas daughter"},it="people"},{q="Why does Pelturas Whitemoon want this done?",a="Pelturas is desperate to save his sick daughter, Relara. Orendil Broadleaf's initial remedy only managed to slow the insidious corruption ravaging her body rather than purge it. With time running out, Pelturas turns to the legendary curative powers of Elune's Tear as his best hope to cleanse the disease before it claims her life.",al={"why does pelturas want elunes tear","pelturas motive","why help pelturas"},it="motive",add="58c1c268"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the faith placed in sacred stones named for the Moon Goddess, and in Elune's grace to cleanse wounds ordinary remedies cannot reach.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest devoted to Elune, you know the faith placed in holy relics to fight dark, unnatural plagues when prayer calls for a physical aid.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the waters of Ashenvale and the erratic elementals that guard the quiet heart of Iris Lake.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help Astranaar's defenders through a personal crisis as danger grows across Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","cure","elune","elune's tear","iris lake","orendil broadleaf","pelturas whitemoon","relara","water elementals"},rel={"quest:1020","quest:1034","npc:pelturas-whitemoon","subzone:iris-lake","subzone:astranaar","topic:elune","quest:1010","quest:1035"},m={start="Pelturas Whitemoon",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1033,ri={"Elune's Tear"}},src={"Elune's Tear (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1034"] = {t="quest",n="The Ruins of Stardust",z="ashenvale",s="In Astranaar, Pelturas Whitemoon still seeks a cure for his daughter Relara. Elune's Tear eased her nightmares, but a fierce fever grips her. Orendil Broadleaf sends him south for cooling stardust among ancient night elven stones.",h="In Astranaar, Pelturas Whitemoon still seeks a cure for his daughter Relara.",sec={{t="A Father's Lingering Despair",b="Pelturas Whitemoon keeps vigil beside his daughter, Relara, as a malignant illness burns through her. Elune's Tear brought her some relief from the nightmares, but the sickness remains. A fierce fever still racks her, beyond the reach of ordinary medicines. With the temple healers stretched thin, Pelturas turns to old remedies drawn from nature, hoping to save her life.",sp=0},{t="The Glint of Stardust",b="Orendil Broadleaf, an elder herbalist, points Pelturas toward the Ruins of Stardust, south across the river from Astranaar. Frosted, shimmering dust settles on the plants among the fallen marble columns and archways of this ancient kaldorei sanctuary. The powder, called stardust, has a natural chill strong enough to draw out unnatural heat. Pelturas hopes to grind it into a poultice and ease Relara's fever.",sp=0},{t="Prowlers in the Waters",b="Water elementals and wildlife make gathering the frosted dust dangerous among the flooded stones. Elementals, corrupted or stirred by changes in Ashenvale's balance, surge around the sunken plazas where the bushes grow thickest. You wade into shallows that look calm, watching for ambushes from the murky depths. The sparkling bushes must yield enough clean dust to carry back to Astranaar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Pelturas need stardust?",a="Relara, Pelturas Whitemoon's daughter, suffers from a severe fever in Astranaar. Elune's Tear eased her nightmares, but the fever remains. Orendil Broadleaf says the frosted dust in the Ruins of Stardust can cool her in a poultice.",al={"why stardust","ruins of stardust purpose","relara fever cure"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Ruins of Stardust located?",a="The Ruins of Stardust lie south of Astranaar in central Ashenvale, around a small lake amid ancient, overgrown kaldorei stonework.",al={"ruins of stardust location","where is ruins of stardust","find stardust ruins"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is stardust in this context?",a="Stardust is frosted dust that gathers on vegetation by the lake. Pelturas hopes to use its cooling effect in a poultice for his daughter's fever.",al={"what is stardust","nature of stardust","stardust lore"},it="item"},{q="Does the stardust cure Relara completely?",a="Pelturas hopes a stardust poultice will lower Relara's fever. Whether it restores all her strength is learned after the treatment.",al={"does stardust cure relara","relara cured","is the girl saved"},sp=1},{q="What threats are found at the Ruins of Stardust?",a="Aggressive water elementals lurk beneath the surface of the flooded ruins and defend the waters. They threaten anyone wading through the shallows to search the shimmering bushes.",al={"ruins of stardust enemies","what attacks at ruins of stardust"},it="threat",gp=true},{q="Who is Orendil?",a="Orendil Broadleaf is a night elf herbalist who lives in northern Ashenvale near Maestra's Post. He has studied the region's plants for centuries and advises Pelturas on rare botanical remedies when temple treatments fall short.",al={"who told pelturas about stardust","orendil broadleaf"},it="people"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ruins south of Astranaar are remnants of ancient kaldorei civilization. Their lingering magic can still be put to use in healing.",["class:Priest"]="Elune's grace soothed Relara's nightmares, but the body may need earthly remedies alongside prayer to preserve mortal life.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Finding sparkling powder in the brush takes the knowledge to recognize rare plants in Ashenvale's damp places.",["class:Druid"]="To gather soothing stardust, you contend with perturbed water spirits in flooded ruins. Their presence speaks to Ashenvale's fragile balance."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","cure","elune","fever","orendil","pelturas","poultice","relara","stardust"},rel={"npc:pelturas-whitemoon","subzone:ruins-of-stardust","subzone:astranaar","quest:1033","quest:1035","quest:1020","quest:1010","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Pelturas Whitemoon",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=1034,ri={"Handful of Stardust"}},src={"The Ruins of Stardust (quest)"}}
E["quest:1035"] = {t="quest",n="Fallen Sky Lake",z="ashenvale",s="At Fallen Sky Lake, a moonstone may be the only hope for Relara, whose fever has broken but whose strength is nearly gone. Her father, Pelturas Whitemoon, sends you to the waters southeast of Astranaar, where a corrupted Shadethicket Oracle guards the fallen stones.",h="At Fallen Sky Lake, a moonstone may be the only hope for Relara, whose fever has broken but whose strength is...",sec={{t="A Daughter's Fading Breaths",b="Pelturas Whitemoon has watched his young daughter, Relara, slip closer to death through days of illness. Remedies made from Bathran's hair and stardust broke her raging fever, but left her body hollow and frail. Pelturas fears she has only breaths remaining before her spirit fades permanently into the night.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Moonstone",b="Pelturas turns to moonstones to restore Relara's strength. These celestial fragments once fell into Fallen Sky Lake, southeast of Astranaar, and night elves gathered them for their healing power. Aggressive elementals or corrupted bark now claim the stones, so gathering one means facing danger with blade and spell.",sp=0},{t="The Shadethicket Domain",b="Night elves lost easy access to Fallen Sky Lake when Shadethicket bog beasts claimed the surrounding wilderness. Their leader, the Shadethicket Oracle, hoards the fallen moonstones on an islet in the lake's center. To reclaim one, you must confront and slay the Oracle before Relara's strength runs out. Pelturas crushes the recovered stone into tea, and Relara drinks it and regains her strength.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Relara need a moonstone if her fever already broke?",a="Relara's fever drained her life force so severely that rest alone cannot revive her. Pelturas believes only a fallen moonstone's restorative power can renew her depleted spirit before she succumbs to exhaustion.",al={"why moonstone","relara still sick","relara fever gone"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Fallen Sky Lake located?",a="Fallen Sky Lake lies in central-eastern Ashenvale, southeast of Astranaar. Hostile bog beasts dominate its waters, which hold a small island at their center.",al={"where is fallen sky lake","lake location","shadethicket lake location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who has the fallen moonstone?",a="The Shadethicket Oracle, leader of the hostile bog beasts at the lake, holds the moonstone. The Oracle lairs on an island in the center of Fallen Sky Lake.",al={"who drops moonstone","shadethicket oracle location","where to get moonstone"},it="target"},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="This is the final step in Pelturas's search for a remedy. He needs a fallen moonstone to restore Relara's strength, and her fate is revealed when the stone is delivered.",al={"is there a follow up","what next","quest continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Shadethickets hoarding the moonstones?",a="As Ashenvale's wild creatures and bog beasts grow more volatile and corrupted, the Shadethickets begin violently driving off outsiders. Their Oracle gathers and guards the lunar relics, keeping them from the night elves of Astranaar.",al={"why treants taking stones","oracle hoarding moonstones"},it="why_here"},{q="What previous quests lead up to this task?",a="The chain begins with Bathran's Hair, followed by Orendil's Cure, Elune's Tear, and The Ruins of Stardust. Each step gathers rare components to treat Relara's worsening condition.",al={"chain before fallen sky lake","quest prerequisites","what comes before"},it="history",gp=true},{q="What is the Fallen Moonstone used for?",a="The fallen moonstones gathered around Fallen Sky Lake carry restorative magic tied to the night sky. While Relara's severe fever has broken, her body remains critically frail. Pelturas believes ordinary rest will not save her; only the concentrated mystical power within a moonstone can replenish her lost vitality before her strength gives out entirely.",al={"fallen moonstone use","what does the moonstone do","why fallen moonstone"},it="item",add="fb73f711"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, protecting Astranaar's young is a sacred duty shared by the community. Retrieving moonstones tied to Elune's blessings is an act of mercy and reverence.",["class:Druid"]="The hostile Shadethicket bog beasts show the tragic discord spreading through Ashenvale's natural guardians. Facing them weighs heavily on those seeking to restore balance.",["class:Priest"]="Fallen moonstones are sought for their divine energies. Their healing grace, tied to the Moon Goddess Elune, can help save a dying child.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Pelturas Whitemoon supports the Alliance's duty to defend Astranaar's citizens from the creeping corruption overtaking Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","fallen moonstone","fallen sky lake","pelturas whitemoon","relara","shadethicket oracle"},rel={"npc:pelturas-whitemoon","subzone:astranaar","quest:1034","quest:1033","quest:1020","quest:1010","zone:ashenvale","topic:elune"},m={start="Pelturas Whitemoon",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1035,ri={"Fallen Moonstone"}},src={"Fallen Sky Lake (quest)"}}
E["quest:1037"] = {t="quest",n="Velinde Starsong",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Melyria Frostshadow seeks word of the commander who came before her. Velinde Starsong vanished while fighting the corruption spreading from Felwood, and Melyria sends you to Darnassus for answers.",h="In Ashenvale, Melyria Frostshadow seeks word of the commander who came before her.",sec={{t="A Vanished Predecessor",b="Melyria Frostshadow keeps watch in Ashenvale, following Velinde Starsong, who once held the same post. A priestess, Velinde was charged with containing demonic corruption spreading south from Felwood. Early reports said she had the danger under control, but her campaign faltered over time. Then she vanished without warning or formal relief, leaving the fight unfinished and her fate unknown.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Terrace",b="Disturbing clues in the forest lead Melyria to send you to Darnassus. On the Warrior's Terrace, Sentinel commander Thyn'tel Bladeweaver oversees military deployments. The Sentinels know Velinde disappeared, but her command keeps the circumstances close. Thyn'tel will need persuading before sharing any deeper records.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Velinde Starsong?",a="Velinde Starsong was a priestess and Sentinel commander stationed in Ashenvale. She was charged with holding the northern border against demonic horrors from Felwood, then vanished from duty.",al={"velinde starsong lore","who is velinde","priestess velinde"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Sentinel Melyria asking about her now?",a="Melyria Frostshadow took Velinde's place after she disappeared. Discoveries in the Howling Vale have renewed her concern for what happened and for Ashenvale's safety.",al={"why investigate velinde","melyria quest reason"},it="motive"},{q="Where do I need to go to complete this quest?",a="Travel from Ashenvale to Darnassus, atop Teldrassil. Commander Thyn'tel Bladeweaver is stationed on the Warrior's Terrace.",al={"where to turn in velinde starsong","thyntel bladeweaver location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is Commander Bladeweaver reluctant to talk?",a="The Sentinels know Velinde went missing, but the details of her final missions are sensitive military matters. Darnassus's leaders do not share them lightly with outsiders.",al={"why secret","why wont thyntel speak"},it="why_here"},{q="What connection does Velinde have to Felwood?",a="Velinde led the Sentinels' effort to contain demonic corruption spreading from Felwood. Her campaign faltered after early success, shortly before she vanished.",al={"velinde felwood","what happened in felwood"},it="history"},{q="What quest leads directly into this one?",a="This follows The Howling Vale, where you investigate strange and hostile events deep in Ashenvale's forests.",al={"velinde starsong prerequisite","previous quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Melyria send you to Darnassus instead of going herself?",a="Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow was posted to Ashenvale specifically to take up Velinde Starsong's abandoned duties and contain the growing threats pressing down from Felwood. With the northern border perpetually unstable, she cannot abandon her frontier post to make the long journey back to Darnassus herself. An adventurer can travel freely to seek out Commander Thyn'tel Bladeweaver without leaving Ashenvale's defenses undermanned.",al={"why send me","why melyria doesn't go","why can't melyria go herself"},it="why_me",add="8a014bde"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf defender, you face the fate of a respected commander and priestess amid northern Kalimdor's fragile state after the Third War.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest of Elune, you may feel a kinship with a sister of the faith who fought to stem the demonic corruption from Felwood.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Darnassus's strict military protocol, which keeps battlefield disappearances within the Sentinel command."},kw={"ashenvale","darnassus","felwood","melyria frostshadow","sentinels","thyn'tel bladeweaver","velinde starsong","warrior's terrace"},rel={"npc:thyn-tel-bladeweaver","quest:1038","subzone:warrior-s-terrace","topic:sentinels","zone:ashenvale","zone:darnassus","zone:felwood"},m={start="Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow",["end"]="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1037},src={"Velinde Starsong (quest)"}}
E["quest:1040"] = {t="quest",n="Passage to Booty Bay",z="ashenvale",s="Wharfmaster Dizzywig’s records send the search for Velinde Starsong from Ratchet to Booty Bay. From there, Alliance travelers seek Ruzzgot, a goblin caravan driver.",h="Wharfmaster Dizzywig’s records send the search for Velinde Starsong from Ratchet to Booty Bay.",sec={{t="A Trail Across the Sea",b="Wharfmaster Dizzywig’s records carry the search for night elf Sentinel Velinde Starsong from Ashenvale to the sea. In Ratchet, the goblin port, Dizzywig finds old shipping manifests showing that Velinde booked passage on the Black Osprey. The vessel was bound for Booty Bay in Stranglethorn Vale.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Booty Bay",b="A neutral goblin ferry crosses the Great Sea between Ratchet and the southern tip of the Eastern Kingdoms. In Booty Bay, the trail leads to Caravaneer Ruzzgot, a goblin transport master Dizzywig recommended to Velinde. She had asked about dangerous overland journeys through the southern wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Velinde Starsong?",a="Velinde Starsong was a night elf priestess who led efforts to hold back the demonic presence in Felwood. Her efforts faltered, and she disappeared. The Sentinels are tracing her journey across the sea.",al={"velinde","who is velinde","velinde starsong lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Velinde travel to Booty Bay?",a="Velinde traveled to Booty Bay to seek passage across the Great Sea. The Black Osprey sailed from Ratchet to Booty Bay, where she asked about overland travel toward the human and dwarven kingdoms.",al={"why booty bay","velinde booty bay","why did she go to booty bay"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Wharfmaster Dizzywig?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig manages Ratchet’s shipping docks for the Steamwheedle Cartel. Impatient by nature, he keeps logbooks and passage manifests for vessels traveling between Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"dizzywig","who is dizzywig","wharfmaster"},it="people"},{q="Who is Caravaneer Ruzzgot?",a="Caravaneer Ruzzgot is a goblin teamster based in Booty Bay. He coordinates supply convoys and overland transport through the dangerous jungles of Stranglethorn Vale and beyond.",al={"ruzzgot","caravaneer ruzzgot","who is ruzzgot"},it="people"},{q="What ship did Velinde take?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig’s shipping records show that Velinde Starsong booked passage aboard the Black Osprey. The ship sailed from Ratchet across the Great Sea to Booty Bay.",al={"velindes ship","what boat did velinde take","black osprey"}},{q="How do I travel to Booty Bay from Ratchet?",a="The Steamwheedle Cartel runs a passenger ferry from Ratchet’s southern dock across the Great Sea. It docks at Booty Bay on the southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"getting to booty bay","how to get to booty bay","boat to booty bay"},gp=true},{q="Why does Wharfmaster Dizzywig want you to go to Booty Bay?",a="He has no personal stake in Velinde Starsong or her fate—he simply wants you out of his office. Dizzywig keeps the busy docks of Ratchet running, and digging through old shipping ledgers for an ancient passenger is already more courtesy than a goblin wharfmaster usually offers for free. Once he confirms she sailed on the Black Osprey and mentioned overland caravans, pointing you toward Caravaneer Ruzzgot across the sea in Booty Bay gets you to stop bothering him so he can get back to business.",al={"dizzywig motive","why does dizzywig send you","dizzywig booty bay why"},it="motive",add="416fbc17"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei, you have urgent reason to find Velinde Starsong. She disappeared with the Scythe of Elune, leaving a dangerous mystery in Ashenvale’s forests.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you need patience and diplomacy in neutral goblin ports like Ratchet and Booty Bay. Mercenaries and cartel bureaucrats are part of the way."},kw={"black osprey","booty bay","caravaneer ruzzgot","passage to booty bay","ratchet","scythe of elune","velinde starsong","wharfmaster dizzywig"},rel={"quest:1039","quest:1041","quest:1492","subzone:booty-bay","zone:ashenvale","topic:goblin"},m={start="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",["end"]="Caravaneer Ruzzgot",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1040},src={"Passage to Booty Bay"}}
E["quest:1041"] = {t="quest",n="The Caravan Road",z="ashenvale",s="In Booty Bay, the search for Velinde Starsong turns north toward Darkshire. Caravaneer Ruzzgot remembers the missing night elf priestess traveling with his caravan through Stranglethorn Vale.",h="In Booty Bay, the search for Velinde Starsong turns north toward Darkshire.",sec={{t="A Priestess in the Jungle",b="Caravaneer Ruzzgot remembers Velinde Starsong as a passenger on his caravan. The search for the missing night elf priestess has brought you from Ashenvale to Booty Bay, at the southern edge of Stranglethorn Vale. She traveled with his caravan through the jungle, an unusual journey for a night elf priestess.",sp=0},{t="North to Darkshire",b="Ruzzgot says he and Velinde parted ways as they traveled north through Stranglethorn Vale. She set out toward Duskwood, and her trail leads to Darkshire. Clerk Daltry keeps the town's records, including the names of unfamiliar travelers who enter. His ledger may hold the next clue to Velinde's whereabouts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Velinde Starsong?",a="Velinde Starsong is a night elf priestess of Elune who left her homeland in Kalimdor under mysterious circumstances. Her disappearance led to a search across the continents, following her trail from Ashenvale through the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"velinde","who is velinde","who are we looking for"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Velinde traveling with a caravan?",a="Velinde traveled through goblin territory with Caravaneer Ruzzgot's shipping outfit. She hired passage for the dangerous journey north through Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"why caravan","velinde caravan","ruzzgot caravan"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Clerk Daltry?",a="Clerk Daltry is Darkshire's town clerk and archivist in Duskwood. He records outsiders and visitors amid the strange occurrences and threats in the region.",al={"clerk daltry","daltry darkshire","who is daltry"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead after Darkshire?",a="After you consult Clerk Daltry's records, he directs you to Jonathan Carevin. Speaking with Jonathan begins the search into Velinde's stay in Duskwood through his family.",al={"next quest","what comes next","after darkshire"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is traveling from Booty Bay to Darkshire dangerous?",a="Stranglethorn Vale is home to predatory beasts, hostile troll tribes, and Bloodsail buccaneers. The journey north is dangerous, and travelers need to stay close to the main road.",al={"jungle danger","stranglethorn level","stranglethorn dangerous"},it="danger"},{q="Where did this investigation start?",a="The search began in Ashenvale, where night elf investigators noticed Velinde's unexplained departure with an artifact of great power. Clues pointed to a ship bound for the southern seas.",al={"starting point","where did chain start","ashenvale start"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Caravaneer Ruzzgot help you find Velinde?",a="Caravaneer Ruzzgot initially misjudged you, but after you proved yourself, he is willing to share what he knows in good faith. A night elf priestess traveling alongside his rough-and-tumble shipping outfit was unusual enough to stick in his memory. Having parted ways with Velinde Starsong on the road north, he has nothing to lose by pointing you toward Darkshire and its record-keeper.",al={"ruzzgot motive","why does ruzzgot help","why help find velinde"},it="motive",add="a495199a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may share your kin's concern over Velinde Starsong, a Sentinel priestess of Elune whose secretive actions have taken her to the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you carry news between neutral goblin ports and remote Alliance outposts such as Darkshire, linking places in a world fractured by recent wars."},kw={"booty bay","caravaneer ruzzgot","clerk daltry","darkshire","duskwood","stranglethorn vale","the caravan road","velinde starsong"},rel={"npc:clerk-daltry","subzone:darkshire","subzone:booty-bay","quest:1040","quest:1042","zone:stranglethorn","zone:ashenvale","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Caravaneer Ruzzgot",["end"]="Clerk Daltry",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1041},src={"The Caravan Road"}}
E["quest:1042"] = {t="quest",n="The Carevin Family",z="ashenvale",s="In Darkshire, the search for Velinde Starsong brings strangers to the Carevin family. Clerk Daltry points them to the hunters after hearing of wolf-men in Ashenvale.",h="In Darkshire, the search for Velinde Starsong brings strangers to the Carevin family.",sec={{t="A Trail of Claws and Shadows",b="The search for Velinde Starsong leads from Kalimdor’s ancient forests to Duskwood. In Darkshire, clerk Daltry finds no town record of an elven priestess staying there. But mention the savage wolf-men seen in Ashenvale, and he listens closely. Beasts like those have begun terrorizing the woods around town.",sp=0},{t="Hunters of the Night",b="The Carevin family hunts the horrors that trouble Duskwood. Known locally for tracking demons, undead, and other monsters, the family has already faced the wolf-men. Their tracker, Calor, recently hauled a grisly string of severed wolf-men heads through Darkshire’s streets. Clerk Daltry sends you to Jonathan Carevin, the stern head of the household, to learn what the hunters know about the worgen.",sp=0},{t="A Cold Reception",b="Jonathan Carevin meets strangers with deep wariness. The horrors consuming Duskwood leave him wary of anyone who arrives unannounced and asks about worgen. Before sharing what his hunters have learned about the beasts, he demands to know who stands before him and why they seek things best left buried in the dark.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Jonathan Carevin?",a="Jonathan Carevin leads the Carevin household in Darkshire. His family is known across the blighted region as seasoned hunters who track and slay demons, undead, and monstrous beasts.",al={"jonathan carevin","who is carevin","carevin family head"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Clerk Daltry direct you to the Carevin family?",a="Clerk Daltry has no record of the missing night elf Velinde Starsong, but recognizes the wolf-men you describe. The Carevins’ tracker, Calor, recently brought severed heads of these creatures into Darkshire, so Daltry sends you to the family for what they know.",al={"why see carevin","clerk daltry carevin","why go to jonathan"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Calor?",a="Calor is a hunter and tracker allied with the Carevin family in Darkshire. He recently marched through town with a string of severed worgen heads, a grim sign that the wolf-men are active nearby.",al={"calor","who is calor","carevin hunter calor"},it="people"},{q="How does this quest connect Ashenvale to Duskwood?",a="The search begins in Ashenvale, where Velinde Starsong has disappeared and worgen have appeared. Following the caravan route takes you across the sea from Kalimdor to Duskwood, where the same monstrous wolf-beasts have surfaced.",al={"velinde starsong connection","why duskwood","ashenvale to darkshire"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Jonathan Carevin so suspicious of strangers?",a="Duskwood is overrun by shadows, undead, and sinister forces, and its surviving residents have grown deeply wary. When a stranger arrives asking about deadly worgen, Jonathan suspects ill intent until you prove yourself.",al={"why carevin hostile","carevin suspicion"}},{q="What monsters do the Carevins specialize in fighting?",a="The Carevin family hunts monstrous threats, especially demons, undead, and strange beasts like the worgen that haunt Duskwood.",al={"carevin monsters","what do carevins hunt"},it="purpose"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, finding human monster hunters with severed heads of creatures tied to Velinde Starsong gives you an unsettling clue about her journey.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can recognize the Carevin family as a band of local beast hunters who pursue unnatural fiends and cursed predators.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see how isolated and watchful Duskwood’s settlements must be to endure the blighted woods."},kw={"calor","carevin","clerk daltry","darkshire","duskwood","jonathan carevin","velinde starsong","wolf-men","worgen"},rel={"npc:jonathan-carevin","npc:clerk-daltry","npc:calor","quest:1041","subzone:darkshire","quest:1037","topic:worgen","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Clerk Daltry",["end"]="Jonathan Carevin",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1042},src={"The Carevin Family"}}
E["quest:1043"] = {t="quest",n="The Scythe of Elune",z="ashenvale",s="In Darkshire, the trail of the Scythe of Elune leads into the worgen hunt. Jonathan Carevin sends you to Roland's Doom, where the beasts were first seen, linking an ancient night elf relic in Kalimdor to the worgen now troubling Duskwood.",h="In Darkshire, the trail of the Scythe of Elune leads into the worgen hunt.",sec={{t="A Hunt in the Dark",b="After tracing Priestess Velinde Starsong across Kalimdor and speaking with the Carevin household in Darkshire, you find common cause with Jonathan Carevin. Nightbane worgen have overrun southern Duskwood, driving miners out and threatening what remains of the township. Carevin does not fully understand the beasts' supernatural origin, but he recognizes the value of someone willing to hunt them. He points you toward Roland's Doom, the mine where the fiends were first sighted.",sp=0},{t="Ghosts of Roland's Doom",b="Deep in Roland's Doom, among packs of vicious Nightbane, an undisturbed mound of earth lies beneath the tunnels. Disturbing the soil reveals the lingering specter of Velinde Starsong. The night elf priestess came into this cave carrying the Scythe of Elune, but met her end beneath Duskwood. Velinde laments that the worgen she unleashed now run rampant, and that the Scythe granted by her goddess is lost.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I look for signs of the Scythe?",a="Search Roland's Doom, the abandoned mine in southeastern Duskwood. Fight through the Nightbane worgen to an undisturbed mound of earth in the tunnels.",al={"where is the scythe","scythe of elune location","roland's doom cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Jonathan Carevin?",a="Jonathan Carevin belongs to the Carevin family in Darkshire. With few defenders left against evil, he trades information with outsiders seeking to cull the worgen numbers.",al={"jonathan carevin","carevin darkshire"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Velinde Starsong in the mine?",a="An undisturbed mound of earth deep in Roland's Doom holds the answer to Velinde Starsong's fate and the Scythe's whereabouts. Examine it to learn what to carry back to Jonathan Carevin.",al={"velinde starsong fate","what happened to velinde"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="What is the Scythe of Elune?",a="The Scythe of Elune is a sacred night elf artifact received by Priestess Velinde Starsong. The Sentinels believe the goddess Elune granted it to her as a boon.",al={"what is the scythe","scythe of elune lore"},it="item"},{q="Why did the worgen appear in Duskwood?",a="Jonathan Carevin says the worgen appeared out of nowhere, and they were first found in Roland's Doom to the south. Signs of the Scythe of Elune in the mine reveal why they appeared.",al={"why worgen in duskwood","duskwood worgen origin"},sp=1,it="origin"},{q="Who is Calor?",a="Calor is an associate of the Carevin family in Darkshire. After your discoveries in Roland's Doom, Jonathan instructs him to focus entirely on containing the worgen threat.",al={"npc calor","who is calor"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Why does Jonathan Carevin want this done?",a="Duskwood is beset on all sides by monsters, and the worgen are among the deadliest predators stalking the darkened woods. Jonathan Carevin may not fully understand your pursuit of the Scythe of Elune, but he recognizes an opportunity. If your hunt drives back the beasts infesting Roland's Doom and uncovers how they arrived, it aids Darkshire's defense. The Night Watch has scarce resources to spare, so any information or cull of the feral pack directly helps protect the surviving townsfolk.",al={"why carevin help","jonathan carevin motive","why carevin wants scythe"},it="motive",add="48e90786"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Finding Priestess Velinde Starsong's final resting place reveals the terrible price paid when the Scythe of Elune passed beyond the Sisterhood's supervision.",["faction:Alliance"]="Unraveling the Nightbane worgen mystery gives Darkshire and the Alliance their first real answers about the horrors stalking southern Duskwood.",["class:Druid"]="The wild worgen loosed by the Scythe of Elune warn druids of the cost of forces beyond control."},kw={"calor","darkshire","duskwood","jonathan carevin","nightbane","roland's doom","scythe of elune","velinde starsong","worgen"},rel={"quest:1042","quest:1044","quest:1037","subzone:roland-s-doom","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","npc:jonathan-carevin","npc:calor"},m={start="Jonathan Carevin",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1043},src={"The Scythe of Elune (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1044"] = {t="quest",n="Answered Questions",z="ashenvale",s="The search for Velinde Starsong carries you from Ashenvale to Darnassus, where a report awaits.",h="The search for Velinde Starsong carries you from Ashenvale to Darnassus, where a report awaits.",sec={{t="A Tragic Truth",b="Velinde Starsong's trail runs from Ashenvale across two continents to the haunted groves and abandoned mines of Duskwood. She took up the Scythe of Elune to defend Kalimdor from demons, then used it to summon the ferocious worgen. Velinde lost control of them and died deep in Roland's Doom mine. Duskwood was left to face the monstrous fallout.",sp=1},{t="Return to Darnassus",b="After Velinde's journal is recovered and her fate learned, Jonathan Carevin in Duskwood sends you back to Teldrassil. Sentinel Thyn'tel Bladeweaver receives your report in Darnassus. Velinde was a close friend of High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, so her fate brings a personal and spiritual blow to the Sisterhood of Elune.",sp=1},{t="A Missing Artifact",b="Velinde's fate is known, but the Scythe of Elune is still missing. The goddess gave it as a sacred boon and weapon, and now it lies lost in the wild, far from the priestesses who revered it. Feral worgen roam across the Eastern Kingdoms, a lingering and unpredictable threat born from the scythe's loss.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest Answered Questions?",a="Answered Questions concludes the search for Velinde Starsong. Jonathan Carevin in Duskwood sends you to Darnassus to report her fate and the whereabouts of the Scythe of Elune to Thyn'tel Bladeweaver.",al={"answered questions quest","answered questions classic","end of scythe of elune quest"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Who was Velinde Starsong?",a="Velinde Starsong was a night elf priestess of Elune and Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow's predecessor in Ashenvale. Charged with holding back demons in Felwood, she received the Scythe of Elune, then disappeared. Her trail led across the sea to Duskwood.",al={"velinde starsong","who is velinde","what happened to velinde"},it="history"},{q="Where is the Scythe of Elune at the end of this quest?",a="The Scythe of Elune is still missing when you report to Thyn'tel Bladeweaver in Darnassus. Jonathan Carevin asks you to bring her what you learned.",al={"where is the scythe of elune","did we find the scythe","scythe of elune location"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="How is Tyrande Whisperwind connected to Velinde?",a="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and Velinde Starsong were close friends before Velinde disappeared. Her fate weighs heavily on night elf leaders.",al={"tyrande and velinde","high priestess connection"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Jonathan Carevin?",a="Jonathan Carevin is a human resident of Duskwood who helps you search the local mines. He vows to contain the worgen there, then sends you to Kalimdor to share what you found with Velinde's people.",al={"jonathan carevin","who gives answered questions"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Where does Thyn'tel Bladeweaver stand?",a="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver is in Darnassus, on the isle of Teldrassil. She serves the night elf leadership and oversees the search for missing sentinels and priestesses.",al={"where is thyntel bladeweaver","thyntel bladeweaver location","hand in answered questions"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Jonathan Carevin send you back to Darnassus?",a="Jonathan Carevin recognizes that what was uncovered in the mines of Duskwood reaches far beyond the Night Watch. Velinde Starsong served the night elves and the goddess Elune, and Carevin believes her fate—and the unsettling loss of the Scythe of Elune—is vital news that must be delivered directly to her people in Darnassus, rather than buried in the mines.",al={"why does jonathan carevin want this done","jonathan carevin motive","why return to darnassus"},sp=1,it="motive",add="6f485fee",bt={"q1022.6"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can help the leadership follow the trail of a missing priestess and a sacred artifact.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may feel the spiritual weight of Velinde's story: the power of Elune's gifts, and the danger of trying to bend unknown beasts to your will.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the ties between night elves in Kalimdor and the beleaguered human settlements of Duskwood, both facing shadowy threats."},kw={"answered questions","darnassus","duskwood","jonathan carevin","roland's doom","scythe of elune","thyn'tel bladeweaver","velinde starsong","worgen"},rel={"quest:1043","npc:thyn-tel-bladeweaver","npc:jonathan-carevin","zone:duskwood","zone:darnassus","topic:worgen","topic:elune","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Jonathan Carevin",["end"]="Thyn'tel Bladeweaver",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1044},src={"Answered Questions"}}
E["quest:1045"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="Disguised by Dartol's Rod of Transformation, adventurers gain the trust of Krolg, an uncorrupted furbolg near Lake Mystral. Disillusioned with both the arrogant night elves and the corruption rotting his own kin, Krolg asks for the death of the depraved chieftain Ran Bloodtooth so that the furbolgs can police their own.",h="Disguised by Dartol's Rod of Transformation, adventurers gain the trust of Krolg, an uncorrupted furbolg near...",sec={{t="A Bitter Hermit",b="Near the waters of Lake Mystral, Krolg keeps a secluded vigil. Displaced and weary, he carries deep resentment toward the night elves, whose ancient hubris he blames for bringing ruin upon Kalimdor and stirring the dark rot festering in Ashenvale. To reach him, seekers use Dartol's Rod of Transformation to walk among furbolgs undetected. Yet despite his bitter hatred of the kaldorei, Krolg does not seek senseless butchery or innocent deaths.",sp=0},{t="Policing Their Own",b="Rather than surrendering entirely to the demonic taint gripping the tribes, Krolg believes his people must remain accountable for their own deeds. The demonic corruption did not originate their flaws—it merely amplified their worst impulses. Ran Bloodtooth embodies this fall: already ruthless and power-hungry before the taint, Ran embraced the darkness eagerly, posing an existential threat to elves and innocent beasts alike. Krolg refuses to let such malice speak for all furbolgs.",sp=0},{t="A Shared Duty",b="By asking an outsider—disguised by Dartol's magic—to strike down Ran Bloodtooth and his elite guards, Krolg ensures justice is served without igniting further internal tribal strife. Ran's death strikes a blow against the encroaching madness, briefly uniting an embittered furbolg and an Alliance agent in a shared desire to cleanse the sacred woodland.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Krolg hate the night elves?",a="Krolg views the night elves as arrogant stewards whose historical meddling with dangerous magic brought corruption upon the land. He holds them responsible for the tainted state of Ashenvale and the suffering of the native tribes.",al={"krolg night elf hatred","why does krolg hate elves","krolg backstory"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Ran Bloodtooth?",a="Ran Bloodtooth is a corrupt and power-hungry furbolg chieftain camped in the mountains east of Lake Mystral. Driven mad by the dark forces poisoning Ashenvale, his lust for violence poses a threat to all natural creatures in the forest.",al={"ran bloodtooth lore","who is bloodtooth","ran bloodtooth"},it="target"},{q="Why does Krolg want Ran Bloodtooth dead?",a="Even though Krolg resents the night elves, he draws the line at wanton savagery against the innocent. He believes the furbolgs must police their own evil and that Ran's corruption has turned him into a monster who threatens the entire forest.",al={"why kill ran bloodtooth","krolg motive bloodtooth"},it="motive"},{q="How can Alliance players speak to Krolg without being attacked?",a="Alliance heroes use Dartol's Rod of Transformation, an enchanted rod obtained during the quest chain, to take on the guise of a furbolg and safely approach Krolg.",al={"how to talk to krolg","dartols rod krolg","why is krolg friendly"},gp=true},{q="Where is Ran Bloodtooth located?",a="Ran Bloodtooth and his guards maintain an encampment along the mountains east of Krolg's refuge near Lake Mystral.",al={"ran bloodtooth location","where is ran bloodtooth","bloodtooth camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does killing Ran Bloodtooth help cleanse Ashenvale?",a="Killing Ran Bloodtooth removes one of the most violent, taint-empowered furbolgs, a threat to every natural creature in the forest. As Krolg puts it, the forest is still tainted, but it is a small part of returning it to its former glory.",al={"cleansing ashenvale ran","why is bloodtooth part of raenes cleansing"},it="purpose"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Confronting Krolg offers night elves an uncomfortable mirror: despite thousands of years guarding Ashenvale, local tribes hold kaldorei pride directly accountable for the ancient sundering and lingering taint.",["class:Druid"]="For druids dedicated to preserving Ashenvale's balance, Ran Bloodtooth represents the tragic fall of natural creatures yielding entirely to demonic corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aided by Dartol's enchanted rod, Alliance champions act as clandestine intermediaries to quell rogue chieftains deep behind enemy lines."},kw={"ashenvale","bloodtooth guard","corruption","dartol's rod","furbolg","krolg","lake mystral","ran bloodtooth"},rel={"npc:krolg","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Krolg",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1045},src={"Raene's Cleansing (10)"}}
E["quest:1046"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="In Astranaar, Raene's Cleansing reaches its end as you return with Ran Bloodtooth's skull. The search began with Teronis and now leaves Ashenvale's furbolg threat diminished.",h="In Astranaar, Raene's Cleansing reaches its end as you return with Ran Bloodtooth's skull.",sec={{t="A Bitter Trophy",b="After Ran Bloodtooth falls, Krolg sends you back to Astranaar. You carry the chieftain's severed skull to Sentinel Raene Wolfrunner, proof that the threat prowling the forest depths has been struck down.",sp=0},{t="In Memory of Teronis",b="Raene Wolfrunner sets Ran Bloodtooth's skull beside Dartol's Rod in a place of reverence. The grim token honors Teronis, whose investigation into cleansing the corrupted furbolgs began this desperate effort.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ran Bloodtooth?",a="Ran Bloodtooth was the fiercest corrupted furbolg threat in Ashenvale's forests. His defeat removes a chieftain who preyed on the woodland.",al={"ran bloodtooth","bloodtooth skull","who was ran bloodtooth"}},{q="Why does Raene Wolfrunner want the skull?",a="Raene Wolfrunner keeps Ran Bloodtooth's skull beside Dartol's Rod to honor victory and remember the danger overcome. The skull proves that the Sentinel forces and their allies struck down a mortal threat to Ashenvale.",al={"why skull","wolfrunner skull","what does raene do with the skull"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was Teronis?",a="Teronis was a night elf investigator whose death early in the search spurred the hunt for the cleansing gemstones and Dartol's Rod. Finishing the work carries forward his unfinished mission.",al={"teronis","who is teronis","teronis proud"},sp=1},{q="Where does this quest end?",a="You complete the work in Astranaar by speaking with Sentinel Raene Wolfrunner, in Ashenvale's main night elf settlement.",al={"turn in location","where is raene","raene wolfrunner location"},gp=true},{q="Who is Krolg?",a="Krolg is an ally who sends you to carry Ran Bloodtooth's severed skull back to Astranaar, where your people can recognize the victory.",al={"krolg","who gives quest","npc krolg"},it="identity"},{q="What is Dartol's Rod?",a="Dartol's Rod is an enchanted relic assembled during the chain of events. It has deep magical ties to furbolg nature and cleansing.",al={"dartol's rod","rod of transformation","furbolg rod"},it="item"},{q="Why does Krolg send you to Astranaar?",a="With Ran Bloodtooth, the fiercest furbolg threat in Ashenvale, slain, Krolg recognizes your triumph. An uncorrupted furbolg who takes you for one of his own kind thanks to Dartol's Rod, he gives you Ran's skull and tells you to return to your own tribe, show them the trophy, and bask in the glory of your victory.",al={"why does krolg want this done","krolg motive","why krolg skull astranaar"},it="motive",add="d3b35236"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, ending Ran Bloodtooth's fury honors fallen allies such as Teronis and helps reclaim Ashenvale's sacred groves.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, delivering Bloodtooth's skull shows your people's commitment to defending Astranaar alongside the night elf Sentinels."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","dartol's rod","furbolg","krolg","raene wolfrunner","raene's cleansing","ran bloodtooth","teronis"},rel={"npc:raene-wolfrunner","subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","topic:sentinels","npc:krolg","topic:alliance"},m={start="Krolg",["end"]="Raene Wolfrunner",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1046},src={"Raene's Cleansing (11)"}}
E["quest:1054"] = {t="quest",n="Culling the Threat",z="ashenvale",s="In Astranaar, fear grows as the Thistlefur furbolgs multiply to the north. Raene Wolfrunner calls for Dal Bloodclaw's death before the tribe can assault the town.",h="In Astranaar, fear grows as the Thistlefur furbolgs multiply to the north.",sec={{t="A Looming Peril to the North",b="Astranaar stands in the heart of Ashenvale, with danger close on every side. The Thistlefur furbolgs dwell just north of town. Once peaceful forest dwellers, they have fallen to madness and aggression, as have many of their kin. Sentinel scouts have watched their numbers swell over recent months. Now they fear a coordinated attack on Astranaar is only a matter of time.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Chieftain",b="Raene Wolfrunner calls travelers to strike before the Thistlefur overrun Astranaar's modest palisades. Dal Bloodclaw leads the tribe, giving its members order and courage. The Sentinels ask for his skull, brought back to Astranaar. They hope his death will break the furbolgs' coordination and buy the beleaguered town precious time.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Culling the Threat?",a="Raene Wolfrunner, a Sentinel commander in the night elf town of Astranaar, asks you to act.",al={"quest giver","who starts culling the threat","where do i get culling the threat"},gp=true},{q="Why does Astranaar want Dal Bloodclaw dead?",a="Dal Bloodclaw leads the Thistlefur tribe just north of Astranaar. Their numbers are multiplying rapidly, and Raene Wolfrunner fears he will lead an attack on the town unless his leadership is broken.",al={"why kill dal bloodclaw","dal bloodclaw lore","why attack thistlefur"},it="motive"},{q="Why are the Thistlefur furbolgs hostile to the night elves?",a="Furbolgs and night elves were once allies, but demonic and corrupting influences across Ashenvale have driven many tribes, including the Thistlefur, into violent frenzy and territorial paranoia.",al={"why do furbolgs attack","corrupted furbolgs ashenvale","thistlefur lore"},it="hostile"},{q="Where can Dal Bloodclaw be found?",a="Dal Bloodclaw is in Thistlefur Village and its nearby barrows, directly north of Astranaar in Ashenvale.",al={"dal bloodclaw location","where is dal bloodclaw"},gp=true},{q="Does killing Dal Bloodclaw solve the furbolg threat permanently?",a="No. Raene Wolfrunner says Dal Bloodclaw's death stifles the Thistlefur's aggression only for a time. While corruption grips Ashenvale, the furbolg population remains a danger.",al={"is thistlefur defeated","did we save astranaar"},it="threat"},{q="What proof of Dal Bloodclaw's death is required?",a="You need to bring Dal Bloodclaw's Skull directly to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.",al={"what do i bring raene","culling the threat turn in item"},it="item"},{q="Who is Dal Bloodclaw?",a="Dal Bloodclaw is the chieftain of the Thistlefur furbolgs residing in their village directly north of Astranaar. Under his leadership, the corrupted furbolgs have multiplied rapidly over recent months, threatening to overwhelm the surrounding woods and launch a full-scale assault on the night elf settlement.",al={"who is dal bloodclaw","who is the furbolg chieftain","dal bloodclaw lore"},it="target",add="d8b26d15"},{q="Why does Raene Wolfrunner need an adventurer instead of the Astranaar sentinels?",a="The Sentinels stationed in Astranaar are stretched thin guarding the town itself against encroaching threats from all sides. Raene Wolfrunner must remain behind to coordinate local defenses, making capable travelers the ideal choice to slip into Thistlefur territory and strike down their leader before an attack materializes.",al={"why send me","why doesn't raene send guards","why astranaar sentinels not attacking"},it="why_me",add="05594dd8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you face the sorrow of striking down ancient allies corrupted by madness, while taking brutal measures to protect Astranaar from ruin.",["faction:Alliance"]="You know Astranaar is vital to Alliance supply lines and communication across central Kalimdor, so danger north of town demands urgent action.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the Thistlefur's madness with deep sorrow. The lingering taint on Ashenvale drives noble furbolgs into bloodthirsty beasts."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","culling the threat","dal bloodclaw","furbolg","raene wolfrunner","thistlefur"},rel={"npc:raene-wolfrunner","subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","zone:darnassus","topic:elune"},m={start="Raene Wolfrunner",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=1054,ri={"Dal Bloodclaw's Skull"}},src={"Culling the Threat"}}
E["quest:1055"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="At the hidden shrine in Ashenvale, Raene's Cleansing reaches a turning point. The Rod of Transformation is assembled and its magic restored, and you must return it to Shael'dryn at her moonwell sanctuary.",h="At the hidden shrine in Ashenvale, Raene's Cleansing reaches a turning point.",sec={{t="A Restored Relic",b="At the hidden shrine in Ashenvale, you have restored the Rod of Transformation. Its shaft, pommel, and glowing gem are joined, and the rod has been re-enchanted. Shael'dryn needs it for Raene's investigation of the furbolg attacks.",sp=0},{t="Return to Shael'dryn",b="Shael'dryn waits beside the forest moonwell, where she has guided the rod's restoration. You bring her the finished relic and confirm its magic has returned. Then the Sentinel defenders can take their next steps to protect their besieged homeland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this stage of the quest?",a="You have assembled the Rod of Transformation at the hidden shrine. Return it to Shael'dryn, who waits at the moonwell in northern Ashenvale.",al={"what to do raenes cleansing 7","what is this quest","quest goal"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Shael'dryn?",a="Shael'dryn is a dryad who tends a sacred moonwell in Ashenvale. She works to cleanse the ancient forest of spreading corruption and directs trusted allies to gather relics, purify components, and restore sacred artifacts.",al={"shaeldryn","who is shael'dryn","priestess at moonwell"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Shael'dryn located?",a="Shael'dryn waits at a quiet moonwell in northern Ashenvale, east of the main road between Astranaar and Felwood. The tranquil waters are in her care.",al={"shael'dryn location","where is shaeldryn","where moonwell"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Rod of Transformation?",a="The Rod of Transformation is Dartol's magical creation. Its restored power is meant to help Raene investigate the furbolgs; the form it grants is discovered later.",al={"what is rod of transformation","rod of transformation lore","the rod"},it="item"},{q="Why is assembling the rod so important to Astranaar?",a="Raene Wolfrunner hopes the rod will let an investigator approach the furbolgs and learn more about the attacks threatening Astranaar.",al={"why raenes cleansing","why astranaar cares","raene importance"},it="threat"},{q="Does assembling the rod end the cleansing chain?",a="No. Shael'dryn next asks you to return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar and tell her the rod is finished.",al={"is this the last quest","does raenes cleansing end here","chain end"},it="next_step"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, restoring the rod helps Raene investigate the furbolg attacks threatening Astranaar and the surrounding groves.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, securing Ashenvale matters to your standing in northern Kalimdor and helps protect Astranaar from local corruption and hostile forces.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you help Shael'dryn restore a magical relic Raene needs for her investigation in Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","elune","hidden shrine","moonwell","raene's cleansing","rod of transformation","shael'dryn"},rel={"npc:shael-dryn","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Hidden Shrine",["end"]="Shael'dryn",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1055},src={"Raene's Cleansing (7)"}}
E["quest:1133"] = {t="quest",n="Journey to Astranaar",z="ashenvale",s="Fiora Longears sends Alliance travelers from Theramore north to Astranaar. There, they report to Shindrell Swiftfire in Ashenvale, where the night elves face war and unrest.",h="Fiora Longears sends Alliance travelers from Theramore north to Astranaar.",sec={{t="From the Coast into the Woods",b="Alliance travelers arrive in Dustwallow Marsh aboard the ferry from Menethil Harbor, often seeking purpose in northern Kalimdor. At Theramore, Fiora Longears directs capable hands inland toward Astranaar, Ashenvale's main night elven settlement. The route winds beneath ancient, shadowed canopies and leads into a forest strained by war and unrest.",sp=0},{t="An Unspoken Recommendation",b="Fiora tells travelers not to mention her name in Astranaar because Shindrell Swiftfire does not know her. Fiora's role is to direct fresh Alliance talent where it is needed. Shindrell welcomes able-bodied defenders when they arrive. Ashenvale remains breathtaking, but it is no longer the peaceful sanctuary it once was.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Journey to Astranaar quest begin?",a="The journey begins with Fiora Longears in Theramore, on the coast of Dustwallow Marsh. She offers it to Alliance travelers from the Eastern Kingdoms who seek to help in Kalimdor.",al={"who gives journey to astranaar","journey to astranaar start","where to pick up journey to astranaar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who do I need to talk to in Astranaar?",a="Speak with Shindrell Swiftfire, a night elf in Astranaar, the central Alliance town in Ashenvale.",al={"where to turn in journey to astranaar","journey to astranaar end npc","who is shindrell swiftfire"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Fiora say not to mention her name?",a="Fiora says not to mention her name because Shindrell does not know her personally. She directs eager newcomers to an outpost in need of assistance.",al={"why not mention fiora","fiora longears connection to shindrell"},it="motive"},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It leads Alliance travelers from Dustwallow Marsh into Ashenvale and introduces them to Astranaar, their main base in the forest.",al={"why do journey to astranaar","journey to astranaar lore purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What kind of trouble is happening in Ashenvale?",a="Ashenvale is no longer tranquil. Horde incursions, demonic corruption lingering from the Third War, and local wildlife stirred by recent conflicts trouble the forest.",al={"why does astranaar need help","ashenvale troubles lore"},it="danger"},{q="What quest leads into Journey to Astranaar?",a="The journey follows a short introduction called Fiora Longears, which directs travelers arriving in Dustwallow Marsh to speak with her in Theramore.",al={"journey to astranaar prerequisite","fiora longears chain"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Fiora Longears send you to Astranaar?",a="Fiora sees fresh Alliance travelers arriving at Theramore and directs capable adventurers where they are needed most. Astranaar is the central night elf settlement in Ashenvale, a region currently fraught with escalating dangers and hostile incursions. She points you toward Shindrell Swiftfire so your skills can immediately aid the Alliance's strained defense of the ancient forest.",al={"why send to astranaar","fiora longears motive","why does fiora send you"},it="motive",add="5f2da217"},{q="Why does Fiora ask you to go instead of going herself?",a="Fiora remains at Theramore Inn in Dustwallow Marsh and directs willing travelers to Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar, where their help is needed.",al={"why me journey to astranaar","why doesnt fiora go to astranaar","why not fiora"},it="why_me",add="432055d5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit, you travel from the relatively safe ports of Dustwallow Marsh into Ashenvale's contested wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you return to your heartland under siege and defend Ashenvale's sacred boughs alongside foreign allies.",["race:Human"]="As a human arriving from Menethil Harbor, you take your first steps into Kalimdor's interior and honor the Alliance pledge to aid the night elves."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","theramore","dustwallow marsh","fiora longears","journey to astranaar","menethil harbor","shindrell swiftfire"},rel={"subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","npc:shindrell-swiftfire","quest:1132","topic:alliance"},m={start="Fiora Longears",["end"]="Shindrell Swiftfire",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=1133},src={"Journey to Astranaar"}}
E["quest:1134"] = {t="quest",n="Pridewings of Stonetalon",z="ashenvale",s="In the Stonetalon Mountains, pridewing venom has become a threat to the uneasy peace. Shindrell reports an unconfirmed claim from Theramore that orc assassins gather the poison for covert raids. Astranaar's Sentinels send scouts south to claim the venom sacs first.",h="In the Stonetalon Mountains, pridewing venom has become a threat to the uneasy peace.",sec={{t="A Fragile Truce",b="The Alliance and Horde have not declared open war across northern Kalimdor, but their peace is fragile. Skirmishes break out beneath the forest canopy, and quiet attacks take the place of full armies. Sentinel commanders in Astranaar watch for enemy movements, knowing a careless moment could put their sanctuary at risk.",sp=0},{t="Poison from the Crags",b="Shindrell reports an unconfirmed claim from contacts in Theramore about activity in the crags of Stonetalon. Orcish stalkers are said to gather venom from wild pridewings around Mirkfallon Lake and coat their blades for deadly ambushes against Alliance forces. Shindrell Swiftfire sends champions to kill the beasts and claim their venom sacs before Horde agents can reach them.",sp=0},{t="A Painful Duty",b="Shindrell Swiftfire regrets ordering the deaths of native beasts. Night elves revere Kalimdor's wilderness, and the creatures had no part in choosing this war. Yet Astranaar's defenders cannot let an enemy gather poison for lethal attacks, even at the cost of the beasts' lives.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are pridewings?",a="Pridewings are dangerous, venomous flying beasts related to wyverns. They nest in high crags, especially around Mirkfallon Lake in the Stonetalon Mountains, and their venom makes them deadly predators and a sought-after poison.",al={"what are pridewings","pridewing lore","stonetalon pridewings"},it="target"},{q="Why is the Alliance hunting them?",a="Shindrell reports an unconfirmed claim that Horde assassins gather pridewing venom to coat weapons for covert attacks on Alliance positions. The Alliance hunts the beasts to claim their venom sacs first and deny the Horde that poison.",al={"why kill pridewings","quest purpose","alliance pridewing venom"},it="motive"},{q="Who provided the intelligence about the orc assassins?",a="The warning came from hidden Alliance informants in Theramore, who watch Horde movements and supply lines throughout the southern Barrens and Stonetalon.",al={"who warned the alliance","theramore spy info","shindrell intel source"}},{q="Where is Mirkfallon Lake located?",a="Mirkfallon Lake lies in the northern Stonetalon Mountains, just south of the border trail from Ashenvale.",al={"mirkfallon lake location","where are the pridewings","find pridewings"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Are the Alliance and Horde at open war in Ashenvale?",a="The Alliance and Horde have no declared open war in Ashenvale, but covert killings, resource skirmishes, and border clashes continue beneath the forest canopy.",al={"are horde and alliance at war","ashenvale war status","peace treaty ashenvale"},it="conflict"},{q="How does Shindrell Swiftfire feel about killing the beasts?",a="Shindrell Swiftfire grieves that she must order the deaths of beasts that chose no side in the conflict. As an officer defending Astranaar, she sees the hunt as a painful necessity to protect her people.",al={"shindrell reaction","druidic guilt","night elf killing beasts"}},{q="What is the Pridewing Venom Sac for?",a="Shindrell Swiftfire has you harvest the venom sacs to prove the beasts are culled and to deny the Horde a lethal supply. Unconfirmed intelligence from Theramore warns that orc assassins harvest venom from Mirkfallon Lake's pridewings to coat their weapons for covert raids against the Alliance. By gathering the sacs yourself, you ensure that poison never reaches enemy blades.",al={"pridewing venom sac use","why collect venom sacs","what does shindrell do with venom sacs"},it="item",add="9b2e4c3f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you face the hard choice of killing wild pridewings to keep their venom from the enemy, despite your care for nature.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an ally of the Alliance, you see how Theramore's quiet intelligence network supports Sentinel outposts in Ashenvale against Horde attacks.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know how deadly pridewing venom can make a coated blade in a hidden ambush.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may grieve for the innocent creatures killed to keep their poison from warmongers."},kw={"assassins","astranaar","mirkfallon lake","pridewings","shindrell swiftfire","stonetalon mountains","theramore","venom"},rel={"npc:shindrell-swiftfire","subzone:mirkfallon-lake","zone:stonetalon","subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},m={start="Shindrell Swiftfire",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=1134,ri={"Pridewing Venom Sac"}},src={"Pridewings of Stonetalon"}}
E["quest:1918"] = {t="quest",n="The Befouled Element",z="ashenvale",s="Around Mystral Lake, you find glowing globes of tainted water among the slain elementals. You carry a specimen to Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post to learn what has poisoned the lake and its spirits.",h="Around Mystral Lake, you find glowing globes of tainted water among the slain elementals.",sec={{t="Tainted Waters of Mystral Lake",b="Mystral Lake lies in south-central Ashenvale, and its water elementals have grown violently aggressive and visibly corrupted. When slain, they leave strange, intensely glowing spheres of putrid fluid instead of pure elemental essence. The globes hold the corruption that has settled over the lake, showing that something more than natural territorial aggression is at work.",sp=0},{t="Seeking Splintertree's Counsel",b="Horde scouts seek guidance at Splintertree Post, where Mastok Wrilehiss oversees the outpost. He is disgusted by the vile specimen. A soldier rather than a scholar, Mastok knows mundane steel cannot cure diseased water, so he points you toward the elemental specialists of the Earthen Ring.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Befouled Water Globe?",a="The Befouled Water Globe holds a disgusting, concentrated sample of the corruption poisoning Mystral Lake. It forms from slain elementals, showing that their spiritual corruption has taken physical and potent form.",al={"befouled globe contents","what is in the water globe","mystral lake water globe"},it="item"},{q="Where does this quest begin?",a="You find the globe while fighting enraged or befouled water elementals at Mystral Lake in south-central Ashenvale.",al={"where do i find the water globe","how to start the befouled element","quest start"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Why does Mastok Wrilehiss want nothing to do with it?",a="Mastok Wrilehiss is a Horde officer focused on military survival and logistics at Splintertree Post. He has no affinity for diagnosing diseased magical waters, so he points you toward the Earthen Ring.",al={"who is mastok","why talk to mastok","mastok wrilehiss role"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Earthen Ring's interest in this?",a="The Earthen Ring is an order of shamans devoted to studying, soothing, and restoring harmony to the elements. Corrupted elementals like those at Mystral Lake fall under their spiritual care.",al={"why earthen ring","earthen ring connection","who are the earthen ring"},it="ties"},{q="Where does the investigation lead next?",a="Mastok points you toward Je'neu Sancrea, an Earthen Ring shaman stationed along Ashenvale's western shore at Zoram'gar Strand. Je'neu can examine the tainted relic.",al={"what comes next","next quest after befouled element","where do i go next"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you hear the pain in Mystral Lake's twisted spirits and know the Earthen Ring must intervene.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Splintertree Post cannot let an elemental menace threaten its backyard while Alliance sentinels and furbolgs menace Horde supply routes.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you feel a deep cultural duty to heal the land's corrupted waters, making Mystral Lake's restoration an urgent spiritual task."},kw={"ashenvale","befouled water globe","corrupted elementals","earthen ring","mastok wrilehiss","mystral lake","splintertree post"},rel={"npc:mastok-wrilehiss","subzone:mystral-lake","subzone:splintertree-post","quest:824","quest:25","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Befouled Water Globe",["end"]="Mastok Wrilehiss",faction="Horde",id=1918},src={"The Befouled Element"}}
E["quest:1944"] = {t="quest",n="Waters of Xavian",z="ashenvale",s="Deino seeks a sample from the waters of Xavian, deep in Ashenvale. The troll mage hopes to study the ancient city's lingering arcane power, and sends her apprentice to draw water from its highest waterfall.",h="Deino seeks a sample from the waters of Xavian, deep in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Mage's Curiosity",b="Deino, a troll mage in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits, searches Kalimdor for traces of primal arcane energy. Her attention turns to Xavian, an ancient night elf city hidden beneath Ashenvale's eastern canopy. Scholars say the city held great magical knowledge before the Sundering. Its waters are believed to retain arcane power that modern mages hope to understand.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Xavian",b="Xavian lies in ruins, overrun by feral, corrupt satyrs who defend their ground from outsiders. To reach the water, you travel past Satyrnaar and through dangerous waterways, avoiding prowling beasts and demonic sentinels. Deino needs a sample from the pool at the base of the city's highest waterfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deino?",a="Deino is a troll mage trainer and scholar in Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits. She teaches Horde mages and studies relics of ancient Kalimdor magic.",al={"who gives waters of xavian","deino orgrimmar"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Xavian located?",a="Xavian is a ruined city in northeastern Ashenvale, north of Splintertree Post and northwest of Satyrnaar.",al={"xavian location","where is xavian","finding xavian"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Deino want this water?",a="Deino wants to study the water's lingering arcane power. Scholars say Xavian held great magical knowledge, and she needs a fresh sample from the waterfall's source to examine its properties.",al={"why get xavian water","purpose of xavian water"},it="motive"},{q="What dangers guard the ruins of Xavian?",a="Satyrs overrun Xavian. These demonic, corrupted beings despise trespassers and guard their territory against intruders.",al={"xavian enemies","who controls xavian"},it="threat"},{q="Where exactly is the water sample collected?",a="You collect the sample from the pool at the base of Xavian's highest waterfall and place it in Deino's flask.",al={"waterfall location","where to fill flask","xavian waterfall"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What comes next after returning the sample to Deino?",a="After you return the sample, Deino sends you to study the dryads in Ashenvale.",al={"waters of xavian followup","next quest after waters of xavian"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Xavian Water Sample for?",a="The ancient city of Xavian is legendary among scholars for its forgotten knowledge, and its waters are reputed to hold vast magical powers. Deino wants an untainted sample scooped directly from the base of the city's highest waterfall so she can study its latent arcane properties back in Orgrimmar.",al={"what does xavian water do","why gather xavian water","xavian water sample use"},it="item",add="6a4223ea"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Horde mage, you study arcane reagents by venturing into hostile wilderness to collect them.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can use Splintertree Post as the nearest staging ground in eastern Ashenvale before traveling through the satyr-infested wilds around Xavian."},kw={"ashenvale","deino","flask","mage quest","orgrimmar","satyr","splintertree","waters of xavian","xavian"},rel={"npc:deino","subzone:xavian","quest:1945","quest:1943","zone:ashenvale","subzone:satyrnaar","subzone:splintertree-post","topic:satyr"},m={start="Deino",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1944,ri={"Xavian Water Sample"}},src={"Waters of Xavian"}}
E["quest:1945"] = {t="quest",n="Laughing Sisters",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, dryad hair is sought for an empowered robe. The experienced troll tailor Kil'hala at the Crossroads needs the enchanted locks to weave a mage robe, as Horde mages press against the woodland's native defenders.",h="In Ashenvale, dryad hair is sought for an empowered robe.",sec={{t="Weaving the Arcane",b="After securing water from Xavian, rising mages are sent by Deino in Orgrimmar to help craft their own enchanted vestments. These arcane garments need materials touched by raw magic. Dryad locks carry the forest's ancient vitality, giving them what is needed to weave intricate robes that shield and strengthen a caster.",sp=0},{t="Stalking Raynewood",b="Mages seek the laughing sisters near Raynewood Retreat in Ashenvale. These nimble dryads ally with the night elves and fiercely guard their groves from woodsmen and outsiders. They will not willingly give their hair to Horde spellcasters, so the locks are taken by force beneath the ancient trees.",sp=0},{t="The Weaver's Prerogative",b="The locks travel south across the border to the dusty settlement of the Crossroads in the Barrens. There, troll tailor Kil'hala receives them without remorse. Kil'hala acknowledges the woodland creatures' loss with a touch of irony, then puts the enchanted strands to use, knowing Horde power demands resolve.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns the quest to hunt the Laughing Sisters?",a="Deino, a troll mage at Darkbriar Lodge in Orgrimmar, sends mages to gather what is needed for their mage class robes.",al={"who gives laughing sisters quest","laughing sisters quest giver","deino quest"},gp=true},{q="What are the laughing sisters?",a="The laughing sisters are dryads, daughters of the demigod Cenarius. With night elf women's upper bodies and fawn-like lower bodies, they protect Ashenvale's woodlands and sacred clearings.",al={"what is a laughing sister","laughing sister dryad","are laughing sisters dryads"},it="target"},{q="Where can the laughing sisters be found?",a="They roam the forest near Raynewood Retreat and the Laughing Sister clearing in central Ashenvale, not far from the trade road.",al={"laughing sisters location","where are laughing sisters","where to find laughing sisters"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Kil'hala need dryad hair?",a="Dryad hair carries natural enchantment, making it suitable thread for Kil'hala to weave into specialized robes that resonate with magic and suit the arcane arts.",al={"why dryad hair","why laughing sister hair","what is the hair for"},it="item"},{q="Where do I deliver the hair once it is collected?",a="Take the hair to Kil'hala, a tailor at the Crossroads in the Barrens.",al={"where is kilhala","turn in laughing sisters","crossroads tailor warlock"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Kil'hala takes the hair?",a="Kil'hala works briefly with the hair, then offers Nether-lace Garment to finish the robe.",al={"next quest after laughing sisters","after laughing sisters","nether lace garment follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Deino send you to hunt the Laughing Sisters?",a="Deino is rewarding your ongoing service to the Horde's mages by arranging the crafting of specialized robes. Rather than simply gifting them to you, she demands that you gather the exotic magical reagents yourself, sending you deep into Ashenvale to wrest dryad hair from the forest's defenders.",al={"why does deino want laughing sisters hair","deino motive laughing sisters","why collect laughing sister hair"},it="motive",add="6db1d5c5"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, this rite of passage shows how even Ashenvale's sacred woodland spirits are harvested for arcane craft.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you see the rare art of weaving living magical fibers into cloth armor, using the high-level technique Kil'hala practices at the Crossroads.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you strike at Ashenvale's dryads and deepen the conflict with the sacred forest guardians allied with the night elves."},kw={"ashenvale","crossroads","deino","dryad","hair","kil'hala","laughing sisters","raynewood","warlock robe"},rel={"quest:1944","quest:1946","npc:kil-hala","npc:deino","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","subzone:raynewood-retreat"},m={start="Deino",["end"]="Kil'hala",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1945,ri={"Laughing Sister's Hair"}},src={"Laughing Sisters"}}
E["quest:2"] = {t="quest",n="Sharptalon's Claw",z="ashenvale",s="Ashenvale's trails grow safer when Sharptalon's Claw is taken from the forest. Bring the trophy to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post to prove Sharptalon has fallen and protect Horde supply lines.",h="Ashenvale's trails grow safer when Sharptalon's Claw is taken from the forest.",sec={{t="A Scourge of the Forest Trails",b="Sharptalon hunts the paths to Splintertree Post as the Horde seeks resources in Ashenvale. The aggressive hippogryph strikes peons and couriers traveling between forward logging camps and the outpost. Its attacks hinder Horde work in the region, where night elven sentinels and dangerous wildlife both threaten the newcomers.",sp=0},{t="Proof of the Hunt",b="Senani Thunderheart, a tauren huntress, directs Horde hunters against Ashenvale's deadliest predators. Sharptalon's talon proves the hippogryph has fallen. Bring the trophy to Splintertree Post, where the outpost's defenders honor the hunt and frightened laborers can walk the woods with less fear.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sharptalon?",a="Sharptalon is a fierce, predatory hippogryph that hunts in Ashenvale. It ambushes travelers moving through the forest.",al={"who is sharptalon","sharptalon mob","what kind of beast is sharptalon"},it="target"},{q="Why does Senani Thunderheart want the claw?",a="Senani Thunderheart wants the claw as proof that Sharptalon, a predator threatening Horde workers and supply routes, has been killed.",al={"why turn in claw","senani thunderheart trophy","purpose of sharptalon's claw"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do I turn in Sharptalon's Claw?",a="Bring the claw to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post in eastern Ashenvale.",al={"where turn in","who takes the claw","claw hand in location"},gp=true},{q="How does killing Sharptalon help the Horde?",a="Sharptalon attacks peons traveling between remote lumber mills and Splintertree Post. Killing it makes travel safer for supplies, lumber, and messengers.",al={"why kill sharptalon lore","horde interest in sharptalon"},it="purpose"},{q="Is this quest part of a larger chain?",a="Yes. It belongs to The Ashenvale Hunt, Senani Thunderheart's series of beast hunts, which ends with The Hunt Completed.",al={"ashenvale hunt chain","quest chain sharptalon"},gp=true},{q="Who is Senani Thunderheart?",a="Senani Thunderheart is a tauren huntress at Splintertree Post. She watches the forest's balance and tests Horde hunters against Ashenvale's most dangerous creatures.",al={"senani lore","who is senani"},it="identity"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure trails for Warsong lumber operations and protect peons traveling between forward outposts and Splintertree Post.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you test your tracking and marksmanship against Sharptalon, a feared flying predator beneath Ashenvale's thick canopy.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you follow Senani Thunderheart's hunt and test yourself against nature's fiercest beasts, as tauren tradition demands.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you ease the Warsong clan's hard work gathering wood by removing an aerial threat from the forest."},kw={"ashenvale","ashenvale hunt","hippogryph","peons","senani thunderheart","sharptalon","splintertree post","warsong"},rel={"quest:235","quest:247","npc:senani-thunderheart","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Sharptalon's Claw",["end"]="Senani Thunderheart",level="30",faction="Horde",id=2},src={"Sharptalon's Claw (Classic)"}}
E["quest:23"] = {t="quest",n="Ursangous's Paw",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Ursangous's Paw proves you brought down one of the forest's fiercest predators. Bring it to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post to earn honor among the Horde's trackers.",h="In Ashenvale, Ursangous's Paw proves you brought down one of the forest's fiercest predators.",sec={{t="A Trophy of the Great Hunt",b="The Ashenvale Hunt sends trackers from Splintertree Post after the ancient beasts that rule the forest canopy. Ursangous is among the fiercest, known for killing travelers and warriors who cross his path. Bringing back his paw proves the mighty beast has fallen to your hunt.",sp=0},{t="The Night Elf Connection",b="A quarter-crescent mark is carved or pressed into Ursangous's paw. Senani Thunderheart recognizes it as a sign of kaldorei influence. Night elves train and bond with formidable forest beasts to defend their sacred borders, so Ursangous may have been more than a wild predator: he may have guarded or served as a weapon for the Alliance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Ursangous?",a="Ursangous is an exceptionally massive, deadly bear that roams Ashenvale. Hunters and wayfarers fear him, and he claimed countless lives before the Horde's hunt brought him down.",al={"who is ursangous","ursangous bear","ursangous lore"},it="target"},{q="What does the crescent emblem on the paw mean?",a="The quarter-crescent mark on the paw is a mystery when you inspect the trophy. Senani Thunderheart can examine it when you bring her the paw.",al={"crescent mark on paw","paw emblem","why is there a crescent"},it="origin"},{q="Who do I bring Ursangous's Paw to?",a="Bring Ursangous's Paw to Senani Thunderheart, the tauren huntress at Splintertree Post in eastern Ashenvale.",al={"where turn in paw","who wants ursangous paw","senani thunderheart location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="How does this fit into the Ashenvale Hunt?",a="Ursangous is one of three great beasts hunted in Ashenvale, alongside Shadumbra and Sharptalon. Defeat all three and present their trophies to complete the rite.",al={"ashenvale hunt chain","what is the hunt","hunting quest line"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Horde hunting the great beasts of Ashenvale?",a="Horde hunters, especially the tauren and orcs at Splintertree Post, hunt these deadly beasts to test their martial prowess and curb threats near their vulnerable supply lines and encampments.",al={"why hunt bears","splintertree hunting lore"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after turning in the paw?",a="After you collect Ursangous's trophy and those of the other designated quarry, Senani Thunderheart will acknowledge your triumph in the concluding trial, The Hunt Completed.",al={"next quest after paw","what follows ursangous"},it="next_step"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren hunter, taking Ursangous's paw honors the beast and shows your martial resolve and respect for the spirits of the hunt.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can earn honor at Splintertree Post by defeating the dangerous Ursangous.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking and defeating one of Ashenvale's oldest and deadliest predators tests your fieldcraft, survival, and combat skill."},kw={"ashenvale","ashenvale hunt","bear","crescent emblem","paw","senani thunderheart","splintertree post","ursangous"},rel={"npc:senani-thunderheart","quest:235","quest:247","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Ursangous' Paw",["end"]="Senani Thunderheart",level="24",faction="Horde",id=23},src={"Ursangous's Paw (quest)"}}
E["quest:24"] = {t="quest",n="Shadumbra's Head",z="ashenvale",s="At Splintertree Post, Shadumbra's Head is proof that a feared predator has fallen. Bringing it to Senani Thunderheart completes a trial of the Ashenvale Hunt and helps secure the western roads toward the Zoram Strand.",h="At Splintertree Post, Shadumbra's Head is proof that a feared predator has fallen.",sec={{t="A Menace of the Western Road",b="Shadumbra hunted the woods west of Splintertree Post, where Horde scouts and couriers traveled toward the Zoram Strand. Her speed and stealth made those paths perilous, and each westward patrol kept the post's defenders wary.",sp=0},{t="Proof of the Hunt",b="Senani Thunderheart, a tauren huntress, challenges Horde champions to track and fell Ashenvale's great beasts as part of the Ashenvale Hunt. Shadumbra's head proves the hunter has brought down one of Kalimdor's deadliest native stalkers, and that travelers can use the roads with less danger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Shadumbra?",a="Shadumbra was a savage nightsaber that prowled the forests west of Splintertree Post. She ambushed travelers heading toward the coast and was counted among Ashenvale's most dangerous local beasts.",al={"what is shadumbra","shadumbra lore","who is the cat"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Senani Thunderheart want the head?",a="Senani Thunderheart oversees the Ashenvale Hunt at Splintertree Post. The head honors a difficult hunt and confirms that westward travelers are no longer threatened by Shadumbra.",al={"why bring head","senani thunderheart trophy","ashenvale hunt proof"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this fit into the Ashenvale Hunt?",a="Shadumbra's hunt is one of the primary trials of the Ashenvale Hunt. Slaying her alongside other great forest beasts such as Ursangous and Sharptalon leads to final recognition and The Hunt Completed.",al={"what is ashenvale hunt","hunt questline","next hunt quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is clearing this beast important to the Horde?",a="Scouts and runners travel west from Splintertree Post to the Horde encampment at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand. Shadumbra threatened those on foot as they crossed the untamed woods.",al={"why horde care","zoram strand road danger","splintertree post safety"},it="threat"},{q="Where can Shadumbra be found?",a="Shadumbra prowls the woodlands west of Splintertree Post, among the trees between the road and the ancient night elf ruins scattered through central and western Ashenvale.",al={"shadumbra location","where is shadumbra","find shadumbra"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Shadumbra allied with the night elves?",a="No. Shadumbra is a wild, feral nightsaber that threatens any who cross her territory. Though night elves often tame and revere nightsabers, she acts on predatory instinct.",al={"is shadumbra a pet","sentinel pet","shadumbra night elf"},it="allies"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor the Earth Mother's natural order by testing your skill against an apex predator and protecting your tribal brothers on the road.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you test your marksmanship, patience, and woodland survival when you track an elusive nightsaber like Shadumbra.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep the supply lines from isolated Splintertree Post open to the Zoram Strand by removing threats like Shadumbra."},kw={"ashenvale hunt","nightsaber","senani thunderheart","shadumbra","splintertree post","trophy","zoram strand"},rel={"quest:235","npc:senani-thunderheart","subzone:splintertree-post","quest:247","subzone:zoram-strand","zone:ashenvale","quest:1008"},m={start="Shadumbra's Head",["end"]="Senani Thunderheart",level="27",faction="Horde",id=24},src={"Shadumbra's Head (Classic)"}}
E["quest:247"] = {t="quest",n="The Hunt Completed",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, the hunt tests a Horde champion against three legendary predators. Felling Ursangous, Shadumbra, and Sharptalon proves strength, tenacity, and primal prowess in a contested forest.",h="In Ashenvale, the hunt tests a Horde champion against three legendary predators.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Proof",b="Senani Thunderheart tests travelers among the Horde forces in Ashenvale. Her hunt tests more than loyalty to the warchief; it asks whether a hunter understands survival in the wild. Three legendary predators are its quarry: the bear Ursangous, the cat Shadumbra, and the fierce hippogryph Sharptalon. Felling all three and securing their trophies proves a hunter's blood runs true.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Ancestors",b="For the tauren, hunting is a sacred act of balance and respect, even in an active warfront. Overcoming Ashenvale's greatest terrors honors the spirits of the land and earns a hunter the ancestral blessings of Thunderheart. A formal commendation and token of favor mark the hunt's end, while the champion's reputation spreads throughout the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest and where are they located?",a="Senani Thunderheart, a tauren hunter, offers the hunt among the Horde forces in Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","where to turn in","senani thunderheart location"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What are the requirements to complete the hunt?",a="You must slay three great predators and bring proof of their deaths: Ursangous's paw, Shadumbra's head, and Sharptalon's claw.",al={"what beasts to kill","prerequisites","which animals"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does Senani Thunderheart want these beasts slain?",a="The hunt tests strength and tenacity. Felling such formidable beasts proves a traveler has the heart and instincts of a predator able to survive Ashenvale's dangerous wilderness.",al={"why hunt them","senani motive","purpose of hunt"},it="motive"},{q="What is the cultural significance of the hunt to the Horde?",a="For tauren like Senani Thunderheart, testing your mettle against mighty beasts is an honorable tradition that honors the spirits and ancestors. It shows mastery of the wilderness without reckless dishonor.",al={"tauren hunt lore","cultural meaning","why do tauren hunt beasts"},it="history"},{q="Is this trial recognized by the entire Horde?",a="Yes. Completing the hunt marks you as a proven hunter to the Horde forces in Ashenvale. You earn ancestral blessings and the respect of your comrades.",al={"horde recognition","is it official","horde commendation"},it="ties"},{q="Which three beasts are targeted in the Ashenvale hunt?",a="The three targets are Ursangous the great bear, Shadumbra the nightsaber, and Sharptalon the hippogryph.",al={"the three beasts","hunt targets","named animals"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What beasts were you tasked with slaying for the Ashenvale hunt?",a="The trial demanded you track and fell three of Ashenvale's most ferocious predators: the ancient bear Ursangous, the elusive nightsaber Shadumbra, and the fierce hippogryph Sharptalon. These wild beasts ruled the forest canopy and thickets, posing severe threats to travelers while serving as the ultimate test of strength, patience, and hunting skill in the untamed wilderness.",al={"what beasts did i kill","ashenvale hunt targets","which beasts hunt completed"},it="target",add="ded238b8"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you prove your tracking and marksmanship against three of Ashenvale's greatest predators. Your instincts must match the wild beasts.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor a time-honored test of respect, balance, and ancestral pride by hunting Ursangous, Shadumbra, and Sharptalon.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure your people's foothold in Ashenvale, a dangerous woodland filled with predators and Alliance sentinels."},kw={"ashenvale","beasts","hunt","predator","senani","shadumbra","sharptalon","thunderheart","trophy","ursangous"},rel={"quest:235","npc:senani-thunderheart","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},m={start="Senani Thunderheart",level="30",faction="Horde",id=247},src={"The Hunt Completed"}}
E["quest:25"] = {t="quest",n="Stonetalon Standstill",z="ashenvale",s="At Mystral Lake, befouled water spirits have halted Horde supply transports on the way to Stonetalon. Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post sends you to clear the hostile elementals and scout a night elf gazebo overlooking Silverwind Refuge.",h="At Mystral Lake, befouled water spirits have halted Horde supply transports on the way to Stonetalon.",sec={{t="A Choked Supply Route",b="The Horde needs lumber, supplies, and messengers to travel between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains. The Talondeep Path carries them past Mystral Lake’s western shore. Hostile water elementals have stopped travel and battered the supply caravans. Mastok Wrilehiss calls for action to reopen the route before the Horde’s supply lines collapse.",sp=0},{t="The Corrupted Waters",b="Water elementals in Mystral Lake have become befouled, aggressive, and unpredictable. They attack those who take the nearby trails. You are sent to cull them and defeat the greater spirit Tideress so the area may become safer. What has tainted the lake’s spirits remains unknown amid the turmoil in Ashenvale’s sacred groves.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Across the Water",b="A night elf gazebo stands on Mystral Lake’s central island, with a clear view across the water to Silverwind Refuge. Horde scouts are sent to assess whether it could serve as a forward observation post. From there, Splintertree’s commanders could watch nearby Alliance movements without being detected.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is causing the standstill near Stonetalon?",a="Befouled water elementals in Mystral Lake have turned violent and attack travelers on the nearby Talondeep Path. Their attacks have halted supply transports between Ashenvale and the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"why are transports stopped","talondeep path blocked","what stopped the supply route"},it="motive"},{q="Who orders the elementals cleared?",a="Mastok Wrilehiss, an orc at Splintertree Post in eastern Ashenvale, orders you to clear the elementals and scout the Alliance position.",al={"who gives stonetalon standstill","mastok wrilehiss quest","who is mastok"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why scout the gazebo in the middle of Mystral Lake?",a="The gazebo on Mystral Lake’s central island offers a view across the water toward the nearby night elf settlement of Silverwind Refuge. Mastok wants it assessed as a hidden observation post for watching enemy movements.",al={"why scout gazebo","mystral lake gazebo purpose","gazebo observation post"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Talondeep Path?",a="The Talondeep Path is the mountain trail connecting southwestern Ashenvale to the Stonetalon Mountains. It runs past Mystral Lake’s western shore.",al={"talondeep path location","path to stonetalon","stonetalon road"},it="place"},{q="Why are the water elementals in Mystral Lake befouled?",a="The cause of the water elementals’ corruption is unknown. Turmoil in Ashenvale has disrupted the lake, leaving its spirits hostile to outsiders.",al={"why are elementals corrupted","mystral lake water corrupted","befouled elementals origin"},it="origin"},{q="Which Alliance outpost is being watched from the gazebo?",a="The gazebo overlooks Silverwind Refuge, a night elf settlement just north of the lake. Sentinels there defend Ashenvale against the Horde’s lumber-harvesting operations.",al={"what alliance base near mystral lake","alliance outpost ashenvale"},it="threat"},{q="What are you fighting at Mystral Lake?",a="You are sent to destroy the befouled water elementals inhabiting Mystral Lake, as well as Tideress. The lake's waters have churned to life, aggressively assaulting anyone traveling along the nearby road.",al={"mystral lake target","who are you sent against","what do you kill stonetalon standstill"},it="target",add="46f9d708"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Splintertree Post depends on open supply routes. Keeping the Talondeep Path clear maintains communication and trade with Stonetalon.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you recognize the water elementals’ twisted state as a sign of deep elemental disharmony in Ashenvale’s ancient forests.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Horde relies on Ashenvale’s timber and trails to supply its settlements. The disruption of mountain supply lines cannot stand."},kw={"befouled water elemental","gazebo","mastok wrilehiss","mystral lake","splintertree post","stonetalon standstill","talondeep path","tideress"},rel={"subzone:mystral-lake","subzone:talondeep-path","subzone:splintertree-post","npc:mastok-wrilehiss","zone:ashenvale","topic:alliance","zone:barrens"},m={start="Mastok Wrilehiss",level="25",faction="horde",id=25},src={"Stonetalon Standstill"}}
E["quest:4581"] = {t="quest",n="Kayneth Stillwind",z="ashenvale",s="Sentinel Shindrell Swiftfire sends a courier east from Astranaar with a scouting missive for Forest Song. Druid Kayneth Stillwind needs help watching corruption spread through Ashenvale's ancient woods.",h="Sentinel Shindrell Swiftfire sends a courier east from Astranaar with a scouting missive for Forest Song.",sec={{t="A Dispatch to the East",b="In Astranaar, Sentinel Shindrell Swiftfire watches over western Ashenvale. Druid Kayneth Stillwind, stationed at Forest Song in the forest's eastern reaches, has asked her to assess the region's security. Shifting wildlife and dark omens along the coasts and through the woods trouble him. Swiftfire puts her observations in a sealed note, trusting a traveler to carry it safely across the dangerous central forest.",sp=0},{t="Watchers at Forest Song",b="The way to Forest Song crosses Nightsong Woods, where satyrs encroach, wildlife turns hostile, and the Horde makes excursions from the south. At Forest Song's shrine, Kayneth Stillwind studies the balance of Ashenvale's natural spirits. Swiftfire's reconnaissance confirms his fear that corruption is spreading through the forest, not confined to one place or passing quickly. The druids will need more help to confront the wickedness taking root.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Kayneth Stillwind located?",a="Kayneth Stillwind is at Forest Song, a night elf sanctuary in Nightsong Woods, far east in Ashenvale and north of the main road.",al={"where is kayneth","kayneth stillwind location","find kayneth stillwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Sentinel Shindrell Swiftfire offers it from Astranaar, the night elf settlement in western Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","who starts kayneth stillwind","where do i start"},it="identity"},{q="What is in Shindrell's Note?",a="Shindrell's Note reports security conditions along Ashenvale's western coast and around Astranaar's woodlands, helping Kayneth Stillwind investigate unnatural corruption in the forest.",al={"shindrell's note contents","what did shindrell write","shindrell note"},it="item"},{q="Why is Kayneth Stillwind investigating the forest?",a="Kayneth Stillwind investigates because he fears a pervasive wickedness is spreading through Ashenvale. As a druid, he seeks reports from the Sentinels to learn where it is taking hold and uphold nature's balance.",al={"why does kayneth care","kayneth stillwind motive","druid corruption"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Forest Song safe for Alliance travelers?",a="Forest Song is a peaceful Alliance refuge with friendly sentinels and druids. Hostile beasts and corrupted satyrs threaten the surrounding Nightsong Woods, making the journey hazardous.",al={"is forest song safe","alliance town forest song","forest song guards"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after delivering the note?",a="After reviewing Shindrell's report, Kayneth investigates the forest's corruption and enlists travelers to act against the blighted forces threatening the region.",al={"what comes next","follow up quest","kayneth continuation"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Shindrell Swiftfire want this report delivered?",a="Kayneth Stillwind reached out to Shindrell requesting a formal account of recent occurrences along the coast and throughout the woods surrounding Astranaar. Shindrell shares the druid's growing concern that a foul corruption is creeping through Ashenvale. By compiling her observations and dispatching them to Forest Song, she hopes to aid Kayneth in pinpointing the source of this spreading wickedness.",al={"why send report to kayneth","shindrell swiftfire motive","why deliver shindrell's note"},it="motive",add="20722aea"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you answer a calling by helping Kayneth Stillwind and the Cenarion Circle heal Ashenvale from spreading demonic and elemental blights.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share with the Sentinels a duty to keep communication open between Astranaar and distant holdings like Forest Song.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help maintain communication and defense across Ashenvale, from its center to eastern Nightsong Woods, against wilderness threats and Horde incursions."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","corruption","druid","forest song","kayneth stillwind","nightsong woods","shindrell swiftfire"},rel={"npc:shindrell-swiftfire","subzone:forest-song","subzone:astranaar","subzone:nightsong-woods","zone:ashenvale","topic:druid"},m={start="Shindrell Swiftfire",["end"]="Kayneth Stillwind",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=4581},src={"Kayneth Stillwind (quest)"}}
E["quest:6382"] = {t="quest",n="The Ashenvale Hunt",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Horde hunters face a new test beneath the ancient trees. Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo sends proven hunters north to Splintertree Post, where Senani Thunderheart awaits.",h="In Ashenvale, Horde hunters face a new test beneath the ancient trees.",sec={{t="Into the Ancient Canopy",b="Horde hunters who have proven themselves in the Barrens are sent toward Ashenvale. Jorn Skyseer sees when a traveler has outgrown the local game and points the way north. For the young Horde, these old forests offer resources and mark a political and spiritual frontier they must learn to understand and claim.",sp=0},{t="Splintertree Post",b="The road north passes the Mor'shan Rampart before reaching Splintertree Post, a fortified Horde camp deep among the trees. The tauren huntress Senani Thunderheart welcomes experienced hunters seeking harder tests of survival. The Horde depends on skilled trackers to face Ashenvale's native predators and the watchful defenders of the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on the Ashenvale Hunt?",a="Jorn Skyseer, a tauren hunter at Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, sends you north after you prove your skill hunting local beasts.",al={"who gives the ashenvale hunt","quest giver ashenvale hunt","jorn skyseer quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Splintertree Post located?",a="Splintertree Post lies in east-central Ashenvale, along the north side of the road. Follow the main road north from the Barrens, past the Mor'shan Rampart and up through the woods.",al={"splintertree post location","where is senani thunderheart","find splintertree post"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Senani Thunderheart?",a="Senani Thunderheart is a tauren huntress at Splintertree Post. She coordinates hunts across Ashenvale and teaches arriving Horde hunters to pursue the forest's fiercest predators and spirits.",al={"senani thunderheart","who is senani","huntress senani"},it="identity"},{q="What other Horde outposts are nearby in Ashenvale?",a="The Horde also keeps the Warsong Lumber Camp to the east and Zoram'gar Outpost on the far western coast at the Zoram Strand.",al={"horde bases ashenvale","other camps ashenvale"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde interested in hunting in Ashenvale?",a="The wilds offer meat, pelts, and resources scarce in arid Durotar and the Barrens. Facing Ashenvale's dangerous beasts also tests the will and spiritual strength of Horde hunters and warriors.",al={"why hunt ashenvale","horde ashenvale motivation"},it="purpose"},{q="What challenges follow this journey?",a="Senani Thunderheart sends experienced hunters to track woodland threats beneath the canopy, including the great bear Ursangous, the cat Shadumbra, and the hippogryph Sharptalon.",al={"next quest after ashenvale hunt","what does senani give you"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Jorn Skyseer send you to Ashenvale?",a="Jorn Skyseer recognizes your burgeoning strength and your willingness to embrace the hunt in the Barrens. To him, you have outgrown local trials and are ready for greater glory. The dense forests of Ashenvale represent a wild frontier where the Horde strives to claim both spiritual mastery and political control, and he wants capable hunters like you to help establish that dominance.",al={"why does jorn skyseer want this done","jorn skyseer motive","why go to ashenvale"},it="motive",add="854a1b41"},{q="Why does Jorn Skyseer choose you for this hunt?",a="Jorn has watched you prove your skill and mettle across the Barrens. As a seasoned guide and elder stationed at Camp Taurajo, his duty is to recognize potential in rising warriors and direct them where the Horde needs strength most. Ashenvale demands tested, capable hunters rather than untested guards bound to outpost defense.",al={"why me ashenvale hunt","why does jorn choose me","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="2c1005c5"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you leave Kalimdor's plains for Ashenvale's dense canopy, where exotic beasts await tracking, study, and taming.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you follow the guidance of Jorn Skyseer and Senani Thunderheart. They see the hunt as a spiritual balance and a way to honor the wilderness.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you enter a strategic frontier. A foothold in Ashenvale brings timber and food to settlements across Durotar and the Barrens."},kw={"ashenvale","ashenvale hunt","barrens","camp taurajo","jorn skyseer","senani thunderheart","splintertree post"},rel={"npc:senani-thunderheart","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","zone:barrens","subzone:zoram-strand","topic:horde"},m={start="Jorn Skyseer",["end"]="Senani Thunderheart",level="20",faction="Horde",id=6382},src={"The Ashenvale Hunt (The Barrens)"}}
E["quest:6383"] = {t="quest",n="The Ashenvale Hunt",z="ashenvale",s="In Ashenvale, Horde hunters face the ancient forest's three great predators. Senani Thunderheart oversees the trial at Splintertree Post, where hunters track Ursangous, Shadumbra, and Sharptalon to prove their skill.",h="In Ashenvale, Horde hunters face the ancient forest's three great predators.",sec={{t="A Tauren Tradition in an Ancient Forest",b="Senani Thunderheart gives the Horde's presence in Ashenvale a different kind of test. While Orcs gather lumber, she sends hunters into the shadowed forest to face its strongest predators. The hunt calls for more than strength: hunters must meet the wilderness with cunning and respect, and learn what they can endure.",sp=0},{t="The Three Great Beasts",b="Three solitary beasts test those who take up the hunt. Ursangous, an immense elder bear, roams near the Talondeep Path. Shadumbra, a cunning nightsaber, stalks the eastern borders near Raynewood Retreat and the Laughing Sisters. South of Splintertree Post, Sharptalon, a fierce hippogryph, wheels above the forest canopy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the Ashenvale Hunt?",a="Senani Thunderheart, a tauren hunter stationed in Ashenvale, directs the hunt. She challenges Horde travelers to prove their survival skills against the wilderness.",al={"quest giver ashenvale hunt","who gives the hunt","senani thunderheart quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What beasts do I need to track down?",a="Track Ursangous the great bear, Shadumbra the nightsaber, and Sharptalon the hippogryph.",al={"what animals to kill","three beasts","ashenvale hunt targets"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Where can Ursangous be found?",a="Ursangous roams just west of the Talondeep Path among other wild bears of the forest.",al={"ursangous location","where is the bear","find ursangous"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where is Shadumbra prowling?",a="Shadumbra prowls south of Raynewood Retreat, near the road where the dryads called the Laughing Sisters dwell.",al={"shadumbra location","where is shadumbra","nightsaber location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where can Sharptalon be tracked?",a="Sharptalon ranges south of Splintertree Post, flying over the trees and clearing.",al={"sharptalon location","where is sharptalon","hippogryph location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Senani Thunderheart send hunters after these beasts?",a="Senani means the hunt as an honorable trial, not wanton slaughter. Facing the forest's deadliest natural residents should teach hunters about the wilderness and their own strength.",al={"why do the hunt","purpose of the hunt","hunt lore"},it="motive"},{q="What are the beasts of the Ashenvale Hunt?",a="The hunt challenges you to stalk three legendary predators native to Ashenvale's ancient woods: Ursangous, a massive and ferocious bear prowling near the Talondeep Path; Shadumbra, an elusive nightsaber stalking the forests south of Raynewood Retreat; and Sharptalon, a fierce hippogryph circling south of Splintertree Post. Each represents the untamed might and cunning of the forest itself.",al={"what beasts do I hunt","ashenvale hunt targets","who are the beasts"},it="target",add="e25adf54"},{q="Why does Senani Thunderheart have adventurers undertake the hunt instead of local guards?",a="The Ashenvale Hunt is not a military task or a call for extermination. It is a traditional rite of passage meant to test a hunter's personal cunning, strength, and resolve against the wilderness. Splintertree's garrison is tasked with defending the Horde's outpost in hostile territory, but this trial is an individual journey where you seek out the forest's fiercest beasts to prove your own worth.",al={"why send me","why adventurers","why not splintertree guards"},it="why_me",add="a64a5cc6"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren hunter, tracking Ursangous, Shadumbra, and Sharptalon honors the Earth Mother's creation. The hunt balances respect for nature's ferocity with the honor of the stalk.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you scour wide stretches of forest, read the terrain, and face beasts that can easily overcome an unwary tracker.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find a path of martial honor and spiritual connection in Ashenvale, even as the Warsong clear-cut the forest."},kw={"ashenvale hunt","raynewood retreat","senani thunderheart","shadumbra","sharptalon","splintertree post","talondeep path","ursangous"},rel={"npc:senani-thunderheart","quest:24","quest:2","zone:ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:raynewood-retreat","subzone:talondeep-path","quest:1945"},m={start="Senani Thunderheart",level="20",faction="Horde",id=6383},src={"The Ashenvale Hunt (Ashenvale)"}}
E["quest:6441"] = {t="quest",n="Satyr Horns",z="ashenvale",s="At Splintertree Post, Pixel hires Horde adventurers to gather satyr horns for Ratchet. The traveling goblin sees a chance to trade them in the port town.",h="At Splintertree Post, Pixel hires Horde adventurers to gather satyr horns for Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Lucrative Opportunity",b="Pixel, a traveling goblin, sees a chance to profit while resting at Splintertree Post. Satyr horns are in high demand in Ratchet, and Pixel wants them for the journey back south to the port town. Rather than risk facing the corrupted creatures, Pixel hires passing adventurers to bring back sixteen intact horns.",sp=0},{t="Haunts of the Corrupted",b="Demonic satyrs haunt scattered, fel-tainted ruins across Ashenvale, remnants of their betrayal during the ancient sundering. Hunters can search their strongholds at Night Run, the fortified camp of Satyrnaar, and the shadowed groves of Xavian. Horns gathered from any of these places are the trophies Pixel seeks for Ratchet's merchant wharves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pixel?",a="Pixel is a traveling goblin who stops at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale before heading south to Ratchet, a neutral port.",al={"who is quest giver","pixel lore","goblin at splintertree"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Ratchet want satyr horns?",a="Pixel says satyr horns fetch a high price in Ratchet, where merchants, alchemists, and collectors of exotic goods pay well for raw demonic reagents and curios from the northern woods.",al={"why satyr horns","what are horns used for","ratchet satyr horns"},it="item"},{q="Where can satyr horns be found in Ashenvale?",a="Satyrs haunt tainted places across Ashenvale, including Night Run northwest of Splintertree Post, Satyrnaar just off the main road toward Azshara, and Xavian in northeastern Ashenvale.",al={"satyr locations","where to find satyrs","night run xavian satyrnaar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are satyrs?",a="Satyrs are ancient night elves corrupted by the Burning Legion thousands of years ago. Now cloven-hoofed and horned, they serve dark powers and corrupt the forest around them.",al={"what is a satyr","satyr lore","are satyrs demons"},it="target"},{q="Why is this contract handled at Splintertree Post?",a="Splintertree Post is the Horde's main fortress in central Ashenvale. Pixel rests there between trade routes and hires nearby Horde warriors already fighting the forest's dangers.",al={"splintertree satyr quest","why horde only"},it="why_here"},{q="Does Pixel have any allegiance to the Horde?",a="No. Pixel is an independent goblin merchant seeking profit. Like many goblins based around Ratchet, Pixel trades with anyone who can provide valuable goods, regardless of faction politics.",al={"is pixel horde","pixel faction"},it="side"},{q="Why does Pixel want satyr horns?",a="Pixel is an enterprising traveler on her way to Ratchet with an eye for trade. Recognizing that satyr horns fetch a handsome price in the goblin port, she aims to turn a tidy profit before completing her journey. Rather than facing the perilous beasts herself, she is willing to pay capable adventurers to handle the dirty work so she can deliver the goods.",al={"why does pixel want this","pixel motive satyr horns","why gather satyr horns"},it="motive",add="22d423d7"},{q="Why doesn't Pixel hunt the satyrs herself?",a="Pixel readily admits that she is no match for the vicious, magic-wielding satyrs lurking in Ashenvale's ruins. Lacking the combat prowess to survive an encounter in places like Satyrnaar or Xavian, she relies entirely on seasoned mercenaries passing through Splintertree Post to secure the merchandise for her.",al={"why does pixel need me","why cant pixel get the horns","why hire an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="fc903cbf"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing satyr enclaves in central Ashenvale weakens demonic threats to Splintertree Post's fragile supply lines.",["class:Warlock"]="Satyrs carry potent fel magic, and their remains interest those who study demonic power.",["class:Hunter"]="Tracking demonic humanoids through corrupted woodland ruins like Satyrnaar and Night Run puts your wilderness skills to a dangerous test."},kw={"ashenvale","night run","pixel","ratchet","satyr horns","satyrnaar","splintertree post","xavian"},rel={"npc:pixel","subzone:splintertree-post","topic:satyr","zone:ashenvale","subzone:satyrnaar","subzone:night-run","subzone:xavian","subzone:ratchet"},m={start="Pixel",faction="horde",id=6441,ri={"Satyr Horns"}},src={"Satyr Horns (quest)"}}
E["quest:6442"] = {t="quest",n="Naga at the Zoram Strand",z="ashenvale",s="At Zoram Strand, Naga threaten the Horde's hold on Ashenvale's coast. From Zoram'gar Outpost, Marukai seeks to drive the Wrathtail away from the sunken ruins of ancient Zoram.",h="At Zoram Strand, Naga threaten the Horde's hold on Ashenvale's coast.",sec={{t="A Precarious Foothold",b="The Horde's hold on Zoram Strand is fragile. Hostile night elf territory and bitter woodland fighting surround the outpost, whose coast links the Horde to the sea. Aggressive naga have now crawled ashore. They could cut off that link and overwhelm the small garrison before its defenses are ready.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of Doomed Zoram",b="Zoram Strand's sandy shoals hide the shattered remains of Zoram, an ancient elven city swallowed by the Great Sundering thousands of years ago. Marukai and the outpost's defenders do not know why the Wrathtail have come out of the deep trenches now. Their sudden interest in the sunken ruins threatens anyone walking above them.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Survival",b="Marukai sees a simple fight for survival. With swords and tridents drawn, reason matters little. She demands twenty severed heads from the Wrathtail, hoping force will drive the naga back into the depths and secure the shore for the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Naga at the Zoram Strand?",a="Marukai, a Darkspear troll, gives the task from the Horde outpost of Zoram'gar on Zoram Strand in northwestern Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","marukai location"},it="identity"},{q="What is the history behind the Zoram Strand?",a="Zoram Strand lies along the resting place of the ancient city of Zoram. The Sundering destroyed and submerged it beneath the Great Sea long ago, and its ruins now lie partly underwater along the Ashenvale coast.",al={"what is zoram","history of zoram","sunken city"},it="history"},{q="Why are the naga attacking the shore?",a="The Horde garrison does not know why the Wrathtail have arrived. The naga have surged from the deep ocean to claim the sunken ruins and drive off land-dwellers.",al={"why are naga here","wrathtail motive","naga goal"},it="threat"},{q="Which enemies do I need to fight for this quest?",a="You face members of the Wrathtail tribe, who crawl across Zoram Strand's beaches and surf. Marukai asks you to bring her twenty of their severed heads.",al={"which naga","wrathtail heads","target enemies"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What quest follows Naga at the Zoram Strand?",a="Marukai offers no further task after this one. She thanks you and asks for more of your kind to help hold Zoram Strand.",al={"next quest","follow up","marukai next"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde care about this remote beach?",a="Ashenvale is fiercely contested by the Horde and the Night Elves. A secure beachhead at Zoram Strand gives the Horde sea access and supply lines beyond the dense inland forests.",al={"why is horde here","zoram'gar outpost purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Marukai want the naga killed?",a="Marukai views the naga as an active danger to the Horde's presence on the strand. The Horde has fought bitterly to claim and secure this outpost along the Ashenvale coast. Whatever mysterious motive brings the serpentine invaders ashore, their growing numbers threaten to overwhelm the encampment unless they are culled and driven back into the ocean depths.",al={"why does marukai want this","marukai motive","why kill naga zoram strand"},it="motive",add="b1ee6e7c"},{q="Who are the Wrathtail naga and why are they at the Zoram Strand?",a="The Wrathtail tribe of naga has crawled from the sea to occupy the ruins of Zoram, an ancient Kaldorei city destroyed and submerged during the Sundering. While their deeper intentions remain hidden from the Horde defenders, their creeping presence and hostile incursions along the shoreline make them an immediate threat to anyone venturing near the strand.",al={"who are the wrathtail","wrathtail naga lore","why are wrathtail here"},it="target",add="7626cdcb"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help hold Zoram'gar Outpost and secure a foothold in Ashenvale. Driving off the naga is a matter of military survival.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the value of Marukai's direct, forceful approach to defending a frontier."},kw={"ashenvale","marukai","naga","wrathtail","wrathtail heads","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:marukai","subzone:zoram-strand","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale","quest:1008"},m={start="Marukai",faction="Horde",id=6442},src={"Naga at the Zoram Strand"}}
E["quest:6462"] = {t="quest",n="Troll Charm",z="ashenvale",s="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Mitsuwa seeks sacred charms stolen from his kin. A traveling party of Darkspear trolls was ambushed and slaughtered by the Thistlefur furbolgs, who took the talismans into their den.",h="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Mitsuwa seeks sacred charms stolen from his kin.",sec={{t="An Ambushed Caravan",b="Zoram'gar Outpost is a remote Horde refuge on Ashenvale's western coast. Woodland paths make travel there dangerous. A party of Darkspear trolls never reached the post after the Thistlefur furbolgs ambushed them. Mitsuwa accepts that his kin have died and will one day meet him in the afterlife. Their sacred charms were stolen from the dead, however, and he cannot abide that insult.",sp=0},{t="Sacred Trinkets",b="Troll charms and talismans mark identity, offer spiritual protection, and bind their bearers to the Loa. Mitsuwa sees a troll without her charm as hollow and worthless, like an orc without battle scars. The Thistlefur furbolgs carried the stolen charms to Thistlefur Hold, deep in the caves beyond Thistlefur Village. They hid the talismans in chests, far from their rightful owners.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest and where are they located?",a="Mitsuwa, a Darkspear troll, is at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand along Ashenvale's northwestern coast.",al={"quest giver","where is mitsuwa","who starts troll charm"},gp=true},{q="Why are the troll charms so important to Mitsuwa?",a="Troll charms carry deep spiritual and cultural meaning. Mitsuwa sees a troll without her charm as an orc without battle scars, and the furbolgs' possession of these relics desecrates his slain kin.",al={"charm importance","why troll charms matter","significance of charms"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the troll charms located?",a="The charms are in chests inside Thistlefur Hold, a deep cavern complex at the northern edge of Thistlefur Village, north of Astranaar.",al={"charm location","where are chests","find charms"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who stole the charms?",a="The Thistlefur furbolgs stole the charms. They ambushed and killed Mitsuwa's kin as they traveled toward Zoram'gar Outpost, then carried the charms into their caverns.",al={"who took charms","ambush culprits"},it="target"},{q="What happened to the trolls who originally carried the charms?",a="The Thistlefur furbolgs killed the trolls along the trail. Mitsuwa mourns them and believes they will meet again in the afterlife, while he seeks to recover their sacred relics.",al={"caravan fate","slain trolls","mitsuwa kin"},it="history"},{q="Is this quest available to the Alliance?",a="No. Mitsuwa offers this to the Horde at Zoram'gar Outpost.",al={"alliance troll charm","can alliance do it"},gp=true},{q="What is the Troll Charm?",a="These charms are deeply sacred relics carried by the Darkspear trolls. To their culture, a charm represents honor, identity, and spiritual belonging—as Mitsuwa puts it, a troll without her charm is as hollow and worthless as an orc without battle scars. Though their fallen owners will reunite with their kin in the afterlife, letting these venerated tokens remain soiled in the hands of savage beasts is an intolerable disgrace to their memory.",al={"troll charm lore","what does troll charm do","what are troll charms"},it="item",add="3db0517e"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a troll, recovering the charms is a spiritual duty. These sacred ancestral items must be rescued from the furbolgs.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, striking into Thistlefur territory pushes back against woodland threats that ambush Horde supply lines and travelers in Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","darkspear","furbolg","mitsuwa","thistlefur hold","thistlefur village","troll charm","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:mitsuwa","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","subzone:thistlefur-hold","subzone:thistlefur-village","topic:furbolg","topic:troll","zone:ashenvale","subzone:astranaar"},m={start="Mitsuwa",faction="Horde",id=6462,ri={"Troll Charm"}},src={"Troll Charm (quest)"}}
E["quest:6482"] = {t="quest",n="Freedom to Ruul",z="ashenvale",s="In northern Ashenvale, Ruul waits in a cage deep inside Thistlefur Hold. He needs a Horde ally to help him fight through the corrupted furbolg den and reach safety.",h="In northern Ashenvale, Ruul waits in a cage deep inside Thistlefur Hold.",sec={{t="A Druid in Chains",b="Ruul Snowhoof, a druid, is trapped in Thistlefur Hold. While exploring the corrupted woods of northern Ashenvale in bear form, he strayed too close to the den. The corrupted furbolgs had lost their ancestral wisdom and, driven by feral paranoia, mistook him for an ordinary beast. They caged and starved him instead of honoring him, draining his magic until he could no longer break free alone.",sp=0},{t="Escape from the Den",b="After hunger and imprisonment have weakened Ruul, he cannot change form or fight through the furbolg settlement alone. A Horde ally frees him and clears a path past hostile Thistlefurs. When they reach the outskirts of Splintertree Post, Ruul briefly takes his tauren form and gives heartfelt thanks. Then he returns to the wilderness to sleep off his exhaustion.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why was Ruul Snowhoof locked up by the furbolgs?",a="Ruul was exploring the forest in bear form when the corrupted Thistlefur furbolgs mistook him for a wild beast instead of a druid. They caged him and starved him until he was too weak to escape.",al={"why is ruul trapped","how did ruul get captured","why caged"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Yama Snowhoof?",a="Yama Snowhoof is Ruul's sister, stationed at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. She grew deeply worried when Ruul disappeared into the forest days earlier and did not return.",al={"ruul sister","yama splintertree","who is yama"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Why couldn't Ruul just shift out of bear form to escape?",a="The Thistlefur furbolgs weakened Ruul through prolonged captivity and deliberate starvation. Without food or strength, his natural energy was spent, leaving him helpless until someone rescued him.",al={"why didnt ruul shapeshift","druid bear trap"}},{q="What happens after Ruul reaches safety?",a="At the borders of Splintertree Post, Ruul briefly shifts into his natural tauren form to express his gratitude. Then he returns to bear form and finds a quiet place to sleep and recover.",al={"where does ruul go","ruul ending"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Are all furbolgs in Ashenvale hostile like the Thistlefurs?",a="No. Many furbolg tribes have a noble heritage and deep ties to nature, but the Thistlefurs of northern Ashenvale have fallen under corrupting influences that made them aggressive and unpredictable.",al={"are furbolgs evil","thistlefur corruption"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the rescue take place?",a="Ruul is held inside Thistlefur Hold, a furbolg den in the hills northwest of Splintertree Post and north of Astranaar in Ashenvale.",al={"where is ruul","ruul snowhoof location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Ruul Snowhoof need you to escort him rather than escaping on his own?",a="Ruul has spent days trapped inside a Thistlefur cage, enduring starvation and captivity at the hands of the corrupted furbolgs. His physical strength has almost completely failed him. Weakened, malnourished, and trapped deep inside the hostile Thistlefur Hold, he cannot fight his way past the surrounding tribe alone and relies on you to carve a path to freedom.",al={"why does ruul need help","why can't ruul escape alone","why me ruul snowhoof"},it="why_me",add="cd4f3bf3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know the risk of crossing feral lands in animal form, where corrupted locals may mistake you for prey.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor the bonds of the Earthmother and the Horde when you rescue a Cenarion brother and ease his kin's worry at Splintertree Post.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you strengthen the precarious outpost at Splintertree Post with every soul rescued from northern Ashenvale's corrupted hollows."},kw={"ashenvale","druid escort","furbolg","splintertree post","thistlefur hold","yama snowhoof"},rel={"npc:ruul-snowhoof","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","topic:tauren"},m={start="Ruul Snowhoof",["end"]="Yama Snowhoof",faction="Horde",id=6482},src={"Freedom to Ruul"}}
E["quest:6503"] = {t="quest",n="Ashenvale Outrunners",z="ashenvale",s="Night elf scouts have slipped out from Silverwing Outpost into Ashenvale. Kuray'bin calls for a strike against the Ashenvale Outrunners before they can report on Horde encampments and defenses.",h="Night elf scouts have slipped out from Silverwing Outpost into Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Canopies",b="Night elf scouts from Silverwing Outpost are moving through the woods east of their base and south of nearby Horde holdings. In Ashenvale's contested forest, they watch the paths and ridges, mapping fortifications and tracking troop movements. Kuray'bin has learned that these scouts, known as Ashenvale Outrunners, have slipped into the wilderness to gather intelligence.",sp=0},{t="Blinding the Alliance",b="The Horde strikes at enemy scouts before they can return to Silverwing Outpost. Hunting down the outrunners denies its commanders knowledge of Horde troop strength and outpost defenses. Without their forward eyes, the night elves are left disoriented and less willing to risk aggressive moves through the contested woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Ashenvale Outrunners?",a="Kuray'bin, a Horde scout coordinator stationed in Ashenvale, gives the order. He tracks and counters night elf movements across the forest.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","kuray'bin quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Ashenvale Outrunners located?",a="The outrunners patrol the forests east of Silverwing Outpost and south of Kuray'bin's camp, gathering intelligence through the underbrush.",al={"outrunners location","where are outrunners","where to find outrunners"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the outrunners a threat to the Horde?",a="The outrunners are advanced scouts operating from Silverwing Outpost. If they map Horde encampments and troop counts, the Alliance can plan precise raids against vulnerable positions.",al={"why kill outrunners","threat of outrunners","outrunner purpose"},it="threat"},{q="What is Silverwing Outpost?",a="Silverwing Outpost is a prominent night elf military installation in Ashenvale. Alliance forces use it as a frontline base to defend the forest and contest Horde expansion.",al={"silverwing outpost lore","what is silverwing outpost","silverwing alliance"},it="place"},{q="Is this quest part of a longer storyline?",a="This is a standalone tactical effort to reduce Alliance reconnaissance in the area. Fighters who help Kuray'bin secure the perimeter earn a reward.",al={"quest chain","follow up quest","outrunner chain"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Can Alliance players complete this quest?",a="No. This is for the Horde alone. Kuray'bin operates strictly on behalf of the Horde's frontlines in Ashenvale.",al={"is this horde only","alliance version","can alliance do this"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why does Kuray'bin want the Ashenvale Outrunners killed?",a="Kuray'bin wants to blind the Alliance and prevent them from mounting an organized assault on Horde territory. The outrunners recently slipped out from Silverwing Outpost to prowl near Horde lines, and if they map out your camp's defenses and troop movements, an Alliance offensive is almost certain to follow. Eliminating them denies the enemy crucial battlefield intelligence.",al={"kuraybin motive","why kill outrunners","kuray'bin reason"},it="motive",add="2873db73"},{q="Who are the Ashenvale Outrunners?",a="They are night elf scouts dispatched from the nearby Alliance stronghold of Silverwing Outpost. Operating under the dense canopy of the forest, these agile advance scouts creep close to Horde borders to monitor fortifications, watch patrol routes, and prepare the ground for future Alliance incursions.",al={"what are ashenvale outrunners","who are the outrunners","ashenvale outrunner target"},it="target",add="884af179"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, each night elf scout you cut down helps protect local encampments and lumber operations from coordinated Alliance counterattacks.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you rely on keen instincts, heightened tracking senses, and sharp marksmanship to find concealed outrunners in deep woodland.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you turn night elf stealth against them by neutralizing their outrunners, helping Horde infiltrators hold the forest's shadows."},kw={"alliance","ashenvale","ashenvale outrunners","horde","kuray'bin","night elf scouts","silverwing outpost"},rel={"npc:kuray-bin","subzone:silverwing-outpost","zone:ashenvale","topic:alliance"},m={start="Kuray'bin",level="24",faction="Horde",id=6503},src={"Ashenvale Outrunners (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6504"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Pages",z="ashenvale",s="A gust has scattered The Lost Pages across Ashenvale. Gurda Ragescar is stranded near Splintertree Post, unable to run the shredder she is taking from Ratchet to the Warsong Lumber Camp without its manual.",h="A gust has scattered The Lost Pages across Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Gust of Bad Luck",b="The Warsong Clan uses steam-powered shredders bought from Ratchet to clear lumber across Ashenvale. Their delicate workings are not easy for an orc warrior to master. As Gurda Ragescar carried a newly bought shredder north, a sudden gust tore the instruction booklet from her hands. Twelve parchment leaves scattered across the forest floor.",sp=0},{t="Pages in the Wilderness",b="The wind carried the manual pages across Ashenvale, and wandering creatures, cultists, and forest denizens have taken them. The shredder cannot run without all three chapters. Gurda is stranded on the road to Splintertree Post, unable to report for logging duty.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gurda Ragescar?",a="Gurda Ragescar is a Horde laborer carrying a goblin shredder from Ratchet to Ashenvale for the Warsong Lumber Camp's logging work.",al={"gurda","ragescar","who is the quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gurda need an instruction manual to drive the shredder?",a="Goblin machinery is finicky and hard to understand. Even an eager orc cannot safely operate the shredder without its manufacturer's manual.",al={"why manual","why cant she drive it","shredder operating manual"},it="motive"},{q="How did the manual pages end up scattered all over Ashenvale?",a="A violent gust tore the book from Gurda's grasp as she traveled north along the forest road. Its loose pages scattered through the woods, leaving her with only the empty front cover.",al={"how did pages get lost","wind blew pages"},it="origin"},{q="Where does the shredder ultimately belong?",a="The shredder is bound for the Warsong Lumber Camp, where the Horde cuts timber to supply Orgrimmar and Durotar.",al={"where is the shredder going","warsong shredder destination"},it="place"},{q="Where can the missing pages be found?",a="The pages have spread across Ashenvale and been picked up by humanoids and hostile forest denizens roaming the region.",al={"where to find pages","who drops the pages"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde purchase machinery from Ratchet?",a="Ratchet is the nearest neutral port with trade links to goblin cartels. The Horde buys specialized engineering, demolition tools, and steam-driven vehicles there for its military logistics.",al={"horde goblin machinery","ratchet trade horde"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Gurda Ragescar need you to find the manual pages?",a="Gurda is stuck on the road near Splintertree Post with an idle goblin shredder she cannot operate. She was entrusted to bring the expensive machine back from Ratchet to report for duty at the Warsong Lumber Camp. Without the manual, she has no idea how to drive it, and abandoning the vehicle in the wilderness to search the forest on foot would leave valuable Horde equipment undefended.",al={"why does gurda need help","why can't gurda find the pages","why me lost pages"},it="why_me",add="63589195"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can understand Gurda's trouble: running a goblin shredder without its maker's instructions risks a boiler failure.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know each shredder at the Warsong Lumber Camp helps gather timber for walls, huts, and warships in Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may share Gurda's frustration with lost technical pages; manual labor and warrior traditions leave little patience for goblin paperwork."},kw={"ashenvale","gurda ragescar","ratchet","shredder","shredder operating manual","splintertree post","the lost pages","warsong lumber camp"},rel={"npc:gurda-ragescar","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","subzone:ratchet","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Gurda Ragescar",level="30",faction="Horde",id=6504},src={"The Lost Pages"}}
E["quest:6544"] = {t="quest",n="Torek's Assault",z="ashenvale",s="From Ashenvale's wilds, Torek's Assault strikes Silverwing Outpost. Under orders from Splintertree Post, the orc raider Torek leads a brazen, bloody skirmish to crush Sentinel resistance and slay their commander, Duriel Moonfire, in the war for Ashenvale's borders.",h="From Ashenvale's wilds, Torek's Assault strikes Silverwing Outpost.",sec={{t="A Strike from the Shadows",b="The Horde's lumber camps and the native night elves are locked in an escalating border war across Ashenvale. Torek gathers a pack of Splintertree raiders just outside Silverwing Outpost to break the Alliance's defensive perimeter. He leads a head-on charge before the night elves can counterattack or mount a reinforced campaign against Splintertree Post.",sp=0},{t="Taking Silverwing",b="Silverwing Outpost is a fortified woodland garrison held by vigilant Silverwing Sentinels and fierce elven warriors. Torek targets their leader, Duriel Moonfire. Bringing Duriel down decapitates the local night elf military hierarchy, allowing the raiders to report a bloody victory to their commander, Ertog Ragetusk, at Splintertree Post.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Torek?",a="Torek is an aggressive orc raider based at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. Fierce and hungry for battle, he commands a detachment tasked with taking the fight directly to the night elf forces in the forest.",al={"torek npc","who is torek","torek orc"},it="identity"},{q="What is Silverwing Outpost?",a="Silverwing Outpost is a fortified night elf settlement in Ashenvale. Elite Sentinels and warriors guard it as a military bulwark watching Horde troop movements along the woodland trails.",al={"silverwing outpost","what is silverwing"},it="place"},{q="Who is Duriel Moonfire?",a="Duriel Moonfire is the night elf commander defending Silverwing Outpost. As head of the garrison, she directs the local Sentinels against Horde incursions until Torek's raiding party breaches the camp and strikes her down.",al={"duriel moonfire","duriel"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Who is Ertog Ragetusk?",a="Ertog Ragetusk is a Horde officer stationed at Splintertree Post. He is Torek's superior, oversees military operations in the region, and receives reports of victories against the Alliance.",al={"ertog ragetusk","ertog"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Horde attack Silverwing Outpost?",a="The Horde and night elves are engaged in active territorial warfare across Ashenvale. The strike on Silverwing Outpost relieves pressure on Horde supply lines and weakens the Sentinel defenses guarding the deeper forest.",al={"why attack silverwing","ashenvale conflict silverwing"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this attack take place?",a="The assault begins just outside Silverwing Outpost, on the eastern, Horde-held side of the Falfarren River in Ashenvale. It ends inside the night elf encampment.",al={"torek assault location","where is torek"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Torek need my help for the assault?",a="Torek already commands a squad of Splintertree raiders, but his scouts report that Silverwing Outpost is heavily fortified by seasoned night elf sentinels and warriors. Knowing the defenders won't yield easily, he welcomes an able-bodied champion to bolster their frontline and ensure the strike against Duriel Moonfire ends in decisive Horde victory.",al={"why does torek need me","why torek recruit player","why help torek"},it="why_me",add="6e6dcd55"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, pushing past Silverwing Outpost tests their strength and weakens the night elf blockade around Splintertree Post.",["faction:Alliance"]="Duriel Moonfire's fall exposes Silverwing Outpost and threatens the night elves' ancestral woodland holdings.",["class:Warrior"]="A brutal frontal melee tests your endurance against seasoned Sentinel archers and blademasters.",["race:NightElf"]="The raid strikes the Sentinels' frontline command, spilling elven blood beneath Ashenvale's boughs."},kw={"ashenvale","duriel moonfire","ertog ragetusk","raiders","sentinels","silverwing outpost","splintertree post","torek"},rel={"subzone:silverwing-outpost","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","topic:sentinels","topic:night-elf","subzone:falfarren-river"},m={start="Torek",["end"]="Ertog Ragetusk",faction="horde",id=6544},src={"Torek's Assault"}}
E["quest:6545"] = {t="quest",n="Warsong Runner Update",z="ashenvale",s="Runners carry word through Ashenvale as the Warsong Clan faces growing pressure along the border. Their report warns commanders of increasingly bold naga attacks on Horde outposts.",h="Runners carry word through Ashenvale as the Warsong Clan faces growing pressure along the border.",sec={{t="Frontline Dispatches",b="Warsong scouts and runners watch the fighting across Ashenvale and keep supply lines open. They face night elf sentinels and the dangers of the forest, so commanders need word from the frontier quickly. Couriers carry dispatches to remote garrisons and commanders such as Kadrak at the Mor'shan Rampart.",sp=0},{t="The Naga Threat",b="Horde defenders expect to face night elves among the trees, but outpost sentries report bolder attacks by naga. The serpentine invaders strike from waterways and ancient ruins, testing the barricades and drawing defenders away from forest and border patrols. The dispatch to the Mor'shan Rampart warns of these coordinated attacks from the water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the report being sent to?",a="The report goes to Kadrak, an overseer at the Mor'shan Rampart on the border between Ashenvale and the northern Barrens.",al={"who receives update","kadrak report","where does report go"},it="target"},{q="What threats are mentioned in the update?",a="The scout reports repeated assaults on the local outpost and an escalating threat from hostile naga in nearby waters.",al={"what is in report","runner update content","naga attacks"},it="threat"},{q="Why does the Horde rely on foot runners here?",a="Dense foliage, night elf marksmen, and isolated outposts make flight difficult or dangerous across parts of Ashenvale. Runners carry messages quickly and discreetly along guarded paths.",al={"why runners","warsong runners lore","why not wyverns"}},{q="Who are the Warsong Runners?",a="Warsong Runners are scouts, couriers, and vanguard fighters of the Warsong Clan. They protect supply lines and watch enemy movements along the forest's contested borders.",al={"warsong clan ashenvale","who are warsong runners"},it="people"},{q="Where are the naga attacking in Ashenvale?",a="Naga attack from strongholds in ruins along Ashenvale's shores and lakes, ambushing travelers and raiding nearby camps.",al={"where are naga","ashenvale naga"},it="place"},{q="What is the outpost's purpose in this area?",a="The outpost warns of danger and anchors the defenses, guarding communication between lumber operations deep in the forest and the Barrens.",al={"why is the outpost here","horde camp purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does the Warsong Runner need this report delivered?",a="The outpost faces mounting pressure from recent naga assaults, and command needs an accurate picture of the front lines. The runner has stood watch and repelled several waves of attackers, but Kadrak back at the Mor'shan Rampart must understand how perilous the situation has grown so the Horde can coordinate its defenses across Ashenvale.",al={"why send report","runner motive","why deliver warsong report"},it="motive",add="3fdffadb"},{q="What is the Warsong Report for?",a="The Warsong Report contains vital field intelligence detailing the escalating naga incursions against the outpost. Carrying it back informs Kadrak of current frontline defenses and troop needs, ensuring the Horde leadership remains apprised of the region's newest threats.",al={"warsong report purpose","what is warsong report","what does the report say"},it="item",add="ae645a70"},{q="Why does the runner ask you to deliver the update instead of going themselves?",a="The outpost's garrison is stretched thin actively repelling naga incursions. As an able-bodied courier already travelling between the frontline stations, you allow the local defenders to remain at their posts rather than abandoning the ramparts to carry parchment back to the Barrens border.",al={"why me warsong runner","why not deliver it himself","why does the runner need you"},it="why_me",add="0f7ad725"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Along the forest frontier, every soldier counts. Keeping communication open between the Barrens and forward outposts is vital to survival.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Warsong Clan depends on its runners' grit and watchfulness to hold ground claimed under Warchief Thrall's command."},kw={"ashenvale","kadrak","mor'shan","naga","rampart","report","runner","scout","warsong"},rel={"npc:kadrak","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Warsong Runner",level="19",faction="Horde",id=6545,ri={"Warsong Report"}},src={"Warsong Runner Update (quest)"}}
E["quest:6546"] = {t="quest",n="Warsong Outrider Update",z="ashenvale",s="A Warsong scout keeps watch along eastern Ashenvale’s perilous paths. Warsong Outrider Update carries intelligence about nearby Alliance forces, entrenched satyr, and naga moving through neighboring Azshara.",h="A Warsong scout keeps watch along eastern Ashenvale’s perilous paths.",sec={{t="Eyes Along the Forest Edge",b="A lone Warsong Outrider watches the contested eastern edge of Ashenvale. Horde supply lines face constant harassment here, so the outriders scout enemy movements before raiding parties can strike Mor'shan Rampart or Splintertree Post. Meeting one on patrol means the forest is under watch, and the report he carries may help decide whether a Horde fortification holds or falls to ambush.",sp=0},{t="Threats on Every Horizon",b="A Warsong Outrider’s report describes danger across Kalimdor’s central forests. Night elves and the wider Alliance remain a threat, while cunning, demonic satyr haunt eastern Ashenvale. Scouts have also found a massive naga presence spreading through the ruined coastal lands of neighboring Azshara. The Horde faces hostile powers from almost every direction.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Warsong Report?",a="The Warsong Report is an intelligence dispatch written by a Warsong Outrider about enemy positions and dangers in the region. It names nearby Alliance forces, active satyr covens in eastern Ashenvale, and newly discovered naga movements across Azshara.",al={"warsong report quest item","what does the report say","scout report"},it="item"},{q="Who is Kadrak?",a="Kadrak is a Horde commander stationed at Mor'shan Rampart, the defensive barricade guarding the northern border between the Barrens and Ashenvale. He oversees incoming scouts and coordinates forward operations into the forest.",al={"who is kadrak","where is kadrak","kadrak turn in"},it="target"},{q="Why are the naga in Azshara mentioned?",a="Azshara borders eastern Ashenvale, and naga movements there could threaten the Horde’s flank. The outriders watch adjacent lands so the Horde is not surprised by a massive incursion while contending with the night elves.",al={"naga azshara connection","why mention azshara","azshara naga threat"}},{q="What makes eastern Ashenvale so dangerous for the Horde?",a="Eastern Ashenvale puts the Horde between active Alliance detachments, ancient ruins infused with demonic corruption and inhabited by satyr, and untamed woodland beasts. Couriers and patrols risk ambush from every direction.",al={"why is eastern ashenvale dangerous","ashenvale threats","satyr threat"},it="threat"},{q="Who are the Warsong Outriders?",a="The Warsong Outriders are the Warsong clan’s forward vanguard and reconnaissance cavalry in Ashenvale. They track night elf movements, screen logging camps, and secure trade roads.",al={"what are outriders","warsong scouts","outriders lore"},it="people"},{q="Why can't the outrider deliver the report himself?",a="The outrider must keep watch on the trail and track hostile movements as they develop. If he leaves his vantage point, the frontline could miss an unexpected Alliance or satyr advance.",al={"why do i deliver report","why not deliver himself"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does the Warsong Outrider need this report delivered?",a="The Horde faces threats on every front in eastern Ashenvale. With the Alliance nearby, satyrs corrupting the forests, and naga seizing territory across the border in Azshara, Kadrak needs immediate intelligence on enemy movements. Delivering this report ensures the outpost commanders understand the regional dangers and can reinforce vulnerable positions before enemies strike.",al={"why send report","warsong outrider motive","why deliver update"},it="motive",add="43097ba7"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know every dispatch along the Mor'shan line matters to the Horde’s fragile foothold in Ashenvale’s forests.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Warsong clan takes pride in holding the vanguard. Its scouts also know bravery alone cannot stop enemies closing in from every side."},kw={"ashenvale","azshara","kadrak","mor'shan rampart","naga","satyr","warsong outrider","warsong report"},rel={"npc:warsong-outrider","npc:kadrak","zone:ashenvale","zone:azshara","topic:satyr","topic:naga","topic:alliance"},m={start="Warsong Outrider",level="25",faction="Horde",id=6546,ri={"Warsong Report"}},src={"Warsong Outrider Update (quest)"}}
E["quest:6547"] = {t="quest",n="Warsong Scout Update",z="ashenvale",s="Orders from Kadrak reach Warsong Scout Update as scouts watch the contested woods. The Horde depends on their reports to guard its positions in Ashenvale against night elf attacks.",h="Orders from Kadrak reach Warsong Scout Update as scouts watch the contested woods.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="Kadrak depends on scattered Warsong scouts to watch the Ashenvale border. The forest gives night elf sentinels cover, and the scouts face the risk of being cut off. Couriers carry written updates between them so isolated outposts can report what they see and remain connected to Horde command.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Ground",b="Warsong scouts watch for night elf raids meant to reclaim the forest. Every stretch of Ashenvale the clan has cleared or occupied has cost lives. Kadrak's orders keep the forward scouts in touch with the Horde and give them a way to report that their defenses are holding against elven resistance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kadrak?",a="Kadrak is a Horde commander on the boundary between the Barrens and Ashenvale. He coordinates scouting, border defense, and supplies for Warsong operations in the forest.",al={"kadrak","who is kadrak","kadrak role"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Warsong scouts so paranoid about night elves?",a="Night elves know how to hide in their ancestral forests and strike Horde patrols by surprise. The Warsong Clan clears lumber and settles land the elves consider sacred, leaving its scouts at risk of sudden attack.",al={"why fear night elves","night elves in shadows","warsong scout elven danger"},it="danger"},{q="Why is Ashenvale being fought over?",a="The Horde needs Ashenvale's lumber and other resources to build Orgrimmar and supply settlements in the Barrens and Durotar. The night elves consider the forest sacred and fight to drive out the orcish loggers and garrisons.",al={"why fight over ashenvale","ashenvale war","horde ashenvale conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Warsong Clan's role here?",a="The Warsong Clan leads the Horde's effort to claim resources in Ashenvale. Grom Hellscream led them into the woods during the Third War. They remain entrenched there, operating lumber camps and fighting the Sentinels.",al={"warsong clan ashenvale","warsong role"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this report go after reaching the scout?",a="After receiving Kadrak's instructions, the scout reports local success against elven counterattacks. The report keeps Horde leaders informed about conditions at the front.",al={"who gets report","kadrak report","scout update result"},it="next_step"},{q="Are the Horde's plans in Ashenvale succeeding at this point?",a="The frontline scouts believe their defenses are holding: they keep their fortified positions and fend off elven attacks. Ashenvale remains fiercely contested, with neither side in full control.",al={"is horde winning ashenvale","warsong progress"},it="today"},{q="Why does the Warsong Scout want this done?",a="Warsong scouts patrol deep within hostile Ashenvale territory, surrounded by night elves lurking in the shadows. The scout needs fresh orders from Kadrak to coordinate the frontline defense, maintain their hard-won foothold in the forest, and communicate whether their efforts to push back the elves are holding strong.",al={"warsong scout motive","why deliver the report","why does the scout need orders"},it="motive",add="aadbe711"},{q="What is the Warsong Report for?",a="The Warsong Report contains strategic directives and troop dispositions dispatched by Kadrak from the Mor'shan Rampart. For scouts holding isolated outposts in Ashenvale, receiving this report ensures they remain updated on the Horde's tactical maneuvers while defending the clan's claims against lurking night elf forces.",al={"warsong report purpose","what does the warsong report do","warsong report lore"},it="item",add="ae4f0954"},{q="Why does Kadrak need an adventurer to deliver the report?",a="The border between the Barrens and Ashenvale is fraught with ambush. Mor'shan Rampart's stationed grunts and sentries cannot easily abandon their battlements without compromising the outpost's defense, making an independent traveler an ideal courier to slip through the woods and deliver sensitive military directives to isolated scouts.",al={"why send me warsong report","why can't the guards deliver it","why me warsong scout"},it="why_me",add="f7519c0a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep its Ashenvale foothold secure when you carry orders from Kadrak to the outer scouts, who face night elf ambushes.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you inherit the Warsong Clan's fight for timber in Ashenvale, where the land and its ancient defenders resist them.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Warsong scouts on the borders as a continuing desecration of Elune's sacred forests, which the Sentinels strive to purge."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","kadrak","night elves","report","scout","sentinels","warsong"},rel={"npc:kadrak","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Warsong Scout",level="21",faction="Horde",id=6547,ri={"Warsong Report"}},src={"Warsong Scout Update (quest)"}}
E["quest:6564"] = {t="quest",n="Allegiance to the Old Gods",z="ashenvale",s="Horde scouts find a waterlogged message inside Blackfathom Deeps. You carry the naga's note to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, where its words reveal a ritual plot deep within the flooded ruins.",h="Horde scouts find a waterlogged message inside Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="A Scribbled Declaration",b="Horde scouts find a damp, crumpled note while battling the naga in Blackfathom Deeps. Its frantic handwriting gives orders to the naga priestesses: gather elemental water crystals. The crystals are not for random pillaging. They will fuel the summonings of naga aquamancers, who are marshaling elemental forces for a darker purpose.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of the Deep",b="The recovered orders say the naga will use the crystals' elemental energy to appease and fully summon Aku'mai, a monstrous hydra in the service of the Old Gods. The note claims this will herald the return of the world's greatest era, the prehistoric reign of the Old Gods. At Zoram'gar Outpost, Je'neu Sancrea, a Darkspear mystic, identifies the author as Lorgus Jett, a Twilight's Hammer cultist.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Damp Note?",a="The Damp Note holds orders written by the Twilight's Hammer cultist Lorgus Jett. It tells naga priestesses to gather elemental-infused crystals to strengthen their aquamancers and summon Aku'mai, a monstrous servant.",al={"damp note","what does the note say","note lore"},it="item"},{q="Who is Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is a Darkspear troll seer and scholar at Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale. He represents the Earthen Ring and investigates elemental imbalances and ancient threats rising from Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"jeneu sancrea","who is jeneu","zoram outpost questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Lorgus Jett?",a="Lorgus Jett is a human shaman of the Twilight's Hammer cult, working inside Blackfathom Deeps alongside the naga. He oversees the gathering of elemental crystals to empower naga rituals and reawaken dark ancient horrors.",al={"lorgus jett","who wrote the note","naga leader zoram"},it="target"},{q="What is Aku'mai?",a="Aku'mai is a colossal three-headed hydra in the submerged depths of Blackfathom Deeps. The Twilight's Hammer cult and the naga revere the creature, which is bound to the primordial darkness of the Old Gods.",al={"akumai","who is akumai","aku'mai lore"},it="threat"},{q="Why are the naga collecting water crystals?",a="The naga gather water crystals to use the elemental spirits trapped inside them as raw power for their aquamancers. By siphoning that magic, they hope to appease Aku'mai and gather enough power to bring back the Old Gods.",al={"why naga crystals","elemental crystals naga","aquamancer crystals"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead?",a="Carrying the note to Je'neu Sancrea leads to a follow-up effort to track down and execute Lorgus Jett, disrupting the cult's ritual plans in Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"what comes after allegiance to the old gods","allegiance to the old gods part 2","next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help uncover Lorgus Jett's note and protect Zoram'gar Outpost from the Twilight's Hammer and its naga allies, who threaten the Horde's foothold on Ashenvale's western coast.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know that forcing water elemental spirits into ritual crystals perverts the natural balance and demands swift correction.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you help your Darkspear kin Je'neu Sancrea uncover ancient cosmic entities whose return would threaten every tribe across Azeroth."},kw={"aku'mai","allegiance","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","damp note","je'neu sancrea","lorgus jett","old gods","wrathscale","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:je-neu-sancrea","npc:lorgus-jett","npc:aku-mai","zone:blackfathom","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","zone:ashenvale","topic:old-god","topic:naga"},m={start="Damp Note",["end"]="Je'neu Sancrea",level="22",faction="Horde",id=6564},src={"Allegiance to the Old Gods"}}
E["quest:6571"] = {t="quest",n="Warsong Supplies",z="ashenvale",s="At Splintertree Post, Locke Okarr needs supplies to keep the Warsong Lumber Camp running. Some await in town, some in Booty Bay, and others lie in enemy hands across Ashenvale.",h="At Splintertree Post, Locke Okarr needs supplies to keep the Warsong Lumber Camp running.",sec={{t="Keeping the Saws Spinning",b="Locke Okarr works to keep the Warsong Lumber Camp supplied from Splintertree Post. The Warsong Clan needs a steady flow of heavy tools to harvest Ashenvale's ancient timber. Raids by furbolgs and satyrs have scattered or seized local supplies, leaving the camp short of vital gear.",sp=0},{t="A Scattered Logistics Chain",b="You gather equipment from across Kalimdor and beyond. Pixel, the goblin courier at Splintertree Post, has circular saw blades, while Wharfmaster Lozgil in Booty Bay holds a crate of heavy axes. Foulweald and Thistlefur furbolgs have taken logging ropes, and satyrs at Night Run, Satyrnaar, and Xavian have stolen barrels of Warsong machinery oil for their profane rites.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the required Warsong Supplies?",a="Locke Okarr needs four items: Warsong Saw Blades held by Pixel, a crate of Warsong Axes shipped to Booty Bay, Logging Rope taken by local furbolgs, and Warsong Oil stolen by Ashenvale's satyrs.",al={"warsong supplies list","what items needed","supplies needed"},gp=true},{q="Who is Locke Okarr?",a="Locke Okarr is an orc at Splintertree Post who coordinates material deliveries to the Warsong Lumber Camp. He needs help recovering scattered shipments before the camp's work is delayed.",al={"locke okarr lore","who gives warsong supplies","splintertree quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Horde shipping equipment from Booty Bay?",a="The Horde uses neutral trade networks such as the Steamwheedle Cartel to import specialty goods that Durotar and the Barrens cannot easily forge in bulk. Goblin channels route the heavy lumbering axes through maritime hubs such as Booty Bay on their way to Ashenvale.",al={"why booty bay","booty bay axe shipment","steamwheedle tools"}},{q="Why do the satyrs want Warsong Oil?",a="Satyrs at Satyrnaar, Night Run, and Xavian divert the stolen industrial oil from machinery to corrupted rites dedicated to the Burning Legion and the spreading taint of Felwood.",al={"satyr oil lore","why do satyrs have oil","warsong oil rituals"}},{q="Which furbolgs stole the logging rope?",a="The Foulweald and Thistlefur furbolg tribes took the Logging Rope. Both are fiercely hostile to the Horde's clear-cutting across Ashenvale.",al={"who stole the rope","furbolg rope lore","foulweald thistlefur rope"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is the Warsong Lumber Camp so vital to the Horde?",a="The Warsong Lumber Camp provides timber the Horde needs for construction and military supplies. Durotar's arid lands offer virtually no usable timber, so the Warsong Clan harvests Ashenvale's massive trees to build Orgrimmar and support the Horde's growing military infrastructure.",al={"why harvest ashenvale","warsong lumber importance","orcs cutting trees"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Locke Okarr need these supplies gathered?",a="Locke Okarr is responsible for provisioning the Warsong Lumber Camp, where critical tools have fallen into dangerously short supply. Shipments have been delayed, pilfered, or intercepted across Ashenvale and beyond. If he fails to deliver these essential logging materials promptly, he faces severe trouble from his superiors in the Warsong clan.",al={"why locke okarr supplies","why gather supplies locke okarr","locke okarr motive"},it="motive",add="b7ffa730"},{q="What are the Warsong Saw Blades used for?",a="The saw blades are crucial industrial components for the mechanized shredders and mills operated at the Warsong Lumber Camp. Without fresh blades, the Horde's heavy logging machinery cannot efficiently cut through Ashenvale's massive ancient trees to supply timber for the construction of Orgrimmar and local encampments.",al={"what are saw blades for","warsong saw blades use","saw blades logging camp"},it="item",add="54c7a3c1"},{q="What is the Warsong Axe Shipment used for?",a="Imported all the way from the goblin foundries in Booty Bay, this crate of heavy-duty axes supplies the Warsong outriders and laborers who clear thick brush and fell Ashenvale's dense timber by hand. In a hostile forest crawling with night elves and beasts, these sturdy tools double as reliable weapons of war.",al={"what is axe shipment for","warsong axe shipment use","axe shipment booty bay"},it="item",add="9c63ad01"},{q="What is the Warsong Oil used for?",a="Warsong Oil is a heavy lubricant required to keep the camp's steam engines, shredders, and complex logging rigs functioning smoothly under punishing conditions. Without it, the heavy ironworks seize up and stall timber operations entirely.",al={"what is warsong oil for","warsong oil purpose","why logging camp oil"},it="item",add="74cafbab"},{q="What is the Logging Rope used for?",a="This durable heavy-duty rope is used by the lumber camp's crews to haul, secure, and hoist massive timber trunks after they are felled. Managing towering Ashenvale trees without adequate rigging is nearly impossible and risks crushing workers or damaging valuable gear.",al={"what is logging rope for","logging rope purpose","rope warsong camp"},it="item",add="76a0db14"},{q="Why does Locke Okarr ask an adventurer instead of the outpost guards?",a="Splintertree Post's garrison is stretched thin defending against constant incursions from the Silverwing Sentinels and hostile forest dwellers. Locke cannot pull vital guards away from the perimeter, nor can he personally leave his post to scour distant corners of Ashenvale and travel as far as Booty Bay.",al={"why me locke okarr","why cant guards get supplies","why not send guards"},it="why_me",add="4e02126d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's expansion into Durotar depends on lumber secured by the Warsong Clan. Recovering these tools helps support Orgrimmar.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you help honor the Warsong Clan's legacy in Ashenvale by keeping its axes sharp and camps supplied, despite harassment from forest natives.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how goblin supplies, from Pixel's saw blades to steam-engine lubricants, help keep the machinery working as the Warsong Clan cuts Ashenvale's ancient forests."},kw={"ashenvale","booty bay","locke okarr","logging rope","pixel","saw blades","splintertree post","warsong lumber camp","warsong oil","warsong supplies"},rel={"subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","quest:6581","npc:pixel","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:satyrnaar","subzone:xavian","subzone:night-run"},m={start="Locke Okarr",level="27",faction="Horde",id=6571,ri={"Logging Rope","Warsong Axe Shipment","Warsong Oil","Warsong Saw Blades"}},src={"Warsong Supplies (quest)"}}
E["quest:6581"] = {t="quest",n="Warsong Saw Blades",z="ashenvale",s="At Splintertree Post, the Warsong loggers wait on blades from Ratchet. Pixel, their courier, will trade the shipment for a weapon to protect herself on Ashenvale's dangerous roads. The blades are needed to keep the Horde's lumber camps working.",h="At Splintertree Post, the Warsong loggers wait on blades from Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Courier's Shrewd Barter",b="Pixel has brought heavy saw blades from Ratchet to Splintertree Post, but she will not hand them over for free. In Ashenvale's wilds, she values safety more than coin. She asks for a Deadly Blunderbuss in trade, so she can protect herself on her dangerous travels through hostile territory.",sp=0},{t="Supplying the War Effort",b="The Horde needs timber from Ashenvale to ease shortages across Durotar and the Barrens. Axes dull quickly against the ancient groves, so the Warsong loggers need goblin-forged blades. Pixel's shipment supplies the lumber camps, where the Horde cuts timber for outposts and war machines despite fierce resistance from the night elves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pixel and why does she have the saw blades?",a="Pixel is a courier at Splintertree Post who brought saw blades from Ratchet. She keeps the shipment until she can secure a weapon for her protection.",al={"who is pixel","pixie splintertree","saw blade courier"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Pixel want a Deadly Blunderbuss instead of gold?",a="Pixel considers personal safety more valuable than coin on the dangerous road from the Barrens into Ashenvale. She asks for a Deadly Blunderbuss to defend herself on her travels.",al={"why deadly blunderbuss","pixel gun trade","why want a gun"},it="motive"},{q="Why are these saw blades so important to the Horde?",a="The Warsong Clan needs timber for the Horde's outposts and war machines. Axes wear down against Ashenvale's ancient trees, so the lumber camps rely on imported mechanical blades.",al={"why are saw blades needed","warsong lumber importance","why warsong supplies"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where did the saw blades originally come from?",a="The saw blades came from Ratchet and were hauled overland to Splintertree Post.",al={"origin of saw blades","ratchet blades","where did saw blades come from"},it="origin"},{q="Where does this quest fit into the Warsong logging effort?",a="The saw blades are one of the supplies needed to keep the Warsong lumber camps working in Ashenvale.",al={"warsong supplies chain","warsong saw blades prerequisite"},it="history"},{q="Can anyone make the weapon Pixel wants?",a="Skilled Engineers can craft a Deadly Blunderbuss from copper tubes, copper bolts, a wooden stock, and leather. Couriers and warriors can also trade for one through local markets or fellow adventurers.",al={"how to get deadly blunderbuss","blunderbuss source","engineering gun"},gp=true},{q="What is the Deadly Blunderbuss for?",a="Pixel needs personal protection out in the wild. As a courier transporting freight through untamed frontiers like Ashenvale and the Barrens, traveling alone is perilous. Rather than coin, which cannot fend off beasts or night elves, she demands a dependable engineering firearm so she can look after herself on the road.",al={"why blunderbuss","deadly blunderbuss pixel","what does pixel use blunderbuss for"},it="item",add="496db877"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an Engineer, you can craft the Deadly Blunderbuss Pixel wants. Engineering supplies weapons and machinery for the Horde's war effort.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you depend on Ashenvale's lumber camps for timber to build in Orgrimmar. Each machinery delivery helps keep the camps working.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know the Warsong Clan stakes its pride on logging Ashenvale under Grommash Hellscream. Keeping the blades turning supports the clan's foothold in the forest."},kw={"ashenvale","deadly blunderbuss","pixel","ratchet","splintertree post","warsong outriders","warsong saw blades","warsong supplies"},rel={"npc:pixel","subzone:splintertree-post","quest:6571","zone:ashenvale","subzone:ratchet"},m={start="Pixel",level="27",faction="Horde",id=6581,ri={"Deadly Blunderbuss"}},src={"Warsong Saw Blades (quest)"}}
E["quest:6621"] = {t="quest",n="King of the Foulweald",z="ashenvale",s="Karang Amakkar orders a Horde strike against the Foulweald furbolgs southeast of Astranaar. Horde champions plant a war banner on the tribe’s sacred totem mound, drawing out Chief Murgut and killing him.",h="Karang Amakkar orders a Horde strike against the Foulweald furbolgs southeast of Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Show of Force",b="Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar Outpost sees the corrupted Foulweald as a danger to the Horde. The tribe is smaller than the northern Thistlefur, but its members are fierce. Rather than wait for them to ambush Horde patrols, Karang orders a show of force meant to break their will.",sp=0},{t="Desecration and Challenge",b="Greenpaw Village lies northeast of Mystral Lake. Karang prepares a tribal war banner to plant in the center of the Foulweald totem mound, insulting the tribe’s ancestral spirits and pride. Furbolg defenders rush to tear it down, and Chief Murgut emerges to defend his honor in open combat. Taking Murgut’s personal totem breaks the tribe’s leadership and establishes Horde supremacy in the area.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders the death of Chief Murgut?",a="Karang Amakkar, an orc at Zoram'gar Outpost on Ashenvale’s western coast, orders Chief Murgut’s death after investigating the neighboring Thistlefur furbolgs.",al={"quest giver king of the foulweald","who gives king of the foulweald","karang amakkar quest"}},{q="Where is Greenpaw Village located?",a="Greenpaw Village lies southeast of Astranaar, northeast of Mystral Lake, and just south of Ashenvale’s main eastern highway.",al={"where is greenpaw village","foulweald location","where to plant karang banner"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde plant a banner on the totem mound?",a="Karang’s banner is planted on the sacred totem mound to provoke the Foulweald. The insult drives them to attack and brings Chief Murgut into open combat to defend his standing.",al={"why place banner","totem mound banner purpose","why challenge murgut"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the Foulweald furbolgs?",a="The Foulweald are one of Ashenvale’s furbolg tribes, driven mad and corrupted after the Third War. Though fewer in number than the Thistlefur, they remain violent and hostile to outsiders.",al={"what are the foulweald","foulweald tribe lore","who is chief murgut"},it="people"},{q="What does retrieving Murgut's Totem accomplish?",a="Taking Chief Murgut’s totem to Zoram'gar Outpost proves his defeat. Without their leader and with their sacred mound disgraced, the surviving Foulweald are intimidated into avoiding further conflict with the Horde.",al={"murgut totem purpose","what happens after murgut dies"},it="item"},{q="How does this quest fit into the earlier furbolg investigations?",a="Karang turns south to the Foulweald after dealing with the northern Thistlefur in 'Between a Rock and a Thistlefur.' He seeks to crush them before they can launch coordinated raids.",al={"between a rock and a thistlefur connection","prerequisite king of the foulweald"},it="history"},{q="Why does Karang Amakkar want Chief Murgut defeated?",a="Karang Amakkar views the Foulweald tribe as a growing danger to the Horde's foothold in Ashenvale. Though fewer in number than the neighboring Thistlefur, their sheer ferocity makes them an unpredictable hazard. By issuing a direct challenge and slaying their chieftain, Karang aims to break their will and deliver an unmistakable warning that the Horde will brook no threats in the forest.",al={"karang motive","why kill murgut","why defeat foulweald"},it="motive",add="b1528232"},{q="Who is Chief Murgut?",a="Chief Murgut is the ferocious leader of the Foulweald furbolgs, dwelling within Greenpaw Village southeast of Astranaar. He maintains dominion over the tribe from their sacred totem mound, leading through sheer might and territorial aggression. Karang sends you to provoke him into open combat by defiling his tribe's grounds with a Horde war banner.",al={"who is murgut","chief murgut foulweald","who is the king of the foulweald"},it="target",add="9b8cfe09"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Karang Amakkar use shows of force to cow hostile Ashenvale tribes and secure central trails for Horde supply caravans.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you know that provoking an enemy chieftain into single combat is a classic way of war, favoring strength and decisive confrontation over long skirmishes.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you recognize the Foulweald’s distorted totems and aggression as signs of the spiritual imbalance that plagued Ashenvale’s native tribes after the Burning Legion’s invasion."},kw={"ashenvale","foulweald","furbolg","greenpaw village","karang amakkar","murgut","totem mound","zoram'gar"},rel={"npc:karang-amakkar","subzone:greenpaw-village","topic:furbolg","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde","subzone:mystral-lake","subzone:astranaar"},m={start="Karang Amakkar",level="26",faction="Horde",id=6621},src={"King of the Foulweald (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6641"] = {t="quest",n="Vorsha the Lasher",z="ashenvale",s="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Vorsha the Lasher terrorizes the Horde's foothold on Ashenvale's coast. The nearby naga honor the hydra's ferocity with an offering brazier on an offshore island. Muglash plans to extinguish its flame, drawing Vorsha ashore to end her attacks.",h="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Vorsha the Lasher terrorizes the Horde's foothold on Ashenvale's coast.",sec={{t="A Terror from the Deep",b="Northwestern Ashenvale's Zoram Strand is among the most dangerous stretches of coast. Zoram'gar Outpost holds a narrow strip there, beset by hostile wildlife, night elves, and serpentine invaders. Among the strand's most destructive threats is Vorsha the Lasher, a gargantuan hydra known for brutal, unprovoked strikes against the outpost. She surges from the surf to crush its defenses and butcher its warriors, then vanishes into the deep tides.",sp=0},{t="The Brazier of the Naga",b="The nearby naga venerate Vorsha's ravenous violence. On a rocky outcrop offshore, they keep an offering brazier burning in her honor. Muglash, an orc determined to end the outpost's constant harassment, has realized that defiling the ritual flame will enrage both the naga guardians and the hydra. Vorsha will surge to the surface in fury, giving the defenders a chance to draw her into an ambush instead of waiting for another surprise slaughter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vorsha the Lasher?",a="Vorsha the Lasher is a fierce, massive hydra that haunts the waters off the Zoram Strand. She makes frequent, unprovoked attacks on Zoram'gar Outpost, destroying its defenses and slaughtering Horde personnel.",al={"vorsha","what is vorsha","vorsha hydra"},it="target"},{q="Why do the naga honor Vorsha?",a="The naga of the Zoram Strand honor Vorsha for her unrelenting ferocity and destructive appetite. They keep an offshore brazier burning in tribute to her wicked nature.",al={"why naga like hydra","vorsha naga brazier","why worship vorsha"}},{q="How is Vorsha lured out to fight?",a="Muglash leads an assault on the island where the naga tend Vorsha's brazier. Extinguishing the sacred flame enrages the naga guardians and Vorsha, driving the hydra to surface and retaliate.",al={"how to summon vorsha","how do you call vorsha","brazier island vorsha"},gp=true},{q="Who is Muglash?",a="Muglash is an orc stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost. Tired of living in fear of Vorsha's unprovoked coastal attacks, he devises a plan to snuff out the naga's ritual brazier and fight the beast alongside dependable allies.",al={"who is muglash","muglash orc","zoramgar muglash"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Zoram'gar Outpost vulnerable to coastal beasts?",a="Zoram'gar Outpost is an isolated frontier camp on Ashenvale's exposed beaches. Naga dominate the ruins in the sea, while wild hydras patrol the surf; the outpost's closeness to the water leaves it open to amphibious attacks from all directions.",al={"why is zoramgar attacked","zoram strand danger"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after Vorsha is slain?",a="After Vorsha is slain, the victory is reported to the Warsong Runners maintaining the lines at Zoram'gar Outpost. The frontier guards' constant burden eases, and the immediate coast is secured from sudden assault.",al={"vorsha quest turn in","who to report vorsha to"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Muglash want Vorsha killed?",a="Vorsha is a constant terror to Zoram'gar Outpost. The vicious hydra repeatedly surges from the sea unprovoked, laying waste to Horde forces and anything else caught in her path along the coast. Muglash aims to put an end to these devastating raids once and for all by confronting the beast at its sacred summoning site.",al={"muglash motive","why kill vorsha","why fight vorsha"},it="motive",add="4cca3bd5"},{q="Why does Muglash need your help against Vorsha?",a="Slaying Vorsha requires traveling out to an island held by coastal naga and extinguishing the sacred brazier they keep in her honor. Muglash intends to fight alongside you, but he knows the ritual will draw down not only the massive hydra itself, but waves of furious naga defenders. A single warrior cannot hold off such numbers alone.",al={"why does muglash need help","why not horde guards vorsha","why me muglash"},it="why_me",add="23eb1be6"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Defending Zoram'gar Outpost preserves the Horde's northern foothold in Ashenvale and its logistics, though supply lines there face constant attack.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may share Muglash's refusal to cower behind makeshift palisades, choosing to charge into the surf and hunt predatory beasts face to face."},kw={"ashenvale","brazier","hydra","muglash","naga","vorsha","zoram strand","zoram'gar"},rel={"subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Muglash",["end"]="Warsong Runner",faction="Horde",id=6641},src={"Vorsha the Lasher (quest)"}}
E["quest:8725"] = {t="quest",n="Riversong the Elder",z="ashenvale",s="During the Lunar Festival, pilgrims seek Riversong the Elder beneath a shrine in Astranaar. The night elf spirit offers wisdom and points them toward other honored ancestors across Kalimdor.",h="During the Lunar Festival, pilgrims seek Riversong the Elder beneath a shrine in Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Astranaar",b="In Astranaar, Riversong the Elder waits beneath an open night elf shrine. A shaft of light falls through the Ashenvale canopy onto her spirit. During the Lunar Festival, pilgrims gather there to honor those who came before.",sp=0},{t="Gazing at the Heavens",b="Riversong the Elder recalls how night elves read truth and mystery in the stars. She urges patience and contemplation, then guides pilgrims toward other spirits, including Elder Starweave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Elder Riversong?",a="You can find Riversong the Elder beneath a small night elf shrine in Astranaar, Ashenvale. A beam of light falls through the forest canopy onto her.",al={"riversong location","where is riversong","elder riversong loc"}},{q="What is the purpose of visiting Elder Riversong?",a="Pilgrims honor Riversong the Elder during the Lunar Festival to pay respect to their ancestors. She grants an ancestral blessing and coins of ancestry, and guides them toward other elders across Kalimdor.",al={"why visit riversong","what does riversong do"}},{q="Which elder does Riversong direct you toward?",a="Riversong the Elder directs you toward Elder Starweave, another honored night elf spirit observing the festival.",al={"next elder after riversong","who does riversong mention"}},{q="Can Horde players speak to Elder Riversong?",a="You can speak with Riversong the Elder as a Horde traveler, though Astranaar's guards and sentinels stand in your way. Festival elders do not refuse communion based on faction.",al={"can horde visit riversong","is riversong alliance only"}},{q="Why is Elder Riversong surrounded by a beam of light?",a="The beam of light around Riversong the Elder represents the favor of Elune and the heavens. It illuminates each ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival.",al={"why does riversong glow","light on riversong"}},{q="What does Elder Riversong say when honored?",a="Riversong the Elder speaks of the countless stars and the answers they hold to earthly mysteries. She asks whether the wise and lucky might gaze upward and find truth.",al={"riversong quote","riversong dialogue"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can honor Riversong the Elder beneath an Astranaar shrine, joining your people's long history beneath Ashenvale's stars.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance pilgrim, you can visit Riversong the Elder easily in Astranaar, one of the Alliance's primary strongholds in central Kalimdor.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the Lunar Festival's celestial elders as part of the ancient Cenarion bond with nature, spirits, and the night sky."},kw={"ancestor","ashenvale","astranaar","elder","lunar festival","riversong","shrine","starweave"},rel={"subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","npc:elder-starweave","topic:night-elf","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Riversong",id=8725},src={"Riversong the Elder"}}
E["quest:945"] = {t="quest",n="Therylune's Escape",z="ashenvale",s="Therylune is cornered by cultists at the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore. She wandered into its dig sites, and you are needed to guide her to safety and tell her worried sister, Therysil, at the Shrine of Aessina that she survived.",h="Therylune is cornered by cultists at the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Perilous Stroll",b="At the Master's Glaive, Therylune is pinned down by Twilight's Hammer cultists. The ravine is dominated by the skull of an ancient monstrosity, pierced by a huge stone blade. Therylune wandered into the heart of the valley despite the dread surrounding it. She survives by reacting quickly and hiding among the rough terrain.",sp=0},{t="Word to the Shrine",b="Therysil waits far to the south at the Shrine of Aessina. Her adventurous sister Therylune rarely minds getting dirt on her clothes, but even Therysil was shocked to learn she had ventured into the unwholesome excavations at the Master's Glaive. Word that Therylune is safe will ease her worry. Therysil knows the dark forces digging through Darkshore's ancient earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Therylune?",a="Therylune is an adventurous young night elf who wandered into the dangerous excavations at the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore. She is Therysil's sister.",al={"therylune","who is the girl","trapped elf"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Therysil?",a="Therysil is Therylune's sister and lives at the Shrine of Aessina in Ashenvale. She is dismayed that her sibling wandered so close to a dark, tainted place.",al={"therysil","therylune sister"},it="allies"},{q="Why is the Master's Glaive so dangerous?",a="The Master's Glaive is a foreboding ravine where an ancient old lord fell long ago. Twilight's Hammer cultists swarm the site, digging there and attacking trespassers.",al={"masters glaive danger","cultists masters glaive"},it="place"},{q="Where does Therylune need to be escorted?",a="Therylune needs an escort away from the Master's Glaive to safety. Afterward, you need to travel to the Shrine of Aessina and tell her sister she survived.",al={"escort destination","where does therylune go"},gp=true},{q="Where is the Shrine of Aessina located?",a="The Shrine of Aessina lies in southwestern Ashenvale, west of Astranaar. It is a sanctuary dedicated to the forest spirit Aessina.",al={"shrine of aessina location","where is therysil"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How did Therylune survive surrounded by cultists?",a="Therylune avoided capture by hiding among the rocks and terrain before the surrounding Twilight's Hammer cultists could spot her.",al={"how did therylune hide"},it="history"},{q="Why does Therylune need your help to escape?",a="Therylune wandered into the sinister excavation at the Master's Glaive and quickly found herself trapped and surrounded by Twilight's Hammer cultists. While her knack for hiding kept her alive, she cannot slip past the encircling zealots on her own to reach safety and reassure her sister, Therysil.",al={"why does therylune want help","therylune motive","why help therylune"},it="motive",add="8c0c4bd7"},{q="Why can't Therylune escape on her own?",a="While skilled enough at hiding to avoid immediate capture, Therylune is completely unarmed, defenseless, and trapped deep within hostile territory. With no local guards or allies nearby to aid her, she depends entirely on a passing adventurer to cut an escape path through the cultists.",al={"why does therylune need me","why cant therylune escape","why me therylune"},it="why_me",add="cc515991"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Master's Glaive marks an ancient scar in Kalimdor's history. Seeing a fellow kaldorei wander into cultist excavations is a sobering reminder of the threats within Ashenvale.",["faction:Alliance"]="When you help wayfarers like Therylune, you strengthen the Alliance's presence and goodwill among the night elves defending Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","cultists","escort","master's glaive","shrine of aessina","therylune","therysil","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:therylune","npc:therysil","subzone:master-s-glaive","subzone:shrine-of-aessina","zone:ashenvale","quest:944"},m={start="Therylune",["end"]="Therysil",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=945},src={"Therylune's Escape"}}
E["quest:970"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="ashenvale",s="Reports from the Tower of Althalaxx lead south into Ashenvale, where the Cult of the Dark Strand also threatens the woods. Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post sends you to the ruins of Ordil'Aran to recover a Glowing Soul Gem.",h="Reports from the Tower of Althalaxx lead south into Ashenvale, where the Cult of the Dark Strand also...",sec={{t="A Plea Across the Border",b="After the trouble around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, reports lead south to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post. The Cult of the Dark Strand is pressing into the ancient elven woods, and Delgren has fought them for a long time. Their reach crosses both territories, so he seeks to strike at the source of their sorcery.",sp=0},{t="The Secrets of Ordil'Aran",b="The ruins of Ordil'Aran lie northeast of Maestra's Post, overrun by Dark Strand cultists. Delgren says their operatives carry glowing soul gems, vessels enchanted with magic that sustains the cult's power. Hunt the cultists among the ruins and recover one of the gems so Delgren can break its enchantment and uncover the source of their rite.",sp=0},{t="A Spirit Trapped",b="Delgren finds a tormented spirit bound inside the Glowing Soul Gem. When its wards break, Sargath appears, one of the elves of Ameth'Aran whom Athrikus Narassin trapped in soul gems during the Sundering and has slowly drained ever since. Sargath names Athrikus's lieutenant, Ilkrud Magthrull, whose tome may reveal where the remaining soul gems are held.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Glowing Soul Gem?",a="Cult of the Dark Strand members in the ruins of Ordil'Aran northeast of Maestra's Post carry Glowing Soul Gems. The ruins are in Ashenvale, and you may need to search several cultists to recover one.",al={"soul gem location","where does soul gem drop","dark strand soul gem"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion stationed at Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. He fights forces invading the forest, especially the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"delgren","who is delgren"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Cult of the Dark Strand?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand is a sect based in the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore and in ancient elven ruins such as Ordil'Aran in Ashenvale. Its members practice dark sorcery, soul binding, and necromantic rites.",al={"dark strand cult","who are dark strand"},it="threat"},{q="Why is a Darkshore quest sending me to Ashenvale?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand's reach crosses from the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore into Ashenvale. Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post knows how to oppose the cult's soul-binding magic.",al={"why maestra's post","why go to ashenvale"},it="place"},{q="What happens when the soul gem is deciphered?",a="Delgren plans to decipher the dark enchantment on the Glowing Soul Gem. What he finds becomes clear after you bring it to him.",al={"what is in the soul gem","soul gem ghost"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Ordil'Aran located?",a="Ordil'Aran is an ancient elven ruin northeast of Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. The Cult of the Dark Strand has overrun it.",al={"ordil'aran location","where is ordilaran"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier want this done?",a="Delgren has been locked in combat against the Cult of the Dark Strand, who have entrenched themselves northeast of Maestra's Post. To him, they are a dangerous thorn that must be torn out completely. The dire warnings in Balthule Shadowstrike's letter confirm that their corrupt influence is escalating, and Delgren believes unraveling the secrets trapped within their enchanted soul gem is the only way to expose and dismantle their power.",al={"delgren motive","why does delgren want soul gem","why fight cult of dark strand"},it="motive",add="a63b3648"},{q="What is the Glowing Soul Gem for?",a="The Glowing Soul Gem is a dark, enchanted artifact carried by the Cult of the Dark Strand at Ordil'Aran. Delgren believes it holds the secret to the cult's vile magic and the power they wield. By bringing the gem to him, you allow Delgren to decipher the dark enchantments woven into the stone and uncover whatever essence or entity is trapped inside.",al={"what is glowing soul gem","glowing soul gem purpose","soul gem dark strand"},it="item",add="c112c454"},{q="Who are you sent against at Ordil'Aran?",a="You are sent to confront the Cult of the Dark Strand occupying the ruins of Ordil'Aran, northeast of Maestra's Post. Cultists, fanatics, acolytes, and adept spellcasters have gathered among the elven ruins to conduct forbidden rites. One of their members carries an enchanted soul gem that Delgren needs to unlock the cult's secrets, requiring you to cut through their ranks until the relic is recovered.",al={"who is at ordil'aran","dark strand at ordil'aran","who holds soul gem"},it="target",add="d0742ede"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, purging unholy corruption from the world includes destroying dark soul vessels and fighting the cultists who twist them.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, examining a dark soul vessel reflects your calling to oppose corruption and comfort tormented souls.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the Cult of the Dark Strand defile ancient ruins like Ordil'Aran and corrupt the northern woods. Removing them is urgent.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help outposts in Darkshore and Ashenvale protect the northern frontier from dark practitioners who threaten Alliance travelers."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","dark strand","darkshore","delgren","delgren the purifier","glowing soul gem","maestra's post","ordil'aran"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=970,ri={"Glowing Soul Gem"}},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (4)"}}
E["quest:976"] = {t="quest",n="Supplies to Auberdine",z="ashenvale",s="Feero Ironhand carries provisions and messages north from Maestra's Post toward Auberdine, with Alliance adventurers guarding the way. Trouble around the Tower of Althalaxx and hostile infiltrators make the road unsafe.",h="Feero Ironhand carries provisions and messages north from Maestra's Post toward Auberdine, with Alliance...",sec={{t="A Perilous Road North",b="Maestra's Post lies on Ashenvale's western frontier, between the forest and Darkshore. After investigations into sinister activity around the Tower of Althalaxx, Delgren the Purifier sends supplies and intelligence to Sentinel Starbreeze in Auberdine. The outpost relies on armed escorts instead of solitary couriers, so Feero Ironhand travels with guards along the forest road.",sp=0},{t="Shadows Along the Trail",b="Feero Ironhand's road north brings him through woods where ambushes threaten his delivery. Cultists of the Dark Strand seek to silence reports of their demonic rituals. Forsaken scouts stalk the underbrush, while Balizar the Umbrage, Aligar the Tormentor, and Caedakar the Vicious each attempt to cut down the caravan before it reaches the border.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Feero Ironhand?",a="Feero Ironhand is a human courier stationed at Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale. Delgren the Purifier entrusts him with messages and logistical aid for Auberdine, and he will not travel without capable bodyguards.",al={"feero","feero ironhand lore","who is the dwarf escort"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Auberdine need these supplies?",a="Darkshore and northern Ashenvale face growing corruption and threats from demonic cultists operating out of the Tower of Althalaxx. The night elf Sentinels in Auberdine, led locally by Sentinel Starbreeze, need provisions and current intelligence to defend the coast.",al={"why send supplies to auberdine","auberdine supplies","sentinel starbreeze"},it="purpose"},{q="Who attacks Feero along the road?",a="Feero warns that dangerous foes operate throughout the forest and asks for guards. Their identities become clear during the escort.",al={"who ambushes feero","feero ambushers","who attacks on the road"},it="threat"},{q="What is the connection to the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="Delgren the Purifier is orchestrating efforts to uncover and disrupt the dark rituals of the cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx. This escort grows from that investigation, carrying intelligence and support to the Night Elf leadership in Auberdine.",al={"althalaxx connection","tower of althalaxx","delgren connection"},it="ties"},{q="Where do I report after protecting Feero?",a="After you see Feero safely through the Ashenvale ambushes, you report to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post and confirm the delivery succeeded.",al={"turn in supplies to auberdine","where do i go after escorting feero","quest turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Feero Ironhand want to deliver these supplies?",a="Delgren the Purifier tasked Feero with delivering crucial supplies and vital messages northward to Sentinel Starbreeze in Auberdine. Dark forces and cultists infested with sinister designs operate throughout western Ashenvale, and Feero knows that allowing these sensitive communications or provisions to fall into enemy hands could prove disastrous for the Alliance defense.",al={"feero ironhand motive","why does feero need help","why supplies to auberdine"},it="motive",add="1813fb85"},{q="Why does Feero Ironhand ask you for protection instead of the post's guards?",a="Feero is loath to travel alone while carrying important supplies and messages through dangerous Ashenvale. He asks for bodyguards to help the delivery reach Auberdine safely.",al={"why me feero","why does feero need escort","why doesn't feero go alone"},it="why_me",add="affb8fb0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="By safeguarding this route, you help keep Ashenvale's outposts connected to Auberdine, preserving the Alliance's fragile hold on northern Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="The supplies and dispatches you escort north aid the Sentinels in Auberdine as they face growing darkness across Darkshore and along the Ashenvale border.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Feero Ironhand represent your people's willingness to support kaldorei allies in unfamiliar, dangerous ancient forests."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","balizar the umbrage","darkshore","delgren the purifier","feero ironhand","maestra's post","sentinel starbreeze","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:feero-ironhand","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:auberdine","quest:965","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Feero Ironhand",["end"]="Delgren the Purifier",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=976},src={"Supplies to Auberdine"}}
E["quest:990"] = {t="quest",n="Trek to Ashenvale",z="ashenvale",s="Sentinel Selarin sends travelers south from Auberdine into Ashenvale. There, you report to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar, where the Sentinels face spreading corruption.",h="Sentinel Selarin sends travelers south from Auberdine into Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Leaving the Coast",b="Sentinel Selarin's call for aid brings you from Auberdine, on Darkshore's somber gray coast, toward the night elf lands to the south. The Sentinel trusts capable fighters and scouts to make the journey into the heart of that territory. With local threats in Darkshore handled, the greater perils of Ashenvale now demand attention.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Astranaar",b="An ancient night elf road winds south beneath Ashenvale's dense canopy. Raene Wolfrunner, who leads the Sentinels in Astranaar, has urgently called for reinforcements. Demonic taints, rampant wildlife, and incursions from beyond ancestral lands have stretched the defenders thin. They need outside aid to hold the sacred forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this trek?",a="Sentinel Selarin, a night elf sentinel sent to Auberdine by Raene Wolfrunner to seek help, directs you south toward Astranaar.",al={"quest giver","who starts trek to ashenvale","selarin"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Raene Wolfrunner?",a="Raene Wolfrunner leads the Sentinels in Astranaar. She organizes Ashenvale's defense and coordinates efforts against the corruption afflicting the forest.",al={"raene","wolfrunner","astranaar leader"},it="target"},{q="Why are adventurers being sent to Ashenvale?",a="Spreading corruption and mounting threats from beyond Ashenvale's borders are overwhelming the local night elf Sentinels. They urgently need capable allies to aid Astranaar's citizens and defenders.",al={"why ashenvale","what is happening in ashenvale","corruption ashenvale"},it="purpose"},{q="Is the road between Darkshore and Ashenvale safe?",a="Sentinel Selarin advises you to stay close to the road. The deep woods hold aggressive predators, satyrs, and hostile forces along the untamed borders.",al={"road safety","ashenvale road safe"},it="danger"},{q="What should I do upon arriving in Astranaar?",a="Report directly to Raene Wolfrunner when you reach Astranaar. She advises you to speak with the town's residents and defenders, many of whom need immediate aid with local crises.",al={"what to do in astranaar","astranaar arrival"},it="next_step"},{q="What level of adventurer is this intended for?",a="This journey usually marks your departure from Darkshore around level nineteen. It carries intermediate adventurers into Ashenvale's broader, more contested frontier.",al={"what level","level requirement"},gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Selarin want you to go to Ashenvale?",a="Sentinel Selarin answers to Raene Wolfrunner, who oversees the defense and restoration efforts in Astranaar. With spreading corruption afflicting the ancient woods of Ashenvale, the local Sentinels are stretched thin and under dire stress. Selarin directs proven champions from Darkshore straight to her mistress so that capable hands can immediately begin easing the forest's plight.",al={"why send to ashenvale","selarin motive","why trek to ashenvale"},it="motive",add="b4a50545"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you return to Kalimdor's sacred heartland, where your sisters call for help protecting ancient holy grounds from unnatural rot.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you answer Astranaar's call, strengthening ties with the night elves and shoring up the Alliance's primary foothold in northern Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","darkshore","night elf","raene wolfrunner","sentinel selarin","trek to ashenvale"},rel={"npc:raene-wolfrunner","npc:sentinel-selarin","subzone:astranaar","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Sentinel Selarin",["end"]="Raene Wolfrunner",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=990},src={"Trek to Ashenvale"}}
E["quest:991"] = {t="quest",n="Raene's Cleansing",z="ashenvale",s="Raene's Cleansing begins when Raene Wolfrunner asks an adventurer to track down her missing friend, Teronis. Seeking a way to halt the rampant furbolg aggression across Ashenvale, Teronis set off toward Lake Falathim to recover a magic gemstone.",h="Raene's Cleansing begins when Raene Wolfrunner asks an adventurer to track down her missing friend, Teronis.",sec={{t="A Friend's Concern",b="Raene Wolfrunner serves alongside the Sentinels in Astranaar, defending Ashenvale against mounting threats. Among her closest companions was Teronis, who took it upon himself to find a potent defense against the increasingly violent furbolg tribes. When days passed without his return, Raene grew deeply worried, unable to abandon her post while fearing the worst.",sp=0},{t="The Quest for the Rod",b="Teronis pursued rumors of a powerful rod forged by a deceased, wicked wizard, believing its magic could quell the furbolg fury. To restore the artifact, he required an enchanted gem hidden within an elven shrine at Lake Falathim, located near the mountains to the west. Unfortunately, the tranquil waters had recently fallen to aggressive murloc tribes.",sp=0},{t="Tragedy at Lake Falathim",b="Following Teronis's trail to the island within Lake Falathim reveals a grim sight. Teronis never made it out of the waters alive; his body lies slain upon the shrine, covered in deep slashes delivered by murloc weapons and claws, marking an untimely end to his search.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Raene Wolfrunner?",a="Raene Wolfrunner is a night elf allied with the Sentinels of Ashenvale, stationed in Astranaar. She oversees various defensive efforts to protect the forest from encroaching enemies.",al={"raene","who is raene","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Teronis?",a="Teronis was a close friend of Raene Wolfrunner who sought ancient magical solutions to save the forest. Believing an enchanted rod could calm the corrupted furbolgs, he journeyed alone to secure its components.",al={"who is teronis","teronis background","missing friend"},it="target"},{q="Where did Teronis go missing?",a="Teronis vanished at Lake Falathim, a body of water situated at the foot of the western mountains in Ashenvale, which had become overrun by hostile murlocs.",al={"where is teronis","teronis location","lake falathim"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was Teronis looking for a gem?",a="The gem was a vital component needed to empower a magic rod crafted by a deceased evil wizard. Teronis hoped the rod's power could be repurposed to stem the attacks of enraged furbolgs.",al={"what gem","why gem","teronis gem"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happened to Teronis?",a="Raene has not heard from him since he went to Lake Falathim. Following his trail reveals his fate.",al={"how did teronis die","teronis killer","who killed teronis"},sp=1,it="danger"},{q="Why are the furbolgs attacking Ashenvale?",a="The furbolgs of Ashenvale have succumbed to demonic corruption and madness in the wake of the Third War, driving once-peaceful tribes into relentless, violent hostility against their old allies.",al={"furbolg attacks","why furbolgs aggressive","furbolg madness"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Raene Wolfrunner want Teronis found?",a="Teronis is an old and trusted friend of Raene Wolfrunner who stepped forward to assist the Sentinels against the raging furbolgs. He left seeking a magical rod and gem that might halt the assaults on their people, but he never returned. Raene is deeply worried for his safety and desperate to uncover whatever aid he might have secured for their beleaguered lands.",al={"why raene wants teronis","raene wolfrunner motive","why look for teronis"},it="motive",add="82e89856"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The disappearance of Teronis is another bitter blow to the night elves, who are already stretched thin trying to heal Ashenvale and protect their shrines from corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance recruits arriving in Astranaar quickly learn that Ashenvale's sacred groves are under siege by hostile wild beasts, furbolgs, and invasive murlocs."},kw={"ashenvale","falathim","furbolg","gem","murloc","raene","teronis","wolfrunner"},rel={"npc:raene-wolfrunner","npc:teronis-corpse","subzone:lake-falathim","zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","topic:murloc","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Raene Wolfrunner",["end"]="Teronis' Corpse",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=991},src={"Raene's Cleansing"}}
E["subzone:astranaar"] = {t="subzone",n="Astranaar",z="ashenvale",s="Astranaar holds the Night Elves’ ground in central Ashenvale, across an island in the forest lake. The ancient forest road runs beside it, and Alliance travelers find refuge there as furbolgs, satyrs, and the Horde threaten the region.",h="Astranaar holds the Night Elves’ ground in central Ashenvale, across an island in the forest lake.",sec={{t="Heart of the Forest",b="Wooden footbridges link Astranaar’s island to the mainland, crossing the forest lake. It is Ashenvale’s largest night elven settlement, where sentinels, priests, and artisans keep watch over the woodlands. Travelers find an inn, traders, and an expert leatherworker. On the high perches, a flight master sends hippogryphs to distant outposts across Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Bastion Under Siege",b="Lanterns glow over Astranaar’s tranquil waters, but the town stays ready for attack. Raene Wolfrunner and other local leaders coordinate patrols and defenses against the corrupted Thistlefur furbolgs advancing from the north. The Sentinels fear the furbolgs may assault the settlement.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What services are available in Astranaar?",a="Astranaar has an inn, general goods vendors, an expert leatherworking trainer, and a flight master with routes to key outposts across Ashenvale and Kalimdor.",al={"astranaar amenities","what is in astranaar","astranaar flight master"},gp=true},{q="Who is buried in the graveyard across the lake?",a="No account from this era names who rests in the cemetery across the lake from Astranaar. Its graves keep their secrets.",al={"astranaar grave","valstann staghelm grave","who is buried here"},it="history"},{q="Why are the Sentinels in Astranaar worried about the local furbolgs?",a="The Thistlefur furbolgs to the north have fallen under dark, corrupting influences. Sentinel Raene Wolfrunner fears their growing aggression may lead them to attack Astranaar.",al={"thistlefur threat","why fight furbolgs","raene wolfrunner quest"},it="threat"},{q="Can Horde players visit Astranaar safely?",a="No. Armed Night Elf Sentinels guard Astranaar, a fortified Alliance stronghold, and attack Horde members on sight.",al={"is astranaar friendly to horde","horde in astranaar"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What is Astranaar?",a="Astranaar is the primary night elven town in central Ashenvale and the largest settlement in the entire forest. Built on an island within a serene lake and straddling the main trade road, it connects to the wilderness via two wooden bridges. For the night elves and their Alliance allies, it serves as the beating heart and central bastion of defense against encroachments across Ashenvale.",al={"what is astranaar","astranaar lore","about astranaar"},it="place",add="7c629b8a"},{q="Who lives in and oversees Astranaar?",a="Astranaar is populated primarily by night elf civilians, crafters, and the Sentinels tasked with safeguarding Ashenvale. Notable leaders and defenders here include Sentinel Raene Wolfrunner, who coordinates local reconnaissance and keeps watch over growing threats in the surrounding woods.",al={"who runs astranaar","astranaar leadership","who leads astranaar","astranaar sentinels"},it="residents",add="262340cc"},{q="Is Astranaar dangerous?",a="Within its bridges, Astranaar is a heavily fortified haven for Alliance travelers, guarded around the clock by vigilant Sentinels. However, it sits in an increasingly contested forest. Aggressive Thistlefur furbolgs lurk just to the north, and nearby Warsong orc encampments pose an ever-present danger of raids across central Ashenvale. For Horde travelers, stepping foot inside invites immediate Sentinel attack.",al={"is astranaar safe","danger in astranaar","threats to astranaar"},it="danger",add="62cff95a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, Astranaar guards their ancient homeland in central Kalimdor and its sacred groves against growing threats in the forest.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Astranaar is a command post and logistical hub in Ashenvale’s contested wilderness."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","kalimdor","night elf","raene wolfrunner","sentinels","thistlefur"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","npc:raene-wolfrunner","quest:1054","subzone:forest-song","topic:furbolg","topic:alliance"},src={"Astranaar"}}
E["subzone:bathran-s-haunt"] = {t="subzone",n="Bathran's Haunt",z="ashenvale",s="Forsaken herbalists now harvest rare plants at Bathran's Haunt, east of the Zoram Strand in northwestern Ashenvale. Their work is withering the woodland around the ancient kaldorei ruin.",h="Forsaken herbalists now harvest rare plants at Bathran's Haunt, east of the Zoram Strand in northwestern...",sec={{t="A Blighted Refuge in the Ancient Woods",b="At Bathran's Haunt, crumbling night elf pillars stand north of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran, tangled in Ashenvale's thick foliage. Once a tranquil kaldorei relic, the ruin now shelters Forsaken herbalists and their enforcers. They work among the broken marble in an open-air laboratory, harvesting rare woodland reagents for their experiments. The grass rots brown, blossoms wilt, and decay creeps through the grove as their work blights the ancient soil.",sp=0},{t="The Harvest of Bathran's Hair",b="Bathran's Hair, a unique remedial herb, grows only among these stones. Night elf and Alliance scouts see its harvest as a desecration of sacred elven soil, while Forsaken herbalists seek the plant's potent properties. The Horde has an interest in the herb's yield, but the Forsaken keep their methods secret. The corruption of the earth draws suspicion from outsiders and allies alike.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bathran's Haunt located?",a="Bathran's Haunt lies in northwestern Ashenvale, north of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran and inland, east of the Zoram Strand.",al={"where is bathrans haunt","bathrans haunt location","how to get to bathrans haunt"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken here?",a="Forsaken herbalists have set up an encampment and laboratory among the ruins to gather and study the forest's unique plants, especially Bathran's Hair, a rare remedial herb.",al={"what are undead doing in ashenvale","why are forsaken at bathrans haunt","forsaken purpose bathran"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Bathran's Hair?",a="Bathran's Hair is a distinctive, valuable remedial herb with potent restorative qualities. It grows only among the crumbling stones of Bathran's Haunt.",al={"bathrans hair plant","what is bathrans hair","bathran herb"},it="item"},{q="Why is the ground dying around the ruins?",a="The Forsaken's presence and alchemical work have corrupted the ground near the ruins. Grass withers brown, and woodland flowers die.",al={"why is grass brown here","blight in bathrans haunt","why is the land decaying"},it="threat"},{q="What is Bathran's Haunt?",a="Bathran's Haunt is an ancient Kaldorei ruin set in northwestern Ashenvale, north of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran. Abandoned long ago by the night elves, its crumbling marble pillars and overgrown courtyards have recently been occupied by Forsaken herbalists and their guardians, who have established a makeshift camp among the stones.",al={"bathrans haunt","what is this place","bathran haunt lore"},it="place",add="72c7f68d"},{q="Who lives in or runs Bathran's Haunt?",a="The ruins are currently occupied by Forsaken herbalists and hired thugs who have set up an outdoor laboratory among the ancient marble. While they welcome members of the Horde, their experiments and presence are kept under watchful eyes, and Alliance interlopers are driven away on sight.",al={"who controls bathrans haunt","who lives at bathrans haunt","bathrans haunt inhabitants"},it="residents",add="43b0b094"},{q="Is Bathran's Haunt dangerous?",a="It is quite dangerous, particularly for Alliance travelers. The Forsaken stationed here are armed, aggressive toward outsiders, and actively conducting unnatural experiments. Even the surrounding soil has withered and browned under the taint of their occupation, signaling an environment deeply hostile to the living.",al={"bathrans haunt danger","is bathrans haunt safe","is it dangerous here"},it="danger",add="0d907f15"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Forsaken encampment at Bathran's Haunt defiles kaldorei heritage: undead intruders occupy ancient elven stonework and blight sacred soil.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Bathran's Haunt is the only known habitat for Bathran's Hair, a unique remedial herb sought for its rare restorative properties."},kw={"ashenvale","bathran's hair","bathran's haunt","forsaken","herbalism","kaldorei ruins","ruins of ordil'aran","zoram strand"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","quest:1010","subzone:ruins-of-ordil-aran","subzone:zoram-strand","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Bathran's Haunt"}}
E["subzone:blackfathom-deeps"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackfathom Deeps",z="ashenvale",s="Blackfathom Deeps lies flooded beneath the Zoram Strand on Ashenvale's northwestern coast. Its halls once honored Elune, but naga, satyr, and the Twilight's Hammer now hold the ruins.",h="Blackfathom Deeps lies flooded beneath the Zoram Strand on Ashenvale's northwestern coast.",sec={{t="From Elune's Temple to Darkest Abyss",b="Beneath Ashenvale's northwestern cliffs, flooded halls mark the remains of an ancient temple. Before the Great Sundering shattered Kalimdor ten thousand years ago, the temple honored Elune and held its own moonwell. When the Well of Eternity collapsed, the shrine sank beneath the waves and was presumed lost forever. Over millennia, shorelines receded and the ground shifted below, leaving the temple partly flooded beneath the cliffs.",sp=0},{t="Aku'mai and the Cult",b="The Twilight's Hammer has made its home in the flooded temple, under Twilight Lord Kelris. Corruption from an Old God has risen through the deep earth and tainted the sacred Moon Well. Aku'mai, a monstrous three-headed hydra and servant of the Old God, rose from its waters. Naga led by Lady Sarevess and prowling satyrs join the cultists, who sacrifice innocents to Aku'mai for power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was Blackfathom Deeps originally built for?",a="Before it sank beneath the waves during the Sundering, Blackfathom Deeps was a night elven temple to Elune, with a sacred moonwell at its heart.",al={"bfd history","what was blackfathom deeps","bfd temple"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer cult here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer came to worship Aku'mai, a primeval hydra and servant of an Old God. Under Twilight Lord Kelris, the cult sacrifices innocents to the beast for dark power.",al={"why are cultists in bfd","twilight's hammer blackfathom","kelris goal"},it="why_here"},{q="Where is the entrance located?",a="The entrance lies among cavernous ruins along the Zoram Strand, on Ashenvale's far northwestern coast. You must pass through submerged chambers and hostile naga outposts to reach the temple portal.",al={"where is bfd","blackfathom deeps location","how to enter bfd"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Ghamoo-ra?",a="Ghamoo-ra is a giant, maddened turtle that lurks on an island in one of the temple's flooded caverns. The turtle attacks any intruder who comes near.",al={"giant turtle boss","ghamoo-ra lore","tortoise bfd"},it="identity"},{q="What is Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps is a flooded subterranean ruin resting beneath the Zoram Strand along Ashenvale's coast. Once a resplendent night elven temple dedicated to the moon goddess Elune, it shattered and sank during the Great Sundering. Today, its partially submerged halls and sea caverns form a dark sanctuary claimed by cultists, ancient beasts, and the vile servants of the Old Gods.",al={"what is blackfathom deeps","blackfathom deeps overview","tell me about blackfathom deeps"},it="place",add="f0315c0b"},{q="What happened at Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Long ago, the night elves raised this temple to Elune, complete with sacred pools and a moonwell. Ten thousand years ago, the Great Sundering tore Kalimdor apart and cast the sanctuary beneath the waves. While thought lost forever, Old God corruption has seeped into its moonwell, drawing sinister forces back into the lightless ruins to awaken an ancient terror.",al={"blackfathom deeps history","what happened here","lathar'lazal history"},it="history",add="11da3285"},{q="Who lives in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The sunken temple is dominated by the Twilight's Hammer cult, led by Twilight Lord Kelris, who conducts dark rituals and blood sacrifices to their shadowy masters. Alongside the cultists dwell serpentine naga under Lady Sarevess, corrupted satyrs drawn to the ancient power, and aquatic monstrosities—foremost among them Aku'mai, a monstrous hydra and servant of an Old God.",al={"who lives here","who controls blackfathom deeps","who is in blackfathom"},it="residents",add="e07691c2"},{q="Why is Blackfathom Deeps ruined?",a="The temple was destroyed when the Well of Eternity imploded during the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago. The cataclysm fractured the continent and submerged the temple complex beneath the encroaching sea, drowning its moonwells and reducing its magnificent architecture into a dark, flooded cavern system.",al={"why is it ruined","why is blackfathom submerged","why is it destroyed"},it="ruin",add="bfbbd665"},{q="Is Blackfathom Deeps dangerous?",a="It is extraordinarily dangerous. Deep inside, fanatical cultists slaughter captives in blasphemous rites to empower Aku'mai, a primordial beast whose awakening threatens to unleash chaos upon Kalimdor. Intruders must brave flooded tunnels prowled by frenzied aquatic beasts, cruel naga sorcerers, cunning satyrs, and cultists who will kill any outsider to conceal their rituals.",al={"is blackfathom deeps safe","how dangerous is blackfathom deeps","bfd danger"},it="danger",add="e7974e12"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei, you may mourn the defilement of this ancient shrine to Elune. Void cultists and naga have desecrated its sacred halls and moonwell.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know the deeps lie uncomfortably close to Zoram'gar. The cultists and naga gathering on the Zoram Strand threaten the outpost's defenders."},kw={"aku'mai","blackfathom","deeps","ghamoo-ra","kelris","sarevess","twilight's hammer","zoram strand"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","zone:ashenvale","subzone:zoram-strand","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","npc:aku-mai","npc:lady-sarevess","npc:ghamoo-ra-classic","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Blackfathom Deeps"}}
E["subzone:bloodtooth-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Bloodtooth Camp",z="ashenvale",s="In central Ashenvale, Bloodtooth Camp lies west of the Falfarren River. Ran Bloodtooth leads the corrupted furbolgs, who attack anyone who approaches. Alliance scouts target the camp as they work to cleanse the surrounding woodlands.",h="In central Ashenvale, Bloodtooth Camp lies west of the Falfarren River.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Den",b="Bloodtooth Camp lies southwest of the southern Moonwell and west of the Falfarren River. Its furbolgs were once bound to Kalimdor's sacred wilderness, but a lingering spiritual corruption has consumed their tribe. Ran Bloodtooth commands the crude settlement. His followers attack travelers and night elven protectors alike.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Forest",b="Ran Bloodtooth's band threatens nearby sacred sites, drawing Alliance sentinels and their allies to the camp. As they aid Raene Wolfrunner's efforts to cleanse the forest, Krolg directs adventurers to enter the camp, kill Ran Bloodtooth, and defeat his bodyguards.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Bloodtooth Camp located?",a="Bloodtooth Camp lies in central Ashenvale, west of the Falfarren River and southwest of the southern Moonwell.",al={"bloodtooth camp location","where is bloodtooth camp","find bloodtooth camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="A dark demonic corruption lingering in Ashenvale's wilderness has driven the Bloodtooth clan, like many furbolg tribes there, into madness and aggression toward outsiders.",al={"why are bloodtooth furbolgs attacking","bloodtooth corruption","are furbolgs evil here"},it="hostile"},{q="Who leads the furbolgs at Bloodtooth Camp?",a="Ran Bloodtooth leads the furbolgs at the camp and commands his bodyguards.",al={"bloodtooth camp boss","ran bloodtooth","who leads bloodtooth camp"},it="leader"},{q="Why does the Alliance send scouts here?",a="During the efforts around Raene's Cleansing, Krolg, an exiled furbolg, directs Alliance champions to attack the camp, kill Ran Bloodtooth, and remove the threat his followers pose to the region.",al={"bloodtooth camp quest","why kill ran bloodtooth","krolg mission"},it="threat"},{q="What is Bloodtooth Camp?",a="Bloodtooth Camp is an encampment nestled in central Ashenvale, situated west of the Falfarren River and southwest of a sacred night elf moonwell. It serves as a stronghold for a band of corrupted furbolgs who have fallen under dark influences and now violently lash out against anyone venturing into their territory.",al={"what is bloodtooth camp","bloodtooth camp lore","bloodtooth camp ashenvale"},it="place",add="f92ad28e"},{q="Who lives in Bloodtooth Camp?",a="The camp is inhabited by a tribe of feral, corrupted furbolgs under the command of Ran Bloodtooth. Guarded by loyal furbolg protectors and bodyguards, these once-peaceful creatures view all outsiders as mortal enemies and defend their encampment with savage hostility.",al={"who lives in bloodtooth camp","bloodtooth camp furbolgs","bloodtooth camp inhabitants"},it="residents",add="15670459"},{q="Is Bloodtooth Camp dangerous?",a="Yes, it is exceptionally dangerous. The furbolgs here are consumed by corruption and attack on sight with feral rage. Stepping into the camp pits you against hardened furbolg warriors and Ran Bloodtooth's personal bodyguards, making any careless approach a deadly mistake.",al={"is bloodtooth camp dangerous","danger bloodtooth camp","bloodtooth camp threats"},it="danger",add="3d0c2137"},{q="Why is it called Bloodtooth Camp?",a="The settlement takes its name from Ran Bloodtooth, the fierce chieftain who rules over the corrupted furbolg tribe gathered here.",al={"why called bloodtooth camp","bloodtooth camp name meaning","who is bloodtooth"},it="name",add="39c5c848"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers, Bloodtooth Camp is a pocket of corruption threatening Ashenvale's southern groves and moonwells.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Ran Bloodtooth's maddened tribe as a tragic sign of the corruption blighting your ancestral homeland."},kw={"ashenvale","bloodtooth camp","falfarren river","furbolg","krolg","raene's cleansing","ran bloodtooth"},rel={"quest:991","npc:krolg","topic:furbolg","zone:ashenvale","subzone:falfarren-river","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","topic:alliance"},src={"Bloodtooth Camp"}}
E["subzone:bough-shadow"] = {t="subzone",n="Bough Shadow",z="ashenvale",s="In northeastern Ashenvale, Bough Shadow lies east of Forest Song beneath a colossal Great Tree. Its roots surround an ancient portal into the Emerald Dream.",h="In northeastern Ashenvale, Bough Shadow lies east of Forest Song beneath a colossal Great Tree.",sec={{t="A Gateway to the Dream",b="Bough Shadow gathers beneath a Great Tree whose roots wind around a natural crossing into the Emerald Dream. The Green Dragonflight guards the quiet grove. Emerald drakes such as Phantim and Dreamstalker circle above the canopy, while Emeraldon dragonspawn and oracles patrol the swirling green portal at the tree’s base. Mortals who approach without permission are turned away.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the glowing green portal here?",a="The swirling vortex beneath the Great Tree opens directly into the Emerald Dream, Azeroth’s untamed spirit realm. Similar natural crossings lie elsewhere in the world.",al={"bough shadow portal","what is the portal in bough shadow","green portal ashenvale"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are green dragons guarding Bough Shadow?",a="Ysera’s Green Dragonflight watches over the Emerald Dream and its passages into the physical world. Emerald drakes and dragonspawn patrol Bough Shadow to keep intruders and corrupting forces from crossing.",al={"why are there dragons in ashenvale","green dragonflight bough shadow","why green dragons here"},it="why_here"},{q="Can players enter the portal?",a="No. The gateway is sealed to mortals, and the elite dragonkin guards will attack anyone who comes too close.",al={"can i go through the portal","enter bough shadow portal","how to enter dream portal"},gp=true},{q="What is Bough Shadow?",a="Bough Shadow is a secluded glade tucked into the northeastern edge of Ashenvale, east of Forest Song. It is centered around one of the world's Great Trees and houses a mystical gateway leading directly into the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is this place","bough shadow lore","about bough shadow"},it="place",add="ca240e18"},{q="What happened at Bough Shadow?",a="Bough Shadow holds one of the world's Great Trees, rooted over one of the portals into the Emerald Dream, and the green dragonflight keeps a close watch over it.",al={"bough shadow history","history of bough shadow"},it="history",add="626e8e50"},{q="Who lives at Bough Shadow?",a="The grove is inhabited entirely by members of the Green Dragonflight. Drakes such as Phantim and Dreamstalker watch over the glade, supported by patrols of green dragonspawn, including Emeraldon Tree Warders, Boughguards, and Oracles.",al={"who is here","who inhabits bough shadow","bough shadow residents"},it="residents",add="f0692632"},{q="Is Bough Shadow dangerous?",a="Yes, it is very dangerous for travelers. The green dragons and their dragonspawn sentinels guard the portal with fierce vigilance, and they will not hesitate to strike down any mortals who wander too close to their sacred vigil.",al={"is bough shadow safe","bough shadow danger"},it="danger",add="30f2c168"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you stand on sacred ground at Bough Shadow, where a natural threshold links Azeroth to the Green Flight’s domain and the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you find Bough Shadow deep beyond Forest Song. Its Great Tree and sleeping portal speak to the bond between the kaldorei and the Emerald Dream."},kw={"ashenvale","bough shadow","dragonspawn","dreamstalker","emerald dream","great tree","green dragons","phantim","portal"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid","subzone:forest-song"},src={"Bough Shadow"}}
E["subzone:demon-fall-canyon"] = {t="subzone",n="Demon Fall Canyon",z="ashenvale",s="Demon Fall Canyon bears the scars of the battle that freed the orcs from the blood curse. Here, Thrall and Grommash Hellscream faced Mannoroth in southern Ashenvale.",h="Demon Fall Canyon bears the scars of the battle that freed the orcs from the blood curse.",sec={{t="The Fall of Mannoroth",b="In southern Ashenvale, the canyon lies near Felfire Hill and Demon Fall Ridge, its land scarred by the Third War. Warchief Thrall and chieftain Grommash Hellscream tracked the pit lord Mannoroth here to break his hold over the Horde. Mannoroth struck Thrall down, and Grom seized the chance to drive his axe, Gorehowl, into the demon’s chest. The infernal blast shattered Mannoroth and killed Grom. With the pit lord’s death, the orcs were free of their lingering demonic servitude.",sp=0},{t="A Sacred Yet Dangerous Chasm",b="The Horde named the canyon for Grom’s final stand and raised a monument nearby to honor his redemption. Mannoroth’s death unleashed demonic power that tainted the surrounding land. Fel magic still saturates the canyon, where lesser demons roam. Pilgrims who come to this hallowed ground face danger at every turn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this place called Demon Fall Canyon?",a="The Horde named the canyon for the fall of Mannoroth, slain here by Grommash Hellscream.",al={"demon fall canyon name origin","why called demon fall canyon","how did it get its name"},it="name"},{q="What happened between Grom and Mannoroth here?",a="Thrall and Grom confronted Mannoroth together. The pit lord knocked Thrall unconscious, but Grom struck a lethal blow with his axe. Mannoroth’s blast of demonic fire fatally wounded Grom, whose dying act freed his people from the blood curse.",al={"grom death","grom vs mannoroth","how did grom die"},it="history"},{q="Why are there still demons roaming the canyon?",a="Mannoroth’s death unleashed a tremendous blast of demonic energy that permanently corrupted the canyon floor. Lingering fel corruption still attracts and harbors lesser demons.",al={"why demons in demon fall","demon fall canyon mobs","why is it fel corrupted"},it="residents"},{q="Where is Grom Hellscream's memorial?",a="A monument honoring Grom Hellscream stands near Demon Fall Canyon, where Horde pilgrims pay tribute to the warrior who freed their people.",al={"grom monument location","hellscream memorial","where is grom's grave"},gp=true},{q="What is Demon Fall Canyon?",a="Demon Fall Canyon is a scarred, fel-corrupted ravine tucked into the southern hills of Ashenvale, east of Demon Fall Ridge. It is the historic battleground where Warchief Thrall and Grommash Hellscream confronted the demonic pit lord Mannoroth during the Third War. Today, the canyon remains tainted by lingering demonic energies and serves as a hallowed pilgrimage site for the Horde, who come to remember Grom's ultimate sacrifice.",al={"what is demon fall canyon","demon fall canyon lore","about demon fall canyon"},it="place",add="f0a5bd72"},{q="Is Demon Fall Canyon dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. The death of the pit lord Mannoroth bathed the gorge in raw fel magic that continues to corrupt the earth. Hostile lesser demons and lingering fiends wander the canyon depths, attacking anyone who dares enter. Even though the Burning Legion's primary commanders here were defeated, any traveler or pilgrim paying respects must remain constantly on guard against the restless monsters stalking the crags.",al={"how dangerous is demon fall canyon","is demon fall dangerous","threats in demon fall canyon"},it="danger",add="1e62195e"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you stand on sacred ground where Grommash Hellscream made his ultimate sacrifice and broke the Burning Legion’s blood curse.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you owe your spiritual and physical freedom to the battle in this canyon, where Grom gave his life to end your demonic bondage."},kw={"ashenvale","blood curse","demon fall canyon","gorehowl","grommash hellscream","mannoroth","pit lord","thrall"},rel={"subzone:demon-fall-ridge","subzone:felfire-hill","zone:ashenvale","topic:grommash-hellscream","npc:thrall","topic:burning-legion","topic:horde"},src={"Demon Fall Canyon"}}
E["subzone:demon-fall-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Demon Fall Ridge",z="ashenvale",s="In southeastern Ashenvale, demons hold the high ground above the place where Mannoroth fell. Lingering fel magic stains the ridge, and the Burning Legion has claimed a night elf barrow den.",h="In southeastern Ashenvale, demons hold the high ground above the place where Mannoroth fell.",sec={{t="A Perch Over Corruption",b="Demon Fall Ridge rises west of Demon Fall Canyon, its cliffs stained by fel left from the Third War. Below, the canyon marks the clash between Grommash Hellscream and the pit lord Mannoroth. Surviving demons use the ridge as a staging ground. Lesser demons patrol the rocky heights, defiling the woodland and threatening travelers along Ashenvale's southern border.",sp=0},{t="The Desecrated Barrow",b="A night elf barrow den lies abandoned in the ridge's side, its passages turned into a stronghold of dark sorcery. Fel fiends fill the halls where druids once slept. In the deepest reaches, Diathorus the Seeker, a cunning dreadlord, rules the conclave and directs the remaining demons across the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Demon Fall Ridge?",a="Demon Fall Ridge rises in southeastern Ashenvale, west of Demon Fall Canyon and near the Barrens border.",al={"ridge location","where is demon fall ridge","ashenvale demon ridge"},gp=true},{q="Why are there demons on this ridge?",a="The ridge overlooks the place where Mannoroth died in the Third War. Demons who survived the Legion's defeat scattered into the heights and entrenched themselves on the ridge and in an abandoned barrow den.",al={"why demons here","demon fall ridge demons","burning legion presence"},it="why_here"},{q="Who leads the demons here?",a="Diathorus the Seeker, a powerful nathrezim dreadlord, commands the conclave from the deepest reaches of the barrow den.",al={"who is the boss here","demon leader","diathorus the seeker"},it="leader"},{q="What is the structure carved into the ridge?",a="The structure is an ancient night elf barrow den, once a druid sanctuary for entering the Emerald Dream. It was abandoned and overrun and desecrated by the Burning Legion.",al={"barrow den","demon fall cave","what is the den"}},{q="What is Demon Fall Ridge?",a="Demon Fall Ridge is a high, desolate cliff in southern Ashenvale, towering above Demon Fall Canyon. Once a sacred barrow haven for night elf druids, the ridge and its subterranean halls have fallen into darkness, overrun by surviving members of the Burning Legion who maintain a foul foothold deep within the forest.",al={"what is demon fall ridge","demon fall ridge lore","demon fall ridge overview"},it="place",add="38a8c952"},{q="Who lives in Demon Fall Ridge?",a="The ridge is crawling with demonic remnants of the Burning Legion. Various lesser demons prowl the surface paths and guard the entrance to the abandoned barrow den, while deep inside resides their master, the dreadlord Diathorus the Seeker, commanding the demonic conclave.",al={"who lives in demon fall ridge","demon fall ridge inhabitants","who is at demon fall ridge"},it="residents",add="f78b2bbc"},{q="Is Demon Fall Ridge dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The ridge swarms with hostile demonic forces ready to slaughter any who trespass. Venturing inside the hollowed barrow den pits you against entrenched demonic fiends culminating in an encounter with a cunning and lethal dreadlord.",al={"is demon fall ridge dangerous","demon fall ridge threats","danger demon fall ridge"},it="danger",add="c0607561"},{q="Why is Demon Fall Ridge called that?",a="The ridge takes its name from the adjacent Demon Fall Canyon below, the historic battleground where Grom Hellscream struck down the pit lord Mannoroth during the Third War, breaking the demonic blood curse over the orcs and marking the fall of the Legion's vanguard.",al={"why is it called demon fall ridge","demon fall ridge name origin","demon fall name meaning"},it="name",add="45002eaf"},{q="Why is the barrow den on Demon Fall Ridge abandoned?",a="The barrow den carved into the cliff was once used by night elf druids for their long slumber. Following the turmoil of the Third War and the demonic corruption spreading from the nearby canyon, the elves lost or abandoned the sanctuary, allowing the Legion's survivors to desecrate and occupy it.",al={"why is demon fall ridge ruined","abandoned barrow den demon fall ridge","why is the den abandoned"},it="ruin",add="e8f31dd4"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see demons occupying a barrow den once sacred to the Emerald Dream, an affront to the Cenarion Circle.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you find an active dreadlord leading the fel forces, a glimpse of organized Legion remnants in Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","barrow den","burning legion","demon fall canyon","demon fall ridge","diathorus the seeker","dreadlord"},rel={"subzone:demon-fall-canyon","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Demon Fall Ridge"}}
E["subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Dor'Danil Barrow Den",z="ashenvale",s="In central Ashenvale, south of Splintertree Post, Dor'Danil Barrow Den lies under Forsaken shadow. Druids once slept here while their spirits roamed the Emerald Dream, but now the sanctuary is filled with horror.",h="In central Ashenvale, south of Splintertree Post, Dor'Danil Barrow Den lies under Forsaken shadow.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary Desecrated",b="Night elven druids have slept for centuries in barrow dens across Kalimdor, their bodies sheltered underground as their spirits traveled the Emerald Dream. When the Horde pushed into Ashenvale, Dor'Danil lay deep behind enemy lines. The orcs mostly left the sleeping elves alone, but the newly allied Forsaken saw an opportunity. Their agents entered the depths and began experiments to sever the druids from their spirits. The ordeal fractured the dreamers' minds and drove them mad. Now sinister Forsaken assassins prowl the dark hollows, alongside the tormented spirits of druids who cannot return to their bodies.",sp=0},{t="The Tormented Guardians",b="Deep in Dor'Danil's tunnels, three druidic spirits wander in madness: Uthil Mooncall, Mavoris Cloudsbreak, and Taneel Darkwood. Darkslayer Mordenthal, a Forsaken agent, stalks the den as well. For night elves and their Cenarion Circle allies, laying the anguished spirits to rest is a grim mercy. The Forsaken presence also shows the ruthless, morbid curiosity Sylvanas's agents bring to Kalimdor's conflicts.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Dor'Danil Barrow Den?",a="Dor'Danil Barrow Den lies underground in Ashenvale, south of Splintertree Post and southwest of Felfire Hill. Druids once slept here in deep trances, their bodies sheltered as their spirits entered the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is this place","dor danil barrow den info","dor'danil lore"},it="place"},{q="Why are the druid spirits inside hostile and insane?",a="Forsaken agents entered the den and experimented on the sleeping druids, severing their spirits from their bodies. The trauma left the druids violently insane.",al={"why are druids crazy here","why are spirits angry","insane druids lore"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Darkslayer Mordenthal?",a="Darkslayer Mordenthal is a Forsaken found deep in the barrow den among its undead occupants. His presence is known, but he is not identified as the experiments' director.",al={"mordenthal","who is the undead inside"},it="residents"},{q="Which notable spirits haunt the depths?",a="Three prominent druidic spirits haunt the lower chambers: Uthil Mooncall, Mavoris Cloudsbreak, and Taneel Darkwood. Severed from their bodies, they wander the dark tunnels in unending rage.",al={"named mobs dor danil","named druids inside"},it="threat"},{q="What happened at Dor'Danil Barrow Den?",a="Historically, this barrow den served as a peaceful sanctuary where night elf druids entered the Emerald Dream. When the Horde pushed into Ashenvale, the site fell deep behind enemy lines. While the orcs largely ignored the slumbering druids, the Forsaken took a darker interest. They conducted experiments aimed at severing the sleeping elves from their spirits, a process that shattered the druids' minds and drove them entirely mad.",al={"dordanil history","what happened at dordanil","dor danil backstory"},it="history",add="b36fa772"},{q="Is Dor'Danil Barrow Den dangerous?",a="Dor'Danil Barrow Den is exceptionally perilous to enter. Its winding subterranean tunnels crawl with stealthy Forsaken assassins who continue their sinister work, as well as the violent, tormented ghosts of the severed druids. Venturing into its deepest chambers brings you face to face with especially formidable restless spirits like Uthil Mooncall, Mavoris Cloudsbreak, and Taneel Darkwood.",al={"is dordanil dangerous","dor danil dangers","threats in dordanil"},it="danger",add="c4765c4c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know barrow dens as sacred places where druids commune with the Emerald Dream. The torture and fractured minds of those within Dor'Danil are an unforgivable sacrilege.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see Forsaken research in Dor'Danil as a relentless inquiry into life, death, and soul-severing magic, even on Kalimdor's distant battlefields."},kw={"ashenvale","barrow den","dor danil","dor'danil","insane druids","mavoris cloudsbreak","mordenthal","taneel darkwood","uthil mooncall"},rel={"quest:1012","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","topic:forsaken","topic:druid","subzone:felfire-hill","quest:1152"},src={"Dor'Danil Barrow Den"}}
E["subzone:falfarren-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Falfarren River",z="ashenvale",s="The Falfarren River cuts through central Ashenvale, from Mount Hyjal toward the northern mountains of the Barrens. Its banks mark the divide between night elven lands and Horde outposts, where travelers face wild dangers and open conflict.",h="The Falfarren River cuts through central Ashenvale, from Mount Hyjal toward the northern mountains of the...",sec={{t="A Contested Natural Boundary",b="The Falfarren River descends from Mount Hyjal, spilling over waterfalls into Xavian before winding between Splintertree Post and Night Run. In ordinary weather, its waters are neither especially deep nor impassable. The river marks a rough boundary through central Ashenvale. Astranaar and the heart of the Kaldorei lands lie west; Horde camps and lumber operations lie east. The wooden bridges on the main road carry travelers into the contested forest, where patrols clash along the banks.",sp=0},{t="Hazards in the Shallows",b="The Falfarren River holds dangers beyond clashes between sentinels and grunts. Near Felfire Hill, corrupted bog beasts and aggressive water creatures prowl the muddy shallows. Rain can swell the currents. Dense canopies line both shores, where ambushes and skirmishes often spill into the stream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Falfarren River begin and end?",a="The Falfarren River begins in the heights of Mount Hyjal, then tumbles over waterfalls into the lake at Xavian. It winds southwest across Ashenvale before disappearing underground beneath the northern mountains of the Barrens.",al={"falfarren river source","where does the river go"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Falfarren River significant to the war in Ashenvale?",a="The Falfarren River marks a rough boundary between night elf and Horde control in central Ashenvale. Astranaar lies to the west, while the orc outpost of Splintertree Post and active Horde lumber operations lie to the east.",al={"why is falfarren river important","river border ashenvale"},it="conflict"},{q="What threats should travelers expect along the riverbanks?",a="Aggressive bog beasts prowl the shallows, especially near the corrupted lands around Felfire Hill. Patrols from both the Alliance and the Horde watch bridges and crossings, and skirmishes and ambushes can break out along the banks.",al={"monsters in falfarren river","dangers at falfarren"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Falfarren River?",a="The Falfarren River is a central waterway running northeast to southwest across Ashenvale. Flowing down from the slopes of Mount Hyjal past Xavian and disappearing beneath the northern Barrens mountains, it serves as the rough natural boundary separating night elven lands around Astranaar from the Horde's foothold at Splintertree Post.",al={"what is falfarren river","falfarren river info","where is falfarren"},it="place",add="553b1115"},{q="Is the Falfarren River dangerous?",a="Yes. Beyond the ongoing military clashes between the Sentinels and the Horde along its crossings, the waters themselves hold natural hazards. Aggressive bog beasts lurk beneath the surface around Felfire Hill, posing a lethal surprise to anyone trying to ford the shallows.",al={"is falfarren river dangerous","dangers of falfarren","falfarren threats"},it="danger",add="6238ff52"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Night Elves and their allies, crossing east over the Falfarren River brings you into the Horde's front lines near Splintertree Post.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the Falfarren River marks the western edge of your expansion from Splintertree Post. Fortified night elf territory lies beyond it."},kw={"ashenvale river","astranaar","falfarren","falfarren river","felfire hill","splintertree","xavian"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:astranaar","subzone:silverwing-outpost","subzone:xavian","subzone:felfire-hill","subzone:night-run"},src={"Falfarren River"}}
E["subzone:fallen-sky-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Fallen Sky Lake",z="ashenvale",s="In eastern Ashenvale, Fallen Sky Lake lies between Silverwing Outpost and the Warsong Labor Camp. Shadethickets defend its shores and central isle.",h="In eastern Ashenvale, Fallen Sky Lake lies between Silverwing Outpost and the Warsong Labor Camp.",sec={{t="A Contested Sanctuary",b="Fallen Sky Lake lies south of Silverwing Outpost and west of the Warsong Labor Camp. Shadethickets, hulking bog beasts, roam its shores and the small isle at its center, treating intruders as threats. A powerful Shadethicket Oracle rules from the isle's heart. The Oracle hoards the fallen moonstones once gathered at the lake and keeps the shadethickets bound to the waters, ever watchful for travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Fallen Sky Lake located?",a="Fallen Sky Lake lies in eastern Ashenvale, south of Silverwing Outpost, west of the Warsong Labor Camp, and northeast of Silverwing Grove.",al={"fallen sky lake location","where is fallen sky lake","how to find fallen sky lake"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures live around Fallen Sky Lake?",a="Shadethickets, aggressive bog beasts, roam the lake and its banks. A Shadethicket Oracle leads them from the central isle.",al={"mobs at fallen sky lake","what is at fallen sky lake","fallen sky lake enemies"},it="residents",gp=true},{q="Why is the Shadethicket Oracle important?",a="The Shadethicket Oracle leads the shadethickets at the lake and hoards the fallen moonstones night elves once gathered there. Anyone who needs a moonstone must slay the Oracle on the central isle.",al={"oracle at fallen sky lake","shadethicket oracle","who is on the island"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is Fallen Sky Lake?",a="Fallen Sky Lake is a small, secluded body of water tucked away in central Ashenvale, resting south of Silverwing Outpost and west of the Warsong Labor Camp. At its heart lies a solitary island surrounded by tranquil yet eerie waters, set amidst the ancient, contested woodlands.",al={"fallen sky lake","about fallen sky lake","what is this lake"},it="place",add="0e5e2d0e"},{q="Is Fallen Sky Lake dangerous?",a="Yes, it is far from peaceful. The lake and its shores are overrun by hostile shadethickets, hulking bog beasts wandering through the waters and along the banks. At the center of the lake's island lurks the Shadethicket Oracle, a particularly formidable and hostile creature who hoards the lake's fallen moonstones.",al={"fallen sky lake dangers","is it safe here","fallen sky lake threats"},it="danger",add="62a4135b"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know night elves once gathered moonstones at Fallen Sky Lake. Shadethicket bog beasts now claim its waters and make this quiet forest corner dangerous.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you find Fallen Sky Lake just south of Silverwing Outpost, in your sacred ancestral forest. Wild beasts have grown erratic amid the Horde's gathering drums."},kw={"ashenvale","fallen sky lake","oracle","shadethicket","silverwing outpost","warsong labor camp","bog beast"},rel={"quest:1035","zone:ashenvale","subzone:silverwing-outpost","subzone:silverwing-grove","subzone:warsong-labor-camp"},src={"Fallen Sky Lake"}}
E["subzone:felfire-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Felfire Hill",z="ashenvale",s="In eastern Ashenvale, Felfire Hill remains a blighted rise crawling with demons. Infernals struck it during the Third War, and its soil still burns with fel power. Horde guards hold the bridges leading to the hill, near their settlements.",h="In eastern Ashenvale, Felfire Hill remains a blighted rise crawling with demons.",sec={{t="A Scar of the Burning Legion",b="During the Third War, the Burning Legion sent flaming meteors across Kalimdor, carrying its fearsome infernals. Several struck this ridge in Ashenvale, burning away the ancient woodland and corrupting the earth. The Legion fell at Mount Hyjal, but demons that survived its defeat still prowl the scorched slopes. Fel energy saturates the land they haunt.",sp=0},{t="Guarding the Crossings",b="Felfire Hill lies southeast of Splintertree Post and southwest of the Warsong Lumber Camp, close to vital Horde operations. Demonic remnants threaten to spill into the surrounding forest. Horde forces have raised fortified barricades and guard towers at both bridges leading to the hill, keeping the creatures within their blighted haven.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Felfire Hill corrupted?",a="During the Third War, infernals of the Burning Legion rained from the sky and struck Felfire Hill. Their impact and the fel contamination burned away the elven forest, leaving scarred rock and demonic energies that never dispersed.",al={"why is felfire hill green","felfire hill lore","what happened to felfire hill"},it="ruin"},{q="What creatures live on Felfire Hill?",a="Surviving demons and infernal constructs from the Legion's invasion during the Third War occupy Felfire Hill. They remain hostile to mortals who approach their corrupted ground.",al={"monsters at felfire hill","felfire hill mobs"},it="residents"},{q="Why did the Horde fortify the bridges here?",a="Felfire Hill lies between Splintertree Post and the Warsong Lumber Camp. Horde commanders fortified both bridges to keep roaming demons from breaking out and overrunning nearby camps, supply convoys, and lumber operations.",al={"horde bridge guards felfire","why are orcs guarding felfire hill"},it="conflict"},{q="Is Felfire Hill connected to the night elves?",a="Felfire Hill lies menacingly northeast of the Dor'Danil Barrow Den, on ground once part of Ashenvale's sacred forest. Its spreading demonic taint and roaming fiends endanger the nearby slumbering grounds and surrounding wildlands.",al={"dor danil felfire hill","barrow den demons"},it="ties"},{q="What is Felfire Hill?",a="Felfire Hill is a blighted elevation in central Ashenvale, situated southeast of Splintertree Post and southwest of the Warsong Lumber Camp. Unlike the lush woodlands surrounding it, this scarred rise serves as an entrenched demonic beachhead within the forest.",al={"what is felfire hill","felfire hill info","where is felfire hill"},it="place",add="1806e9cd"},{q="What happened at Felfire Hill?",a="During the Third War, the Burning Legion rained destruction upon Ashenvale. Felfire Hill marks the exact crash site where several flaming infernals crashed from the skies, scorching the earth and corrupting the landscape into an enduring stronghold for lingering demons.",al={"felfire hill history","what happened here","felfire hill third war"},it="history",add="168acc03"},{q="Is Felfire Hill dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The hill crawls with hostile demons that threaten any travelers passing through central Ashenvale. The danger is severe enough that the Horde actively fortifies both bridges leading toward the area to protect settlements like Splintertree Post from demonic incursions.",al={"is felfire hill dangerous","felfire hill danger","threat of felfire hill"},it="danger",add="d9143043"},{q="Why is it called Felfire Hill?",a="The hill earned its grim name from the catastrophic arrival of the Burning Legion's infernals during the Third War. Their fiery descent blasted the ground with demonic felfire, leaving the blackened earth permanently infused with corrupt, burning energies.",al={"why felfire hill","felfire hill name origin","name of felfire hill"},it="name",add="4c2c069f"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde holds the fortified bridges around Felfire Hill to protect the transit road between Splintertree Post and the Warsong Lumber Camp from demonic raids.",["class:Warlock"]="Fel energy lingers on the ridge where the Legion's infernals landed, drawing the dangerous curiosity of those who practice dark magic."},kw={"ashenvale","burning legion","demons","felfire hill","infernals","splintertree post","warsong lumber camp"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den","topic:third-war","topic:horde"},src={"Felfire Hill"}}
E["subzone:fire-scar-shrine"] = {t="subzone",n="Fire Scar Shrine",z="ashenvale",s="At Fire Scar Shrine, fel corruption scars the forest southwest of Astranaar. Once a night elf place of worship, the shrine now draws demons to its altar stones.",h="At Fire Scar Shrine, fel corruption scars the forest southwest of Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Blight in the Forest",b="Fire Scar Shrine lies southwest of Astranaar and west of the Ruins of Stardust. Demonic corruption has seized the shrine, fed by servants of the Cult of the Dark Strand and the Shadow Council. Fel magic has scorched the earth around it, and demons gather openly among the trees, defying the forest's defenders.",sp=0},{t="Shadows of the Dark Strand",b="Agents of the Cult of the Dark Strand and the Shadow Council brought corruption to Fire Scar Shrine. The orc warlock Ilkrud Magthrull acted under Athrikus Narassin's orders. Summoned fiends now patrol the altar stones unchecked. A tear in the veil sometimes draws greater horrors, including the towering doomguard Akkrilus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Fire Scar Shrine located?",a="Fire Scar Shrine lies in southwestern Ashenvale, southwest of Astranaar, south of the Shrine of Aessina, and west of the Ruins of Stardust.",al={"fire scar shrine location","where is fire scar shrine","fire scar shrine map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are there demons at Fire Scar Shrine?",a="Agents of the Shadow Council and the Cult of the Dark Strand corrupted Fire Scar Shrine, with the orc warlock Ilkrud Magthrull among them. Their rituals summoned demons and left fel taint on the sacred ground.",al={"why demons here","what corrupted fire scar shrine","who summoned the demons"},it="residents"},{q="Who is Akkrilus?",a="Akkrilus is a doomguard that sometimes appears around Fire Scar Shrine, drawn by the demonic energies gathered around its corrupted stones.",al={"akkrilus","doomguard at fire scar","rare demon fire scar shrine"}},{q="What connection does this place have to the Cult of the Dark Strand?",a="Ilkrud Magthrull, the orc warlock who operated at Fire Scar Shrine, served Athrikus Narassin, leader of the Cult of the Dark Strand. They used the shrine as a foothold for demonic summoning and their ambitions in Ashenvale.",al={"cult of the dark strand fire scar","dark strand connection","athrikus narassin fire scar"},sp=1,it="history",bt={"q965.3"}},{q="What is Fire Scar Shrine?",a="Fire Scar Shrine is a corrupted holy site nestled in southwestern Ashenvale, southwest of Astranaar and just west of the Ruins of Stardust. Once a peaceful sanctuary of the ancient woods, it has fallen into malice and ruin under dark, demonic influence.",al={"fire scar shrine lore","what is this shrine","fire scar shrine ashenvale"},it="place",add="2cfd3821"},{q="Why is Fire Scar Shrine ruined and corrupted?",a="The shrine fell to the foul machinations of the Shadow Council and their mortal pawns, the Cult of the Dark Strand. Corrupted by their rituals, the sanctuary was stripped of its natural grace and transformed into a blighted stronghold of demonic power.",al={"why is fire scar ruined","why is fire scar shrine corrupted","what ruined fire scar shrine"},it="ruin",add="45677f07"},{q="How dangerous is Fire Scar Shrine?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The shrine grounds crawl with aggressive demons left behind by dark summoners, and on occasion, the dread doomguard Akkrilus manifests to hunt any travelers who dare approach.",al={"is fire scar shrine dangerous","fire scar shrine threats","dangers of fire scar shrine"},it="danger",add="81dc8561"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, the desecration of Fire Scar Shrine so near Astranaar calls for swift retribution against the demons sullying the forest.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can read the Shadow Council's mark in the fel scars and wild demonic summons at Fire Scar Shrine, signs of its infiltrations across Kalimdor."},kw={"akkrilus","ashenvale","astranaar","athrikus narassin","cult of the dark strand","fire scar shrine","ilkrud magthrull","shadow council"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:astranaar","subzone:shrine-of-aessina","subzone:ruins-of-stardust","topic:shadow-council"},src={"Fire Scar Shrine"}}
E["subzone:forest-song"] = {t="subzone",n="Forest Song",z="ashenvale",s="Forest Song watches over northeastern Ashenvale, near Satyrnaar and Bough Shadow. The ancient kaldorei ruins are largely deserted, with the druid Kayneth Stillwind guarding the eastern border.",h="Forest Song watches over northeastern Ashenvale, near Satyrnaar and Bough Shadow.",sec={{t="A Lonely Vigil in Eastern Ashenvale",b="Forest Song's white columns and broken arches rise among the trees of northeastern Ashenvale. Once an elegant kaldorei settlement, the ruin now lies overgrown with ivy and wild ferns. Satyrnaar lies to the southwest, and the Warsong Lumber Camp presses in from the south. From here, eastern trails lead toward Azshara and Bough Shadow. Demonic corruption and Horde incursions trouble the surrounding woods, while the ruins remain quiet.",sp=0},{t="Watcher of the Border",b="Kayneth Stillwind keeps watch over Forest Song alone. From the crumbling outpost, the druid watches for enemies entering the wilderness, including the Forsaken in the eastern forests. Astranaar lies far away, and Forest Song has no garrison fortifications. Still, Alliance travelers heading north toward Felwood or seeking the corruption spreading through the canopy can gather here.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Forest Song?",a="Kayneth Stillwind, a night elf druid, lives alone among Forest Song's ancient ruins.",al={"who is at forest song","forest song npcs","forest song inhabitants"},it="residents"},{q="What threats are near Forest Song?",a="Satyrnaar lies to the southwest, where corrupted satyrs gather, and the Warsong Lumber Camp is to the south. Bough Shadow lies northeast, where the green dragonflight guards a Great Tree leading into the Emerald Dream.",al={"forest song dangers","enemies near forest song"},it="danger"},{q="Why is Kayneth Stillwind stationed here?",a="Kayneth Stillwind watches hostile movements in the eastern forests and directs allies against local dangers, including the Forsaken's sinister ventures and the diseases they spread.",al={"why is kayneth here","kayneth stillwind purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Forest Song a major Alliance settlement?",a="No. Forest Song is an unfortified ruin without an active garrison, vendors, or military infrastructure. Kayneth Stillwind maintains it as a lone forward lookout.",al={"alliance town forest song","is forest song a town"},it="fame"},{q="What is Forest Song?",a="Forest Song is an ancient night elf ruin located in northeastern Ashenvale, nestled between Satyrnaar, the Warsong Lumber Camp, and the great green dragon portal at Bough Shadow. Rather than a bustling city, it stands largely quiet under the ancient boughs, serving as a lone watchpost.",al={"what is forest song","forest song ashenvale","tell me about forest song"},it="place",add="3234d9c0"},{q="What happened to Forest Song?",a="Like many ancient kaldorei sites scattered throughout Ashenvale, Forest Song fell into ruin over long ages past. By the present day, the settlement lies crumbling, long left behind by major civilization until recent encroaching perils brought renewed attention to its strategic vantage.",al={"forest song history","what happened at forest song","why is forest song in ruins"},it="history",add="766b0515"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you find Kayneth Stillwind keeping a solitary Cenarion Circle vigil in the corrupted borderlands beneath the canopy near Bough Shadow's Great Tree.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can use Forest Song as a lone outpost while crossing northeastern Ashenvale toward Azshara or Felwood."},kw={"ashenvale","bough shadow","eastern ashenvale","forest song","kaldorei ruins","kayneth stillwind","satyrnaar"},rel={"quest:4581","quest:1011","zone:ashenvale","subzone:bough-shadow","subzone:satyrnaar","subzone:astranaar","subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","topic:druid"},src={"Forest Song"}}
E["subzone:greenpaw-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Greenpaw Village",z="ashenvale",s="Greenpaw Village lies between Raynewood Retreat and Silverwind Refuge, where the Foulweald furbolgs remain hostile. Chief Murgut and Shaman Oakpaw lead the corrupted tribe, and Alliance and Horde forces clash with them in Ashenvale.",h="Greenpaw Village lies between Raynewood Retreat and Silverwind Refuge, where the Foulweald furbolgs remain...",sec={{t="A Corrupted Settlement",b="Greenpaw Village lies south of Raynewood Retreat and northeast of Silverwind Refuge. Since the Third War, the Foulweald furbolgs who live there have fallen to the corruption tainting Ashenvale’s soil and spirits. Chief Murgut leads them, with Shaman Oakpaw as their corrupted spiritual guide. The tribe attacks travelers who enter its forest territory.",sp=0},{t="Caught in the Crosshairs",b="The Foulweald’s attacks draw fighting from every side of Greenpaw Village. Alliance sentinels and night elf druids seek to purge the furbolgs to protect nearby outposts and sacred moonwells. Horde forces advancing through Ashenvale also clash with them as both factions press through the woodland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Greenpaw Village located?",a="Greenpaw Village lies in central Ashenvale, south of Raynewood Retreat, northeast of Silverwind Refuge, and northwest of the southern moonwell.",al={"greenpaw location","where is greenpaw village","find greenpaw"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives in Greenpaw Village?",a="The Foulweald furbolg tribe lives in Greenpaw Village, led by Chief Murgut and their corrupted spiritual advisor, Shaman Oakpaw.",al={"who is here","greenpaw mobs","greenpaw furbolgs"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Greenpaw Village hostile?",a="Demonic corruption left after the Burning Legion invaded Ashenvale drove the Foulweald into maddened aggression.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","are greenpaw furbolgs corrupt"},it="threat"},{q="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting here?",a="Both factions see the aggressive Foulweald as a threat to their roads and settlements. Night elves seek to cleanse or contain the madness near their moonwells, while Horde forces clash with the furbolgs as they advance through Ashenvale.",al={"greenpaw quests","who attacks greenpaw"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Greenpaw Village?",a="Greenpaw Village is a furbolg settlement nestled in central Ashenvale, situated south of Raynewood Retreat and northeast of Silverwind Refuge. Once a peaceful enclave amidst the ancient forest, it serves as the home encampment for the Foulweald tribe, complete with rustic wooden dwellings, totems, and fire pits beneath the dense woodland canopy.",al={"what is greenpaw village","greenpaw village lore","tell me about greenpaw village"},it="place",add="44cbc3fb"},{q="What happened at Greenpaw Village?",a="Like many furbolg communities across Ashenvale, the inhabitants of Greenpaw Village succumbed to the creeping demonic corruption that tainted the forest during the Third War. Driven mad by dark energies, the Foulweald turned violently aggressive toward outsiders, transforming their tranquil settlement into a hostile den that draws intervention from both night elves and nearby Horde outposts.",al={"greenpaw village history","what happened to greenpaw","history of greenpaw village"},it="history",add="e6fbac57"},{q="Is Greenpaw Village dangerous?",a="Greenpaw Village is exceptionally perilous to wander into unprepared. The Foulweald furbolgs are aggressive and attack any intruder on sight, fighting with feral strength. Among their ranks are potent shamans such as Oakpaw and fierce leaders like Chief Murgut, making the camp hazardous for solitary travelers moving through the heart of the forest.",al={"how dangerous is greenpaw village","is greenpaw dangerous","dangers of greenpaw village"},it="danger",add="303ee734"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the Foulweald’s corruption near Raynewood Retreat and their sacred moonwells is a reminder of Ashenvale’s lingering demonic scars.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you witness the ancient bear folk’s pain at Greenpaw Village, where nature’s balance has broken into feral madness."},kw={"ashenvale","foulweald","furbolg","greenpaw village","murgut","oakpaw","raynewood retreat","silverwind refuge"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","subzone:raynewood-retreat","subzone:silverwind-refuge","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Greenpaw Village"}}
E["subzone:howling-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Howling Vale",z="ashenvale",s="The Terrowulf worgen howl through Howling Vale in north-central Ashenvale, near the Felwood border. Their caves hide an ancient shrine to Elune, bound to the worgen’s origins on Kalimdor.",h="The Terrowulf worgen howl through Howling Vale in north-central Ashenvale, near the Felwood border.",sec={{t="A Haunted Haven",b="North of the road to Felwood, Ashenvale’s calm gives way to the howls of the Terrowulf. Ancient trees still fill the vale, but corrupted packlords and aggressive wildlife roam among them. A cave at its heart holds the shrine of Mel'Thandris, an ancient night elf priestess. Once a place of quiet devotion, the shrine now lies in ruins, defiled by feral wolf-men whose origin puzzles the nearby Sentinels.",sp=0},{t="The Scythe and the Starsong Legacy",b="The Tome of Mel'Thandris tells of recent events at the shrine. Night elf Velinde Starsong came into possession of the Scythe of Elune, a fateful artifact. She tried to channel its power against demons, but instead unleashed the worgen in the surrounding woods. The vale now echoes with the beasts she summoned.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Howling Vale?",a="The Terrowulf worgen gave the vale its grim name with their chilling calls. Their constant howls echo through the canyon and cavern, drowning out Ashenvale’s natural sounds.",al={"why howling vale","origin of howling vale name","why does it howl"},it="name"},{q="What is the Shrine of Mel'Thandris?",a="The Shrine of Mel'Thandris is an ancient night elf sanctuary dedicated to Elune and named for Mel'Thandris. The Tome of Mel'Thandris kept there records events that may explain the wolf-men’s arrival.",al={"shrine of melthandris","who was mel'thandris","melthandris shrine"},it="place"},{q="Where did the worgen here come from?",a="The Sentinels are puzzled by the worgen’s origin. Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow sends Alliance scouts to study the Tome of Mel'Thandris at the shrine, where its history holds the key to where the wolf-men came from.",al={"how did worgen get to ashenvale","terrowulf origin","why are worgen in ashenvale"},sp=1,it="origin"},{q="What is the Tome of Mel'Thandris?",a="The Tome of Mel'Thandris is a sacred historical text kept at the shrine deep inside the cave. Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow sends Alliance scouts to study it and learn where the wolf-men plaguing the forest came from.",al={"tome of mel'thandris","tome in howling vale","melthandris book"},it="item"},{q="What is the Howling Vale?",a="The Howling Vale is a shadowed hollow and cavern in north-central Ashenvale, nestled just southwest of the Felwood border. Once a peaceful sanctuary sacred to the night elves, it centers around the ancient Shrine of Mel'Thandris. Today, its sacred groves have fallen into darkness, overrun by feral beasts and unnatural horrors.",al={"what is howling vale","howling vale info","about howling vale"},it="place",add="8276f532"},{q="What happened at the Howling Vale?",a="Long ago, the Shrine of Mel'Thandris was raised here as a sacred place of Elune. In recent times, the night elf Velinde Starsong came into possession of the Scythe of Elune; after its disturbing power was unleashed, savage worgen emerged and overran the vale, defiling the once-hallowed ground.",al={"howling vale history","what happened at howling vale","history of howling vale"},sp=1,it="history",add="aa8b1a44"},{q="Who lives in the Howling Vale?",a="No civilized people dwell here any longer. The vale has been claimed by the Terrowulf worgen, a savage pack of wolf-beasts who stalk the ruined shrine under the rule of their packlords. They share the hollow with hostile ghostpaw wolves and crazed, withered ancients twisted by the corruption seeping through northern Ashenvale.",al={"who lives in howling vale","howling vale inhabitants","who controls howling vale"},it="residents",add="17e899ac"},{q="Why is the Howling Vale ruined?",a="The vale fell into ruin when the feral worgen arrived. The night elf tenders were either slain or driven out, leaving the Shrine of Mel'Thandris neglected and broken. With the surrounding forest corrupted by madness and creeping blight, the sacred grove degraded into a savage den of predatory beasts.",al={"why is howling vale ruined","why is howling vale abandoned","shrine of mel'thandris ruined"},it="ruin",add="af0435d5"},{q="Is the Howling Vale dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The vale swarms with bloodthirsty Terrowulf worgen that hunt in coordinated packs, alongside vicious alphas. Worse, the ancient treants guarding the grounds have grown withered and crazed, attacking anyone foolish enough to tread near the shrine's remains without caution.",al={"is howling vale dangerous","how dangerous is howling vale","threats in howling vale"},it="danger",add="2daeb8a3"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the defilement of Mel'Thandris’s shrine is a bitter wound. A sacred place of Elune now lies overrun by savage wolf-men.",["class:Druid"]="The feral wolf-men in the cave are a dark mirror of druidic shapeshifting. Their arrival in Ashenvale remains a mystery to the Sentinels."},kw={"ashenvale worgen","howling vale","mel'thandris","scythe of elune","terrowulf","velinde starsong"},rel={"quest:1022","quest:1037","zone:ashenvale","topic:worgen","topic:elune","topic:druid","zone:felwood"},src={"Howling Vale"}}
E["subzone:iris-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Iris Lake",z="ashenvale",s="In north-central Ashenvale, Iris Lake lies east of Astranaar, its waters turned yellow-green by corruption from Felwood. Bog beasts prowl its shores.",h="In north-central Ashenvale, Iris Lake lies east of Astranaar, its waters turned yellow-green by corruption...",sec={{t="A Tainted Refuge",b="Iris Lake lies between Astranaar and the moonwell tended by Shael'dryn, its waters fouled since the Third War. Fel energies drift south from the tainted heights of Felwood and poison the basin, turning clear water into a yellow-green mire. The corruption has twisted the native plants and water spirits, and aggressive bog beasts lash out at travelers who come near.",sp=0},{t="Tears of the Goddess",b="Pollution chokes Iris Lake, yet sacred remnants of the past linger along its edges. Rare crystalline stones called Elune's Tears sometimes rest on the muddy banks. Keepers of elven traditions, including Shael'dryn, seek the holy stones to help purify tainted moonwells and resist the demonic blight spreading across Ashenvale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the water at Iris Lake green and murky?",a="Demonic corruption from neighboring Felwood has tainted Iris Lake. The dark magic poisons the water, turning it yellow-green and twisting nearby wildlife into aggressive creatures.",al={"why is iris lake green","iris lake water","why is iris lake tainted"},it="ruin"},{q="What creatures roam around Iris Lake?",a="Corrupted bog beasts roam the lake and its shores. Fel energy has maddened these creatures of plant and mud, and they attack anyone who approaches the water.",al={"iris lake monsters","iris lake mobs","what attacks at iris lake"},it="threat"},{q="What are Elune's Tears?",a="Elune's Tears are sacred blue stones found near Iris Lake's shores. Night elf priests and keepers use them in purification rites, especially to cleanse corrupted moonwells.",al={"elunes tears","elune tear","what is elunes tear"}},{q="Where is Iris Lake located?",a="Iris Lake lies in north-central Ashenvale, directly east of Astranaar and west of Shael'dryn's moonwell.",al={"where is iris lake","iris lake location","how to get to iris lake"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Iris Lake?",a="Iris Lake is a corrupted body of water situated in north-central Ashenvale, resting east of Astranaar and west of Shael'dryn's moonwell. Once a tranquil and pristine part of the ancient night elven woodland, the lake has been blighted by taint spreading from Felwood, turning its waters into a murky, yellowish-green mire.",al={"what is iris lake","iris lake lore","about iris lake"},it="place",add="8ae92a66"},{q="What happened to Iris Lake?",a="Iris Lake fell victim to the demonic blight seeping southward from Felwood. The pervasive corruption poisoned the once-pure waters and twisted the local flora and fauna, transforming what was once a sacred natural retreat into a decayed, hostile swamp.",al={"iris lake history","what happened here","how did iris lake get corrupted"},it="history",add="4294757e"},{q="Is Iris Lake dangerous?",a="Yes, Iris Lake is quite dangerous. In addition to the foul, poisoned waters, twisted bog beasts prowl the shoreline and shallows. These corrupted plant creatures are fiercely aggressive and will attack any travelers who venture near the waters searching for rare herbs or Elune's Tears.",al={"iris lake dangers","is it safe here","threats at iris lake"},it="danger",add="b432431a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Iris Lake shows the corruption threatening Ashenvale. Finding Elune's Tears along its fouled shores offers hope of cleansing the forest.",["class:Druid"]="The twisted bog beasts and corrupted waters show the harm demonic energy brings to nature when left unchecked."},kw={"ashenvale","bog beasts","elune's tear","felwood corruption","iris lake","shael'dryn"},rel={"quest:1033","npc:shael-dryn","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","zone:ashenvale","zone:felwood","subzone:astranaar","topic:elune"},src={"Iris Lake"}}
E["subzone:kargathia-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Kargathia Keep",z="ashenvale",s="Warsong overseers hold the eastern edge of their lumber camp at Kargathia Keep. The fortified stronghold guards the Southfury River border in Ashenvale and links the outpost to Orgrimmar.",h="Warsong overseers hold the eastern edge of their lumber camp at Kargathia Keep.",sec={{t="A Bastion on the Southfury",b="Kargathia Keep anchors the eastern edge of the Warsong Lumber Camp, just west of the Southfury River. Spiked barricades fortify the outpost, where Overseer Gorthak and his officers direct the Horde’s logging operations. From the river border, the Warsong clan watches for incursions. When night elf skirmishers strike, reinforcements can come swiftly from Durotar and Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Bladefist",b="Kargathia Keep shares its namesake with Kargath in the Badlands and Bladefist Bay on Durotar’s coast: the famed chieftain Kargath Bladefist. For Warsong orcs facing Ashenvale’s hostile woodlands, its imposing architecture speaks of martial resilience and Horde defiance in lands claimed by the night elves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Kargathia Keep located?",a="Kargathia Keep stands in eastern Ashenvale, at the east edge of the Warsong Lumber Camp, just west of the Southfury River.",al={"kargathia keep location","where is kargathia keep","kargathia outpost location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who leads the keep?",a="Overseer Gorthak commands the Warsong Lumber Camp from Kargathia Keep, directing logging and defenses against Alliance attacks.",al={"who is in charge of kargathia keep","kargathia keep leader","overseer gorthak"},it="leader"},{q="Why was the keep named Kargathia?",a="Kargathia Keep was named for Kargath Bladefist, the legendary chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan. Kargath in the Badlands and Bladefist Bay in Durotar share that naming heritage.",al={"who is kargathia keep named after","kargath bladefist","why kargathia"},it="name"},{q="What is the strategic purpose of this stronghold?",a="Kargathia Keep commands the logging camp’s eastern border along the Southfury River, securing the supply route and allowing troops to come swiftly from Orgrimmar.",al={"why is kargathia keep here","purpose of kargathia keep","kargathia keep importance"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Kargathia Keep?",a="Kargathia Keep is a fortified Horde stronghold situated in the eastern reaches of the Warsong Lumber Camp, just west of the Southfury River. Reinforced with spiked barricades, it functions as the central base of operations for Warsong Clan officers overseeing the Horde's logging operations and territorial defenses across eastern Ashenvale.",al={"what is kargathia keep","kargathia keep lore","about kargathia keep"},it="place",add="95145ea7"},{q="Who lives in or runs Kargathia Keep?",a="The stronghold serves as headquarters for the officers of the Warsong Clan. Foremost among them is Overseer Gorthak, the orc commander charged with running the Warsong Lumber Camp and directing Horde labor and defense in the sector.",al={"who lives in kargathia keep","who is at kargathia keep","who controls kargathia keep"},it="residents",add="30f293af"},{q="Is Kargathia Keep dangerous?",a="To Horde travelers, Kargathia Keep is a secure sanctuary, offering protection behind heavy spiked barricades. For Alliance interlopers, it is perilous ground, heavily manned by veteran Warsong warriors and perfectly positioned to rapidly muster reinforcements direct from Orgrimmar if attacked.",al={"is kargathia keep dangerous","is kargathia keep safe","threats to kargathia keep"},it="danger",add="feb769b0"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde defender, you can hold this frontline stronghold in Ashenvale and secure timber shipments vital to Orgrimmar’s construction.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see this spiked stronghold as a sign of the Horde’s aggressive, entrenched presence in your sacred ancestral forest."},kw={"ashenvale","kargath bladefist","kargathia keep","kargathia outpost","overseer gorthak","southfury river","warsong lumber camp"},rel={"subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","topic:warsong-clan","subzone:southfury-river","zone:ashenvale","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:kargath","subzone:bladefist-bay","topic:horde"},src={"Kargathia Keep"}}
E["subzone:lake-falathim"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Falathim",z="ashenvale",s="At Lake Falathim, murlocs now overrun the western Ashenvale shore southwest of Maestra's Post. Night elves once came here to swim and fish, drawn by Elune's moonlight said to touch the water day and night.",h="At Lake Falathim, murlocs now overrun the western Ashenvale shore southwest of Maestra's Post.",sec={{t="Bathed in Moonlight",b="Lake Falathim lies southeast of the Zoram Strand, where the Kaldorei once swam and fished in peace. Local lore says Elune's gentle light rests on the water at every hour, by day and by night. Now ferocious murlocs have surged inland and seized the shores. Their numbers drive away travelers and scholars.",sp=0},{t="The Scholar's Disappearance",b="Murlocs have made Lake Falathim dangerous for anyone wandering alone. The night elf scholar Teronis recently went missing near the water while pursuing his inquiry. Sentinels fear for anyone who approaches the moonlit pool alone, with hostile murlocs lurking along the banks and in the shallows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Lake Falathim located?",a="Lake Falathim lies in western Ashenvale, in the hills southwest of Maestra's Post and southeast of the Zoram Strand.",al={"lake falathim location","where is lake falathim","find lake falathim"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Lake Falathim special to the night elves?",a="Night elves value Lake Falathim because Elune's moonlight is said to touch its waters by day and night. They once came to its peaceful banks to swim and fish.",al={"why is lake falathim important","lake falathim lore","moonlight lake ashenvale"},it="purpose"},{q="What creatures inhabit the lake?",a="Hostile murlocs have overrun Lake Falathim's shores, making them dangerous for travelers.",al={"lake falathim mobs","what is at lake falathim","lake falathim monsters"},it="residents"},{q="Who was Teronis?",a="Teronis was a night elf scholar who went missing near Lake Falathim. The vicious murlocs in the area are blamed for his disappearance.",al={"teronis lake falathim","who is teronis","missing scholar lake falathim"}},{q="What is Lake Falathim?",a="Lake Falathim is a tranquil body of water nestled in the western forests of Ashenvale, situated southeast of the Zoram Strand and southwest of Maestra's Post. It is renowned for carrying Elune's divine blessing, where moonlight touches its shimmering waters day and night regardless of the hour.",al={"what is lake falathim","lake falathim overview","about lake falathim"},it="place",add="ede2002d"},{q="What happened at Lake Falathim?",a="For generations, the lake was a peaceful haven where night elves gathered to fish, swim, and bask in Elune's blessed moonlight. That serenity came to a bitter end when aggressive murlocs overran the waters, forcing the elves away and threatening anyone who strayed near.",al={"history of lake falathim","what happened to lake falathim","lake falathim past"},it="history",add="1b39db00"},{q="Why was Lake Falathim abandoned?",a="The peaceful night elves who once swam and fished here were driven out when violent murlocs claimed the waters. The infestation turned a revered spiritual retreat into hostile territory, causing travelers to steer clear and leading scholars like Teronis to grave misfortune.",al={"why is lake falathim abandoned","why did night elves leave lake falathim","lake falathim ruined"},it="ruin",add="f94ff24b"},{q="Is Lake Falathim dangerous?",a="Yes. While its blessed waters look inviting, the lake is infested with ferocious murlocs who ruthlessly attack intruders. Even cautious visitors and scholars investigating its sacred shores have vanished into the waters, never to return.",al={"how dangerous is lake falathim","is it safe at lake falathim","threats at lake falathim"},it="danger",add="019a1e1b"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As Kaldorei, you know Lake Falathim as a sanctuary touched by Elune's moonlight. Murlocs now threaten its shores.",["faction:Alliance"]="From Maestra's Post, Alliance scouts watch for murlocs near Lake Falathim and seek word of missing scholars such as Teronis."},kw={"ashenvale","elune","falathim","lake falathim","maestra's post","moonlight","murloc","teronis"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:zoram-strand","topic:murloc","quest:1008"},src={"Lake Falathim"}}
E["subzone:maestra-s-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Maestra's Post",z="ashenvale",s="Along the road through western Ashenvale, Maestra's Post watches the way between Astranaar and the Ruins of Ordil'Aran. Night elven Sentinels guard the settlement, where a few humans serve the Alliance.",h="Along the road through western Ashenvale, Maestra's Post watches the way between Astranaar and the Ruins of...",sec={{t="A Forward Watch",b="Maestra's Post keeps watch beneath the trees of western Ashenvale. A slender night elven tower and an open lodge mark the settlement along the road between the coast of Darkshore and Astranaar. Sentinels scan the surrounding wilds as corrupted furbolg stir nearby. Horde movements also threaten Alliance supply lines.",sp=0},{t="An Alliance Gathering",b="Maestra's Post brings a handful of human allies to live among the night elven Sentinels. Feero Ironhand and Delgren the Purifier lend their martial strength and devotion to the holy Light in service of the Alliance. This remote campsite is an early meeting place between the eastern kingdoms and Kalimdor's ancient defenders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Maestra's Post located?",a="Maestra's Post lies in western Ashenvale, along the road northwest of Astranaar and south of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran.",al={"maestra's post location","where is maestras post","find maestras post"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Maestra?",a="No record at the post names Maestra. The outpost bears her name, but she is not among the Sentinels stationed there.",al={"who is maestra","moon priestess maestra","who was maestra"},it="name"},{q="Why are there humans at an elven outpost?",a="After the third war, the night elves joined the Alliance. Human travelers and warriors such as Feero Ironhand and Delgren the Purifier came to Kalimdor to offer aid and strengthen ties with their night elf allies.",al={"why are humans in ashenvale","feero ironhand why here","delgren the purifier why here"},it="residents"},{q="What threats face Maestra's Post?",a="Corrupted furbolg clans lurk in the surrounding woodland, while Horde scouting parties and incursions press into Ashenvale.",al={"who attacks maestras post","dangers at maestras post"},it="threat"},{q="What is Maestra's Post?",a="Maestra's Post is a small Alliance outpost situated in western Ashenvale, south of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran and northwest of Astranaar. Built around an elven tower and an open night elven lodge, it serves as a staging ground and waystation for travelers journeying between Darkshore and central Ashenvale. Despite its modest size and sparse contingent of defenders, it marks one of the few places in the forest where both night elves and humans work side by side to patrol the woods.",al={"what is maestras post","maestra post info","about maestras post"},it="place",add="3452376e"},{q="Is Maestra's Post dangerous?",a="Within the immediate perimeter of the camp, Alliance travelers are relatively safe, sheltered beneath the watch of local sentinels and defenders. However, the surrounding forest is perilous. Hostile furbolg tribes suffering from foul corruption prowl nearby, and scouts from the Horde frequently roam the road looking for vulnerable targets. Even the post itself sits close to contested frontiers, making vigilance essential whenever you step beyond its sheltered borders.",al={"is maestras post safe","danger maestras post","threats at maestras post"},it="danger",add="a14cd342"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers leaving Darkshore, Maestra's Post offers a friendly welcome and a fortified refuge in Ashenvale's contested forests.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the new Alliance taking shape here: Sentinels share hearth and watch duty with the younger races of the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"ashenvale","delgren the purifier","feero ironhand","maestra's post","maestras post","ordil'aran","sentinels"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:astranaar","subzone:ruins-of-ordil-aran","npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:feero-ironhand","topic:sentinels","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Maestra's Post"}}
E["subzone:moonwell-ashenvale"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonwell (Ashenvale)",z="ashenvale",s="This secluded shrine, known to the night elves as the Moonwell of Purity, rests in central Ashenvale east of Iris Lake and west of Raynewood Retreat. Its blessed waters channel the grace of Elune to nourish the ancient forest and cleanse creeping foulness from the land. Alliance travelers following Raene Wolfrunner's research often seek out Shael'dryn, who keeps watch beside its tranquil basin.",h="This secluded shrine, known to the night elves as the Moonwell of Purity, rests in central Ashenvale east of...",sec={{t="Sanctuary of Purity",b="Tucked away beneath the canopy of central Ashenvale, this moonwell serves as a spiritual anchor for the kaldorei. Its luminescent waters tap into nature's latent magic and the light of the Moon Goddess. As the surrounding forest suffers from satyr corruption, fel taint, and logging incursions, pure shrines like this one become vital lifelines for those trying to heal the woods.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Wood",b="Adventurers aiding Raene Wolfrunner come here to find Shael'dryn, who knows of the rod Dartol once created. She points them toward its scattered pieces and, once they are recovered, reconstructs the rod at the moonwell.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is this specific moonwell called?",a="This site is known as the Moonwell of Purity. It is one of several moonwells across Ashenvale, located east of Iris Lake and west of Raynewood Retreat.",al={"which moonwell is this","moonwell name","moonwell of purity"}},{q="What are moonwells used for?",a="Moonwells are sacred basins consecrated to Elune that blend lunar power with natural magic. Night elves use them to sustain the land, replenish their spiritual strength, and purify items tainted by dark or demonic influences.",al={"what does a moonwell do","moonwell purpose","why moonwells exist"}},{q="Why do Alliance adventurers visit this moonwell?",a="Alliance heroes following Raene Wolfrunner's research out of Astranaar come here to seek Shael'dryn, who helps them recover the scattered pieces of Dartol's rod.",al={"raene's cleansing moonwell","why come here","cleanse rod here"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every moonwell is a sacred home away from home for the kaldorei, serving as both a spiritual font of Elune's grace and a frontline bulwark against the demonic taint threatening Ashenvale.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Tailors can harness the dense lunar energies pooling within the waters to weave pure Mooncloth from felcloth."},kw={"ashenvale","cleansing","elune","iris lake","moonwell","moonwell of purity","raynewood retreat"},rel={"quest:991","zone:ashenvale","subzone:iris-lake","subzone:raynewood-retreat","subzone:silverwing-outpost","subzone:greenpaw-village","topic:alliance"},src={"Moonwell (Ashenvale)"}}
E["subzone:mor-shan-rampart"] = {t="subzone",n="Mor'shan Rampart",z="ashenvale",s="At Mor'shan Rampart, the Horde guards the northern end of the Gold Road and the way into Ashenvale. The Warsong clan built the barricade to shield Horde territory from night elf counterattacks and stage raids into the forest.",h="At Mor'shan Rampart, the Horde guards the northern end of the Gold Road and the way into Ashenvale.",sec={{t="The Northern Gate",b="Mor'shan Rampart guards the northern end of the Gold Road, where the Barrens meet Ashenvale. Its timber walls and watchtowers were raised against night elf strikes over the Horde's logging. From here, raiding parties head north toward Astranaar.",sp=0},{t="Warsong Outpost",b="Warsong fighters and sentries keep Mor'shan Rampart ready for battle. They watch the tree line for night elf scouts and archers, while the post keeps supply lines open between Ashenvale's frontline outposts and Horde settlements to the south.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Mor'shan Rampart?",a="Mor'shan Rampart is a fortified Horde border post where the Barrens meet Ashenvale. It guards the northern end of the Gold Road against attacks on the Barrens.",al={"morshan rampart","what is this barricade","northern barrens gate"},it="place"},{q="Who controls this fortification?",a="The Horde garrisons Mor'shan Rampart with warriors and sentries tied to the Warsong clan. They keep watch from its towers and palisades along the forest boundary.",al={"who holds morshan","who guards the rampart","morshan defenders"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the rampart here instead of deeper in Ashenvale?",a="Mor'shan Rampart guards the northern end of the Gold Road, the main land route between the central Barrens and Ashenvale. Holding this narrow passage makes it harder for night elf forces to strike south into Horde lands.",al={"why build ramparts here","strategic importance morshan"},it="purpose"},{q="Can Alliance travelers pass through the rampart safely?",a="No. Mor'shan Rampart is an active Horde military post, and its guards attack Alliance travelers approaching from Ashenvale or the Barrens.",al={"can alliance pass","alliance crossing morshan"},it="danger"},{q="What is the history of the Mor'shan Rampart?",a="The Mor'shan Rampart was erected as a defensive bulwark at the northern terminus of the Gold Road to hold the border against Alliance incursions from Ashenvale. Over time, the fortified post has served not only to block night elven counterattacks southward into the Barrens, but also as an active staging ground and launching point for Horde raiding parties pushing deep into the forest toward settlements like Astranaar.",al={"history of morshan rampart","morshan rampart past","why was morshan built"},it="history",add="5054dbd0"},{q="Who mans the Mor'shan Rampart?",a="The rampart is garrisoned by Horde forces, primarily Mor'shan Defenders and Watchmen affiliated with the Warsong Outriders. These seasoned orcish warriors maintain a constant vigil atop the wooden watchtowers and palisades, guarding the border road against night elven patrols while supporting Horde logistics moving into Ashenvale.",al={"who lives at morshan rampart","morshan rampart defenders","who guards morshan rampart"},it="residents",add="e2863b82"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Mor'shan Rampart guards the Barrens against night elf incursions and keeps supply lines to Ashenvale's logging operations open.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance fighters see Mor'shan Rampart as an aggressive barricade built to protect Horde logging and stage raids into Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","barrens","gold road","mor'shan rampart","morshan","warsong clan","warsong outriders"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:gold-road","topic:warsong-clan","topic:horde","topic:alliance","subzone:astranaar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Mor'shan Rampart"}}
E["subzone:mystral-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Mystral Lake",z="ashenvale",s="Travelers from both factions reach Mystral Lake in south-central Ashenvale. Its deep waters draw them beneath the watch of the night elves.",h="Travelers from both factions reach Mystral Lake in south-central Ashenvale.",sec={{t="The Forest's Great Lake",b="Mystral Lake draws travelers to its shores in southern Ashenvale. The vast lake lies south of Silverwind Refuge and east of Talondeep Vale, the largest lake in the forest. Night elves keep watch from their outpost on its northern shore. Travelers from both the Horde and the Alliance often find their journeys bringing them to its banks.",sp=0},{t="Spiritual Crossroads",b="Horde shaman come to Mystral Lake during trials of elemental communion. In its deep waters, they seek to understand the element of water. The lake’s raw primal resonance makes it an essential pilgrimage site for those learning to bind and respect the tidal spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Mystral Lake located?",a="Mystral Lake lies in south-central Ashenvale, south of Silverwind Refuge and east of Talondeep Vale. It is the forest’s largest open body of water.",al={"where is mystral lake","mystral lake location","lake mystral map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do shaman visit Mystral Lake?",a="Horde shaman visit Mystral Lake during spiritual trials for the Call of Water. Its deep elemental resonance helps them understand and attune to water spirits.",al={"call of water mystral lake","shaman quest mystral lake"},it="purpose"},{q="Who controls Mystral Lake?",a="Neither faction holds direct military control over Mystral Lake. The night elves watch it from their outpost at Silverwind Refuge on the northern shore.",al={"is mystral lake horde or alliance","who owns mystral lake"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Mystral Lake?",a="Mystral Lake, also known as Lake Mystral, is the largest body of water in Ashenvale. Nestled in the forest's south-central reaches just south of Silverwind Refuge, its tranquil waters are a crucial focal point for travelers, spiritual seekers, and regional factions alike.",al={"what is mystral lake","mystral lake lore","lake mystral"},it="place",add="25dbe280"},{q="What happened at Mystral Lake?",a="Mystral Lake is the largest lake in Ashenvale. The night elves watch over it from Silverwind Refuge on its northern shore, and its deep waters hold a strong elemental resonance that draws Horde shaman during their trials of water.",al={"mystral lake history","what happened here","mystral lake corruption"},it="history",add="aa377247"},{q="Is Mystral Lake dangerous?",a="Like much of Ashenvale, its shores are not safe for the careless. The lake lies in contested forest where night elf Sentinels and Horde forces both range, and wild beasts roam the surrounding woods.",al={"is mystral lake dangerous","dangers of mystral lake","mystral lake threats"},it="danger",add="be483818"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you come to Mystral Lake during the Call of Water, where you confront local spirits to master your elemental craft.",["race:NightElf"]="From Silverwind Refuge, your people watch over Ashenvale’s largest lake, at the heart of the forest they defend."},kw={"ashenvale","call of water","lake mystral","mystral lake","silverwind refuge","water elementals"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:silverwind-refuge","subzone:talondeep-vale","quest:63","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Mystral Lake"}}
E["subzone:night-run"] = {t="subzone",n="Night Run",z="ashenvale",s="In east-central Ashenvale, Night Run crowns a cliff-ringed bluff among the ancient elven ruins. Felmusk satyr dwell there, and dark soul magic gathers within the outpost.",h="In east-central Ashenvale, Night Run crowns a cliff-ringed bluff among the ancient elven ruins.",sec={{t="A Defended Cliffside Perch",b="Night Run is Ashenvale’s smallest and most isolated of its three major satyr strongholds, alongside Xavian and Satyrnaar. Crumbling elven stonework and broken pillars shelter the settlement on a high ridge bounded by steep, impassable cliffs. Travelers can reach it by following the Falfarren River near the waters of Xavian, then turning west up the ridge, or by taking a precarious northern ledge above Raynewood Retreat. Though small, the enclave is dangerous. The Felmusk satyr work with the shadowy Cult of the Dark Strand, anchoring twisted soulgems to gather demonic essence within the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Night Run?",a="The Felmusk satyr occupy Night Run. These demonic night elf corrupters are affiliated with the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"who lives at night run","night run mobs","what is at night run"},it="residents"},{q="How do you reach Night Run?",a="Night Run lies on an elevated bluff bounded by sheer cliffs. You can approach by a narrow ledge north of Raynewood Retreat or follow the Falfarren River toward Xavian before turning west up the ridge.",al={"how to get to night run","night run path","night run entrance"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What is the Cult of the Dark Strand doing here?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand works alongside the satyrs, maintaining a dark soulgem at Night Run to harvest and channel demonic energies across Ashenvale.",al={"cult of the dark strand night run","soulgem night run"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Night Run?",a="Night Run is a small, secluded satyr encampment perched upon an elevated promontory in east-central Ashenvale. Nestled between Raynewood Retreat and Splintertree Post, it is the smallest of the three major satyr holds in the forest, consisting of little more than shattered night elven pillars and ancient stones that now harbor vile demonic corruption.",al={"night run overview","what is night run ashenvale","night run camp"},it="place",add="3ed13181"},{q="Why is Night Run ruined?",a="Like much of Ashenvale's ancient architecture, Night Run's classical night elven columns and foundations fell to ruin long ago, leaving only crumbling masonry for the satyrs to claim as crude shelter.",al={"why is night run destroyed","night run ruins","what ruined night run"},it="ruin",add="c4f1d276"},{q="Is Night Run dangerous?",a="Night Run is intensely perilous to unwary travelers. The promontory is heavily guarded by the Felmusk satyr, who remain hostile to all outsiders and allied with the sinister shadow councilors of the Cult of the Dark Strand. Treacherous sheer cliffs surround the area, leaving little room to maneuver if you are caught by demonic magic.",al={"how dangerous is night run","threats in night run","is night run safe"},it="danger",add="2a13d550"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you see an enduring scar in Night Run: ancient elven stones shelter the twisted Felmusk.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find Night Run just north of Raynewood Retreat, a demonic menace overlooking crucial Sentinel supply lines."},kw={"ashenvale","cult of the dark strand","falfarren river","felmusk","night run","satyr","soulgem"},rel={"subzone:xavian","subzone:satyrnaar","subzone:raynewood-retreat","subzone:falfarren-river","zone:ashenvale","topic:satyr","topic:sentinels"},src={"Night Run"}}
E["subzone:nightsong-woods"] = {t="subzone",n="Nightsong Woods",z="ashenvale",s="In eastern Ashenvale, Nightsong Woods runs from Raynewood Retreat toward Azshara. Night elves and the Warsong clan fight over the forest as the Horde harvests lumber, while demonic corruption lingers among its groves.",h="In eastern Ashenvale, Nightsong Woods runs from Raynewood Retreat toward Azshara.",sec={{t="A Forest Carved by War",b="Nightsong Woods is Ashenvale’s eastern battleground. The Falfarren River cuts through its western reaches, marking a tense boundary between Alliance settlements and Horde incursions. Farther east, Splintertree Post directs Horde campaigns against the Silverwing Sentinels. Warsong orcs fell the southern groves for lumber to fuel the Horde’s expansion, angering the Kaldorei. Satyr strongholds at Satyrnaar and Xavian, along with demonic remnants at Demon Fall Canyon and Felfire Hill, taint the eastern forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Nightsong Woods located?",a="Nightsong Woods covers eastern Ashenvale, from Raynewood Retreat and the northern road to Felwood toward Azshara’s untamed border.",al={"nightsong woods location","where is nightsong woods","ashenvale east woods"},it="place"},{q="Why is there so much fighting in this part of Ashenvale?",a="The Silverwing Sentinels and the Warsong clan fight over this frontier. The Horde depends on dense timber from the southern trees to build and sustain its settlements, while night elves battle to halt the cutting and reclaim their ancestral land.",al={"why fighting in nightsong woods","horde vs alliance ashenvale","warsong conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Who controls Nightsong Woods?",a="No single faction controls Nightsong Woods. The Falfarren River roughly divides western Alliance territory from eastern Horde positions at Splintertree Post and the Warsong Lumber Camp. Corrupt satyr hold parts of the woodland at Satyrnaar and Xavian, while Legion forces are near Demon Fall Canyon.",al={"who owns nightsong woods","nightsong woods faction control"},it="residents"},{q="What demonic threats exist here?",a="Demonic forces and corruption threaten the eastern wilderness. Satyr dwell in fortified ancient ruins at Satyrnaar and Xavian, while lingering Burning Legion fiends inhabit Felfire Hill and the depths of Demon Fall Canyon.",al={"demons in nightsong woods","satyr in eastern ashenvale","felfire hill demons"},it="threat"},{q="What happened at Nightsong Woods?",a="Once an undisturbed part of ancient Ashenvale, Nightsong Woods became a bitter battleground during the Third War when the Warsong Clan began felling its sacred timber. The conflict unleashed demonic corruption when the orcs drank Mannoroth's blood nearby. Following the Legion's defeat, the woods never found peace; the Warsong entrenched themselves permanently at their lumber camp, sparking constant skirmishes with the Silverwing Sentinels that continue to tear the forest apart.",al={"history of nightsong woods","nightsong woods lore","nightsong woods history"},it="history",add="93727362"},{q="Is Nightsong Woods dangerous?",a="It is arguably the most perilous stretch of Ashenvale. Beyond the constant clashes between the Horde's Warsong outriders and the Alliance's Silverwing Sentinels, corrupt satyrs dwell in strongholds like Satyrnaar and Xavian. Farther east, lingering demonic remnants patrol Felfire Hill and Demon Fall Canyon. Any traveler caught between these warring fronts risks ambush from either faction or destruction at the hands of the Legion's lingering minions.",al={"how dangerous is nightsong woods","dangers of nightsong woods","is nightsong woods safe"},it="danger",add="74998be0"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you face a sacred borderland under siege. Defending its ancient groves from Warsong axes and purging lingering satyr corruption are matters of duty for the Kaldorei.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure vital building timber and strategic supply lanes through Splintertree Post. Sentinel ambushes and demonic beasts threaten this eastern front."},kw={"ashenvale","falfarren river","nightsong woods","satyrnaar","silverwing sentinels","splintertree post","warsong lumber camp"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:silverwing-grove","subzone:warsong-lumber-camp","subzone:falfarren-river","subzone:raynewood-retreat","subzone:satyrnaar","subzone:demon-fall-canyon"},src={"Nightsong Woods"}}
E["subzone:raynewood-retreat"] = {t="subzone",n="Raynewood Retreat",z="ashenvale",s="Raynewood Retreat watches the northern approaches to Felwood from a great tree in Ashenvale. Dryads and Cenarion protectors guard the outpost, where Keeper Ordanus makes his home.",h="Raynewood Retreat watches the northern approaches to Felwood from a great tree in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Bastion of the Great Tree",b="At Raynewood Retreat, the great tree rises between Shael'dryn's moonwell and the satyr-infested ruins of Night Run. Cenarion Protectors, faerie dragons, and Laughing Sisters guard the outpost. Their watch turns north, toward the taint spreading from Felwood.",sp=0},{t="The Hunt for Ordanus",b="Keeper Ordanus lives high among the great tree's boughs, one of Cenarius's eldest sons. The canopy shelters him, yet it has drawn the attention of dark forces. Agents tied to the Shadow Council's remnants, including Braelyn Firehand, seek his death. Horde mercenaries are sent to storm the heights and claim his head, bringing battle to the forest sanctuary.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Raynewood Retreat?",a="Raynewood Retreat watches the approaches to Felwood from a night elf and Cenarion settlement around a Great Tree in north-central Ashenvale. The Alliance-aligned outpost guards the northern passes.",al={"raynewood retreat","what is this place","raynewood tree"},it="place"},{q="Who lives at Raynewood Retreat?",a="Cenarion Protectors, Laughing Sisters, and faerie dragons defend Raynewood Retreat. Keeper Ordanus lives high in the great tree.",al={"who is here","raynewood mobs","who guards raynewood"},it="residents"},{q="Who is Keeper Ordanus?",a="Keeper Ordanus is a keeper of the grove and one of Cenarius's eldest sons. He oversees the sanctuary.",al={"keeper ordanus","who is ordanus","ordanus lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Horde attack Raynewood Retreat?",a="Braelyn Firehand hires Horde adventurers to enter the tree and seek Keeper Ordanus. Her motives and allegiances come to light through the events there.",al={"horde raynewood quest","why kill ordanus","braelyn firehand quest"},it="conflict"},{q="Is Raynewood Retreat dangerous?",a="It depends heavily on who you serve. Raynewood Retreat is a fortified Alliance settlement held by the night elves and children of Cenarius, meaning Alliance travelers find a welcoming and guarded haven. For members of the Horde, however, the outpost is fiercely hostile. Cenarion Protectors, Laughing Sisters, and faerie dragons aggressively defend the grove and their keeper against any intruders.",al={"raynewood retreat dangerous","is raynewood retreat hostile","threats at raynewood"},it="danger",add="2822434d"},{q="Why is it called Raynewood Retreat?",a="The retreat takes its name directly from Raynewood itself, the ancient Great Tree around which the entire settlement is built. High within the boughs of this colossal tree, Keeper Ordanus has made his sanctuary and watches over the sacred forests of Ashenvale.",al={"why raynewood retreat","raynewood name origin","who was raynewood"},it="name",add="16c0d3c5"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you find holy ground at Raynewood Retreat, under the care of Cenarius's children. The grove guards against demonic and fel corruption.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face an Alliance-friendly grove at Raynewood Retreat. Its guardian, Keeper Ordanus, is marked for elimination by covert employers."},kw={"ashenvale","braelyn","cenarius","felwood","laughing sister","ordanus","raynewood","retreat"},rel={"npc:braelyn-firehand","quest:1088","topic:cenarius","topic:satyr","zone:ashenvale","zone:felwood","subzone:night-run","npc:shael-dryn"},src={"Raynewood Retreat"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-ordil-aran"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Ordil'Aran",z="ashenvale",s="In northwestern Ashenvale, the Ruins of Ordil'Aran lie between Maestra's Post and Bathran's Haunt. Thistlefur furbolgs have overrun the ancient night elf settlement, once a hidden refuge for shadow cultists.",h="In northwestern Ashenvale, the Ruins of Ordil'Aran lie between Maestra's Post and Bathran's Haunt.",sec={{t="A Contested Ruin",b="Weathered pillars and cracked arches are all that remain of Ordil'Aran's Kaldorei buildings. The Cult of the Dark Strand once hid among the stones, ambushing travelers on Ashenvale's northwestern paths. Recently, Thistlefur furbolgs drove the cultists out in a bloody takeover. Fallen Dark Strand practitioners still litter the ground, while the furbolgs patrol the perimeter and guard the ancient Heartswood tree within the ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Ordil'Aran originally?",a="Ordil'Aran began as an ancient night elf settlement before the Great Sundering. Like many Kaldorei outposts across Ashenvale, it decayed over millennia, leaving overgrown arches and crumbling masonry.",al={"ordilaran history","what is ordil aran","who built ordil'aran"},it="origin"},{q="Why are there dead cultists lying around the ruins?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand used the ruins as a base until Thistlefur furbolgs attacked and drove them out. Slain cultists remain strewn across the site.",al={"dead cultists","dark strand corpses","why are cultists dead here"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Heartswood?",a="The Heartswood is an ancient tree growing within the Ruins of Ordil'Aran. Its branches and wood are sought for their potent magical and natural properties.",al={"heartswood tree","heartswood quest","heartswood ordil'aran"},it="item"},{q="Who currently controls the ruins?",a="Thistlefur furbolgs occupy the ruins now. They killed or drove out the Dark Strand cultists who lived there before.",al={"who lives here","who is at ordil aran","ordilaran mobs"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Ruins of Ordil'Aran?",a="The Ruins of Ordil'Aran are the remnants of an ancient night elven settlement in northwestern Ashenvale, situated just north of Maestra's Post and south of Bathran's Haunt. Once a flourishing city, little now remains aside from crumbling stone pillars, overgrown stonework, and the mystical Heartswood tree rising within its grounds.",al={"what is ruins of ordil'aran","ordil'aran lore","ruins of ordilaran"},it="place",add="39060ab5"},{q="What happened at the Ruins of Ordil'Aran?",a="After the ancient night elven city fell to ruin millennia ago, the secluded site became a haven for the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand. However, violent conflict recently erupted when aggressive furbolgs of the Thistlefur tribe invaded, slaughtering the cultists and taking over the broken grounds for themselves.",al={"ordil'aran history","what happened at ordil'aran","ruins of ordilaran past"},it="history",add="c163d8f1"},{q="Is the Ruins of Ordil'Aran dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely perilous. The Thistlefur furbolgs who recently seized the ruins are fiercely hostile to all outsiders, violently attacking anyone who approaches. Furthermore, lingering dark magic and remnants of the dark cult make wandering near these ancient stones a lethal prospect.",al={"is ordil'aran dangerous","threats in ordil'aran","ordilaran danger"},it="danger",add="511b2ee8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the ruins defiled by corrupt furbolgs and dark cultists.",["faction:Alliance"]="Just north of Maestra's Post, Ordil'Aran's aggressive occupants threaten Alliance scouts and travelers heading toward Darkshore."},kw={"ashenvale","cult of the dark strand","heartswood","maestra's post","ordil'aran","ordilaran","ruins","thistlefur"},rel={"subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:bathran-s-haunt","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:1738","quest:965","zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ruins of Ordil'Aran"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-stardust"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Stardust",z="ashenvale",s="On an island south of Astranaar, the Ruins of Stardust lie under Felwood's spreading corruption. Bog beasts prowl the fallen sanctuary, but stardust shrubs still grow among its stones with healing power.",h="On an island south of Astranaar, the Ruins of Stardust lie under Felwood's spreading corruption.",sec={{t="A Blighted Sanctuary",b="South of Astranaar, you find the Ruins of Stardust on a solitary island. The night elves once held this holy place in reverence. Now a sickly yellow-green hue clouds the water, stained by demonic rot draining south from Felwood, as at nearby Iris Lake. Local plant life has twisted into hostile bog beasts. They prowl the fallen masonry, their temperaments warped by the tainted lake.",sp=0},{t="The Enduring Stardust",b="Stardust shrubs still bloom among the ruins, untouched by the corruption in the soil and along the shore. Their leaves and blossoms can cleanse and heal. Shamans, herbalists, and local night elf defenders seek them for remedies against Ashenvale's encroaching decay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What were the Ruins of Stardust originally used for?",a="The night elves once tended the Ruins of Stardust as sacred holy ground. Its marble pillars and lakeside perch offered a tranquil place of reverence before demonic corruption took root in the forest.",al={"what are the ruins","stardust lore","who built stardust"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the water around the island discolored?",a="Demonic corruption flows from Felwood's blighted peaks into Ashenvale's waterways and taints the lake. The water turns murky yellow-green, disturbing its natural balance.",al={"why is water green","why is the lake corrupted","stardust water"}},{q="What makes the stardust shrubs special?",a="Stardust shrubs remain pure in soil soaked by demonic runoff. They resist the surrounding taint and can restore and heal, making them valuable in cleansing rituals.",al={"what is stardust shrub","stardust plant","stardust bushes"},it="power"},{q="What creatures wander the ruins?",a="Large, corrupted bog beasts wander the island. The tainted water has warped these nature elementals from peaceful forest guardians into aggressive threats that lumber through the shallows.",al={"stardust mobs","what monsters are here","bog beasts"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Ruins of Stardust?",a="The Ruins of Stardust sit on an island in a quiet lake in southwestern Ashenvale, south of Astranaar and west of the Talondeep Path. Once an ancient, sacred night elf sanctuary, it now stands decaying amidst waters tainted with demonic corruption flowing from Felwood. Despite the creeping rot and ruined masonry, resilient stardust shrubs still thrive across the ground.",al={"what is ruins of stardust","ruins of stardust lore","about ruins of stardust"},it="place",add="dd3713f4"},{q="What happened to the Ruins of Stardust?",a="Originally consecrated as a holy site by the night elves, the island eventually fell into abandonment as millennia passed. When demonic corruption seeped southward from Felwood during the Third War, the foul rot seeped into the surrounding waters, sickening the island and mutating its local wildlife into aggressive bog beasts.",al={"history of ruins of stardust","what happened at ruins of stardust","why is ruins of stardust corrupted"},it="history",add="7e5a1a00"},{q="Is the Ruins of Stardust dangerous?",a="Yes. The surrounding waters have been warped by demonic rot into a sickly yellow-green, and large, aggressive bog beasts roam the island and shores. You will have to fight through these corrupted creatures if you hope to reach the ruins or gather the healing stardust shrubs that grow there.",al={"ruins of stardust danger","is it safe at ruins of stardust","ruins of stardust threats"},it="danger",add="74a8e036"},{q="Why is it called the Ruins of Stardust?",a="The ruins take their name from the unique stardust shrubs that grow among the shattered stones. While the island's soil and waters have fallen to demonic rot, these radiant plants remain completely unmarred by the corruption, holding powerful healing properties within their leaves.",al={"why ruins of stardust","name ruins of stardust","stardust name origin"},it="name",add="68167cf8"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can use uncorrupted stardust as a cleansing reagent in spiritual trials, including the Call of Water trials to master the restorative elements.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see a former sanctuary falling to Felwood's slow, putrid runoff. Its fate reminds you of the struggle to protect Ashenvale from enduring demonic corruption."},kw={"ashenvale","bog beasts","felwood taint","night elf ruins","ruins of stardust","stardust shrubs","water corruption"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","quest:63","quest:1034","subzone:iris-lake","zone:felwood","subzone:astranaar","subzone:talondeep-path"},src={"Ruins of Stardust"}}
E["subzone:satyrnaar"] = {t="subzone",n="Satyrnaar",z="ashenvale",s="Satyrnaar lies in ruin under the Bleakheart satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale. The ancient night elf settlement sits beside the road from Splintertree Post toward Azshara, intact enough to be one of the forest’s easiest satyr strongholds to reach.",h="Satyrnaar lies in ruin under the Bleakheart satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Den of Fel and Shadow",b="You find Satyrnaar northeast of Splintertree Post and southwest of Forest Song, among Ashenvale’s three chief satyr settlements with Xavian and Night Run. Its elven buildings remain more intact than those deep in the wilderness, though tents now stand among the broken stone. The Bleakheart satyrs occupy the camp, making the trade road east toward Azshara dangerous for travelers. They have also allied with the Cult of the Dark Strand, whose soulgem lies among the corrupted stones.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Satyrnaar?",a="Satyrnaar lies in ruin in northeastern Ashenvale, occupied by the Bleakheart satyrs. It is one of their chief strongholds in the forest.",al={"satyrnaar overview","what is this place","satyr camp"},it="place"},{q="Who lives in Satyrnaar?",a="The Bleakheart satyrs occupy Satyrnaar, with tents among the ancient ruins. They are allied with the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"who is here","satyrnaar mobs","bleakheart satyrs"},it="residents"},{q="Why is Satyrnaar significant compared to other satyr ruins?",a="Satyrnaar, Night Run, and Xavian are Ashenvale’s three chief satyr settlements. Satyrnaar is the most intact and lies beside the road toward Azshara.",al={"satyrnaar vs xavian","why satyrnaar"}},{q="What is the dark artifact hidden in Satyrnaar?",a="A soulgem of the Cult of the Dark Strand lies in Satyrnaar. The mortal shadow cult is allied with the Bleakheart satyrs.",al={"dark strand soulgem","satyrnaar crystal","soulgem"},it="item"},{q="Is Satyrnaar dangerous?",a="Satyrnaar is extremely perilous for travelers passing through northeastern Ashenvale. Nestled just off the main road between Splintertree Post and Azshara, it is inhabited by the vicious Bleakheart satyr, allied with the Cult of the Dark Strand. Because of its accessible, central location, it is the most contested and violently defended of all satyr holdings in the forest. Trespassers risk facing fel magic, ambushes, and sinister shadow rituals centered around corrupted soulgems.",al={"is satyrnaar safe","how dangerous is satyrnaar","satyrnaar threat"},it="danger",add="2ba518f9"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, seeing ancestral stonework defiled by fel corruption and occupied by the cursed remnants of the Highborne is a bitter sight in Ashenvale.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see how the Bleakheart satyrs’ fel corruption chokes Ashenvale’s natural spirit, calling for swift cleansing."},kw={"ashenvale","bleakheart","dark strand","forest song","satyr","satyrnaar","soulgem","splintertree"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","topic:satyr","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:forest-song","subzone:night-run","subzone:xavian","zone:azshara"},src={"Satyrnaar"}}
E["subzone:shrine-of-aessina"] = {t="subzone",n="Shrine of Aessina",z="ashenvale",s="At the Shrine of Aessina, night elves honor an ancient spirit of nature and wild creatures. The sacred place lies in southwestern Ashenvale, between Maestra's Post and Astranaar, amid growing border friction.",h="At the Shrine of Aessina, night elves honor an ancient spirit of nature and wild creatures.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary of the Deep Woods",b="West of Astranaar, the Shrine of Aessina honors a Wild God who embodies the heart and spirit of the deep forests. For generations, night elves and their woodland kin have revered this quiet place and communed with nature away from the main roads. The Horde is pushing into Ashenvale to gather timber and establish footholds, and sacred grounds across the territory face an uncertain peace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Aessina?",a="Aessina is an ancient nature spirit and Wild God associated with the heart of pristine forests. Night elves and woodland beings honor her as nature's living soul, embodying the untamed wilderness.",al={"aessina lore","who is aessina","shrine of aessina goddess"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Shrine of Aessina located?",a="The shrine lies in southwestern Ashenvale, southwest of Maestra's Post and west of Astranaar.",al={"shrine of aessina location","where is shrine of aessina","find shrine of aessina"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this place significant to the night elves?",a="Night elves honor the shrine as an ancient holy retreat dedicated to woodland spirits. It connects their society and druidic traditions directly to Kalimdor's untamed wilderness.",al={"importance of aessina shrine","night elf sacred site"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Shrine of Aessina?",a="The Shrine of Aessina is a sacred ancient woodland sanctuary nestled in southwestern Ashenvale, situated southwest of Maestra's Post and west of Astranaar. Dedicated to the mysterious forest spirit and Wild God Aessina, the shrine stands as a serene, mystical haven surrounded by the deep wilderness, reflecting the ancient bond between the night elves and the living soul of Kalimdor's forests.",al={"what is shrine of aessina","shrine of aessina lore","about shrine of aessina"},it="place",add="a3085ee2"},{q="Why is it called the Shrine of Aessina?",a="The shrine takes its name from Aessina, an elusive Wild God deeply revered by night elf druids and the denizens of the woods. Described in ancient lore as the beating heart of the deep forest, her presence is said to imbue Kalimdor's densest woodlands with vitality and quiet mystery, making this secluded grove a natural place for her veneration.",al={"why is it called shrine of aessina","shrine of aessina name origin"},it="name",add="d41b0789"},{q="Is the Shrine of Aessina dangerous?",a="The shrine itself is a tranquil natural glade, but Ashenvale as a whole is fraught with peril. Between the creeping corruption spreading through parts of the enchanted forest and violent territorial skirmishes erupting between the Warsong Clan and night elf sentinels, wandering the deep woods alone always carries significant danger.",al={"is shrine of aessina dangerous","danger at shrine of aessina","threats near shrine of aessina"},it="danger",add="5764d345"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid devoted to preserving Kalimdor's natural balance, you honor the living spirit of the wild woods at this ancient shrine.",["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the shrine represents centuries of harmony with Ashenvale's native spirits, now threatened by encroaching outside forces."},kw={"aessina","ashenvale","astranaar","kaldorei","maestra's post","nature shrine","shrine of aessina","wild god"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:astranaar","subzone:maestra-s-post","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Shrine of Aessina"}}
E["subzone:silverwind-refuge"] = {t="subzone",n="Silverwind Refuge",z="ashenvale",s="Silverwind Refuge shelters travelers in south-central Ashenvale, just north of Mystral Lake. Sentinels guard this night elven settlement along the forest trails.",h="Silverwind Refuge shelters travelers in south-central Ashenvale, just north of Mystral Lake.",sec={{t="A Forest Sanctuary",b="Silverwind Refuge rests between Mystral Lake and Iris Lake, to the north. Alongside Astranaar, it is one of central Ashenvale’s major night elven waystations. Craftsmen and wilderness trainers teach herbalism, alchemy, skinning, and hunting. Sentinels guard the refuge, where allies traveling through the ancient woods can rest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Silverwind Refuge?",a="The night elves built and maintain Silverwind Refuge as an Alliance settlement. Sentinels guard its grounds.",al={"who owns silverwind refuge","is silverwind alliance or horde","who lives at silverwind"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where is Silverwind Refuge located?",a="Silverwind Refuge lies in south-central Ashenvale, directly north of Mystral Lake and south of Iris Lake.",al={"silverwind refuge location","where is silverwind refuge","how to get to silverwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services are found at the refuge?",a="Travelers can find trade supply vendors and trainers who teach herbalism, alchemy, skinning, and hunter skills.",al={"what is at silverwind refuge","silverwind refuge trainers","silverwind vendors"},gp=true},{q="What is Silverwind Refuge?",a="Silverwind Refuge is a peaceful night elven outpost nestled in south-central Ashenvale, situated just north of Mystral Lake. Alongside Astranaar, it serves as one of the Alliance's key settlements in the region, boasting craftsmen and trainers under the watchful protection of the Sentinels.",al={"what is silverwind refuge","silverwind refuge lore","silverwind outpost"},it="place",add="18c4c00c"},{q="Who lives in or runs Silverwind Refuge?",a="The refuge is home to night elven tradesfolk and hunters, guarded faithfully by Astranaar Sentinels. Herbalists, alchemists, skinners, and beast tamers dwell here peacefully, tending to travelers journeying through the ancient woods.",al={"who lives at silverwind refuge","silverwind refuge inhabitants","who is at silverwind refuge"},it="residents",add="86e68a41"},{q="Is Silverwind Refuge dangerous?",a="For members of the Alliance, Silverwind Refuge is a safe sanctuary equipped with vigilant Sentinel protectors. For Horde interlopers, however, the guards will aggressively attack on sight to keep the forest haven secure.",al={"is silverwind refuge safe","silverwind refuge danger","is silverwind safe"},it="danger",add="099e4cfb"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler crossing Ashenvale, you can rest at Silverwind Refuge, restock supplies, and improve your wilderness trades without going all the way to Astranaar.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can train at Silverwind Refuge, a useful stop amid the flora around Mystral Lake."},kw={"ashenvale","iris lake","mystral lake","night elf","sentinels","silverwind refuge"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:mystral-lake","subzone:iris-lake","subzone:astranaar","topic:sentinels"},src={"Silverwind Refuge"}}
E["subzone:silverwing-grove"] = {t="subzone",n="Silverwing Grove",z="ashenvale",s="Silverwing Sentinels gather at Silverwing Grove in south-central Ashenvale, near Fallen Sky Lake. From this fortified hollow, night elf warriors muster Alliance forces against the Warsong Clan loggers cutting through the forest.",h="Silverwing Sentinels gather at Silverwing Grove in south-central Ashenvale, near Fallen Sky Lake.",sec={{t="Front Line of the Forest War",b="At Silverwing Grove, Silverwing Sentinels gather beneath the canopy southwest of Silverwing Outpost. The night elves use the post to oppose the Horde's lumbering in Warsong Gulch. Alliance officers, provisions, and scouts assemble here to organize skirmishes and muster champions. They defend Ashenvale against orcish expansion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Silverwing Grove?",a="Silverwing Grove is where the Silverwing Sentinels and their Alliance allies gather to oppose the Warsong Clan's logging and join the fighting in Warsong Gulch.",al={"why is silverwing grove here","what is silverwing grove","purpose of silverwing grove"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Silverwing Grove located?",a="Silverwing Grove lies in south-central Ashenvale, southwest of Silverwing Outpost and just west of Fallen Sky Lake.",al={"silverwing grove location","where is silverwing grove","how to find silverwing grove"},gp=true},{q="Who operates out of Silverwing Grove?",a="Silverwing Sentinels and Alliance forces operate from the grove. Among them are an Alliance Brigadier General, logistical vendors, and officers such as Sentinel Farsong, who coordinates efforts against the Horde.",al={"who is at silverwing grove","silverwing grove npcs","who runs silverwing grove"},it="residents"},{q="Can Horde players enter Silverwing Grove?",a="No. Hostile Alliance sentinels and guards at the grove attack Horde members who approach.",al={"is silverwing grove hostile","can horde go to silverwing grove","horde silverwing grove"},gp=true},{q="What is Silverwing Grove?",a="Silverwing Grove is a fortified night elf enclave nestled in south-central Ashenvale, serving as the main forward base for the Silverwing Sentinels. From this shaded redoubt, the Sentinels organize Alliance forces and coordinate their ongoing battle against the Warsong Outriders in the neighboring Warsong Gulch.",al={"what is silverwing grove","silverwing grove lore","about silverwing grove"},it="place",add="92f0e5de"},{q="Is Silverwing Grove dangerous?",a="For Alliance champions, the grove is a heavily guarded refuge, protected by seasoned Sentinels and command officers. For Horde trespassers, however, it is deadly ground. As the primary staging ground for the conflict against the Warsong Clan, the grove's defenders strike down any Horde intruders on sight.",al={"is silverwing grove safe","silverwing grove danger","threats to silverwing grove"},it="danger",add="e4f50e36"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Silverwing Grove is a rallying place in their effort to stop the Warsong Clan from cutting down sacred trees.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance champions gather at the grove before entering the bloody skirmishes of Warsong Gulch."},kw={"ashenvale","fallen sky lake","sentinel farsong","silverwing grove","silverwing sentinels","warsong gulch"},rel={"subzone:silverwing-outpost","topic:sentinels","npc:sentinel-farsong","quest:1035","zone:ashenvale","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Silverwing Grove"}}
E["subzone:silverwing-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Silverwing Outpost",z="ashenvale",s="Silverwing Outpost guards the eastern bank of the Falfarren River in south-central Ashenvale. Duriel Moonfire commands the garrison, the Alliance's easternmost hold against the Horde in the contested woodland.",h="Silverwing Outpost guards the eastern bank of the Falfarren River in south-central Ashenvale.",sec={{t="East of the Falfarren",b="Silverwing Outpost lies southwest of Splintertree Post and just north of the Barrens border. Its place on the eastern bank of the Falfarren River puts it in territory the Horde contests and patrols. From here, the garrison shields night elf holdings deeper in the forest. Duriel Moonfire and her Silverwing Sentinels face constant attacks from nearby orcs seeking to drive night elf forces from the area.",sp=0},{t="The Constant Front",b="Fierce skirmishes rage around Silverwing Outpost. Orcish war parties from Splintertree Post, including raiders led by Torek, ambush the garrison at its walls. The Horde seeks to neutralize the outpost, secure the road, and expand its resource operations without Sentinel counterattacks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Silverwing Outpost located?",a="Silverwing Outpost stands in south-central Ashenvale, southwest of Splintertree Post, north of the Barrens border, and east of the Falfarren River.",al={"silverwing location","where is silverwing","silverwing outpost map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who commands Silverwing Outpost?",a="Duriel Moonfire commands Silverwing Outpost and leads the Silverwing Sentinels defending the forest's eastern reaches.",al={"silverwing leader","who leads silverwing outpost","duriel moonfire"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does the Horde target this outpost so aggressively?",a="Silverwing Outpost stands east of the Falfarren River near Splintertree Post. The Silverwing Sentinels there can cut off Horde supply lines and threaten orcish operations in Ashenvale.",al={"why attack silverwing","horde interest in silverwing","splintertree vs silverwing"},it="conflict"},{q="Who are the Silverwing Sentinels?",a="The Silverwing Sentinels are night elf warriors and huntresses who protect Ashenvale from incursions, especially Horde lumber camps and war parties.",al={"what are silverwings","silverwing sentinels lore","silverwing faction"},it="people"},{q="What is Silverwing Outpost?",a="Silverwing Outpost is the easternmost Alliance military stronghold in Ashenvale, built to defend night elf lands against the Horde. Situated across the Falfarren River southwest of Splintertree Post, it serves as a critical front-line garrison where the Silverwing Sentinels contest the Horde's expansion out of the Barrens and Warsong Lumber Camp.",al={"what is silverwing outpost","silverwing outpost purpose","about silverwing outpost"},it="place",add="478d573a"},{q="Is Silverwing Outpost dangerous?",a="It is an active combat zone. Because the outpost sits isolated on the eastern side of the Falfarren River, it faces relentless assaults from nearby Warsong orcs and raiding parties from Splintertree Post. Alliance travelers find refuge and armed defenders behind its walls, but Horde forces will find vigilant, hostile sentinels ready to shoot on sight.",al={"is silverwing outpost dangerous","silverwing outpost threats","dangers at silverwing outpost"},it="danger",add="ad619a65"},{q="Why is it called Silverwing Outpost?",a="The garrison takes its name directly from the Silverwing Sentinels, the elite night elf military force stationed here to safeguard Ashenvale and check the Horde's lumber-harvesting encroachments.",al={"why is it called silverwing outpost","silverwing outpost name origin","silverwing meaning"},it="name",add="b348ef17"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Silverwing Outpost is your forward stronghold east of the river, checking orc expansion from Splintertree Post.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Silverwing Outpost obstructs movements and supply lines through southern Ashenvale from Splintertree Post."},kw={"ashenvale","duriel moonfire","falfarren river","silverwing outpost","silverwing sentinels","splintertree post","torek"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:falfarren-river","quest:6544","topic:sentinels","topic:horde","topic:alliance","zone:barrens"},src={"Silverwing Outpost"}}
E["subzone:splintertree-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Splintertree Post",z="ashenvale",s="Splintertree Post holds the Horde’s eastern Ashenvale frontier, northwest of Felfire Hill. Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan established it during the Third War as a fortified base against the night elves and a staging ground for expansion.",h="Splintertree Post holds the Horde’s eastern Ashenvale frontier, northwest of Felfire Hill.",sec={{t="A Frontier Stronghold",b="Splintertree Post anchors the Horde’s military and supply lines across eastern Ashenvale. Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan founded it when the orcs first entered the forest during the Third War. Orcish and tauren scouts and warriors still defend the armed outpost. An inn, a flight master, and steady supplies from Orgrimmar support the Horde’s contested hold beneath the trees.",sp=0},{t="The Constant Threat of Retaliation",b="Splintertree Post remains ready for attack. The night elves have neither forgotten nor forgiven Grommash’s actions during the war. They also oppose the Horde’s continued logging and raids on Astranaar. Sentinels hide in the surrounding woods and launch constant retaliatory guerrilla strikes, testing the post’s watchmen at all hours.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who founded Splintertree Post?",a="Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan established Splintertree Post when the orcs first pushed into Ashenvale during the Third War to gather timber and secure a foothold.",al={"who built splintertree","splintertree founder","grom splintertree"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the night elves frequently attack this base?",a="The night elves regard Splintertree Post as an illegal, desecrating intrusion on their ancestral lands. Their hostility also stems from Grommash’s brutal campaigns during the Third War, continued Horde logging, and skirmishes against Astranaar.",al={"why are elves attacking","splintertree sentinel attacks","night elf raids splintertree"},it="conflict"},{q="What amenities and travel options are available here?",a="Splintertree Post has an inn, stable master, mailbox, armor repair, and a wind rider flight master. Its routes connect to Orgrimmar, the Crossroads, and other Horde outposts across Kalimdor.",al={"splintertree flight path","splintertree services","splintertree inn"},gp=true},{q="Who currently makes up the garrison at Splintertree?",a="Orcs and tauren make up most of Splintertree Post’s garrison. They serve as seasoned scouts, sentries, and frontline officers charged with holding the frontier.",al={"splintertree guards","who lives in splintertree","splintertree races"},it="residents"},{q="What is Splintertree Post?",a="Splintertree Post is a fortified Horde stronghold nestled in eastern Ashenvale, just northwest of Felfire Hill. Established primarily as a military base and staging ground, it anchors the Horde's presence along the forest road. Within its timber palisades, scouts, warriors, and supply handlers gather to reinforce the Horde's territorial foothold, offering weary travelers a vital sanctuary of warmth, repairs, and wind rider transport amidst a hostile and contested woodland.",al={"what is splintertree","splintertree post purpose","splintertree camp"},it="place",add="1c750cca"},{q="What is the history of Splintertree Post?",a="Splintertree Post was originally carved out of the wilderness by Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan during the Third War, when the orcs first ventured into Ashenvale to harvest its massive timber. In the years following the conflict, the camp evolved from a rugged war-camp into a permanent Horde outpost, continually caught in bitter skirmishes against night elf defenders furious over orcish incursions into their sacred woods.",al={"splintertree history","splintertree past","what happened at splintertree"},it="history",add="1352f983"},{q="Is Splintertree Post dangerous?",a="For champions of the Horde, the post provides a safe refuge behind sturdy wooden barricades. However, the surrounding forest is treacherous. Night elf sentinels launch frequent, deadly retaliatory raids against the outpost in response to nearby skirmishes, while corrupted wild beasts and demonic remnants lingering near Felfire Hill pose an ever-present peril just beyond the stockade walls.",al={"is splintertree post safe","splintertree danger","threats to splintertree"},it="danger",add="e71555e8"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde adventurers pressing through Ashenvale, Splintertree Post offers repairs, rest, and vital flight routes across Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="To night elves, Splintertree Post scars Ashenvale. Grommash, the warlord who struck down Cenarius, founded it, and its people continue to butcher their ancient trees."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","felfire hill","grommash hellscream","splintertree post","vhulgra","warsong clan"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","topic:warsong-clan","topic:grommash-hellscream","subzone:astranaar","subzone:felfire-hill","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","topic:third-war"},src={"Splintertree Post"}}
E["subzone:talondeep-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Talondeep Vale",z="ashenvale",s="In south-central Ashenvale, Talondeep Vale lies between familiar landmarks and the road to the mountains.",h="In south-central Ashenvale, Talondeep Vale lies between familiar landmarks and the road to the mountains.",sec={{t="A Sheltered Valley",b="Talondeep Vale lies beneath the trees of south-central Ashenvale. Silverwind Refuge stands to the east, and the Ruins of Stardust lie nearby. To the south, the land rises toward the Stonetalon Mountains. Travelers cross this wooded valley between the heart of Ashenvale and the high crags beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Talondeep Vale located?",a="Talondeep Vale lies in south-central Ashenvale, between Silverwind Refuge, the Ruins of Stardust, and the southern pass into the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"where is talondeep vale","talondeep vale location","how to find talondeep vale"},it="place"},{q="Where does the path leading south through the vale go?",a="The trail through Talondeep Vale leads to Talondeep Path, which climbs through the rugged heights connecting Ashenvale’s woodlands with the arid peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"path south talondeep vale","where does talondeep pass lead","road to stonetalon"},it="place"},{q="What nearby landmarks should travelers watch for?",a="Silverwind Refuge lies to the east, and the Ruins of Stardust stand nearby beneath the trees.",al={"landmarks near talondeep vale","what is near talondeep vale"},it="place"},{q="What is Talondeep Vale?",a="Talondeep Vale is a quiet, heavily forested valley tucked into southern Ashenvale. Nestled between Silverwind Refuge and the ancient Ruins of Stardust, it serves as the verdant approach to Talondeep Path, the tunnel that leads through the southern mountains toward the Stonetalon realm.",al={"what is talondeep vale","talondeep vale info","about talondeep vale"},it="place",add="5eca3f30"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the paths near Mystral Lake and the Ruins of Stardust, familiar ground in southern Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","ruins of stardust","silverwind refuge","talondeep pass","talondeep path","talondeep vale"},rel={"subzone:talondeep-path","subzone:silverwind-refuge","subzone:ruins-of-stardust","zone:ashenvale","quest:1034"},src={"Talondeep Vale"}}
E["subzone:thistlefur-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Thistlefur Hold",z="ashenvale",s="Corruption has turned the furbolgs of Thistlefur Hold against every outsider who draws near. Their cavern den lies at the northern end of Thistlefur Village in west-central Ashenvale.",h="Corruption has turned the furbolgs of Thistlefur Hold against every outsider who draws near.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Den",b="Thistlefur Hold lies at the northern end of Thistlefur Village, at the heart of the Thistlefur tribe's territory. Corruption has driven its furbolgs mad, and they attack travelers and neighbors who draw near. In the winding caverns, the tribe hoards scavenged relics, including troll charms sought by the Darkspear. Captives are kept in wooden cages deep within, among them Ruul Snowhoof, a tauren brave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Thistlefur Hold?",a="Thistlefur Hold lies beneath the northern end of Thistlefur Village in west-central Ashenvale. Its caverns hold the greatest number of hostile Thistlefur furbolgs.",al={"thistlefur hold info","what is this cave","thistlefur cave"},it="place"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Thistlefur Hold hostile?",a="Corruption has twisted the minds of the Thistlefur furbolgs and driven them to attack outsiders.",al={"why are thistlefur mad","thistlefur corruption","why are furbolgs attacking"},it="hostile"},{q="Who is trapped inside the hold?",a="Ruul Snowhoof, a tauren brave, is held in a wooden cage deep in the caverns. Horde champions seek to free him.",al={"thistlefur captive","tauren in thistlefur hold","who is ruul snowhoof"}},{q="Why is the Horde interested in Thistlefur Hold?",a="The Horde seeks to free the captured tauren Ruul Snowhoof and recover the troll charms the furbolgs have hoarded in the caverns.",al={"horde quests thistlefur","troll charms thistlefur"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened at Thistlefur Hold?",a="Once a peaceful enclave of furbolgs deep in Ashenvale, Thistlefur Hold fell into madness when corruption took hold of its inhabitants. Their gentle nature gave way to blind aggression, driving them to attack any outsiders who stray near their dens and turn their home into a hostile fortress.",al={"thistlefur hold history","what happened to thistlefur hold","history of thistlefur"},it="history",add="6573f817"},{q="Who lives in Thistlefur Hold?",a="The cavernous hold houses the main population of the Thistlefur furbolg tribe. Where they once lived harmoniously among Ashenvale's ancient forests, these corrupted furbolgs now fiercely guard their subterranean dens against all intruders, showing hostility to night elves, Horde wayfarers, and any others who cross their threshold.",al={"who lives in thistlefur hold","thistlefur hold inhabitants","who is in thistlefur hold"},it="residents",add="36b0fa4f"},{q="Is Thistlefur Hold dangerous?",a="Venturing inside is extremely hazardous. The caves are packed with enraged Thistlefur furbolgs who attack on sight, driven to frantic violence by corruption. Anyone trying to navigate its tight passages will find themselves swarmed by hostile shamans and warriors defending their corrupted stronghold.",al={"how dangerous is thistlefur hold","is thistlefur dangerous","thistlefur hold threats"},it="danger",add="77184072"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face two aims in Thistlefur Hold: free Ruul Snowhoof and recover the troll charms the furbolgs have hoarded.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the Thistlefur furbolgs' corruption and madness as a tragedy. Their fall shows how nature's guardians in Ashenvale can be corrupted."},kw={"ashenvale","furbolg","remulos","ruul snowhoof","thistlefur hold","thistlefur village","troll charms"},rel={"subzone:thistlefur-village","zone:ashenvale","npc:ruul-snowhoof","topic:furbolg","npc:remulos","quest:6462","topic:horde","topic:troll"},src={"Thistlefur Hold"}}
E["subzone:thistlefur-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Thistlefur Village",z="ashenvale",s="Thistlefur furbolgs attack outsiders from their village north of Astranaar. The tribe has fallen to corruption and now threatens travelers who approach its dens.",h="Thistlefur furbolgs attack outsiders from their village north of Astranaar.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Den",b="North of Astranaar, Thistlefur Village lies among Ashenvale’s woodland communities. Corruption has taken hold of the Thistlefur tribe, leaving its furbolgs maddened and hostile. They guard the paths through their settlement and attack travelers who draw near. Two fierce chieftains, Dal Bloodclaw and Rorgish Jowl, lead the clan. Their aggression threatens those on the roads and in nearby settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Thistlefur Village located?",a="Thistlefur Village lies in west-central Ashenvale, in the woodland hills directly north of Astranaar.",al={"thistlefur village location","where is thistlefur","thistlefur map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the furbolgs here attacking travelers?",a="Corruption spreading through Ashenvale has driven the Thistlefur furbolgs mad. They see outsiders as enemies and attack anyone who approaches their territory.",al={"why are thistlefur hostile","corrupted furbolgs thistlefur","why attack"},it="hostile"},{q="Who leads the Thistlefur furbolgs?",a="Dal Bloodclaw and Rorgish Jowl lead the Thistlefur furbolgs as fierce warrior chieftains.",al={"thistlefur boss","thistlefur leaders","who leads thistlefur"},it="leader"},{q="Does Thistlefur Village pose a danger to Astranaar?",a="Yes. Thistlefur Village lies immediately north of Astranaar, and its aggressive furbolgs threaten night elf scouts, supply lines, and sentries along the central roads.",al={"thistlefur threat to astranaar","danger to astranaar"},it="threat"},{q="What is Thistlefur Village?",a="Thistlefur Village is a furbolg settlement nestled in west-central Ashenvale, situated directly north of Astranaar. It serves as the primary home and stronghold for the Thistlefur tribe, a population of furbolgs that has fallen prey to the dark corruption spreading through the forest.",al={"thistlefur village info","what is thistlefur","thistlefur village lore"},it="place",add="840d1e44"},{q="Is Thistlefur Village dangerous?",a="Thistlefur Village is exceptionally hazardous to any traveler. Driven to madness by corruption, the resident furbolgs are fiercely territorial and violently assault anyone who wanders near their borders. The village is well-defended by formidable warriors and shamans under the ruthless command of Dal Bloodclaw and Rorgish Jowl.",al={"how dangerous is thistlefur village","is thistlefur safe","thistlefur village danger"},it="danger",add="7a812bcb"},{q="Who lives in Thistlefur Village?",a="The village is populated entirely by the Thistlefur tribe of furbolgs. Once peaceful forest dwellers, these corrupted furbolgs now live under the brutal leadership of two ferocious chieftain figures, Dal Bloodclaw and Rorgish Jowl, who organize their defense and raids.",al={"who lives in thistlefur village","thistlefur inhabitants","who lives at thistlefur"},it="residents",add="fc97bd16"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For centuries, night elves lived in harmony with Ashenvale’s native furbolg tribes. The Thistlefur’s corruption so close to Astranaar brings heartbreak and a grave security crisis for the Sentinels.",["class:Druid"]="The Thistlefur tribe’s fall warns of the lingering taint afflicting Ashenvale’s spirits and wildlife. The Cenarion Circle must remain vigilant in cleansing it."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","corruption","dal bloodclaw","furbolg","rorgish jowl","thistlefur","village"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","subzone:astranaar"},src={"Thistlefur Village"}}
E["subzone:warsong-labor-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Warsong Labor Camp",z="ashenvale",s="Warsong Labor Camp cuts Ashenvale timber for the growing Horde. Its Warsong loggers and orcish sentries work in southeastern Ashenvale, far from help and under threat from the forest's defenders.",h="Warsong Labor Camp cuts Ashenvale timber for the growing Horde.",sec={{t="Timber for the Horde",b="East of Fallen Sky Lake and southwest of the Dor'Danil Barrow Den, Warsong loggers cut Ashenvale's dense timber. Durotar's dry plains offer little wood for building cities such as Orgrimmar, so the Warsong clan has pushed into these contested woods. Loggers and orcish guards work far from other Horde settlements, felling ancient trees while night elf scouts and Alliance warbands threaten the camp.",sp=0},{t="A Vulnerable Outpost",b="Warsong Labor Camp lies far from the main road and fortified bases such as Splintertree Post. Alliance raiders strike its working peons and watchmen, knowing help may be slow to arrive. Night elves see each felled tree as a desecration, and the camp remains a point of conflict in the war.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Warsong Labor Camp located?",a="Warsong Labor Camp lies in southeastern Ashenvale, east of Fallen Sky Lake and southwest of the Dor'Danil Barrow Den.",al={"warsong labor camp location","where is warsong labor camp","finding labor camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this camp?",a="Warsong loggers cut and process Ashenvale timber for buildings in Orgrimmar and other Durotar settlements.",al={"why are orcs here","what do they do here","warsong logging camp purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the camp frequently attacked?",a="The camp is isolated and far from major Horde fortifications. Night elves oppose the cutting of their sacred forests, and Alliance raiders strike because nearby guards cannot offer swift help.",al={"alliance attacks labor camp","why is it targeted","is the camp safe"},it="threat"},{q="Did Grommash Hellscream found this camp?",a="During the Third War, Warchief Thrall sent Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan into Ashenvale to harvest lumber. Warsong Labor Camp continues that work.",al={"did grom make this","grom hellscream labor camp","history of the camp"},it="history"},{q="What is the Warsong Labor Camp?",a="The Warsong Labor Camp is an active Horde logging outpost situated in southeastern Ashenvale, east of Fallen Sky Lake and southwest of the Dor'Danil Barrow Den. It serves as a frontline timber operation where laborers and mechanized harvesters fell the ancient trees of the forest to fuel the Horde's expansion, guarded continuously against local threats.",al={"what is warsong labor camp","warsong labor camp info","tell me about warsong labor camp"},it="place",add="f9ba0d17"},{q="Who lives in and runs the Warsong Labor Camp?",a="The camp is staffed by members of the Warsong clan, primarily comprised of orcish loggers, crews managing goblin-built shredders and harvesters, and stalwart guards stationed to keep watch over the perimeter and defend the lumber harvest.",al={"who runs warsong labor camp","warsong labor camp residents","who is at warsong labor camp"},it="residents",add="b37a2225"},{q="Is the Warsong Labor Camp dangerous?",a="It is quite perilous. Because the camp sits in relative isolation deep within Ashenvale, it is prone to surprise raids by Alliance forces and local sentinels who seek to wipe out the logging crews before reinforcements can arrive from larger Horde bases.",al={"is warsong labor camp dangerous","danger warsong labor camp","how dangerous is warsong labor camp"},it="danger",add="f04818dc"},{q="Why is it called the Warsong Labor Camp?",a="The outpost takes its name from the Warsong clan, the fierce orcish clan tasked by Warchief Thrall with harvesting timber throughout Ashenvale. As a dedicated logging worksite rather than a grand stronghold, it is simply designated as their labor camp.",al={"why is it called warsong labor camp","warsong labor camp name meaning","why warsong labor camp"},it="name",add="1e0e0990"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you depend on Ashenvale lumber to build and maintain Orgrimmar. The loggers work far from home in contested territory.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Warsong Labor Camp cutting into Ashenvale's ancestral groves to supply Durotar."},kw={"ashenvale","dor'danil","fallen sky lake","labor camp","loggers","lumber","timber","warsong"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","quest:1035","subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den","topic:grommash-hellscream","npc:thrall","topic:alliance"},src={"Warsong Labor Camp"}}
E["subzone:warsong-lumber-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Warsong Lumber Camp",z="ashenvale",s="Warsong Lumber Camp cuts timber from Ashenvale for the Horde, keeping its conflict with the night elves alive. Kargathia Keep anchors the fortified operation.",h="Warsong Lumber Camp cuts timber from Ashenvale for the Horde, keeping its conflict with the night elves alive.",sec={{t="Heart of the Harvest",b="Warsong Lumber Camp cuts into eastern Ashenvale's dense canopy for the Horde. Orc peons and hired goblin engineers use whirring shredders to turn towering trunks into lumber for nearby Splintertree Post and the fledgling nation of Durotar. Kargathia Keep's stockades anchor the defenses against night elf counterattacks, and the camp keeps war wolves in an active kennel. For the Warsong, each felled tree means survival and strength. For the native Sentinels, each saw blade is an act of sacrilege.",sp=0},{t="A Legacy of War",b="Warsong clan warriors first entered these woods with Grom Hellscream during the Third War, seeking timber for the Horde. Their clearing of the forest enraged the demigod Cenarius and drew the ancient wrath of the night elves. The camp now flies the banners of Thrall's Horde, but old hatreds still burn. Untamed timber, hostile elves, and demonic corruption around neighboring Felfire Hill surround the camp. Its defenders stay armed around the clock, axes in hand as they harvest, ready to abandon their timber when the next ambush comes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde logging in Ashenvale?",a="The Horde's lands, especially Durotar and the Barrens, are arid and sparse, with little timber for buildings, palisades, or war machinery. Ashenvale provides vast stores of wood for the survival and growth of outposts like Splintertree Post and the capital of Orgrimmar.",al={"why cut trees","warsong logging reasons","why does horde need wood"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Kargathia Keep?",a="Kargathia Keep anchors the Warsong Lumber Camp as its fortified stronghold. It provides barracks, strategic command, and a reinforced refuge where peons and overseers can hold off night elf ambushes or attacks by local wildlife.",al={"kargathia keep purpose","fort in lumber camp","warsong keep ashenvale"},it="place"},{q="Why are the night elves so hostile to this camp?",a="Night elves see Ashenvale as a sacred ancestral homeland, protected by nature spirits and ancients. They consider the felling of ancient trees with noisy, smoke-belching goblin machinery wanton destruction and desecration, so they attack to drive the Warsong orcs from the forest.",al={"night elf reaction","why elves attack lumber camp","sentinel attacks"},it="hostile"},{q="What role do goblins play in the camp?",a="Goblin mercenaries and technicians supply specialized equipment for the lumber operation, especially steam-powered shredders. The machines let the Warsong harvest and strip massive ancient trees far faster than hand axes can.",al={"goblins at warsong camp","why are shredders here","goblin machinery ashenvale"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Warsong Lumber Camp?",a="Warsong Lumber Camp is a massive fortified logging outpost established by the Warsong clan in central Ashenvale. Anchored by the fortified fortress Kargathia Keep and complete with wolf kennels, it serves as the Horde's primary base of timber production in the ancient forest, sending steady shipments of wood and supplies across Kalimdor to support young orcish settlements like Orgrimmar.",al={"warsong lumber camp","what is this place","about warsong lumber camp"},it="place",add="4dce9068"},{q="Why is it called the Warsong Lumber Camp?",a="The camp is named for the Warsong clan, the fierce orcish clan that first advanced into the ancient woods of Ashenvale under chieftain Grom Hellscream during the Third War. Although their leader perished freeing the orcs from demonic corruption, his clan remains permanently entrenched here, relentlessly driving the Horde's logging efforts despite ferocious resistance from the wilderness.",al={"why called warsong lumber camp","warsong lumber camp name origin"},it="name",add="ae82815c"},{q="Who runs the Warsong Lumber Camp?",a="The camp is operated and garrisoned by orcs of the Warsong clan, working alongside Venture Company-trained goblin mercenaries, engineers, and machine operators. Warsong grunts and kennel masters secure Kargathia Keep and guard the perimeter, while goblin overseers manage the loud, fuel-belching shredders stripping down Ashenvale's ancient trees.",al={"who leads warsong lumber camp","who is in charge here","warsong lumber camp commander"},it="residents",add="4eda0a15"},{q="Is the Warsong Lumber Camp dangerous?",a="It is intensely dangerous. The relentless cutting of Ashenvale has enraged the night elves and the spirits of the forest. Sentinels and vengeful treants launch frequent ambushes from the canopy to smash shredders and reclaim sacred groves. Moreover, Alliance travelers venturing near the perimeter will find Kargathia Keep bristling with aggressive Warsong defenders ready to strike down any trespasser.",al={"is warsong lumber camp dangerous","how dangerous is the lumber camp"},it="danger",add="7474287b"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The lumber cut here supplies building materials for Splintertree Post and fortifications that protect the Horde's future across Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you hear the shredders and see the falling trees as a brutal assault on Ashenvale's sacred balance. The Sentinels have vowed to end it."},kw={"ashenvale","kargathia keep","shredders","splintertree post","timber","warsong clan","warsong lumber camp"},rel={"topic:warsong-clan","zone:ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","subzone:kargathia-keep","subzone:felfire-hill","topic:goblin","topic:horde","topic:third-war"},src={"Warsong Lumber Camp"}}
E["subzone:xavian"] = {t="subzone",n="Xavian",z="ashenvale",s="Xavian lies in northeastern Ashenvale, where satyrs have claimed an ancient night elf temple. It is their chief seat in the forest, and they use its ruins for dark rites that spread demonic corruption through the woodland.",h="Xavian lies in northeastern Ashenvale, where satyrs have claimed an ancient night elf temple.",sec={{t="A Seat of Shadow",b="Xavian lies in Ashenvale's northeastern hills, west of Forest Song and north of Satyrnaar. Satyrs hold the ruined temple, once sacred to the night elves, and make it their chief stronghold in the forest. Their leaders, including Prince Raze and Geltharis, direct their followers from its desecrated arches and terraces. Across the grounds, satyrs perform rites against the woodland and use stolen Warsong oil to blight it. The place bears the name of Xavius, a highborne councilor who became the first satyr during the War of the Ancients after failing Sargeras.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Vanguard",b="Sentinels and woodland guardians watch Xavian, though the satyrs' threat reaches beyond nearby enclaves such as Night Run. Dryad defenders recently entered the ruins to recover the sacred Branch of Cenarius, but suffered grievous losses. Anilia, a dryad, lies dying on the outer terraces. She was struck down while trying to stop the defilers from using holy relics in their dark incantations.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is this place named Xavian?",a="Xavian takes its name from Lord Xavius, Queen Azshara's highborne courtier. During the War of the Ancients, he helped bring the Burning Legion to Azeroth. After displeasing Sargeras, Xavius became the first satyr, and the demonic curse spread to others of his kind.",al={"origin of xavian","who is xavian named after","xavius xavian"},it="name"},{q="What are the satyrs doing here?",a="The satyrs use Xavian as their chief command center in Ashenvale. They perform dark rites to spread demonic corruption through the ancient forest, using defiled sacred relics such as the stolen Branch of Cenarius and oil taken from the Warsong orcs.",al={"what are they doing in xavian","xavian satyr rituals"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is the dying dryad lying on the ground?",a="The dying dryad is Anilia. She joined an effort to recover the stolen Branch of Cenarius from the satyrs and was mortally wounded in the skirmish. She lies among the ruins, pleading for someone to reclaim the sacred branch before corruption overtakes it.",al={"injured dryad xavian","who is anilia","dryad in xavian"},it="target"},{q="How does Xavian differ from Satyrnaar or Night Run?",a="Satyrnaar and Night Run are notable satyr camps in Ashenvale, while Xavian is the political and ritual heart of their forces in the forest. High-ranking leaders such as Geltharis and Prince Raze make their base among its ruins.",al={"satyrnaar vs xavian","other satyr camps","why is xavian important"}},{q="What is Xavian?",a="Xavian is an ancient night elven temple complex nestled in northeastern Ashenvale, now overrun and claimed by satyrs. Situated north of Satyrnaar and west of Forest Song, it stands as the primary seat of satyr political and dark ritual power throughout the entire forest.",al={"what is xavian","xavian lore","about xavian"},it="place",add="a8b6505e"},{q="What happened at Xavian?",a="Once a peaceful sanctuary of the ancient night elves, Xavian fell into ruin and corruption following the War of the Ancients.",al={"xavian history","what happened in xavian","battle at xavian"},it="history",add="cfe8a8e5"},{q="Who rules Xavian?",a="The stronghold is home to a cabal of vicious satyrs and serves as their regional center of authority. Influential leaders such as Prince Raze and Geltharis dwell here, overseeing corruptive rites and directing the activities of their vile brethren across Ashenvale.",al={"who leads xavian","who lives in xavian","xavian leader"},it="residents",add="e57f7c80"},{q="Why is Xavian in ruins?",a="Like many ancient structures across Kalimdor, this sacred night elf temple was shattered ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering and the War of the Ancients. Rather than rebuilding it, the corrupt satyrs settled within the broken stone, twisting the remnants into a bastion for dark sorcery.",al={"why is xavian ruined","who destroyed xavian","xavian ruins"},it="ruin",add="73205fc1"},{q="Is Xavian dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally perilous. Xavian is heavily guarded by aggressive satyr cultists conducting dark rituals with stolen Warsong oil and defiling artifacts like the Branch of Cenarius. Even forest protectors such as dryads have been ambushed and mortally wounded attempting to breach its grounds.",al={"is xavian dangerous","threat in xavian","how dangerous is xavian"},it="danger",add="bc87c8f6"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, the desecration of an ancient temple by the twisted descendants of the Highborne is a bitter offense. The halls call for swift retribution.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you are called to reclaim the Branch of Cenarius from the satyrs, who use fel rites to corrupt the land, and heal the grove's spiritual wounds."},kw={"anilia","ashenvale","branch of cenarius","geltharis","raze","satyr","xavian","xavius"},rel={"zone:ashenvale","topic:satyr","subzone:satyrnaar","subzone:night-run","subzone:forest-song","topic:cenarius","topic:sargeras","topic:war-of-the-ancients"},src={"Xavian"}}
E["subzone:zoram-gar-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Zoram'gar Outpost",z="ashenvale",s="On Ashenvale's western shore, Zoram'gar Outpost gives the Horde access to the Veiled Sea. The fortified beachhead watches the Zoram Strand and the threats rising from its waters and nearby depths.",h="On Ashenvale's western shore, Zoram'gar Outpost gives the Horde access to the Veiled Sea.",sec={{t="A Bastion on the Strand",b="Zoram'gar Outpost holds the northwestern edge of Ashenvale, where the forest meets the sea. Night elf territory lies inland, and hazards wait offshore. Scouts, hunters, and shaman at the isolated camp track local dangers. Life there is an endless vigil: naga prowl the shallows, while cultists and primal horrors stir in Blackfathom Deeps, the subterranean cavern system down the shore.",sp=0},{t="Strategic Importance",b="Zoram'gar Outpost keeps flight connections to other Horde holdings: Splintertree Post, the Crossroads, and Thunder Bluff. Though small, the camp anchors Horde supply lines on Ashenvale's western coast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did the Horde establish Zoram'gar Outpost?",a="The Horde established Zoram'gar Outpost to secure a foothold on Ashenvale's western shoreline. The camp monitors the Zoram Strand by sea and offers a defensible station against the aggressive naga along the coast.",al={"why is zoram'gar here","purpose of zoram gar","why did horde build zoram gar"},it="purpose"},{q="What threats does the outpost face?",a="Wrathtail naga slither across the Zoram Strand, posing an immediate threat. Twilight cultists and beastly horrors in the nearby temple ruins of Blackfathom Deeps are another constant danger.",al={"threats to zoram gar","enemies at zoram gar"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the outpost connect via flight master?",a="Wind riders carry travelers by air across central Kalimdor from Zoram'gar Outpost, linking it to Splintertree Post, Sun Rock Retreat, the Crossroads, and Thunder Bluff, the tauren capital.",al={"flight paths zoram gar","where can i fly from zoram gar"},gp=true},{q="What is the relation between the outpost and Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps lies just north of Zoram'gar Outpost among shoreline ruins. Horde forces stationed at the outpost watch corruption seep from the flooded temple and send adventurers inside to oppose the cultists and their beast, Aku'mai.",al={"blackfathom deeps near zoram","is bfd near zoram gar"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Zoram'gar Outpost?",a="Zoram'gar Outpost is a fortified Horde beachhead on the Zoram Strand, situated in northwestern Ashenvale along the Veiled Sea. It provides the Horde with vital access to the western coast, functioning as a coastal camp and military staging encampment isolated amidst hostile territory.",al={"what is zoramgar outpost","zoram'gar outpost overview","about zoram strand outpost"},it="place",add="bbfe9eaf"},{q="Is Zoram'gar Outpost dangerous?",a="The outpost itself offers safety, defense, and shelter for travelers of the Horde, but the surrounding Zoram Strand is perilous. Aggressive naga patrol the surf and nearby ruins, while Alliance forces and ancient horrors lurking within Blackfathom Deeps threaten anyone who steps away from the campfire's guard.",al={"how dangerous is zoram'gar","zoram'gar outpost danger","is zoram strand safe"},it="danger",add="53f73dc3"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find your primary haven in northwest Ashenvale at Zoram'gar Outpost, with shelter, rest, and wind rider transport amid dangerous wilderness.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you face an entrenched Horde presence on Ashenvale's coast. Zoram'gar Outpost holds a dangerous supply foothold near night elf ancestral lands."},kw={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","horde","naga","outpost","zoram gar","zoram strand","zoram'gar"},rel={"subzone:zoram-strand","zone:blackfathom","zone:ashenvale","subzone:splintertree-post","quest:6442","quest:6563","npc:aku-mai","topic:horde"},src={"Zoram'gar Outpost"}}
E["subzone:zoram-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Zoram Strand",z="ashenvale",s="At Ashenvale's northwestern edge, Zoram Strand faces the Veiled Sea. The shore holds the ruins of an ancient night elven city, now overrun by Wrathtail naga, shipwrecks, and beached leviathans. Blackfathom Deeps begins in the submerged temple complex nearby.",h="At Ashenvale's northwestern edge, Zoram Strand faces the Veiled Sea.",sec={{t="Ruins of the Sundered Coast",b="Ten thousand years ago, the night elven city of Zoram stood on this coast. The Great Sundering tore Kalimdor apart and sank the settlement beneath the sea. Now the tide brings ancient relics, shattered vessels, and the carcasses of massive sea beasts onto the shore. Wrathtail naga overrun the beaches and tidal pools, guarding the flooded ruins and ancient artifacts from anyone who comes near.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Shoreline",b="Travelers from the mainland and along the coast still come to Zoram Strand despite the naga. South of the shore, the Horde holds Zoram'gar Outpost, where its warriors fight to secure the coast. Nearby, Blackfathom Deeps lies deep within the caverns. The ancient temple of Elune has fallen into dark hands, drawing scouts, scholars, and treasure seekers who brave the surf.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Zoram before it was destroyed?",a="Before the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, Zoram was a grand night elven city. The cataclysm shattered the coast and sank the city beneath the Veiled Sea, leaving jagged ruins and statuettes washed ashore.",al={"zoram history","ancient zoram","what was zoram"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the Zoram Strand today?",a="Wrathtail naga overrun most of the shoreline and defend its shallows and ancient ruins. The Horde holds a fortified outpost along the southern cliffs, while hydras and crabs prowl the sand.",al={"who lives at zoram strand","zoram strand enemies","who controls zoram strand"},it="residents"},{q="Where is the entrance to Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The entrance to Blackfathom Deeps lies in submerged caverns along Zoram Strand. Travelers enter the coastal caves at the water's edge to reach the descent into the sunken temple.",al={"blackfathom deeps location","how to find bfd","bfd entrance zoram"},gp=true},{q="Why are there so many beached sea creatures here?",a="The Veiled Sea's turbulent tides and dark currents often wash massive marine creatures ashore. Researchers and naturalists from both factions search the remains to learn what drives ocean behemoths to perish along the rocks.",al={"beached sea creature quest","dead whales zoram strand","beached creatures"}},{q="What is Zoram Strand?",a="The Zoram Strand is a rugged coastal stretch in northwestern Ashenvale bordering the Veiled Sea. Once part of an ancient night elven city before the Great Sundering, the beach is now a contested shoreline littered with shipwrecks, beached leviathans, and ruins. It serves as both the site of the Horde's fortified Zoram'gar Outpost and the surface entrance leading down into the subterranean labyrinth of Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"what is zoram strand","zoram strand info","about zoram strand"},it="place",add="449b54c1"},{q="Why is Zoram Strand ruined?",a="Ten thousand years ago, during the Great Sundering, the ancient night elven settlement of Zoram was shattered and largely drowned beneath the rising waters of the Veiled Sea. What remains on the coast today is only the ruined fringe of that fallen city, long left to decay until the serpentine naga surfaced from the ocean depths to claim the shoreline and its submerged temples.",al={"why is zoram ruined","what happened to zoram","destruction of zoram strand"},it="ruin",add="7861a3b9"},{q="Is Zoram Strand dangerous?",a="Very. The coastline is overrun by the aggressive Wrathtail naga, who fiercely defend the ruins and strike at travelers along the water's edge. Hostile crab crawlers and vicious hydras lurk among the waves and beached carcasses. Beyond the wilderness threats, dark cultists and sinister horrors hide beneath the surface within the passages of Blackfathom Deeps, making this mist-shrouded beach unsafe for the unwary.",al={"how dangerous is zoram strand","zoram strand threats","threats along zoram strand"},it="danger",add="3de65288"},{q="Why is it called Zoram Strand?",a="The coast takes its name from Zoram, the ancient night elven city that stood along this coastline prior to the Great Sundering. Though the original city was shattered and swallowed by the ocean, the surviving beach and surrounding ruins have carried its name ever since.",al={"where did zoram get its name","why zoram strand","meaning of zoram strand"},it="name",add="8dedb8fb"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, Zoram Strand recalls the ancient world lost to the Sundering. Naga now tread among sacred relics and submerged temples to Elune.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, defending the approaches to Zoram'gar Outpost helps keep a northern naval and coastal presence in Ashenvale against the relentless Wrathtail brood."},kw={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","naga","ruuzel","veiled sea","wrathtail","zoram","zoram strand"},rel={"subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","zone:blackfathom","zone:ashenvale","quest:1008","quest:6442","quest:1007","quest:1009","topic:naga"},src={"Zoram Strand"}}
E["zone:ashenvale"] = {t="zone",n="Ashenvale",z="ashenvale",s="Ashenvale's sacred woods are now a battleground as the Horde cuts timber for Orgrimmar. The ancient forest lies between the Barrens to the south and Darkshore to the north, under the care of the Sentinels and Cenarius. Its canopy shelters moonwells and old ruins, alongside demonic blights, hostile tribes, and a contested frontier.",h="Ashenvale's sacred woods are now a battleground as the Horde cuts timber for Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="The Whispering Canopy",b="Beneath Mount Hyjal, Ashenvale has belonged to the kaldorei and the children of Cenarius for millennia. Immense trees form a close canopy, turning the daily rain to mist and leaving the forest floor in twilight. Moss covers the ruins of elven settlements, where walking ancients and dryads keep watch. For thousands of years, the night elves built no true cities here. They hunted lightly and kept the wild domain in balance.",sp=0},{t="War for the Woods",b="The Third War broke Ashenvale's peace when Grommash Hellscream and the Warsong clan entered for lumber. Their demonic bloodlust led them to slay Cenarius. The struggle is now a full territorial war. From Splintertree Post and the southern Mor'shan Rampart, the Warsong Outriders send axes and shredders into the eastern woods to supply Orgrimmar. The Silverwing Sentinels hold Astranaar, a sanctuary town, and have sworn to drive every orcish logger from the sacred grove.",sp=0},{t="Lingering Shadows",b="The lumber war is only one danger in Ashenvale. The Burning Legion left blighted scars at Felfire Hill and Demon Fall Canyon, where Mannoroth died. Satyrs use ruins such as Satyrnaar and Xavian as bases, corrupting waterways and wildlife. Furbolg tribes, once friends of the elves, have largely fallen to dark madness. Mysterious worgen stalk the northern shrine near Felwood, while cursed dragonkin prowl Bough Shadow and guard a portal into the troubled Emerald Dream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Horde and Alliance fighting in Ashenvale?",a="The Horde needs Ashenvale's timber to build Orgrimmar and sustain its young nation. The orcs of Durotar have little timber in their dry homeland, while the night elves hold Ashenvale as a sacred ancestral home under nature deities' protection. The Silverwing Sentinels see the Warsong clan's clear-cutting as desecration, and the dispute brings skirmishes and pitched fighting in Warsong Gulch.",al={"why horde cutting trees","ashenvale war reason","warsong vs silverwing"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened to Cenarius in this forest?",a="During the Third War, Grommash Hellscream led the Warsong clan into Ashenvale for timber. Cenarius attacked to defend the sacred grove. Desperate to defeat the demigod, Grommash and his clan drank from a fountain tainted by the pit lord Mannoroth. The demonic fury they gained let them slay Cenarius. Grom later broke the curse by killing Mannoroth at Demon Fall Canyon, but the elves have not forgotten their patron demigod's murder.",al={"how cenarius died","grom killed cenarius","cenarius fate"},it="history"},{q="What is Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps lies beneath the Zoram Strand on Ashenvale's northwestern coast. The sunken temple was once an ancient kaldorei temple to Elune, then collapsed into the sea during the Great Sundering. Savage naga, Twilight's Hammer cultists, and aquatic beasts now overrun it and revere the ancient hydra Aku'mai.",al={"where is bfd","bfd lore","blackfathom deeps history"},it="place"},{q="What is the Great Tree at Bough Shadow?",a="Bough Shadow holds one of four Great Trees planted by the Cenarion Circle thousands of years ago to anchor conduits into the Emerald Dream. The tree remains an active gateway between Azeroth and the Dream. Green dragonspawn guard the area, though a sinister taint in the Dream sometimes sends monstrous Nightmare Dragons through the portal.",al={"bough shadow tree","portal bough shadow","green dragons ashenvale"},it="place"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Ashenvale hostile?",a="The furbolgs of Ashenvale were peaceful allies of the night elves for centuries, until demonic taint from the Burning Legion's invasion shattered their minds. Fel magic lingering from places such as Felwood, Satyrnaar, and Demon Fall Canyon drove tribes like the Thistlefur into violent madness. They turned against outsiders and their own kin.",al={"crazy furbolgs ashenvale","thistlefur corrupt","why furbolgs attack"},it="threat"},{q="Who is buried at Demon Fall Canyon?",a="Demon Fall Canyon is where Grommash Hellscream and Thrall faced the pit lord Mannoroth. Grom struck the demon lord a fatal blow, freeing the orcish race from the demonic blood curse at the cost of his life. A monument to Grom Hellscream stands there, and many orcs make pilgrimage to honor the warrior who freed their people.",al={"mannoroth canyon","grommash grave ashenvale","monument demon fall"},it="history"},{q="How do I travel through Ashenvale?",a="Alliance travelers usually enter Ashenvale through the northern mountain pass from Auberdine in Darkshore, then follow the highway east toward Astranaar. Horde travelers march north from the Barrens through the fortified Mor'shan Rampart toward Splintertree Post, or west to Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand. Both factions keep flight masters at their major fortresses.",al={"how to get to ashenvale","ashenvale travel","ashenvale flight paths"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What is Ashenvale?",a="Ashenvale is an ancient, sprawling primordial rainforest lying south of Darkshore and Felwood, and directly north of the Barrens and the Stonetalon Mountains. Known as the ancestral homeland of the night elves, it has been cherished and preserved by them for thousands of years. Its canopy is so massive and dense that soft rains fall almost constantly while barely penetrating to the forest floor. Today, it stands as a contested wilderness where ancient spirits and Kaldorei Sentinels battle encroaching lumber expeditions, invading demonic remnants, and feral beasts.",al={"what is ashenvale","about ashenvale","tell me about ashenvale","ashenvale zone"},it="place",add="97bd7929",nx={10,11}},{q="What happened to Ashenvale during the Third War?",a="During the Third War, Ashenvale suffered catastrophic upheaval. The Warsong clan under Grommash Hellscream first invaded to harvest lumber, inadvertently provoking the demigod Cenarius. Tricked by demonic influence, Grom drank demon blood and slew Cenarius. Soon after, Archimonde and the Burning Legion invaded in force, raining infernals upon the woodland and pushing toward Mount Hyjal. The Legion's dreadlords unleashed foul blights that scarred parts of the wilderness into the corrupted wasteland known as Felwood, leaving lingering demonic scars that persist across the forest today.",al={"ashenvale history","what happened in ashenvale","third war ashenvale"},it="history",add="d00ef10f"},{q="Who lives in Ashenvale?",a="For millennia, the forest was preserved in a wild state, inhabited primarily by forest beasts, dryads, keepers of the grove, and sentient ancients, watched over by roving night elf Sentinels rather than urban settlements. Today, the night elves maintain fortified outposts like Astranaar and Maestra's Post. In the east and along the western coast, the Horde has carved out enclaves like Splintertree Post and Zoram'gar Outpost. The wild interior shelters furbolg tribes, hostile satyrs, harpies, and lingering demonic broods.",al={"who lives in ashenvale","ashenvale inhabitants","who lives here"},it="residents",add="3f2d3290"},{q="Why is the forest being cut down?",a="The orcs of the Horde, led by the Warsong clan, need lumber to sustain their settlements and fuel their expansion in the arid plains of Durotar and the Barrens. To the night elves, Ashenvale's ancient trees and living ancients are sacred and alive. Cutting them down is viewed as an unforgivable desecration, turning every logging camp and saw into an open provocation that sparks endless blood shed.",al={"why cut trees","why are they logging","warsong lumber why","deforestation ashenvale"},it="motive",add="24f461e0"},{q="Is Ashenvale dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. Roads are overgrown and choked by shadows, prowled by giant bears, predatory cats, and wildkin. Beyond the beasts, violent satyrs haunt ancient ruins, corrupted furbolgs attack all who approach, and pockets of burning fel corruption harbor demons. Travelers must also contend with the open faction war: the Silverwing Sentinels and Warsong Outriders actively hunt enemy scouts across the canopy.",al={"is ashenvale dangerous","how dangerous is ashenvale","dangers of ashenvale"},it="danger",add="d5bfe513"},{q="Who is in charge of Ashenvale?",a="No single authority holds undivided dominion over Ashenvale. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and the night elf Sentinels claim rightful stewardship over their ancestral lands, commanding outposts like Astranaar and guarding the groves with wandering ancients. However, the Horde fiercely contests eastern Ashenvale through the Warsong clan and Splintertree Post, turning the heart of the forest into a bitterly disputed frontier.",al={"who rules ashenvale","who is in charge here","ashenvale leadership"},it="in_charge",add="534156e4",nx={14}},{q="What are the Sentinels?",a="The Sentinels are the elite, standing military order of the night elves, composed of dedicated female warriors, huntresses, and archers. Founded after the War of the Ancients, they undertook the Long Vigil under High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind while the male druids slumbered in the Emerald Dream. They patrol the forests with deadly panther mounts and unmatched stealth, striking down any trespasser who desecrates nature.",al={"what are the sentinels","night elf sentinels","who are the sentinels"},it="people",add="0575374f"},{q="What is Astranaar?",a="Astranaar is the primary night elven town in central Ashenvale and the main base of Alliance operations in the region. Built atop an island in the middle of a lake and accessed only by bridges straddling the forest road, it serves as a trading hub, sanctuary, and defensive bastion against relentless attacks from the Horde and neighboring corrupted furbolgs.",al={"what is astranaar","astranaar town","tell me about astranaar"},it="place",add="42b1a6f5"},{q="What is Splintertree Post?",a="Splintertree Post is the Horde's fortified stronghold in eastern Ashenvale. Established following the Third War, it acts as the primary military vanguard protecting the Warsong clan's extensive logging operations at the Warsong Lumber Camp and shielding the road leading south to the Mor'shan Rampart and the Barrens.",al={"what is splintertree post","splintertree post","splintertree horde"},it="place",add="56b6ce63"},{q="What are the satyrs and where did they come from?",a="Satyrs are vile, horned demonic humanoids transformed from ancient Highborne night elves who pledged their service to the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients, beginning with Lord Xavius. Sworn enemies of all Kaldorei, they lurk in ancient elven ruins like Xavian, Night Run, and Satyrnaar, wielding foul shadow magic and working to spread corruption across the pristine groves.",al={"what are satyrs","satyr origins","where do satyrs come from"},it="threat",add="64786646"},{q="What is the Zoram Strand?",a="The Zoram Strand is a strip of rugged coastline forming the northwestern boundary of Ashenvale along the Veiled Sea. Once part of the pre-Sundering elven coast, it is now infested by hostile naga and murlocs, and hosts the ruined entrance to Blackfathom Deeps as well as the Horde's isolated coastal redoubt, Zoram'gar Outpost.",al={"what is the zoram strand","zoram strand","zoram beach"},it="place",add="e95425a8"},{q="How did I end up in Ashenvale?",a="Your path here depends on your allegiances. If you fight for the Alliance, you likely followed the sentinel road south from Auberdine in Darkshore, passing into the shadowed boughs toward Maestra's Post and Astranaar. If you ride with the Horde, you marched north along the dusty Gold Road from the Crossroads in the Barrens, crossing through the fortified barricades of the Mor'shan Rampart straight into the dense forest.",al={"how did i get here","how do i reach ashenvale","getting to ashenvale"},it="arrival",add="273c413f"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Ashenvale?",a="You stand in a contested wilderness caught between ancient guardians and bold invaders. Alliance champions rally at Astranaar to defend the night elves' ancestral homeland, repel Horde lumber operations, cleanse corrupted furbolgs, and strike at lingering demonic cults. Horde adventurers push out from Splintertree Post and Zoram'gar Outpost to secure desperately needed timber for Durotar, expand territorial holdings, and survive the wrath of the woodland spirits and Sentinels.",al={"why am i here","what do i do in ashenvale","what is my goal here"},it="purpose",add="023178b1"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Ashenvale is your spiritual homeland and the legacy of Cenarius. Defending its groves from Warsong axes and clearing satyr corruption from its moonwells are matters of kaldorei honor.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, this timber supplies the walls and siege towers of Orgrimmar. Ashenvale is also sacred ground where Grommash Hellscream shed blood to free the orcish race from demonic servitude.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see nature's balance under attack from many sides. Lumber operations, corrupted furbolg dens, and the nightmare-haunted portal at Bough Shadow all leave Ashenvale in need of Cenarion restoration.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you find rich gathering grounds in Ashenvale, fed by ancient magical leyways and steady rain. Briarthorn, Stranglekelp, and Kingsblood grow here, with rare Gromsblood near demonic scars."},kw={"ashenvale","astranaar","bough shadow","cenarius","grommash","mannoroth","silverwing","splintertree","warsong","zoram"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:barrens","zone:blackfathom","subzone:astranaar","subzone:demon-fall-canyon","subzone:bough-shadow","subzone:mor-shan-rampart"},m={levels="18-30"},src={"Ashenvale (Classic)","Ashenvale"}}
